window.GRE_Q = window.GRE_Q || {};
window.GRE_Q["verbal"] = {"id":"verbal","name":"填空","desc":"填空机经 2000 题（285 组，每组 7 题）","official":false,"sets":[{"id":"v1-1","title":"Test 1 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v1.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It is a paradox of the Victorians that they were both _____ and, through their empire, cosmopolitan.","key":"B","opts":["capricious","insular","mercenary","idealistic","intransigent"],"expl":"维多利亚人既“封闭、自守”（insular）又通过帝国变得世界主义，二者形成对照。insular 意为“狭隘、孤立的”。选 B"},{"id":"v1.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)_____ of molecular oxygen on Earth-sized planets around other stars in the universe would not be (ii)_____ sign of life: molecular oxygen can be a signature of photosynthesis (a biotic process) or merely of the rapid escape of water from the upper reaches of a planetary atmosphere (an abiotic process).","key":"CE","groups":[["dearth","presumption","detection"],["a controversial","an unambiguous","a possible"]],"expl":"空1 填 detection（探测）：在别的恒星周围的类地行星上探测到氧气；空2 填 a possible（可能的）：氧气本身既可能是生物过程，也可能是非生物过程，因此并不是“明确的”生命迹象。选 CE"},{"id":"v1.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The skin of the poison dart frog contains deadly poisons called batrachotoxins. But the (i)_____ of the toxins has remained an enigma, as the frog does not (ii)_____ them. Now an analysis suggests that the melyrid beetle is the source. Collected beetle specimens all contained batrachotoxins, suggesting that these beetles are (iii)_____ by the frogs.","key":"BEG","groups":[["effect","origin","purpose"],["pressure","produce","suffer from"],["eaten","neutralized","poisoned"]],"expl":"空1 填 origin（来源）：毒素的来源是个谜；空2 填 produce（产生）：青蛙自身并不生产这些毒素；空3 填 eaten（被吃掉）：甲虫体内有毒素，说明青蛙吃了它们。选 BEG"},{"id":"v1.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The beauty of the scientific approach is that even when individual researchers do _____ bias or partiality, others can correct them using a framework of evidence on which everyone broadly agrees.","key":"CE","opts":["overreact to","deviate from","succumb to","recoil from","yield to","shrink from"],"expl":"在科学方法中，即使研究者有偏见，他人也能纠正。succumb to（屈服于）与 yield to（屈服于）都表示“被偏见左右”。选 CE"},{"id":"v1.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The reconstruct known work is beautiful and also probably _____: it is the only Hebrew verse written by a woman.","key":"AB","opts":["singular","unique","archaic","counterfeit","valuable","fake"],"expl":"这首诗是唯一一首由女性写的希伯来诗，因此它很可能是“独一无二”的（unique）；它也可能是“独一无二”的赝品（counterfeit/fake）。注意题干的 reconstruct 是原文拼写错误，不影响选项。选 AB"},{"id":"v1.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In a book that inclines to _____, an epilogue arguing that ballet is dead arrives simply as one more overstatement.","key":"EF","opts":["pessimism","misinterpretation","imprecision","vagueness","exaggeration","hyperbole"],"expl":"一本倾向于夸大（exaggeration）的书，其后记宣称芭蕾已死，就只是又一个“夸张的说法”（hyperbole）。选 EF"},{"id":"v1.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The political upheaval caught most people by surprise: despite the _____ warnings of some commentators, it had never seemed that imminent.","key":"BC","opts":["stern","prescient","prophetic","indifferent","repeated","apathetic"],"expl":"“预言性的”警告（prescient/prophetic）与“事先感觉不妙”的表达吻合，所以在这里指“预见到危险”的评论员。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v1-2","title":"Test 1 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v1.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"My grandma has a strong belief in all things _____: she insists, for example, that the house in which she lived as a child was haunted.","key":"C","opts":["clamorous","invidious","numinous","empirical","sonorous"],"expl":"numinous 意为“有神秘的、超自然的意味”，与“相信超自然事物”的语境一致。选 C"},{"id":"v1.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Among the Meakambut people of Papua New Guinea, legends are associated with specific caves in the Sepik region, and these legends are _____: only the cave owner can share its secrets.","key":"C","opts":["impenetrable","immutable","proprietary","didactic","self-perpetuating"],"expl":"cave 的传说只有洞穴的主人能分享，说明这些传说是“私有的”（proprietary，属于特定所有者）。选 C"},{"id":"v1.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Given the (i)_____ the committees and the (ii)_____ nature of its investigation, it would be unreasonable to gainsay the committee’s conclusions at first glance.","key":"AF","groups":[["sterling reputation of","lack of finding of","ad hoc existence of"],["superficial","spontaneous","exhaustive"]],"expl":"空1 填 sterling reputation of（卓越声誉）：委员会的卓著声誉让人不便质疑；空2 填 exhaustive（彻底的）：调查既彻底又可靠，因此不能轻易反驳。选 AF"},{"id":"v1.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Now that photographic prints have become a popular field for collecting, auctions are becoming more (i)_____. It is not just the entry of new collectors into the field that is causing this intensification. Established collectors’ interests are also becoming more (ii)_____. Those who once concentrated on the work of either the nineteenth-century pioneers or the twentieth-century modernists are now keen to have (iii)_____ collections.","key":"AEG","groups":[["competitive","tedious","exclusive"],["fickle","wide-ranging","antiquarian"],["comprehensive","legitimate","impressive"]],"expl":"空1 填 competitive（竞争性的）：拍卖变得更激烈；空2 填 wide-ranging（范围广的）：收藏家的兴趣更广；空3 填 comprehensive（全面的）：想要全面的收藏。选 AEG"},{"id":"v1.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Members of the union’s negotiating team insisted on several changes to the company’s proposal before they would support it, making it clear that they would _____ no compromise.","key":"CD","opts":["disclose","reject","brook","tolerate","repudiate","weigh"],"expl":"谈判代表坚持要求改动，说明他们不会让步。brook（容忍）与 tolerate（容忍）都可用于“不允许妥协”的语境。选 CD"},{"id":"v1.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Wilson is wont to emphasize the _____ of ants: how ants with full stomachs will regurgitate liquid food for those without, or how the old will fight so the young can survive.","key":"AB","opts":["beneficence","altruism","unpredictability","intelligence","fecundity","fertility"],"expl":"作者强调蚂蚁的“利他行为”（altruism，无私帮助他人），如让饱食的蚂蚁反刍喂养饥饿者；beneficence（善行）也可表示这种善意。选 AB"},{"id":"v1.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"During the Renaissance, the use of optical lenses, which were capable of projecting images onto blank canvases, greatly aided artists by allowing them to accurately observe and depict the external world; in other words, these lenses were instrumental in conveying _____.","key":"DF","opts":["idealism","optimism","ambition","realism","sanguinity","verisimilitude"],"expl":"光学透镜帮助画家“精确地描绘外部世界”，因此它们帮助实现了“现实主义”（realism）和“逼真”（verisimilitude）。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v2-1","title":"Test 2 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v2.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"We often regard natural phenomena like rainfall as mysterious and unpredictable; although for short time spans and particular places they appear so, in fact on a truly global scale, nature has been a model of _____.","key":"A","opts":["reliability","diversity","complexity","plasticity","discontinuity"],"expl":"自然界在全球尺度上是“稳定、可靠”（reliability）的模型，与“看似不可预测”形成对照。选 A"},{"id":"v2.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The economic recovery was somewhat lopsided: (i)_____ in some of the industrial economies while (ii)_____ in others of them.","key":"BD","groups":[["unexpected","feeble","swift"],["robust","turbulent","predictable"]],"expl":"空1 填 robust（强劲的）：某些工业经济体恢复强劲；空2 填 feeble（疲软的）：其他经济体则疲软（相对于前者的“不均衡”）。选 BD"},{"id":"v2.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Most capuchin monkey conflict involves such a (i)_____ repertoire of gestural and vocal signals that it is difficult for researchers to tease apart the meanings of the individual signals. This (ii)_____ is (iii)_____ by the fact that many signals seem to shift in meaning according to the context in which they are produced and the developmental stage of the individuals producing them.","key":"BDG","groups":[["precise","rich","straightforward"],["problem","opportunity","oversight"],["augmented","ameliorated","anticipated"]],"expl":"空1 填 rich（丰富的）：信号库非常丰富；空2 填 problem（问题）：这造成了研究上的困难；空3 填 augmented（加剧）：多种因素使困难加剧。选 BDG"},{"id":"v2.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The professor’s habitual air of _____ was misleading front, concealing amazing reserves of patience and a deep commitment to his students’ learning.","key":"BF","opts":["cordiality","irascibility","disorganization","conviviality","diffidence","exasperation"],"expl":"“看似的……习惯”是误导性的，掩盖了耐心与热心，所以是“冷漠、缺乏热情”（diffidence，羞怯、拘谨）。选 BF"},{"id":"v2.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In matters of taste, the art patron and collector Peggy Guggenheim was _____, she was for the strangest, the most surprising, the most satisfying, the best, the unique.","key":"DF","opts":["a neophyte","a novice","a realist","an extremist","a pragmatist","a zealot"],"expl":"Peggy 在品位上是“极端派”（extremist），她追求最奇特、最独特的东西，。选 DF"},{"id":"v2.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The laboratory maze has grown ever less _____ since it was first invented instead of hoping to lose a rodent in a labyrinth; today’s scientists design mazes to elicit a few simple, easily measured behaviors.","key":"AD","opts":["intricate","extensive","effective","convoluted","useful","prevalent"],"expl":"迷宫随着时间变得越来越不 intricate（复杂、错综）或 convoluted（曲折、错综），科学家设计的迷宫更简单。选 AD"},{"id":"v2.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In mathematics, judgments about the validity of proofs are mediated by peer-reviewed journals; to ensure _____, reviewers are carefully chosen by journal editors, and the identity of scholars whose papers are under consideration are kept secret.","key":"CE","opts":["timelessness","originality","fairness","comprehensiveness","objectivity","novelty"],"expl":"同行评审的目的是保证公正（fairness）与客观（objectivity）：评审人与作者互不知晓，正是为保证客观。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v2-2","title":"Test 2 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v2.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Though we live in an era of stunning scientific achievement, many otherwise educated people remain indifferent to or contemptuous of such achievement, even going so far as to _____ their ignorance of basic physics.","key":"D","opts":["decry","condone","remedy","boast of","downplay"],"expl":"有些人对科学成就漠不关心甚至鄙视，甚至会“吹嘘”自己的无知（boast of），这是对前半句的递进。选 D"},{"id":"v2.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although trains may use energy more (i)_____ than do automobiles, the latter move only when they contain at least one occupant, whereas railway carriages spend a considerable amount of time running up and down the tracks (ii)_____, or nearly so.","key":"BD","groups":[["lavishly","efficiently","routinely"],["vacant","unimpeded","overlooked"]],"expl":"空1 填 efficiently（有效地）：火车的能效比汽车高；空2 填 vacant（空载的）：火车经常在轨道上空跑。选 BD"},{"id":"v2.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The great (i)_____ of most books that examine the American presidency is their ideological bias, but for most part, this volume on the presidency maintains an impressive degree of (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["contribution","limitation","paradox"],["certainty","fluency","objectivity"]],"expl":"空1 填 limitation（局限）：这些书的最大局限是意识形态偏见；空2 填 objectivity（客观性）：这本书保持了相当的客观。选 BF"},{"id":"v2.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Within the culture as a whole, the natural sciences have been so successful that the word “scientific” is often used in (i)_____ manner: it is often assumed that to call something “scientific” is to imply that its reliability has been (ii)_____ by methods whose results cannot reasonably be (iii)_____.","key":"CFI","groups":[["an ironic","a literal","an honorific"],["maligned","challenged","established"],["exaggerated","anticipated","disputed"]],"expl":"空1 填 an honorific（尊称式的）：“科学的”一词被当作一种褒义词；空2 填 established（确立）；空3 填 disputed（有争议的）：结果不能被合理质疑。选 CFI"},{"id":"v2.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since some contemporary Western dieticians believe that the only function of food is to provide nourishment, these dieticians view an emphasis on the aesthetic dimension of the culinary arts as _____.","key":"BD","opts":["unprecedented","unwarranted","illuminating","groundless","promising","novel"],"expl":"当代营养学者认为食物只为营养，因此他们会认为强调审美的做法是“没有道理的”（groundless）或“不合理的”（unwarranted）。选 BD"},{"id":"v2.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Harper Lee’s narration in To Kill a Mockingbird is _____, mixing an adult’s and a child’s perspective according to no logic other than the immediate exigencies of the plot.","key":"BE","opts":["a paradigm","a hodgepodge","a model","an innovation","a patchwork","an embarrassment"],"expl":"Lee 的叙述混合了成人与儿童的视角，没有逻辑，是“杂拼”（hodgepodge/patchwork）。选 BE"},{"id":"v2.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The employee had a reputation for fractiousness, but his coworkers found him to be, on the contrary, quiet _____.","key":"BE","opts":["insightful","affable","sagacious","capable","easygoing","productive"],"expl":"反义：员工名声不好（fractiousness），但同事发现他很安静、随和（easygoing）、友善（affable）。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v3-1","title":"Test 3 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v3.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Slight but _____ variation in the timing of the star’s pulses led astronomers to deduce that it was being pulled backwards and forwards by three planets orbiting around it.","key":"A","opts":["subtle","regular","undetectable","inconsequential","explicable"],"expl":"脉冲虽然“细微”（subtle），却足以推断出三颗行星的引力影响。选 A"},{"id":"v3.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many of the towns that have voted to keep incinerators in the county’s solid waste plan have done so not because they necessarily (i)_____ incinerators, but because they are (ii)_____ to narrow their waste-disposal options.","key":"BF","groups":[["question","favor","oppose"],["willing","eager","loath"]],"expl":"空1 填 favor（支持）：不是因为他们喜欢焚烧炉，而是不得不接受；空2 填 loath（不情愿）：他们不愿意放弃焚烧这一选择。选 BF"},{"id":"v3.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Just because, as a photographer, Friedlander (i)_____ places that most people consider ugly does not mean that he is out to prove they are beautiful. Instead, his work suggests that the photographer simply cannot ignore so much of the built American landscape but is obligated to (ii)_____ what we pass through day in and day out, regardless of (iii)_____.","key":"CDI","groups":[["tends to avoid","is harshly critical of","is interested in"],["document","emulate","discredit"],["authenticity","truthfulness","aesthetics"]],"expl":"空1 填 is interested in（关注）：摄影师关注被认为丑陋的地方；空2 填 document（记录）；空3 填 aesthetics（美学）：不论美学标准如何。选 CDI"},{"id":"v3.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even though women in the US would not gain the rights to vote until 1920, throughout the nineteenth century many feminist goals were gradually _____, especially the rights of married women to control their own property.","key":"AF","opts":["realized","abandoned","eroded","modified","revised","achieved"],"expl":"女性权利在 19 世纪逐渐被 achieved（实现）：已婚妇女的财产权是实现的例子。选 AF"},{"id":"v3.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Edited collections of scholarly essays generally tend to be somewhat uneven: they suffer from the _____ subject matter of the various essays, the lack of an overarching and consistent thesis, and the variable quantity of the contributions.","key":"BD","opts":["intriguing","heterogeneous","comprehensive","disparate","mediocre","engaging"],"expl":"论文集的主题“杂乱、不统一”（heterogeneous/disparate）。选 BD"},{"id":"v3.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Miller reminded his clients that labor relationship are inherently _____: the interests of business owners are diametrically opposed to those of employees.","key":"AD","opts":["adversarial","exploitative","mercenary","antagonistic","variable","changeable"],"expl":"劳资关系本质上是 adversarial（对抗的）与 antagonistic（对立的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v3.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Progressive and reactionary populist movements are not necessarily _____; each may, and usually does, possess features of the other.","key":"AD","opts":["dichotomous","untenable","unsustainable","contradictory","subversive","efficacious"],"expl":"进步派与保守派民粹运动不一定是“二分对立”（dichotomous）的，二者都可能有对方的特点。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v3-2","title":"Test 3 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v3.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In the last two hundreds years, the practice of archaeology has changed greatly, from digging up ancient artifacts for use by wealthy individuals as art objects to analyzing the detritus of everyday life in the laboratory, and thus from _____ to data collection.","key":"D","opts":["supposition","theorizing","fact-finding","treasure hunting","scientific discovery"],"expl":"从“挖宝”（treasure hunting）转向“数据收集”，是考古学的转变。选 D"},{"id":"v3.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"What they see in Tanaka is the one candidate capable of (i)_____ leadership, in direct contrast to Williamson , whose term in office has been marred by (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["compassionate","decisive","nepotistic"],["grandstanding","partisanship","vacillation"]],"expl":"空1 填 decisive（果断的）；空2 填 vacillation（犹豫不决）：与果断形成对照。选 BF"},{"id":"v3.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Both very good and very bad books are easy to review. Praise and (i)_____ come easily. But what of books that contain a muddle of virtues and vices? Here the reviewer’s task is more (ii)_____: the author’s useful and thought-provoking observations need to be (iii)_____ the useless and tedious.","key":"CEH","groups":[["ambivalence","compliment","censure"],["evident","demanding","manageable"],["supplanted by","sifted from","overshadowed by"]],"expl":"空1 填 ambivalence（矛盾心理）：既有赞美也有批评；空2 填 demanding（需要更多努力的）；空3 填 sifted from（从中筛选出）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v3.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unambiguous texts can allow their readers to (i)_____ them quickly, but ambiguous texts can have the attractive (ii)_____ of multiple possible interpretations, all of which can be considered equally (iii)_____, and none of which is the single true meaning.","key":"BFG","groups":[["misunderstand","comprehend","complicate"],["stigma","blemish","allure"],["valid","frank","inveterate"]],"expl":"空1 填 comprehend（理解）；空2 填 allure（魅力）；空3 填 valid（有效的）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v3.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although extreme and singular events occur in a black hole, its event horizon boundary is _____ space travelers; crossing it would be subject to the same physical laws that apply anywhere else.","key":"CF","opts":["illusory","obscure","unremarkable","immutable","unchanging","commonplace"],"expl":"黑洞的事件视界并不对旅行者造成特殊障碍，服从与其他地方相同的物理规律，因此它是“平常的”（unremarkable）。选 CF"},{"id":"v3.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ocean's heat capacity (the amount of heat needed to change its temperature) is far greater than that of dry land and thus _____ the ocean's seasonal temperature changes.","key":"BE","opts":["reflects","mutes","alters","determines","attenuates","parallels"],"expl":"海洋的热容量大，因此会“缓和”（mutes）或“减弱”（attenuates）季节性温度变化。选 BE"},{"id":"v3.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the nineteenth century, the dish known as lobster Newburg was sometimes associated with the culinary accessory known as the chafing dish, but Welsh rarebit was considered the truly ______ chafing dish recipe.","key":"DF","opts":["indigenous","sumptuous","ubiquitous","paradigmatic","newfangled","archetypal"],"expl":"Welsh rarebit 被认为是最“典型的”（paradigmatic/archetypal）烹饪器皿食谱。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v4-1","title":"Test 4 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v4.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"History teaches us that science is not _____ enterprise; indeed, it is quite the opposite, a motley assortment of tools designed to safeguard researchers against their own biases.","key":"E","opts":["an opportunistic","an anomalous","a haphazard","a collective","a monolithic"],"expl":"科学不是“单一的”（monolithic）事业，而是多种工具的组合。选 E"},{"id":"v4.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite having only recently learned to walk, toddlers make the most (i)_____ dance students. Their joy in movement is so pure, so complete, and so (ii)_____.","key":"CF","groups":[["skilled","inattentive","delightful"],["futile","irrelevant","contagious"]],"expl":"空1 填 skilled（熟练的）；空2 填 contagious（有感染力的）：幼儿的快乐具有感染力。选 CF"},{"id":"v4.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Computers make it spectacularly easy to search for particular pieces of information in downloaded texts. And doing research in this strategic, targeted manner can feel (i)_____. Instead of (ii)_____ the organizing logic of the book you are reading, you can approach the book with your own questions and (iii)_____. You, not the author, are the master.","key":"CEH","groups":[["disorienting","humbling","empowering"],["disregarding","surrendering to","imitating"],["begin to discern the author’s intent","glean precisely what you want from it","evaluate the book on its own terms"]],"expl":"空1 填 empowering（赋权的）；空2 填 surrendering to（屈从于）：不是屈从书本的结构；空3 填 glean precisely what you want from it（精确地获取你想要的）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v4.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although one can adduce myriad of examples of ecosystem disruption by nonindigenous species, nevertheless most introduced species that survive in fact appear to have quite _____ effects on the ecosystem they have invaded.","key":"AB","opts":["minimal","trifling","marked","conspicuous","intriguing","deleterious"],"expl":"大多数存活的外来物种，对生态系统的影响是“轻微的”（minimal/trifling）。选 AB"},{"id":"v4.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although field studies have linked inbreeding to declines among song sparrow populations, some researchers argue that, in nature, inbreeding proves _____ as a factor when compared with crushing blows from weather changes.","key":"CF","opts":["hazardous","momentous","trivial","significant","precarious","inconsequential"],"expl":"近交相对于天气剧变，是“微不足道的”（trivial/inconsequential）因素。选 CF"},{"id":"v4.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since it was committed to the idea of science as an international, politically neutral enterprise, the Royal Society of London refused to _____ members from enemy nations during world wars of the twentieth century.","key":"BD","opts":["betray","expel","endorse","oust","sanction","condemn"],"expl":"皇家学会拒绝“驱逐”（expel/oust）敌国成员。选 BD"},{"id":"v4.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Coagulation factors are useful proteins whose simple names—many are known only by Roman numerals—_____ their importance and the specificity of their roles in the thinning and clotting of blood.","key":"DE","opts":["nullify","obviate","mitigate","belie","mask","accentuate"],"expl":"凝血因子的简单名称“掩盖”（mask/belie，belie 表示“掩饰”）了其重要性。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v4-2","title":"Test 4 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v4.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The Labrador duck is one of the most _____ extinct birds: although there are a fair number of specimens, few have yielded reliable data and little is known about the species’ breeding patterns.","key":"C","opts":["anomalous","controversial","enigmatic","misrepresented","cherished"],"expl":"Labrador duck 是“最神秘”（enigmatic）的灭绝鸟类之一。选 C"},{"id":"v4.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"One view of historicism holds that systems of belief prevalent during different periods in history are _____ and therefore cannot be understood except in their own term.","key":"B","opts":["discriminatory","incommensurable","anachronistic","cosmopolitan","objective"],"expl":"历史主义认为，不同时代的信念体系是“不可通约的”（incommensurable），只能在其自身的术语中理解。选 B"},{"id":"v4.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Readers may initially be irked by the book’s apparent (i)_____ but, once immersed in the author’s prose, they may come to regard the work’s (ii)_____ as an asset.","key":"BE","groups":[["flippancy","aimlessness","tendentiousness"],["subtlety","discursions","exhaustiveness"]],"expl":"空1 填 aimlessness（漫无目的）：读者起初会对书的漫无目的感到不耐烦；空2 填 discursions（离题的论述）：离题的论述后来被视为优点。选 BE"},{"id":"v4.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Given our species’ increasing numbers and appetites—which are reflected in and compounded by global climate change—even (i)_____ species are likely to become endangered within the foreseeable future. If we are to avoid a calamitous loss of biodiversity, according to Golbe, we cannot simply let nature take its course. Ongoing conservation management is (ii)_____, as we have, in a sense, become nature, and the responsibilities that come with the role cannot be (iii)_____.","key":"CEG","groups":[["exotic","vulnerable","now common"],["ineffective","obligatory","promising"],["jettisoned","assumed","contrived"]],"expl":"空1 填 now common（现在很常见的）：即使是常见物种也会濒危；空2 填 obligatory（必须的）；空3 填 jettisoned（抛弃）：责任不能被抛弃。选 CEG"},{"id":"v4.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite her rather _____ choices, Moreland was neither a rebellious spirit nor someone who saw herself as anything out of the ordinary.","key":"AC","opts":["unconventional","impractical","quirky","flamboyant","successful","lucrative"],"expl":"她的选择“非传统”（unconventional）且有些“怪异”（quirky）。选 AC"},{"id":"v4.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite their cultural and social significance, rapid growth, and widespread appear in China, video games—unlike traditional media—have received _____ attention from international communication researches.","key":"BE","opts":["undue","scant","excessive","focused","limited","dwindling"],"expl":"视频游戏很少受到学者的关注（scant/limited）。选 BE"},{"id":"v4.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In Ramachandran’s opinion, it is perfectly acceptable to propose bold speculations about the brain, even if these speculations seem _____; as Ramachandran frequently remarks, science thrives on risky conjecture.","key":"AF","opts":["unfounded","premature","controversial","verifiable","testable","baseless"],"expl":"Ramachandran 认为，即使推测看起来“没有根据”（unfounded/baseless），也能推进科学。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v5-1","title":"Test 5 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v5.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The company suffers from an almost total lack of _____: even the most innocuous communications between departments lend to devolve into acrimony.","key":"C","opts":["dissension","variance","comity","conformity","mordancy"],"expl":"公司缺乏“和睦”（comity），即融洽的关系。选 C"},{"id":"v5.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Mr. Stevens found that home schooling, far from representing (i)_____ philosophy, (ii)_____ some of the most widely accepted education ideas: that children should be treated as individuals, taught in small numbers, and given a measure of discretion over their own learning.","key":"CE","groups":[["a benign","an orthodox","an anomalous"],["overcomes","embodies","anticipates"]],"expl":"空1 填 anomalous（反常的）：家庭教育并非反常的哲学；空2 填 embodies（体现）：它体现了被广泛接受的教育观念。选 CE"},{"id":"v5.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many fairy tales are complex narratives of wish fulfillment. They teach the reader that a struggle against severe difficulties in life is (i)_____, that it is an intrinsic part of human existence, and that if one does not (ii)_____, but steadfastly meets unexpected and often unjust hardships, one masters all obstacles and at the end (iii)_____.","key":"BFH","groups":[["atypical","unavoidable","insurmountable"],["preserve","improvise","shy away"],["elicits adversities","emerges victorious","evades achievements"]],"expl":"空1 填 unavoidable（不可避免的）；空2 填 shy away（退缩）；空3 填 emerges victorious（取得胜利）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v5.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The concert hall’s suspended ceiling is two-inch-thick plaster that reflects low-frequency sound energy; similarly, all wall surfaces are angled and shaped to _____ sound from the stage throughout the audience area.","key":"AC","opts":["diffuse","amplify","spread","dampen","eclipse","deaden"],"expl":"墙面和天花板的设计是为了把声音“扩散”（diffuse）或“放大”（amplify）。选 AC"},{"id":"v5.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Any notion of justice in the fortunes of artists is _____: works of equal value and quality produce quite different returns or no returns at all.","key":"AC","opts":["baseless","cliché","untenable","insulting","condescending","idealistic"],"expl":"艺术家的命运中不存在“公平”的说法，即“没有根据”（baseless）或“站不住脚”（untenable）。选 AC"},{"id":"v5.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Agencies responsible for protecting natural resources too often issue permits allowing exploitation of those resources, a process that remains _____ given that agencies have become experts at masking their decisions in the scientific terms.","key":"CE","opts":["controversial","exacting","obscure","onerous","opaque","misleading"],"expl":"机构把科学术语“掩盖”决策，使程序是“不透明的”（opaque）或“难以理解的”（obscure）。选 CE"},{"id":"v5.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although legislators on both sides of issues have repeatedly _____ a desire to find a middle ground, until now no acceptable compromise has been achieved.","key":"BC","opts":["discussed","proclaimed","professed","rejected","disowned","betrayed"],"expl":"立法者“宣称”（proclaimed/professed）愿意寻找中间立场。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v5-2","title":"Test 5 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v5.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The artist’s career was remarkable partly because it was so _____: she died, with only a few paintings to her credit, while still in her twenties.","key":"E","opts":["felicitous","prolific","enduring","conventional","abbreviated"],"expl":"她只留下很少的画作就英年早逝，因此职业生涯是“短暂的”（abbreviated）。选 E"},{"id":"v5.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"He was never (i)_____; he was nothing if not (ii)_____, so he forbore for the present to declare his passion.","key":"BE","groups":[["chivalrous","impetuous","thoughtful"],["boorish","circumspect","spontaneous"]],"expl":"空1 填 impetuous（冲动的）：他从不冲动；空2 填 circumspect（审慎的）：他很谨慎，所以暂时不表白。选 BE"},{"id":"v5.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"One way to predict the effects of global climate change on an ecosystem is to extrapolate current trend in global change factors into the future. A (i)_____ of this method is that its predictions (ii)_____ actual observation, but the method also makes the questionable assumption that the future will resemble the present.","key":"AE","groups":[["virtue","drawback","peculiarity"],["dispense with","derive from","improve upon"]],"expl":"空1 填 drawback（缺点）；空2 填 derive from（源自）；但。选 AE"},{"id":"v5.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The writer argues that jewelry-grade diamonds, because they are both (i)_____ and (ii)_____, prove one of two conclusions; their purchasers have so much money they can spend it on goods that (iii)_____, or their purchasers are so committed to making others think they have such wealth that they are willing to go into debt to do so.","key":"CEI","groups":[["flawless","fungible","expensive"],["durable","useless","irreplaceable"],["may appreciate in value","reflect the buyers’ connoisseurship","serve no practical purpose"]],"expl":"空1 填 flawless（无瑕的）；空2 填 useless（无用的）；空3 填 serve no practical purpose（没有实际用途）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v5.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The company is so old-fashioned and opposed to innovation that it can seem downright _____.","key":"AC","opts":["antediluvian","flighty","archaic","chauvinistic","capricious","patronizing"],"expl":"公司守旧、反对创新，使它显得“过时”（antediluvian/archaic）。选 AC"},{"id":"v5.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Estimating demographic parameters in marine mammals is challenging, often requiring many years of data to achieve sufficient precision to _____ biologically meaningful change.","key":"CF","opts":["effect","tolerate","discern","envisage","withstand","detect"],"expl":"需要多年数据才能“察觉”（discern/detect）具有生物学意义的变化。选 CF"},{"id":"v5.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientists should hope the faults in their theories will be _____ their peers since the refutation of one hypothesis can free its originator to develop a better one.","key":"AC","opts":["discerned by","disregarded by","discovered by","ignored by","opaque to","inspiring to"],"expl":"科学家希望理论中的错误被同行“发现”（discerned/discovered）。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v6-1","title":"Test 6 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v6.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The province has long claimed to be just another developing region, even as its economy _____ those of other regions and threatens to eclipse the rest of the country combined.","key":"D","opts":["parallels","bolsters","corroborates","outstrips","engages"],"expl":"经济“超过”（outstrips）其他地区。选 D"},{"id":"v6.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"So (i)_____ is the reputation of the city’s police force for (ii)_____ that whenever a new police chief take office, he or she routinely promises to clean up the force.","key":"AD","groups":[["persistent","recent","discouraging"],["corruption","efficiency","inexperience"]],"expl":"空1 填 persistent（持久的）；空2 填 corruption（腐败）：新警察局长都要承诺“清理”腐败。选 AD"},{"id":"v6.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In medieval Europe, watermills were more (i)_____ than windmills. It is true that windmills could be built virtually anywhere, whereas watermills (ii)_____. However, watermills’ greater capacity and reliability provided a better (iii)_____ the money required to build the mill.","key":"BDI","groups":[["problematic","profitable","versatile"],["were suitable only for certain locations","inspired a variety of new technologies","required a good deal of upkeep"],["source of","adjunct to","return on"]],"expl":"空1 填 profitable（有利可图的）；空2 填 were suitable only for certain locations（只适合特定地点）；空3 填 return on（对……的回报）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v6.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though Edmurd certainly had a dignified bearing and made a great first impression, those who became acquainted with him soon realized he had an essentially _____ nature.","key":"AF","opts":["pugnacious","deliberate","punctilious","courteous","complacent","truculent"],"expl":"Edmurd 的本性是“好斗”（pugnacious/truculent）的，与其风度相反。选 AF"},{"id":"v6.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The life of a secret agent is dangerous enough, but the life of a double agent is infinitely more _____: a single slip can send an agent crashing to destruction.","key":"BD","opts":["arduous","precarious","clandestine","perilous","covert","exhilarating"],"expl":"双重间谍的生活是“危险的”（perilous）、“不稳定的”（precarious）。选 BD"},{"id":"v6.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Natural causes nerves to die off and muscles to weaken, but regular exercise of muscle fibers enlarges and can _____ the decline by increasing the strengthen muscle you have left.","key":"BC","opts":["speed up","stave off","forestall","facilitate","assist","exploit"],"expl":"锻炼能“延缓”（stave off/forestall）肌肉的衰退。选 BC"},{"id":"v6.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Creativity is no longer seen as _____ inspiration leading to poem or painting, it has come to be thought of as something permeating the whole of a person’s life.","key":"BD","opts":["a mundane","a momentary","an illusory","an evanescent","a metaphoric","a prosaic"],"expl":"创造力不再是“短暂的”（momentary/evanescent）灵感，而是渗透整个生活的东西。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v6-2","title":"Test 6 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v6.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Parker’s model of human reflects a _____ outlook, in stark contrast to the generally pessimistic analyses of her colleagues in the economics department.","key":"E","opts":["prescient","circumspect","technical","magisterial","sanguine"],"expl":"Parker 的模型体现的是“乐观”（sanguine）的态度，与同事的悲观分析形成对照。选 E"},{"id":"v6.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Scientists said that cosmology was the field where the ratio of theory to data was (i)_____: there was an abundance of theories, but almost no data. Recently, however, that ratio has flipped. A huge and ever-increasing amount of data has (ii)_____ all theories but one.","key":"BD","groups":[["completely unknown","nearly infinite","always variable"],["eliminated","supported","clarified"]],"expl":"空1 填 nearly infinite（几乎无限）：理论多而数据少，比例偏向理论；空2 填 eliminated（淘汰）：数据淘汰了理论。选 BD"},{"id":"v6.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When the Agriculture Department (i)_____ its dietary guidelines, it laid down a challenge: Eat better, smarter, and healthier or else. The “or else” included a long list of (ii)_____ that (iii)_____ the developed world, from heart disease and osteoporosis to diabetes.","key":"AFH","groups":[["make public","debunked","refused to consider"],["intangibles","misconceptions","maladies"],["assuage","plague","ignore"]],"expl":"空1 填 make public（公布）；空2 填 maladies（疾病）；空3 填 plague（困扰）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v6.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The historian’s narrative of the dynasty’s decline is (i)_____, because though there is nothing (ii)_____ the account, largely parts of it rely on (iii)_____.","key":"CEH","groups":[["diffuse","reasonable","questionable"],["psychologically penetrating in","inherently implausible about","fully documented in"],["plagiarism","conjecture","pretense"]],"expl":"空1 填 questionable（可疑的）：叙述有疑点；空2 填 inherently implausible about（本身难以置信）：并非毫无可信之处；空3 填 conjecture（推测）：部分依据是推测。选 CEH"},{"id":"v6.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In establishing that the dust she had observed constitutes two percent of the mass in the quadrant, the astronomer showed that the dust’s extreme visual prominence _____ its relatively minor contribution to the total mass of the region.","key":"AB","opts":["belies","masks","highlights","nullifies","disproves","accentuates"],"expl":"dust 的显著程度与其质量贡献很小形成对照，所以显著的视觉表现“掩盖”（masks）或“掩饰”（belies）了它的实际贡献。选 AB"},{"id":"v6.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Writing about advances in climate science is often problematic, in part because the material is so _____: climate science is the study of shifting, interrelated, and sometimes paradoxical patterns.","key":"CE","opts":["disheartening","pedestrian","complicated","depressing","knotty","mundane"],"expl":"气候科学的研究对象复杂、相互关联、有矛盾，所以材料“复杂”（complicated）且“棘手”（knotty）。选 CE"},{"id":"v6.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are many insights in the essay collected in Observations on modernity, but they are embedded in a dense English translation of a dense German original that may make many of them _____ to most readers.","key":"BF","opts":["vapid","inaccessible","sagacious","banal","distressing","opaque"],"expl":"原文又密又难读，许多见解对多数读者来说“难以理解”（inaccessible）或“晦涩”（opaque）。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v7-1","title":"Test 7 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v7.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"He was so ____ during the filming of the movie that crew members nicknamed his “The Angriest Man in the World”","key":"B","opts":["loquacious","irascible","perfidious","sanguine","voracious"],"expl":"他在拍摄时非常“易怒”（irascible），才会被叫作“世界上最愤怒的人”。选 B"},{"id":"v7.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Scholars have marveled over the (i)_____ that Shakespeare displays in his works, noting that such broad learning is all the more remarkable given that books were relatively (ii)_____ in Shakespeare’s time.","key":"CE","groups":[["meticulousness","humor","erudition"],["edifying","scarce","inexpensive"]],"expl":"空1 填 erudition（博学）；空2 填 scarce（稀缺）：莎士比亚时代书籍稀少，博学更显难得。选 CE"},{"id":"v7.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Galaxy Zoo set a standard for citizen-scientist participation project. Zealous volunteers (i)_____ the project’s organizers by classifying an entire catalog of galaxies years ahead of schedule. (ii)_____ by the (iii)_____ of the volunteers, Galaxy Zoo team was inspired to pursue lines of research they had never even imagined.","key":"CEI","groups":[["beguiled","forestalled","astonished"],["baffled","buoyed","embarrassed"],["insouciance","stoicism","alacrity"]],"expl":"空1 填 astonished（使惊讶）；空2 填 buoyed（使振奋）；空3 填 alacrity（热情、迅速）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v7.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Noise suppression in phones can play an important role in making cellphone networks more efficient, since when sounds that are _____ to the meaningful signal are transmitted, precious network band width is wasted.","key":"CF","opts":["unsuitable","detrimental","irrelevant","confined","limited","extraneous"],"expl":"与有效信号无关（irrelevant）的声音才是“多余的”（extraneous），传输它们会浪费带宽。选 CF"},{"id":"v7.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Changes made to ecosystem in order to achieve a goal, such as food production or flood control, often _____ significant unforeseen trade-offs between other important products and service the ecosystems provide.","key":"EF","opts":["predict","delay","foretell","obscure","yield","engender"],"expl":"为了某个目标而做出的改变，往往会“产生”（engender）出人意料的权衡，也会“导致”（yield）这些代价。选 EF"},{"id":"v7.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The union states its position polemically; its leader say they are fighting to save good jobs while ______ corporations replace full-time workers with part-time ones in order to cut down on both wages and benefits.","key":"CF","opts":["precarious","enterprising","rapacious","troubled","influential","avaricious"],"expl":"公司把全职换成兼职以压低工资，是“掠夺性的”（rapacious）、“贪婪的”（avaricious）行为。选 CF"},{"id":"v7.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"When the atmosphere over the city is at its best, it is peculiarly _____, and this clarity seems to distill this very special beauty of the place.","key":"AE","opts":["limpid","acute","calm","sharp","pellucid","tranquil"],"expl":"清澈的空气是“清澈透明的”（limpid/pellucid）。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v7-2","title":"Test 7 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v7.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The film was a _____: its elements were assembled more or less haphazardly from a dozen of different sources.","key":"C","opts":["burlesque","satire","pastiche","chronicle","parody"],"expl":"影片的元素来自多个来源、拼凑而成，因此是“拼贴”（pastiche）。选 C"},{"id":"v7.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Nylenna’s study showed that errors in scientific manuscripts submitted for publication often escape reviewers’ notice, results that were not _____: when Godlee conducted a study of the same phenomenon, her findings were similar.","key":"C","opts":["credible","unwelcome","anomalous","quantifiable","consequential"],"expl":"错误没有引起注意，这一结果在另一项研究中也得到相同结论，因此它并非“异常的”（anomalous）。选 C"},{"id":"v7.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"She was never (i)_____; she was nothing if not discreet, so she (ii)_____ for the present to declare her passion.","key":"AF","groups":[["precipitate","tactful","thoughtful"],["pretended","decided","forbore"]],"expl":"空1 填 precipitate（轻率的）：她并不轻率；空2 填 forbore（克制）：她谨慎，所以暂时克制不表白。选 AF"},{"id":"v7.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"To label Hamilton a foreigner because he was born outside what later became the United States is to assume anachronistically the existence of the nation before the fact. It is true that Hamilton came to believe that he was a (i)_____ the United States, but his (ii)_____ was stemmed not from his (iii)_____ but from his confrontation with American democracy, which he considered to be a disease afflicting the nation.","key":"CDI","groups":[["symbol of","stranger in","citizen of"],["alienation","ambition","patriotism"],["ideology","profession","birthplace"]],"expl":"空1 填 citizen of（美国公民）：他认为自己是美国公民；空2 填 alienation（疏离）：他的“疏离”来自与美国民主的对抗；空3 填 birthplace（出生地）：不是来自他的出生地。选 CDI"},{"id":"v7.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book brings together many valuable reports on conservation projects, but with less variety than might have been wished: nearly half the contributions are from the same state, and consequently, the case studies are similarly _____ geographically.","key":"BC","opts":["rudimentary","interdependent","interrelated","complex","heterogeneous","dissimilar"],"expl":"案例在地理上彼此“相互关联”（interrelated）或“相互依赖”（interdependent）。选 BC"},{"id":"v7.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For those of us who have been intoxicated by the power and potential of mathematics, the mystery isn’t why that fascination developed but why it isn’t _____.","key":"CF","opts":["advantageous","discounted","prevalent","undervalued","celebrated","widespread"],"expl":"数学的魅力广泛存在（prevalent/widespread），所以疑问是它为何“不普遍”。选 CF"},{"id":"v7.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The nation’s robust economic performance could be _____ by the persistent flaws in its economic institutions and structure that are the result of half-finished and misguided government policies.","key":"CD","opts":["neutralized","concealed","undermined","impaired","obscured","outstripped"],"expl":"经济政策的缺陷会“削弱”（undermined）或“损害”（impaired）良好的经济表现。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v8-1","title":"Test 8 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v8.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The title of her final and unfinished film, Escape, was _____: indeed while shooting it, she was preoccupied with thoughts of desertion.","key":"B","opts":["quixotic","apt","misleading","inconsequential","uncharacteristic"],"expl":"影片名为 Escape（逃离），而她在拍摄时关注“逃跑”的念头，因此片名很“恰当”（apt）。选 B"},{"id":"v8.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Except for a few passages in the biography in which the subject’s flaws are (i)_____, the author’s treatment of her subject is (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["too harshly judged","analyzed in depth","frankly acknowledged"],["erudite","judicious","acrimonious"]],"expl":"空1 填 frankly acknowledged（坦率承认）：传记只在几处坦率承认缺点；空2 填 judicious（明智的）：其余的处理是“审慎、明智”的。选 CE"},{"id":"v8.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In a view of 17 studies from 2008, Trudeau and Shephard concluded that reserving up to an hour a day for (i)_____ in school curricula does not (ii)_____ academic achievement. In fact, they noted that more exercise often (iii)_____ school performance, despite the time it took away from reading, writing, and arithmetic.","key":"AEH","groups":[["physical activity","leisure time","open study"],["contribute to","detract from","correlate with"],["diminished","augmented","counteracted"]],"expl":"空1 填 physical activity（体育活动）；空2 填 detract from（减损）：不会减少学业成绩；空3 填 augmented（增加）：更多运动常常提高成绩。选 AEH"},{"id":"v8.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"An abundance of nutrient-rich pollution in estuaries causes algae to _____, much as houseplants grow better when their soil contains added fertilizer.","key":"AB","opts":["abound","proliferate","stagnate","coalesce","collect","diversify"],"expl":"营养过剩的污染使藻类“激增”（proliferate）或“大量繁殖”（abound）。选 AB"},{"id":"v8.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Taking to the mountains to escape the chaos occasioned by the collapse of the ruling dynasty, artists looked to nature for _____ and a serenity not evident in human society.","key":"AB","opts":["an order","a stability","a fragility","a decadence","an interaction","a degeneracy"],"expl":"艺术家在自然中寻求“秩序”（order）与“稳定”（stability）。选 AB"},{"id":"v8.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Great Lakes wolf is a _____, stumping scientists as to whether it is a subspecies of the gray wolf or a distinct species.","key":"BF","opts":["prototype","riddle","paragon","model","legend","conundrum"],"expl":"大湖狼“是一个谜”（riddle/conundrum），让科学家难以判断其分类。选 BF"},{"id":"v8.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book aims to illuminate how science has changed the meaning of nothingness from _____ philosophical concept to something we can almost put under a microscope.","key":"CF","opts":["a tangible","a palpable","a nebulous","a nettlesome","an incontrovertible","a vague"],"expl":"无的概念从“抽象的”（nebulous）哲学概念变为可以在显微镜下观察的东西。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v8-2","title":"Test 8 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v8.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"This is neither praise nor criticism, neither a compliment nor _____, just an observation.","key":"C","opts":["an exposition","an elucidation","an animadversion","a culmination","a divination"],"expl":"文本既非称赞也非批评（animadversion，批评、责备），只是观察。选 C"},{"id":"v8.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The history of the region’s natural resources has been one of initial (i)_____ followed by (ii)_____; as such the region has over time gone from a resource-rich to a resource-dependent economy.","key":"BF","groups":[["disappointment","abundance","conservation"],["growing interdependence","draconian regulation","rapacious depletion"]],"expl":"空1 填 abundance（丰富）；空2 填 rapacious depletion（掠夺性耗竭）。选 BF"},{"id":"v8.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Any account of experimental music in the United States that (i)_____ the predominantly African American bebop and free jazz movements is (ii)_____, since this body of music constitutes what is arguably the most influential African experimental music in the decades following the Second War War.","key":"AE","groups":[["neglects","exaggerates","reinterprets"],["underappreciated","problematic","self-serving"]],"expl":"任何忽视（neglects）非裔美国人实验音乐的说法都是“有问题的”（problematic）。选 AE"},{"id":"v8.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Gravitational waves—ripples in the geometry of space-time—are analogous to electromagnetic waves. The challenge in trying to observe these waves directly is that they are extremely weak. To make waves large enough to be (i)_____, the most (ii)_____ events in the universe are required: supernova explosions, the formation of black holes, or the collision of stars. Even so, the effects are (iii)_____. The geometry changes so little that a distance of several kilometers changes by less than the diameter of a proton.","key":"AFI","groups":[["detectable","usable","explicable"],["obvious","subtle","violent"],["masked","disastrous","minuscule"]],"expl":"空1 填 detectable（可探测的）；空2 填 violent（剧烈的）：只有剧烈事件才能产生足够强的波；空3 填 minuscule（极小的）。选 AFI"},{"id":"v8.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Readers have long considered Lawd Today! , Richard Wright’s first written and last published novel, _____; the novel simply seems inconsistent with the image of what a Wright text should do or be.","key":"CE","opts":["an artifact","a prototype","an anomaly","a mainstay","an aberration","a model"],"expl":"Lawd Today! 与 Wright 的典型风格不符，因此它是“变例”（anomaly）或“偏离”（aberration）。选 CE"},{"id":"v8.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is hardly _____ for today’s film to try to blur the boundaries between the moral and the immoral. Hollywood has been doing that since at least the 1960s.","key":"BC","opts":["entertaining","original","novel","pertinent","relevant","insightful"],"expl":"当代电影模糊道德边界并不“新颖”（novel），好莱坞早已这么做。选 BC"},{"id":"v8.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Reversing a decade-long trend on global _____, earth’s surface has become brighter since 1990, scientists are reporting.","key":"DE","opts":["warming","cooling","diffusing","dimming","darkening","heating"],"expl":"地球表面变亮，是对“变暗”（dimming/darkening）趋势的逆转。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v9-1","title":"Test 9 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v9.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The identity of hominid remains found in a cave in the Altai Mountains was _____ until Paabo and his colleagues ended the speculation by showing that DNA sequences indicated the bones belonged to Neanderthals.","key":"B","opts":["extraneous","conjectural","improbable","demonstrable","consistent"],"expl":"在 DNA 证明前，骨骼的身份只是“推测的”（conjectural）。选 B"},{"id":"v9.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the abundance and importance of maize, its biological origin has been a long-running mystery. The bright yellow, mouth-watering treat does not grow in the wild anywhere on the planet, so its (i)_____ is not at all (ii)_____.","key":"CF","groups":[["utility","popularity","ancestry"],["helpful","important","obvious"]],"expl":"玉米的起源（ancestry）并不明显（obvious），因为它在野外并不存在。选 CF"},{"id":"v9.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although Thaler employs an innovative mode of analysis, his study offers yet another examination of quite (i)_____ ground—namely, the culture ideology of Norwegian-American preservationist writers in the early twentieth century. The history, literature, and changing internal dynamics of the Norwegian subculture in America constitute a particularly well-studied area. Anyone familiar with the authoritative work of scholars in the field will (ii)_____ little in Thaler’s study that is (iii)_____.","key":"BDH","groups":[["unfamiliar","well-worked","fruitful"],["find","understand","reveal"],["accurate","new","recognizable"]],"expl":"空1 填 well-worked（已被充分研究的）：这是研究充分的领域；空2 填 find（发现）；空3 填 recognizable（熟悉的）：读者会察觉到其中的内容。选 BDH"},{"id":"v9.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"All Shaker furniture implies _____ humanism in design: the Shakers made objects that look like objects, following a nonhuman law of design and rejecting the unconscious self-flattery inherent in making anthropomorphic objects.","key":"AB","opts":["a rejection of","a liberation from","a belief in","an affinity for","an attraction to","a misunderstanding of"],"expl":"工艺设计“拒绝”（rejection of）一种自我美化，并“摆脱”（liberation from）这一观念。选 AB"},{"id":"v9.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The controversial social analysis that Moynihan offered in the 1960s is now generally recognized as having been prescient; in fact, it has been the _____ upon which much of our discussion of social pathology must base.","key":"BE","opts":["concession","bedrock","imperative","compromise","foundations","vision"],"expl":"Moynihan 的分析是这一讨论的“基础”（bedrock/foundations）。选 BE"},{"id":"v9.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The life of a secret agent is dangerous enough, but the life of a double agent is infinitely more _____: a single slip can send an agent crashing to destruction.","key":"BD","opts":["arduous","precarious","clandestine","perilous","covert","exhilarating"],"expl":"双重间谍的生活“危险”（perilous）且“不稳定”（precarious）。选 BD"},{"id":"v9.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The jazz style called bebop was born and nurtured in New York City, and despite a _____ initial reception, it resonated three thousand miles away on the West Coast.","key":"AF","opts":["wary","warm","confused","muddled","convivial","hostile"],"expl":"尽管起初接受“敌意”（hostile）或“谨慎”（wary），爵士乐在西海岸仍然产生了共鸣。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v9-2","title":"Test 9 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v9.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In a production process that is complex and often unpredictable, roles that start out discretely defined may become quite _____.","key":"A","opts":["confused","perfunctory","independent","overt","exacting"],"expl":"生产过程越复杂，角色就越容易变得“混乱”（confused）。选 A"},{"id":"v9.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The description of Green’s scholarship as (i)_____ is grossly misleading: while her research on interstellar particles is not especially novel, the conclusions she draws from her data are (ii)_____.","key":"CD","groups":[["esoteric","tendentious","derivative"],["remarkably pioneering","dubiously supported","strangely comforting"]],"expl":"空1 填 derivative（派生的、缺乏原创性的）；空2 填 dubiously supported（证据存疑的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v9.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"People frequently attempt to relieve their workplace frustrations via surreptitious comments around the water cooler but would be better able to resolve their resentment if they were less (i)_____ about their problem and imitated a more (ii)_____ dialogue.","key":"BF","groups":[["vexatious","clandestine","opportunistic"],["equitable","sincere","open"]],"expl":"空1 填 clandestine（私下的）；空2 填 open（公开的）：应该进行公开的对话。选 BF"},{"id":"v9.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Publisher, publicist, and broadcasters love anniversaries, those occasions when historical events become (i)_____ in (ii)_____ culture of celebration. On such occasions patriotic sentiment and national pride are wrapped in the panoply of history to manufacture a mythical past that is serviceable for public (iii)_____.","key":"BEG","groups":[["elusive moments","marketable artifacts","raging controversies"],["an authentic","a commercial","an elitist"],["consumption","scrutiny","censure"]],"expl":"周年纪念使历史事件变成“商品”（marketable artifacts），以“商业”（commercial）方式用于大众“消费”（consumption）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v9.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite the _____ of medical information available through e-mail, the Internet, and mobile devices, not many patients are taking advantage of the potential of electronic communications for health-related needs.","key":"AD","opts":["wealth","complexity","intricacy","profusion","resurgence","overload"],"expl":"信息的“泛滥”（profusion）和“丰富”（wealth）并未被用起来。选 AD"},{"id":"v9.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The political upheaval caught most people by surprise: despite the _____ warnings of some commentators, it had never seemed that imminent.","key":"BC","opts":["stern","prescient","prophetic","indifferent","repeated","apathetic"],"expl":"“有先见之明的”（prescient/prophetic）警告，说明局势早有征兆。选 BC"},{"id":"v9.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Wilson is wont to emphasize the _____ of ants, how ants with full stomachs will regurgitate liquid food for those without , or how the old will fight so the young can survive.","key":"AB","opts":["beneficence","altruism","unpredictability","intelligence","fecundity","fertility"],"expl":"蚂蚁的“利他行为”（altruism）与“慷慨”（beneficence）是同一意思。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v10-1","title":"Test 10 · Section 1","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v10.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because people expect theater directors to be authoritarians, many were surprised that Clark was so _____.","key":"C","opts":["histrionic","megalomaniacal","egalitarian","indolent","charismatic"],"expl":"普通人以为导演是独裁者，而 Clark 却是“平等主义者”（egalitarian）。选 C"},{"id":"v10.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It would be (i)_____ not to (ii)_____ these tabloid journalists for thriving in hard times: they deserve credit for doing well in a profession in financial straits.","key":"BD","groups":[["apropos","churlish","cagey"],["admire","envy","emulate"]],"expl":"空1 填 churlish（粗鲁的）：不去赞美是粗鲁的；空2 填 admire（钦佩）。选 BD"},{"id":"v10.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Laws protecting intellectual property are intended to stimulate creativity, yet some forms of creative work have never enjoyed legal protection—a situation that ought to be of great interest. If we see certain forms of creative endeavor (i)_____ as a result of uncontrolled copying, we might decide to (ii)_____ intellectual property law. Conversely, if unprotected creative work (iii)_____ in the absence of legal rules against copying, we would do well to know how such flourishing is sustained.","key":"AEH","groups":[["languishing","proliferating","diversifying"],["jettison","extend","relax"],["declines in originality","manages to thrive","openly invites imitation"]],"expl":"空1 填 languishing（衰退）；空2 填 extend（延伸）：扩大保护；空3 填 manages to thrive（设法繁荣）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v10.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though it may seem as if more than a century of _____ has made the electrical grid an all-encompassing web connecting the whole of the continent, many vast and beautiful areas remain without power.","key":"BD","opts":["refinement","expansion","ubiquity","augmentation","omnipresence","isolation"],"expl":"百年来的“扩张”（expansion）与“增强”（augmentation）让电网覆盖大陆，但仍有许多地方没有电。选 BD"},{"id":"v10.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Much of the literature of railroad seeks someone to _____, and it is thus replete with encomiums on entrepreneurs and managers.","key":"CD","opts":["indict","rehabilitate","exalt","valorize","emulate","excoriate"],"expl":"铁路文学寻找“颂扬”（exalt）与“称颂”（valorize）的对象。选 CD"},{"id":"v10.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Not only was this writer content to leave the reading public in the dark, she seems to have _____ the role of trickster, seeding her works with apparent clues that led nowhere.","key":"CE","opts":["rejected","disdained","relished","participated in","delighted in","developed"],"expl":"作者“享受”（relished）或“乐于”（delighted in）误导读者。选 CE"},{"id":"v10.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The major _____ of much popular history is that it betrays no interest in making intellectual contributions to our understanding of an issue.","key":"BF","opts":["characteristic","shortcoming","dilemma","quandary","ploy","fault"],"expl":"通俗历史的“主要缺陷”（shortcoming/fault）是缺少学术贡献。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v10-2","title":"Test 10 · Section 2","group":"Test 1–10","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v10.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The students’ _____ natures were in sharp contrast to the imperturbable dispositions of their teacher.","key":"A","opts":["volatile","duplicitous","apathetic","cunning","blithe"],"expl":"学生的性情“易变的”（volatile）与老师的泰然形成鲜明对比。选 A"},{"id":"v10.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Despite the neighborhood’s lingering reputation for _____, it has in fact become increasingly varied in its architecture and demographics.","key":"E","opts":["boisterousness","unpretentiousness","idiosyncrasy","accessibility","homogeneity"],"expl":"街区的声誉与其现在的多样性相反，因此在过去是“同质化”（homogeneity）的印象。选 E"},{"id":"v10.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It would be imprecise to characterize her scholarship as (i)_____: though her etymological discussion is necessarily esoteric, there is nothing (ii)_____ about the conclusions she derives from it.","key":"BD","groups":[["derivative","arcane","careless"],["obscure","controversial","innovative"]],"expl":"空1 填 derivative（派生的）；空2 填 obscure（晦涩的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v10.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Common sense tells me some people are more (i)_____ than others. The claim that these differences are (ii)_____, or that deep down, everybody acts only to further their own interests, (iii)_____ our everyday observations and deep-seated human practices of moral evaluation.","key":"AEI","groups":[["altruistic","adaptable","disciplined"],["growing","illusory","relevant"],["mimics","explains","contradicts"]],"expl":"空1 填 altruistic（利他的）；空2 填 illusory（幻觉的）；空3 填 contradicts（与……矛盾）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v10.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"After rising continuously over the summer, commodity prices fell, leaving analyst wondering whether the downward trend is a turning point or merely a _____ before demand picks up in the winter months.","key":"EF","opts":["spike","upsurge","harbinger","portent","lull","respite"],"expl":"价格下跌是“暂时的平静”（lull）还是“喘息”（respite），取决于冬季需求。选 EF"},{"id":"v10.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Doris Kearns Goodwin’s elegant, incisive study of Lincoln _____ those whose knowledge of Lincoln is an amalgam of high school history and popular mythology as well as those who are experts.","key":"AF","opts":["gratify","entice","inspire","confuse","perplex","please"],"expl":"Goodwin 的研究既能“满足”（gratify）也能“取悦”（please）各类读者。选 AF"},{"id":"v10.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Explorers could not build each other’s knowledge if they could not trust records of previous explorers; thus exploration depended on the _____ of those who had gone before.","key":"CD","opts":["collegiality","endurance","exactitude","meticulousness","eminence","tenacity"],"expl":"探险者依赖前人记录的“精确”（exactitude）与“细致”（meticulousness）。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v11-1","title":"Test 11 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v11.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"That Seiberg and Witten lack celebrity can be explained by the _____ nature of their pursuit: the mathematical exploration of four-dimensional space.","key":"B","opts":["pedestrian","esoteric","compelling","global","univocal"],"expl":"Seiberg 与 Witten 的研究“深奥”（esoteric），因而缺少名声。选 B"},{"id":"v11.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"While acknowledging behaviors the Prime Minster took in order to remain in office were (i)_____, some politicians nevertheless believed this small amount of (ii)_____ was justified to keep reforming government in office.","key":"AD","groups":[["unethical","impractical","quixotic"],["skullduggery","indolence","incivility"]],"expl":"空1 填 unethical（不道德的）；空2 填 skullduggery（卑劣的手段）。选 AD"},{"id":"v11.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"China’s rapidly growing population is the main threat facing large carnivores in the People’s Republic. Increasingly, policies aimed at limiting population growth have been (i)_____; nevertheless, the country’s vast size and the isolation of many of its regions mean that human populations in areas where large carnivores still occur (ii)_____. This human pressure has (iii)_____ the South China tiger.","key":"CEH","groups":[["modified","deemphasized","implemented"],["could start to decline","can grow unchecked","have stabilized"],["celebrated","doomed","bypassed"]],"expl":"空1 填 implemented（实施）；空2 填 can grow unchecked（可能不受控地增长）；空3 填 doomed（注定）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v11.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Well organized and researched and including all significant discoveries and medical scientists, this history of Western medicine has justly been called _____.","key":"AC","opts":["encyclopedic","long-winded","exhaustive","rambling","overbearing","undiscriminating"],"expl":"历史著作“百科全书式”（encyclopedic）且“详尽”（exhaustive）。选 AC"},{"id":"v11.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Science is arguably a very high-minded pursuit, but that is not to say that all of its practitioners are _____, as numerous articles alleging overly generous pharmaceutical industry payments to medical researchers have tried to show.","key":"CE","opts":["conventional","clever","unimpeachable","ingenious","blameless","predictable"],"expl":"科学家“无可指摘”（unimpeachable）、“无过错”（blameless）是并非绝对的。选 CE"},{"id":"v11.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In a field of egotists, Bloomfield is _____, often praising her competitors and punctuating her correspondence with self-deprecating remarks.","key":"AF","opts":["unassuming","complimentary","acerbic","ingenuous","cutting","modest"],"expl":"Bloomfield “谦逊”（unassuming/modest）。选 AF"},{"id":"v11.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because its previously _____ beliefs had become core tenets of mainstream politics, the activist group disbanded; with no more skeptics to persuade, its purpose had evaporated.","key":"CD","opts":["arcane","seditious","quixotic","idealistic","popular","conventional"],"expl":"激进团体先前“异想天开”（quixotic）或“理想化”（idealistic）的主张，成为主流政治，因此团体解散。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v11-2","title":"Test 11 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v11.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Paintings created in India during the Mughal dynasty were _____ in ambition but ornamental in presentation: in one direction they have a affinity with newspaper photographs, while in the other they have the intricacy of jewels.","key":"B","opts":["metaphorical","documentary","aesthetic","sectarian","baroque"],"expl":"莫卧儿绘画在目的上是“纪实的”（documentary）。选 B"},{"id":"v11.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Attending with equal (i)_____ to any question that presents itself, the sociologist’s work has strengths and weaknesses that flow from this energetically (ii)_____ approach.","key":"CE","groups":[["skepticism","lethargy","fervor"],["hybrid","indiscriminate","conciliatory"]],"expl":"空1 填 fervor（热情）；空2 填 indiscriminate（不加区分的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v11.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The national bank has been uncommonly powerful in comparison to its counterparts in other nations. It retains this potency partly because its control of the nation’s banking system is (i)_____ governmental interference, and thus its actions remain largely (ii)_____.","key":"AE","groups":[["unencumbered by","replete with","hindered by"],["compulsory","discretionary","bureaucratic"]],"expl":"央行的控制“不受”（unencumbered by）政府干预，因而其行动是“自主裁量”（discretionary）的。选 AE"},{"id":"v11.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The usual (i)_____ spending public monies on scientific projects is that such projects have the potential to make our lives healthier, safer, and more productive. However, the fact that science – even “pure” science – can strengthen democracy and promote public participation in the political process is hardly ever (ii)_____. It should be Scientific literacy (iii)_____ democracy, and this is an important ancillary benefit of the promotion of science.","key":"BEH","groups":[["argument against","rationale for","precedent for"],["denied","mentioned","gainsaid"],["stifles","energizes","disregards"]],"expl":"空1 填 rationale for（理由）；空2 填 mentioned（提及）；空3 填 energizes（使……有活力）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v11.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although scientific progress leads to constant revision of ideas, one observation that has remained _____ over the years is that there are a lot of insects in the world: some 950,000 species have been identified.","key":"AC","opts":["robust","significant","strong","perplexing","confounding","obscure"],"expl":"有一个观察“依旧有力”（robust/strong）：世界上有大量昆虫。选 AC"},{"id":"v11.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Anne Carson’s book Nox is, very deliberately, _____ literary object—the opposite of an e-reader, which is designed to vanish in your palm as you read on a train.","key":"BD","opts":["an evanescent","a cumbersome","an immutable","an unwieldy","an ephemeral","a flexible"],"expl":"Carson 的书是有意做成“笨重、难以操作”（cumbersome/unwieldy）的文学物件。选 BD"},{"id":"v11.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the peculiarities of humans is that we irrationally gravitate to the predictable and avoid risk, whatever the reasons for this _____, it is hardly a sound basis for dealing with complex, long-term problems.","key":"BD","opts":["eccentricity","predilection","vacillation","proclivity","wavering","cowardice"],"expl":"人类偏好“可预测性”（predilection/proclivity）是非理性的。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v12-1","title":"Test 12 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v12.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Blake’s reputation for weakness is _____: almost all who have worked with him say he is a disciplined, intellectually formidable, and very tough politician.","key":"A","opts":["specious","pervasive","irreversible","trivial","ambivalent"],"expl":"Blake 的“软弱”名声是“虚假的”（specious）。选 A"},{"id":"v12.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Mr. Billington, at times, can be a (i)_____. For instance, he deplores the Royal Shakespeare Company’s eight-and-a-half hour version of Nicholas Nickelby, which many found (ii)_____.","key":"AF","groups":[["naysayer","pushover","braggart"],["perplexing","unpredictable","absorbing"]],"expl":"空1 填 naysayer（反对者）；空2 填 absorbing（引人入胜的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v12.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Early practitioners of the natural sciences developed methods to remove distortions caused by either the research environment or the researcher. Such methods, especially with respect to the researcher, were considered to (i)_____ those (ii)_____ subjectivity whose unbridled expression was thought to (iii)_____ research.","key":"ADG","groups":[["restrain","reveal","disguise"],["incursions of","restrictions on","acknowledgements of"],["corrupt","justify","expedite"]],"expl":"空1 填 restrain（抑制）；空2 填 incursions of（侵入）；空3 填 corrupt（破坏）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v12.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Williamson had a fierce commitment to achieving an accord, spending enormous amount of time trying to forge a consensus out of an often _____ assembly.","key":"BC","opts":["apathetic","fractious","restive","cynical","compliant","tractable"],"expl":"议会“难以管理的”（fractious）与“不安的”（restive）使共识难以达成。选 BC"},{"id":"v12.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One _____ is that so far, Web services have turned out to be much harder to deliver than their champions had hoped.","key":"BD","opts":["hope","snag","prospect","hitch","upshot","reason"],"expl":"“障碍”（snag/hitch）是网络服务难以实现的原因之一。选 BD"},{"id":"v12.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Asserting a need to preserve the _____ that became the hallmark of her predecessor’s tenure, the new director of federal monetary policy refused to subscribe to rigid or mechanistic rules in policy making.","key":"BF","opts":["firmness","adaptability","unpredictability","autonomy","strictness","flexibility"],"expl":"作者要保持的是“灵活性”（flexibility）与“适应性”（adaptability），与刚性规则相对。选 BF"},{"id":"v12.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"At first, most of the famous fairy tales seem so implausible and so irrelevant to contemporary life that their _____ is hard to understand.","key":"BE","opts":["universality","persistence","appeal","ephemerality","survival","transience"],"expl":"故事看似与现代生活无关，因此人们很难理解它们的持久吸引力（appeal/persistence）。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v12-2","title":"Test 12 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v12.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In protoscientific (for example, in ancient Greece), claims about the physical world were often accepted as true if they were reasonable; experimental verification, if thought necessary at all, was _____.","key":"B","opts":["utilitarian","perfunctory","egregious","empirical","inductive"],"expl":"古代认知中，实验验证只是“走过场”（perfunctory）。选 B"},{"id":"v12.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"At Cerro Portezuelo, the task of separating grinding tools from the larger collection of excavated stone objects was (i)_____ the ancient practice of recycling grinding tool fragments for building materials, hammer stones, and other purposes that (ii)_____ their original use.","key":"AE","groups":[["complicated by","important to","independent from"],["complemented","obscured","underscored"]],"expl":"空1 填 complicated by（因……而变复杂）：分离工具并不容易；空2 填 obscured（掩盖）：回收利用掩盖了原来的用途。选 AE"},{"id":"v12.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Behavioral economists have come to believe that a (i)_____ of choices can be paralyzing as Schwartz pointed out in the recent book The Paradox of Choice. Studies of retirement plans show that the more investment choices a plan offers, the less likely people are to participate in it. It may follow, then, that a lack of flexibility in certain plans may actually be a (ii)_____. People reasonably (iii)_____ some advantages in exchange for peace of mind.","key":"ADI","groups":[["surfeit","reduction","stabilization"],["virtue","conundrum","revelation"],["foresee","forestall","forgo"]],"expl":"空1 填 surfeit（过多）：选择过多令人瘫痪；空2 填 virtue（优点）：缺乏灵活性可能是优点；空3 填 forgo（放弃）：人们愿意放弃某些好处以换取安心。选 ADI"},{"id":"v12.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)_____ quality of much contemporary drawing may be attributable to the use of photography as a drawing shortcut. Photography (ii)_____ modern arts, but when it is used as a tracing tool in order to (iii)_____ the difficulties of achieving correct proportion, the resulting art often feels static and lifeless.","key":"AEI","groups":[["inert","jubilant","sensuous"],["frequently enervated","wonderfully enriched","inevitably circumscribed"],["augment","foreground","circumvent"]],"expl":"空1 填 inert（呆板的）；空2 填 frequently enervated（常使人失去活力）；空3 填 circumvent（绕过）：用照片描摹可以绕开比例上的困难。选 AEI"},{"id":"v12.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Far from _____ innovations, as the patent system was designed to do, the patenting of concepts such as gene sequences gives individuals and corporations a legal choke to hold over ideas that should be useful to all.","key":"AE","opts":["spurring","recognizing","codifying","acknowledging","fostering","cataloging"],"expl":"专利制度本应“促进”（spur/foster）创新，而基因序列专利却起到阻碍作用。选 AE"},{"id":"v12.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Advocates for workers’ rights have adopted a new strategy, one that will require considerable ingenuity but that, if successful, could _____ a movement aimed at making labor rights an unassailable feature of American democracy.","key":"BE","opts":["frustrate","galvanize","presume","affect","animate","thwart"],"expl":"策略若成功，会“激发”（galvanize/animate）一场运动。选 BE"},{"id":"v12.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In Inuit culture, elaborate carving has often been used to enhance _____ object such as harpoon heads and other tools.","key":"AB","opts":["utilitarian","functional","domestic","decorative","manufactured","ornamental"],"expl":"雕刻可以增强物件的实用性（utilitarian/functional）。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v13-1","title":"Test 13 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v13.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While early biographies of Florence Nightingale tended to be quite _____, Lytton Strachey’s irreverent 1918 essay about her ushered in a new era, making it acceptable, even fashionable, to criticize her.","key":"B","opts":["unsympathetic","sycophantic","unsentimental","censorious","pedantic"],"expl":"早期的传记大多“阿谀奉承”（sycophantic），Strachey 的文章打破了这种风气。选 B"},{"id":"v13.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Tagore had a sharply defined sense of the (i)_____ of scientific inquiry. The fact that science dealt in statistics and numbers, that its logic was probabilistic, meant that the domain of moral questions (ii)_____ it: moral questions, for Tagore, required certainties, not probabilities.","key":"BE","groups":[["irrationality","limits","futility"],["guarded over","lay outside","was subject to"]],"expl":"空1 填 limits（界限）：科学的界限；空2 填 lay outside（在……之外）：道德问题超出科学的范围。选 BE"},{"id":"v13.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although political events in different countries were not (i)_____ in the nineteen century, their interrelationship was (ii)_____ compared with the present, when interdependence has become far greater: (iii)_____ has ceased to be an option.","key":"AEG","groups":[["unconnected","trivial","simultaneous"],["conditional","superficial","transparent"],["isolationism","resilience","idealism"]],"expl":"空1 填 unconnected（不相关的）；空2 填 superficial（肤浅的）；空3 填 isolationism（孤立主义）：不再可能选择孤立。选 AEG"},{"id":"v13.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Benjamin Franklin’s reputation is so much one of appearing scientific investigation with commonsense empiricism that it is somewhat startling to realize how _____ the great experiment’s mentoring truly was.","key":"BD","opts":["reasonable","speculative","pragmatic","conjectural","careless","judicious"],"expl":"富兰克林的伟大实验是“审慎的”（judicious）与“推测性的”（speculative/conjectural）之间的对照，题干强调其“令人惊讶地”不审慎的一面。选 BD"},{"id":"v13.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientist reported last month on a sign of relative solar _____: the solar wind, a rush of charged particles continually spewed from the Sun at a million miles an hour, had diminished to its lowest level in 50 years.","key":"AD","opts":["quiescence","turbulence","isolation","calm","remoteness","instability"],"expl":"太阳风减弱，是太阳的“平静”（quiescence/calm）。选 AD"},{"id":"v13.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Publicity surrounding celebrities’ donations to charity is often greeted with cynicism, but a study of celebrity donation shows that they do _____ other donations.","key":"BD","opts":["preclude","elicit","allow","draw","bar","replace"],"expl":"名人慈善会“引发”（elicit）或“吸引”（draw）其他捐款。选 BD"},{"id":"v13.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Aerial viewings of the gigantic stone horse attributed to the Native American Quechuan people fail to _____ the considerable artistry required to create the piece: the horse appears crudely constructed unless carefully examined from the ground.","key":"AC","opts":["reveal","justify","manifest","mitigate","diminish","undercut"],"expl":"从空中观看马的图形，不能“揭示”（reveal）其艺术性。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v13-2","title":"Test 13 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v13.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The modest but functional new wing finally gives the museum the _____ to serve its visitors properly, including multiple entrances to eliminate the lines that used to snake around the building.","key":"B","opts":["visibility","wherewithal","reputation","solemnity","panache"],"expl":"新翼楼提供了服务游客的“财力与资源”（wherewithal）。选 B"},{"id":"v13.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Apparently, advanced tortoises evolved multiple times: the high-domed shells and columnar, elephantine feet of current forms are specializations for terrestrial life that evolved _____ on each continent.","key":"A","opts":["independently","interchangeably","paradoxically","simultaneously","symmetrically"],"expl":"乌龟在各个大陆“独立地”（independently）演化。选 A"},{"id":"v13.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author suggests that cinema archives should become more like museums, justifying their existence by selecting, grouping and commenting on important films. By thus (i)_____ films, archives would not only serve as repositories but would provide (ii)_____ as well.","key":"CE","groups":[["improving","restoring","interpreting"],["conservation","education","income"]],"expl":"空1 填 interpreting（解读）；空2 填 education（教育）。选 CE"},{"id":"v13.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"To read Joanna Scott is to admire the work of a (i)_____. From sentence to story, she narrates with great skill and (ii)_____, so that the reader soon relaxes in the assurance that a hint or a brushstroke delivered in chapter 1 will be (iii)_____ before the novel comes to an end.","key":"CDG","groups":[["proselytizer","sage","master"],["deliberation","enthusiasm","flamboyance"],["given import","largely forgotten","overwhelmed with details"]],"expl":"空1 填 master（大师）；空2 填 deliberation（深思熟虑）；空3 填 given import（被赋予重要性）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v13.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Culture, like speech, is primarily a human faculty, although both functions may exist in a more _____ form in lesser primates.","key":"CF","opts":["indispensable","crucial","primitive","intelligible","recognizable","rudimentary"],"expl":"灵长类中的文化是“原始的”（primitive/rudimentary）形式。选 CF"},{"id":"v13.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Jackie Wullschlager's biography of Hans Christian Andersen _____ the insipid sweetness with which Andersen coated his life and reveals a vulnerable gingerbread man with a bitter almond where his heart should be.","key":"CE","opts":["conjures up","imagines","strips away","overlooks","removes","ignores"],"expl":"传记“剥去”（strips away）了安徒生甜美的外衣，并揭示其内心。选 CE"},{"id":"v13.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While it is always clear that the author's message is heartfelt, it is mostly buried by shortcomings of style, organization, and production, although the book does become more _____ toward the end.","key":"BD","opts":["sincere","intelligible","orthodox","readable","frank","voluble"],"expl":"书越来越“易读”（readable）并且“直率”（frank）。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v14-1","title":"Test 14 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v14.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Politicians who invoke the founders of the United States in support of their views seem to imply that the founders consistently concurred in their own views when in reality they were a highly _____ group of thinkers.","key":"D","opts":["erudite","innovative","predictable","contentious","methodical"],"expl":"开国元勋其实是一群“争论激烈的”（contentious）思想家。选 D"},{"id":"v14.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although Professor Pearson’s colleagues often complained that he was (i)_____, his friends were quick to defend him from this charge of (ii)_____.","key":"CD","groups":[["importunate","garrulous","mercurial"],["inconstancy","dishonest","partiality"]],"expl":"空1 填 mercurial（反复无常的）；空2 填 partiality（偏袒）：朋友们为他辩护。选 CD"},{"id":"v14.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The experimental theater company’s members know that their performances (i)_____ an audience, that they were dense and unpredictable and not always easy to digest. But none of the techniques used would be (ii)_____ anyone with an interest in music or films. Indeed, they would seem strange only to people who expected to see traditionally crafted plays. The actors therefore felt that theater critics’ derisive commentary showed only that the critics (iii)_____ the company’s work.","key":"AEI","groups":[["made demands on","had to command","were sure to please"],["contemplated by","alien to","intuitive for"],["lambasted","exploited","misunderstood"]],"expl":"空1 填 made demands on（对……提出要求）；空2 填 alien to（对……陌生）；空3 填 misunderstood（误解）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v14.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A clever form of diplomacy involves subtly inducing the other party to propose your preference so that your _____ their requests appears as the granting of concession.","key":"AF","opts":["accession to","inattention to","subversion of","abnegation of","repudiation of","acquiescence to"],"expl":"通过让对方主动提出你的偏好，你就能“接受”（accession/acquiescence）对方的请求。选 AF"},{"id":"v14.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Films that critics have slumbered through rarely generate industry excitement, even though the critics’ _____ reception may be less the fault of the movie than of its unfortunate time slot near a fatiguing film festival’s conclusion.","key":"AC","opts":["somnolent","impartial","lethargic","laconic","befuddled","evenhanded"],"expl":"评论者的“昏昏欲睡”（somnolent/lethargic）。选 AC"},{"id":"v14.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even the cleverest use of time management techniques is powerless to _____ the sum of minutes in a person’s life (over 52 million, optimistically assuming a life expectancy of 100 years ), so people squeeze as much as they could into each one of them.","key":"CF","opts":["justify","quantify","augment","enrich","measure","extend"],"expl":"时间总数无法“延长”（extend）或“量化”（quantify）。选 CF"},{"id":"v14.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the absence of a surface gradient, the new laws of refraction and reflection are _____ the conventional law, so they represent more of an extension than a complete revolution.","key":"AB","opts":["inferable from","entailed by","antithetical to","coincident with","antecedent to","oppositional to"],"expl":"新定律与旧定律“相容”（inferable from/entailed by）。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v14-2","title":"Test 14 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v14.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"What once seemed a quixotic vision—the “Subway to the Sea,” connecting Union Station in downtown Los Angeles to the Pacific Ocean in Santa Monica—no longer seems quite so _____.","key":"A","opts":["impracticable","prescient","banal","viable","beneficial"],"expl":"地下铁路从“不切实际”（impracticable）变为“可行”（viable）。选 A"},{"id":"v14.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In a federally governed country, a regional government can function as a (i)_____ for the entire nation—a setting in which new ideas under consideration for national implementation are (ii)_____ without having to involve the country as a whole.","key":"AF","groups":[["laboratory","catalyst","standard"],["dispersed","undermined","tried"]],"expl":"空1 填 laboratory（实验室）：地方政府是实验场；空2 填 tried（试行）。选 AF"},{"id":"v14.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Conventional deposits of oil and gas are actually the final resting place of far-traveled hydrocarbons that were (i)_____ deeper source beds of organic-rich rock. By contrast, shale gas (ii)_____ its birthplace, remaining in the source bed whose organic matter produced the gas.","key":"BD","groups":[["trapped in","generated in","bound for"],["never leaves","swiftly escapes from","rarely stays in"]],"expl":"空1 填 generated in（在……中生成）；空2 填 never leaves（从不离开）。选 BD"},{"id":"v14.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unlike most other serious journals, which drain money from their owners, the Review has long been (i)_____. But the formula is not without its imperfections, which have grown more pronounced in recent years. The publication has always been erudite and (ii)_____ but not always lively and readable. (iii)_____, accompanied by a certain aversion to risk taking, has pervaded its pages for a long time.","key":"ADI","groups":[["lucrative","realistic","unesteemed"],["authoritative","animated","trendy"],["an originality","an impulsiveness","a staleness"]],"expl":"空1 填 lucrative（有利可图的）；空2 填 authoritative（权威的）；空3 填 a staleness（陈旧）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v14.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Flawed as it may be because it is conducted by subjective scientists, science itself has methods that help us _____ our biases and talk about objective reality with some validity.","key":"AF","opts":["bypass","reduce","exacerbate","magnify","acknowledge","circumvent"],"expl":"科学方法能“规避”（circumvent）偏见。选 AF"},{"id":"v14.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In Japanese aesthetics, especially but not only in Noh, beauty contains the idea of _____: beauty must have an air of evanescence, the intimation of its own demise.","key":"CF","opts":["transience","symmetry","decay","simplicity","balance","deterioration"],"expl":"日本美学中，美包含“短暂性”（transience）与“衰败”（decay/deterioration）。选 CF"},{"id":"v14.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The uniquely human ability to rethink and revise our social arrangements is a weird blessing, allowing us to create systems that are as likely to _____ us as to liberate us.","key":"BE","opts":["cheer","shackle","admonish","educate","stifle","enliven"],"expl":"社会安排既可能“束缚”（shackle）我们，也可能“压制”（stifle）我们。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v15-1","title":"Test 15 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v15.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"There is _____ in the director’s most recent film that keeps the melodramatic possibilities latent in its script safely at bay.","key":"C","opts":["a mawkishness","a predictability","an austerity","an ostentatiousness","an emotiveness"],"expl":"导演用“朴素”（austerity）压住了剧本的煽情可能。选 C"},{"id":"v15.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite dispute between the sisters lasted all summer, Megan remained (i)_____ and Laruen was equally (ii)_____.","key":"AE","groups":[["intransigent","feckless","munificent"],["indolent","uncompromising","taciturn"]],"expl":"空1 填 intransigent（固执的）；空2 填 uncompromising（不妥协的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v15.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Cultures can shape attitudes and beliefs in ways that (i)_____ conscious awareness or control; in other words, cultural orientations may develop from processes that do not entail (ii)_____ participation, and cultures may pervade subtle psychological dynamics in ways that individuals may not be able to (iii)_____. Thus, theories and tools developed to study implicit cognition may increase our understanding of the complex interplay between culture and individuals.","key":"ADG","groups":[["operate outside of","tend to facilitate","may not alter"],["active","random","rote"],["report","maintain","condone"]],"expl":"空1 填 operate outside of（在……之外运作）；空2 填 active（主动的）；空3 填 report（报告）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v15.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Chavez Pass archaeological site was initially interpreted as indicative of _____ society, since it was thought to have been at the center of a cluster of smaller, contemporary settlements that it presumably controlled.","key":"BF","opts":["an expansionist","a hierarchical","an urban","a heterogeneous","a diverse","a stratified"],"expl":"Chavez Pass 被认为是“等级制”（hierarchical/stratified）社会的遗址。选 BF"},{"id":"v15.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the insistence on balancing spending against tax revenues has contributed to the economy’s stagnation, unfortunately, the government does not seem likely to _____ this rigid policy.","key":"DF","opts":["initiate","persist in","publicize","repudiate","continue","recant"],"expl":"政府不太可能“放弃”（repudiate）这一政策。选 DF"},{"id":"v15.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although its director _____ that the movie uses a documentary approach in portraying the famous sit-down strike, in practice its characters are heavily fictionalized and fall into familiar Hollywood types.","key":"AF","opts":["asserts","concedes","guarantees","disputes","grants","maintains"],"expl":"导演“宣称”（asserts/maintains）这部电影采用纪录片式手法。选 AF"},{"id":"v15.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For all the _____ the new CEO has received from the press recently, her staff have a decidedly less rosy view of her.","key":"AB","opts":["encomiums","tributes","evaluations","critiques","attention","publicity"],"expl":"首席执行官得到的“赞誉”（encomiums/tributes）。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v15-2","title":"Test 15 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v15.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Unlike some mammals—cows and sheep, for instance—that are notably _____, lions have a wide range of facial expressions.","key":"B","opts":["tractable","impassive","solitary","social","sluggish"],"expl":"与狮子不同，牛和羊是“温顺”（tractable）或“冷漠”（impassive）的。选 B"},{"id":"v15.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"World demand for oil had been intensified, but it slackened because China’s surge in oil consumption had (i)_____. Moreover, high oil price had themselves started to act as a short-term (ii)_____ the global economy, thus further dampening demand.","key":"CE","groups":[["spread","commenced","slowed"],["spur to","drag on","panacea for"]],"expl":"空1 填 slowed（放缓）：中国的消费增长放缓；空2 填 drag on（拖累）：油价的上涨拖累经济。选 CE"},{"id":"v15.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The slow pace of job creation was without precedent for the period of recovery from a recession, but the conditions that conspired to cause the recession were also (i)_____. The stock market declined sharply, and rampant business investment slumped. Then an ensuing spate of scandals (ii)_____ public trust in the way companies were run. And yet, despite these powerful (iii)_____ to growth, the recession proved surprisingly mild.","key":"BDG","groups":[["heartening","atypical","ambiguous"],["weakened","illuminated","consolidated"],["counterforces","stimulants","concomitants"]],"expl":"空1 填 atypical（非典型的）；空2 填 weakened（削弱）；空3 填 counterforces（反作用力）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v15.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Given children’s active fantasy lives, one might think of truthfulness as (i)_____ virtue in young children, but it turns out that lying is the more (ii)_____ skill. A child who is going to lie must recognize the truth, intellectually conceive of an alternate reality, and be able to convincingly sell that new reality to someone else. Therefore, lying (iii)_____ cognitive development and social skills in a way that honesty simply does not.","key":"ADI","groups":[["an instinctive","an acquired","a conscious"],["advanced","practical","mundane"],["undermines","forgoes","demands"]],"expl":"空1 填 an acquired（习得的）；空2 填 advanced（高级的）；空3 填 demands（要求）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v15.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A cure for the common cold has been so elusive that it has become a modern symbol of _____.","key":"BD","opts":["danger","futility","unease","pointlessness","sloth","apathy"],"expl":"感冒无法治愈，成了“徒劳”（futility/pointlessness）的象征。选 BD"},{"id":"v15.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The dictator’s gleaming military uniform and imperial paraphernalia sharply contrast with the _____ fashion favored by most other contemporary political leaders.","key":"AB","opts":["unostentatious","modest","august","majestic","formal","casual"],"expl":"与独裁者的华丽形成对照的是“朴素”（unostentatious）或“朴实的”（modest）风格。选 AB"},{"id":"v15.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"If giant X-ray flares churn circumstellar disks enough to keep newborn planets, such as Earth once was, from spiraling into their suns, it would be an ironic twist on our conception of X-ray flares as _____.","key":"AE","opts":["dangerous","predictable","ancient","ephemeral","perilous","foreseeable"],"expl":"X 射线耀斑是“短暂的”（ephemeral）与“危险的”（perilous）。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v16-1","title":"Test 16 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v16.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Though humanitarian emergencies are frequent features of television news, such exposure seldom _____ the public, which rather seems resigned to a sense of impotency.","key":"D","opts":["paralyzes","demoralizes","assuages","galvanizes","exasperates"],"expl":"人道主义灾难的报道很少“激起”（galvanizes）公众的行动。选 D"},{"id":"v16.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the fact that the book promises a complete rethinking of the factors contributing to the conflict, the picture that the book paints is (i)_____: in identifying cause, it is more orthodox than (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["obscure","detailed","familiar"],["restrictive","revisionist","enigmatic"]],"expl":"空1 填 familiar（熟悉的）；空2 填 revisionist（修正主义的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v16.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Traditional Vietnamese culture has long promoted the idea of gender equality. Founding myths (i)_____ the equal division of labor in child care for mothers and fathers. As is often the case, however, theoretical commitments are (ii)_____ actual processes. In reality, gender-based (iii)_____ persists.","key":"BDI","groups":[["obscure","celebrate","countermand"],["incommensurate with","surpassed by","inspired by"],["parity","inclusiveness","stratification"]],"expl":"空1 填 celebrate（颂扬）；空2 填 incommensurate with（与……不相称）；空3 填 stratification（分层）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v16.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Not only was this writer content to leave the reading public in the dark, she seems to have _____ the role of trickster, seeding her works with apparent clues that led nowhere.","key":"CE","opts":["rejected","disdained","relished","participated in","delighted in","developed"],"expl":"作者“享受”（relished）或“乐于”（delighted in）误导读者。选 CE"},{"id":"v16.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the biography never explicitly assesses what role the dynamic between Mr. Merrill’s parents might have played in the development of his personality, the author offers plenty of _____.","key":"CF","opts":["mystification","elucidation","speculation","reflection","obfuscation","conjecture"],"expl":"没有解释的部分由“推测”（speculation/conjecture）补足。选 CF"},{"id":"v16.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are great _____ in countries’ greenhouse gas emissions, especially in per capita terms: while the United States and China are similar in aggregate emissions, United States per capita emissions are a huge multiple of China’s.","key":"BE","opts":["distortions","disparities","fluctuations","advances","variances","vacillations"],"expl":"人均排放存在巨大“差异”（disparities/variances）。选 BE"},{"id":"v16.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is frequently a protracted time interval between the introduction of an innovative musical composition and its public acceptance; the concert-going public often spurns the _____ in favor of the familiar for a prolonged period.","key":"CD","opts":["comprehensive","intricate","novel","original","intelligible","complex"],"expl":"观众拒绝接受“新颖的”（novel）、“原创的”（original）作品。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v16-2","title":"Test 16 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v16.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The theory that the 1908 Tunguska event was the explosion of a cosmic body in the sky over Siberia is _____: no one has yet found fragments of the object or any impact craters in the affected region.","key":"E","opts":["long-standing","indisputable","plausible","uncontested","unproven"],"expl":"Tunguska 的理论“尚未证实”（unproven）。选 E"},{"id":"v16.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Motivation is the hardest of all managerial tasks, and it is _____ to expect a single memo, no matter how well crafted, to have much effect on the staff’s attitude.","key":"C","opts":["ingenious","reasonable","fanciful","scrupulous","radical"],"expl":"指望一份备忘录改变员工态度是“幻想的”（fanciful）。选 C"},{"id":"v16.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Collecting such fragment of contemporary popular culture as postcards, newspaper clippings, and wallpaper patterns, Susan Hiller transforms these seemingly (i)_____ artifacts into objective (ii)_____ by making them the centerpieces in her compositions.","key":"BD","groups":[["extravagant","trivial","archaic"],["importance","uniformity","banality"]],"expl":"空1 填 trivial（琐碎的）；空2 填 banality（平庸）。选 BD"},{"id":"v16.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"In adolescence, (i)_____ interactions are crucial in forging a self-identity. To be sure, this process often plays out in (ii)_____ as a means of defining and shoring up the sense of self. Kids will seek out like-minded companions, and spurn others who seem different. But when kept within reasonable bounds, this in-group (iii)_____ generally evolves into a more mature friendship pattern.","key":"CDH","groups":[["adult","wide-ranging","peer"],["cliquish social behavior","dramatic changes in personality","heightened sociability"],["alienation","clustering","competition"]],"expl":"空1 填 peer（同龄人）；空2 填 cliquish social behavior（小圈子式的社交行为）；空3 填 clustering（聚集）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v16.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The concept of the Hellenistic period in ancient history has proved useful but also _____, with scholars disagreeing on the dates when the period began and ended.","key":"AB","opts":["slippery","elusive","fruitless","deceptive","futile","compelling"],"expl":"Hellenistic 一词“滑溜”（slippery）、“难以确定”（elusive）。选 AB"},{"id":"v16.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Few ideas are more _____ than the notion that cultures evolve in Darwin fashion; many academics have begun writing about cultural evolution, but few treat the underlying Darwinian logic with the care it deserves.","key":"AC","opts":["abused","archaic","misused","outdated","divisive","derivative"],"expl":"将文化进化说成达尔文式的观念常被“误用”（abused/misused）。选 AC"},{"id":"v16.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"After many years of feeling _____ by his seniors managers, Clark was becoming hopeful of advancement.","key":"BC","opts":["vilified","stymied","hindered","aggrieved","circumvented","overlooked"],"expl":"他觉得被上司“阻碍”（stymied/hindered）。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v17-1","title":"Test 17 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v17.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Many readers today consider the moral sentiments expressed in the ancient writers’ work to be quite vapid, and in the seventeenth century they were similarly regarded as _____.","key":"A","opts":["jejune","didactic","dogmatic","tendentious","arcane"],"expl":"古代作家的道德情感在 17 世纪也被看作“空洞的”（jejune）。选 A"},{"id":"v17.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although movie critic Pauline Kael had a distaste for sycophancy, she also had a need for (i)_____; as a consequence of these competing feelings, she sent very (ii)_____ signals to friends and colleagues.","key":"BF","groups":[["solitude","obeisance","clarity"],["direct","subtle","mixed"]],"expl":"空1 填 obeisance（卑躬屈膝）；空2 填 mixed（复杂的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v17.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"One sometimes hears that Marco Polo introduced pasta to the Western world, having encountered it in China. This durable myth, which (i)_____ that nothing should have been known of pasta in Italy until 1295, when Marco Polo returned from the Far East, can easily be (ii)_____ by pointing out that there are Italian references to pasta that (iii)_____.","key":"AEI","groups":[["requires","demonstrates","symbolizes"],["augmented","debunked","traced"],["praise its virtues","can be authenticated","predate that event"]],"expl":"空1 填 requires（需要）；空2 填 debunked（揭穿）；空3 填 predate that event（早于那一事件）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v17.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Williamson had a fierce commitment to achieving an accord, spending enormous amount of time trying to forge a consensus out of an often _____ assembly.","key":"BC","opts":["apathetic","fractious","restive","cynical","compliant","tractable"],"expl":"固执的（fractious）与“不安的”（restive）使共识难以达成。选 BC"},{"id":"v17.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Readers looking for another condemnation of private equity firms should look elsewhere, this book is not _____ such firms.","key":"AB","opts":["a rant against","a diatribe on","an exculpation","a disquisition on","a vindication of","an argument about"],"expl":"这本书不是“对……的谩骂”（rant against）或“论述”（diatribe）。选 AB"},{"id":"v17.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"His premiership, seemingly cast-iron year ago, is now so vulnerable that even a good day at the office does no more than buy him a few weeks of _____ from rebels within his own party.","key":"CD","opts":["controversy","reproach","respite","relief","blame","deference"],"expl":"首相只能获得几周的“喘息”（respite）与“解脱”（relief）。选 CD"},{"id":"v17.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even before she went to art school, Veronica found the standard design categories _____: she didn’t understand why designing buildings and designing tables should require different sensibilities.","key":"BE","opts":["provocative","limiting","stimulating","confusing","confining","exhilarating"],"expl":"标准的设计分类让她感到“局限”（limiting/confining）。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v17-2","title":"Test 17 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v17.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Though the volume of radioactive waste produced by nuclear power plants is _____, the problem of how to dispose of that waste is not: rather, it is of major importance.","key":"D","opts":["unmanageable","troubling","significant","small","deceptive"],"expl":"废料的量“很小”（small），但处理问题“很重要”（significant）。选 D"},{"id":"v17.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Since fibromyalgia’s symptoms can be (i)_____ and can (ii)_____ other disorder, and its diagnosis depends largely on patients’ descriptions rather than blood tests or biopsies, fibromyalgia’s cause and treatment have been the subject of much debate.","key":"AD","groups":[["wide-ranging","distinctive","debilitating"],["mimic","illuminate","preclude"]],"expl":"空1 填 wide-ranging（范围广的）；空2 填 mimic（模仿）。选 AD"},{"id":"v17.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Architecture scholar Sandy McCreery recently argued that traffic congestion, far from being a sign of urban (i)_____, is a mark of urban (ii)_____; congestion promotes contemplation of our surroundings and provides us with a shared experience, thereby fulfilling the essential task of the city.","key":"BF","groups":[["plentitude","decline","excitement"],["ambition","privation","health"]],"expl":"空1 填 decline（衰落）；空2 填 health（健康）。选 BF"},{"id":"v17.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"For almost two centuries, the German island of Sylt has offered various therapies for every conceivable (i)_____ from broken bones to liver complaints. The local mud, saltwater, thermal pools, and spas have been deemed (ii)_____ by the German medical system, which (iii)_____ some of these treatments. Consequently, the treatments are widely used.","key":"ADI","groups":[["malady","indiscretion","prognosis"],["healthful","suspect","innocuous"],["doubts","denies","funds"]],"expl":"空1 填 malady（病症）；空2 填 healthful（有益健康的）；空3 填 funds（资助）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v17.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author engages this issue from diverse perspectives, supports his arguments with many examples, and manages to avoid antagonizing others in dealing with a very _____ subject.","key":"AC","opts":["contentious","pedestrian","controversial","perplexing","mundane","intriguing"],"expl":"这一话题有争议（contentious/controversial）。选 AC"},{"id":"v17.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Space is often referred to as the final frontier, as the only realm of which humankind has still to gain substantial understanding, yet the ocean is also another vast area about which our knowledge is _____.","key":"DF","opts":["erroneous","confusing","frustrating","rudimentary","delusive","sketchy"],"expl":"海洋的知识仍然“粗浅”（rudimentary/sketchy）。选 DF"},{"id":"v17.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Culture, like speech, is primarily a human faculty, although both functions may exist in a more _____ form in lesser primates.","key":"CF","opts":["indispensable","crucial","primitive","intelligible","recognizable","rudimentary"],"expl":"灵长类中的文化是“原始的”（primitive/rudimentary）形式。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v18-1","title":"Test 18 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v18.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"For the urban researcher, the long lives of ancient cities can provide ample chronological data, making up for the paucity stemming from relative _____ of most present-day cities.","key":"E","opts":["complexity","formlessness","transparency","diversity","youthfulness"],"expl":"现代城市的“年轻”（youthfulness）使可用的历史数据稀少。选 E"},{"id":"v18.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Though many professional book reviewers would agree that criticism should be (i)_____ enterprise, a tendency to write (ii)_____ reviews has risen, partly out of the mistaken belief that sharing personal details will help reviewers stand out of the pack.","key":"AE","groups":[["an anonymous","an evenhanded","a spirited"],["scathing","confessional","superficial"]],"expl":"空1 填 an evenhanded（公允的）；空2 填 superficial（肤浅的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v18.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Biologists have little (i)_____ drawing the link between the success of humanity and human (ii)_____. Indeed, many biologists claim that this attribute, the ability to (iii)_____, or, to put it more sharply, to make individuals subordinate their self-interest to the needs of the group, lies at the root of human achievement.","key":"BEI","groups":[["consensus regarding","compunction about","justification for"],["resilience","sociability","uniqueness"],["reflect","communicate","cooperate"]],"expl":"空1 填 consensus regarding（就……达成共识）：生物学家对这一联系“没有共识”（little consensus）；空2 填 sociability（社会性）；空3 填 cooperate（合作）。选 BEI"},{"id":"v18.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Tompkinson’s prior donations to the university, while very generous, failed to _____ the magnitude of her latest gift.","key":"BD","opts":["compensate for","portend","clarify","predict","offset","undermine"],"expl":"之前的捐款“无法预示”（portend/predict）这一次的规模，并非“弥补”或“抵消”。选 BD"},{"id":"v18.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The first images of Jupiter’s moon Callisto show bright regions of material, as if older and darker ice had slid downhill and exposed the _____ ice underneath.","key":"DF","opts":["ancient","murky","compact","pristine","grimy","unblemished"],"expl":"老旧冰层被滑下，露出“原始的”（pristine）冰层。选 DF"},{"id":"v18.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Mortoris is dour and _____, seemingly incapable of smiling, let alone laughing.","key":"EF","opts":["mirthful","jovial","intelligent","tepid","lugubrious","gloomy"],"expl":"他阴郁、“悲哀的”（lugubrious/gloomy），几乎不会笑。选 EF"},{"id":"v18.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Circulatory systems on organisms originated in widely separated epochs, according to the fossil record, and under a broad range of circumstances, the myriad forms they take attest to that ______ of origin.","key":"DF","opts":["mysteriousness","randomness","ambiguity","heterogeneity","indeterminacy","diversity"],"expl":"循环系统起源于不同时代，形式多样，说明其起源是“多样性”（diversity/heterogeneity）。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v18-2","title":"Test 18 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v18.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Few studies have been published on ground-squirrel dispersal, and most of them have involved very small sample sizes, thus most statement regarding ground-squirrel dispersal must be considered _____.","key":"E","opts":["invaluable","unexceptional","inveterate","routine","conjectural"],"expl":"样本太小，关于地松鼠扩散的说法只能算“推测性的”（conjectural）。选 E"},{"id":"v18.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many of the unusual behaviors attributed to crows—such as drinking coffee or presenting gifts to people who feed them—are based on (i)_____ and therefore fall into the category of (ii)_____ rather than science.","key":"CD","groups":[["long-term observation","controlled experiments","secondhand testimony"],["anecdote","speculation","hypothesis"]],"expl":"空1 填 secondhand testimony（二手证词）；空2 填 anecdote（轶事）。选 CD"},{"id":"v18.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the scathing precision with which she satirizes the lives of social aspirants and moneyed folk, the writer appears to (i)_____ being part of the world she presents as so (ii)_____.","key":"BE","groups":[["abhor","relish","evoke"],["unattainable","insufferable","enchanting"]],"expl":"作者讽刺社会名流，却似乎“享受”（relish）自己也是其中的一员，而这个世界“令人难以忍受”（insufferable）。选 BE"},{"id":"v18.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Inuit print making is less (i)_____ than carving in that it does not have substantial historical precedents, although there are (ii)_____ incised carvings on bone or antler, facial tattoo marks or inlay skin work on clothing, mitts and footwear. Carving materials such as stone, bone, antler, wood, and ivory were (iii)_____, but paper and drawing tools were unknown until introduced by early explorers and missionaries.","key":"ADG","groups":[["traditional","prestigious","anomalous"],["affinities with","objections to","regulations about"],["available locally","rarely used","virtually interchangeable"]],"expl":"空1 填 traditional（传统的）：版画没有传统；空2 填 affinities with（与……相似）；空3 填 available locally（本地可得）：雕刻材料本地就有。选 ADG"},{"id":"v18.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Compared to their predecessors, who were more nationalist than feminist in political orientation, Roman women activists of the younger generation are more inclined to _____ women’s rights, often creating organizations focused primarily on women’s issues.","key":"CF","opts":["expand","de-emphasize","champion","idealize","downplay","defend"],"expl":"年轻一代更倾向“支持”（champion/defend）女性权益。选 CF"},{"id":"v18.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Individuals, governments, and companies show ample ability to _____ themselves by setting goals based on current conditions and then blindly following them even when those conditions change drastically.","key":"AE","opts":["hamstring","reinvent","promote","revitalize","impair","invigorate"],"expl":"各方“束缚”（hamstring）或“损害”（impair）自己，因为他们盲目坚持过时目标。选 AE"},{"id":"v18.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The performer can be _____ in his comedy, but he is fundamentally a bighearted person who displays a core sweetness even at his most manic.","key":"AF","opts":["inflammatory","pedestrian","gloomy","uninspired","puerile","provocative"],"expl":"这位表演者的喜剧“可能很激烈”（inflammatory/provocative），但本质上很善良。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v19-1","title":"Test 19 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v19.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"To criticize a disaster film for being _____ is a bit silly, since people do not go to disaster movies to see an honest portrayed of reality.","key":"E","opts":["expensive","harrowing","derivative","convoluted","implausible"],"expl":"灾难电影“不可信”（implausible）是不公平的批评。选 E"},{"id":"v19.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The benefits offered by information technology do not (i)_____ the need for individual reasoning; for example, Internet user should not allow the reasoning process to be (ii)_____ the mere accumulation raw data.","key":"CF","groups":[["disguise","signal","diminish"],["preceded by","supplemented with","supplanted by"]],"expl":"空1 填 diminish（削弱）：信息技术不会削弱个人推理；空2 填 supplanted by（被……取代）：推理不应被原始数据取代。选 CF"},{"id":"v19.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For many years, Americans have had a love affair with ferryboats. Ferries are said to relieve our frayed nerves after we’ve stewed in bumper-to-bumper traffic, and conventional wisdom also says ferries (i)_____ congestion and air pollution by getting us out of cars. Unfortunately, this (ii)_____ notion recently has (iii)_____ several West Coast mayors, who have in consequence eagerly pursued the implementation of ferry service in their cities.","key":"BEG","groups":[["contribute to","reduce","cover up"],["provocative","misguided","cynical"],["captivated","confused","outraged"]],"expl":"空1 填 reduce（减少）；空2 填 misguided（误导的）；空3 填 captivated（迷住）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v19.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In ways large and small, millions of people are taking active steps to _____ the medical mainstream, whether by taking herbal remedies for disease or by placing their hopes for a cure in alternative treatment.","key":"BE","opts":["augment","sidestep","support","vilify","circumvent","endorse"],"expl":"人们“绕开”（sidestep/circumvent）主流医学。选 BE"},{"id":"v19.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although its gray text blocks and black-and-white illustrations give it a sober mien, this one-stop resource can take the place of a dozen less _____ texts.","key":"AF","opts":["exhaustive","interesting","appealing","original","educational","comprehensive"],"expl":"这本书比其他“不那么全面”（less comprehensive/exhaustive）的书更好。选 AF"},{"id":"v19.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The media have constantly disparaged the governor’s competence and have found a public only too eager to applaud their _____.","key":"CF","opts":["assiduousness","stupefaction","mockery","incredulity","certitude","derision"],"expl":"媒体的“嘲笑”（mockery/derision）获得了公众的认同。选 CF"},{"id":"v19.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The _____ of ophthalmology as a field in the United States from 1820 to 1850 is evident in the opening of at least five eye hospitals during this period, offering new venues for ophthalmic treatment and experimentation.","key":"CF","opts":["sophistication","retrenchment","burgeoning","resurgence","curtailment","expansion"],"expl":"眼科在 1820 年至 1850 年间的“蓬勃发展”（burgeoning/expansion）体现在医院的增加。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v19-2","title":"Test 19 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v19.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In contrast to such sparsely populated terrestrial habitats as desert and tundra, the oceans _____ with a seemingly endless array of creatures.","key":"A","opts":["teem","flow","evolve","roil","ebb"],"expl":"海洋“充满”（teem）各种生物。选 A"},{"id":"v19.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Barring the discovery of new letters, hidden diaries, or the like, fresh information about eminent people is hard to find because their lives have been so intensely _____.","key":"B","opts":["ridiculed","scrutinized","admired","embellished","underrated"],"expl":"名人的生活被“仔细审视”（scrutinized）得很彻底，因此很难发现新信息。选 B"},{"id":"v19.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because the book is largely concerned with an examination of various (i)_____ often encountered in contemporary thinking, such as an exaggerated appreciation for meaningless coincidence and a credulous accept of pseudoscience, much of the writing has a (ii)_____ quality to it. Nevertheless, it avoids the overly earned scolding tone common to many such endeavors.","key":"AD","groups":[["inadequacies","abstractions","complexities"],["debunking","speculative","generalizing"]],"expl":"空1 填 abstractions（抽象概念）；空2 填 debunking（揭穿）。选 AD"},{"id":"v19.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Analysis of 47.5-million-year-old fossils from Pakistan has yielded fresh insights into the early ancestors of modern whales. For example, Maiacetus inuus was a land animal (i)_____ life in the sea. One Maiacetus innus fossil encased a fetus positioned for a head-first delivery, which is typical of a land mammal and suggests the species gave birth onshore. But it probably spent much of its time (ii)_____: its big teeth were suited for catching fish, while its flipper-like feet must have been (iii)_____ walking.","key":"CDH","groups":[["resistant","removed from","adapted to"],["in the water","fleeing from predators","protecting its young"],["incompatible with","clumsy for","strengthened by"]],"expl":"空1 填 adapted to（适应）：这是一种适应海洋生活的陆地动物；空2 填 in the water（在水中）；空3 填 clumsy for（对行走笨拙）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v19.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Aerial viewings of the gigantic stone horse attributed to the Native American Quechuan people fail to _____ the considerable artistry required to create the piece: the horse appears crudely constructed unless carefully examined from the ground.","key":"AC","opts":["reveal","justify","manifest","mitigate","diminish","undercut"],"expl":"从空中看马的形状，无法“揭示”（reveal）其艺术性。选 AC"},{"id":"v19.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book aims to illuminate how science has changed the meaning of nothingness from _____ philosophical concept to something we can almost put under a microscope.","key":"CF","opts":["a tangible","a palpable","a nebulous","a nettlesome","an incontrovertible","a vague"],"expl":"空无从“虚无”（nebulous）的哲学概念变为可以在显微镜下观察的东西。选 CF"},{"id":"v19.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Few ideas are more _____ than the notion that cultures evolve in Darwin fashion;many academics have begun writing about cultural evolution, but few treat the underlying Darwinian logic with the care it deserves.","key":"AC","opts":["abused","archaic","misused","outdated","divisive","derivative"],"expl":"“达尔文式的”文化进化观念常被“误用”（abused/misused）。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v20-1","title":"Test 20 · Section 1","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v20.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Scientists have argued not only that the chains of atoms called ladder compounds have _____ theoretical interest but also that studies of such systems can lead to important practical applications.","key":"E","opts":["limited","dubious","superfluous","unidimensional","intrinsic"],"expl":"梯形化合物的理论兴趣“内在的”（intrinsic）。选 E"},{"id":"v20.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The building affairs minister rightly recognizes that the current planning system—under which the government controls every aspect of construction—creates disastrous developments, but she is wrong to propose the opposite: the wholesale (i)_____ of the building market. Such a complete (ii)_____ of responsibility on the part of the state can hardly be in the public’s interest.","key":"AD","groups":[["liberalization","preservation","regulation"],["abnegation","recapitulation","accretion"]],"expl":"空1 填 liberalization（自由化）：解除管制；空2 填 abnegation（放弃）：国家全面放弃责任。选 AD"},{"id":"v20.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Those who took Clark’s old-mannered compliance for obsequiousness (i)_____ him: his apparent (ii)_____ veiled a fervent (iii)_____ of the authority that others exercised over him, one that he occasionally expressed by discreetly sabotaging their most important projects.","key":"AEI","groups":[["misconstrued","condemned","respected"],["cynicism","acquiescence","intractability"],["veneration","justification","detestation"]],"expl":"空1 填 misconstrued（误解）：误判了 Clark；空2 填 acquiescence（默许）；空3 填 detestation（憎恶）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v20.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The initial, widely shared pessimism turned out to be _____, because it ignored the many things that could be done with resources left behind.","key":"CE","opts":["unintelligible","unfathomable","unfounded","unimaginative","unjustified","unimportant"],"expl":"最初的悲观“没有根据”（unfounded）。选 CE"},{"id":"v20.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Historically, the depletion of soil’s nitrogen has been one of the most _____ problems faced by farmers: an essential nutrient, nitrogen is quickly leached from soil, and farmers have struggled to find ways to replenish it.","key":"DE","opts":["capricious","ubiquitous","worrisome","stubborn","intractable","unpredictable"],"expl":"土壤氮的流失是农民“棘手”（intractable/stubborn）的问题。选 DE"},{"id":"v20.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientists should hope the faults in their theories will be _____ their peers since the refutation of one hypothesis can free its originator to develop a better one.","key":"AC","opts":["discerned by","disregarded by","discovered by","ignored by","opaque to","inspiring to"],"expl":"科学家希望同行“发现”（discerned/discovered）其理论中的错误。选 AC"},{"id":"v20.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although men still dominate the ranks of full professors in the field of astronomy, the increasing numbers of younger women in the field could _____ a change in its gender mix.","key":"DE","opts":["require","alleviate","block","presage","portend","hinder"],"expl":"年轻女性的增加可能“预示”（presage/portend）性别构成的变化。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v20-2","title":"Test 20 · Section 2","group":"Test 11–20","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v20.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some novelists immodestly idealized and exaggerated the significance of their work, but others, _____ to exalt the role of the writer, question a transcendent view of the art.","key":"B","opts":["averring","declining","seeking","feigning","avowing"],"expl":"另一些作家“避免”（declining）夸大作家的角色，因此质疑超验的艺术观。选 B"},{"id":"v20.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Though many avant-garde writers _____ traditional distinctions among literary categories, combining elements of biography and fiction, prose and poetry, this fusion of forms has been slow to catch on with publishers.","key":"A","opts":["flout","presuppose","exploit","imitate","illuminate"],"expl":"先锋作家“无视”（flout）传统的文学类别之分。选 A"},{"id":"v20.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Scholarly works on detective stories often begin with (i)_____, suggesting that there is something vaguely wrong with adults who spend their time reading such fiction and certainly something (ii)_____ those who devote energy to its analysis.","key":"BD","groups":[["chronologies","apologies","synopses"],["awry in","astute about","courageous about"]],"expl":"空1 填 apologies（致歉）：开头常道歉；空2 填 awry in（有问题的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v20.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"There are two opposing theories about mountain formation and climate over the past 40 million years: either the surge of mountain building (i)_____ the global cooling or vice versa. The first of these two theories asserts that widespread mountain building cooled the earth as a result of the (ii)_____ mountains and climate. For example, mountain glaciers tend to be (iii)_____: once established, they increase the reflectivity of the surface, thus lowering temperatures and allowing more ice to form.","key":"CEI","groups":[["superseded","halted","caused"],["disparity between","feedback between","complexity of"],["unpredictable","static","self-perpetuating"]],"expl":"空1 填 caused（导致）；空2 填 feedback between（相互反馈）；空3 填 self-perpetuating（自我维持的）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v20.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"An apparent paradox led the scientists to pursue their present line of research. They were struck by the fact that a single mathematics formula can be used to describe physical phenomena that appear to be so _____.","key":"EF","opts":["rudimentary","interdependent","interrelated","complex","heterogeneous","dissimilar"],"expl":"两种“看似”截然不同的现象可由同一数学公式描述，因此它们“看似”不相关（dissimilar）。选 EF"},{"id":"v20.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the northeastern United States, beaver populations had been critically reduced or even _____ in large areas at the end of nineteenth century; as a result, several states instituted prohibitions on beaver trapping.","key":"BC","opts":["diminished","extirpated","eliminated","devalued","weakened","underrated"],"expl":"海狸在大片区域“被灭绝”（extirpated）。选 BC"},{"id":"v20.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The preliminary analysis being on the whole, reassuring its confirmation would _____ concerns about the dangers of project.","key":"BD","opts":["explain","deflate","rationalize","soothe","reflect","hide"],"expl":"初步分析令人安心，将“平息”（deflate/soothe）对危险的担忧。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v21-1","title":"Test 21 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v21.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"By pointing out the self-serving nature of the governor’s motives for supporting the new health care policy, the columnist implied that the governor’s idealistic-sounding explanation of her position on the issue was almost certainty _____.","key":"D","opts":["impractical","derivative","simplistic","disingenuous","ineffectual"],"expl":"州长的理想化解释几乎肯定是“虚伪的”（disingenuous）。选 D"},{"id":"v21.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Due to the extraordinary circumstances, British business owners found themselves in a (i)_____ position during the Second World War, forced to accept regular interference from government and to acquiesce to (ii)_____ role for labor unions in negotiating the terms and conditions of employment.","key":"AE","groups":[["defensive","dominant","customary"],["a traditional","an enhanced","a diminished"]],"expl":"空1 填 defensive（防御的）；空2 填 a diminished（缩减的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v21.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"With the emergence of scientific history-writing in the late nineteenth century, several authors sought to ignore the glowing myths surrounding George Washington and uncover the human being within, but their biographies were still (i)_____ enough that Washington remained a marbled and remote figure. Indeed, by the 1920s Washington has become such (ii)_____ personage that inevitably someone had to go to the other extreme and try to (iii)_____ the legend.","key":"CDG","groups":[["ponderous","empirical","laudatory"],["a deified","an ignored","a misunderstood"],["debunk","aggrandize","reproduce"]],"expl":"空1 填 laudatory（颂扬的）：早期传记仍然是颂扬的；空2 填 a deified（被神化的）；空3 填 debunk（揭穿）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v21.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some kinds of deadly bacteria, including those that cause tetanus, tuberculosis, and botulism, remain _____ until something triggers their insidious activity.","key":"AB","opts":["harmless","innocuous","anomalous","aberrant","efficacious","undetectable"],"expl":"细菌“保持无害”（harmless/innocuous）直到被触发。选 AB"},{"id":"v21.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Titan, Saturn’s largest moon, looks surprisingly _____, even though it is a cold, dimly lit world made from unknown materials.","key":"BF","opts":["habitable","familiar","forbidding","placid","daunting","recognizable"],"expl":"土卫六看起来“宜居”（habitable/familiar）？。选 BF"},{"id":"v21.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The initial, widely shared pessimism turned out to be _____, because it ignored the many things that could be done with resources left behind.","key":"CE","opts":["unintelligible","unfathomable","unfounded","unimaginative","unjustified","unimportant"],"expl":"与 v20.1.4 相同：最初的悲观“没有根据”（unfounded）。选 CE"},{"id":"v21.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite a tendency to be overtly _____, her poetry does not consist solely of pious sentiments: it often sparks the imagination and provides lively entertainment.","key":"AD","opts":["preachy","querulous","insincere","sanctimonious","plaintive","disingenuous"],"expl":"她的诗“说教”（preachy/sanctimonious）。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v21-2","title":"Test 21 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v21.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In the solar system, collisions involving cosmic object are among the most _____ processes shaping surfaces: images of many solar objects show a proliferation of impact craters formed throughout the past 4.5 billion years.","key":"B","opts":["cataclysmic","pervasive","misleading","uncontrollable","random"],"expl":"撞击是“普遍存在”（pervasive）的过程。选 B"},{"id":"v21.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"As Ellen Donkin explains, in eighteenth-century England, writing plays (i)_____ women. Even when the (ii)_____ meant that playwriting did not bring personal fame, the work nevertheless enabled them to present their own views to the public and offered the possibility of acquiring capital.","key":"AD","groups":[["empowered","overextended","impressed"],["use of a pseudonym","lack of a producer","poor remuneration"]],"expl":"空1 填 empowered（赋予能力）：写剧本使女性获得权力；空2 填 lack of a producer（缺少制作人）。选 AD"},{"id":"v21.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Pioneering medical research scientists’ (i)_____ claims regarding the (ii)_____ new researches make the public wonder their own doctors are not dispensing miracles. There are forces, both external and internal, on scientists that most require them to (iii)_____. Without money, there is no science. Researchers must constantly convince administrators who control tax dollars, investors, and individual donors that the work they are doing will make a difference.","key":"BFH","groups":[["modest","inflated","fastidious"],["serious constraints on","overblown interpretations of","potential beneftis of"],["improvise","oversell","generalize"]],"expl":"空1 填 inflated（夸大的）；空2 填 overblown interpretations of（对……的过度解读）；空3 填 oversell（过度推销）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v21.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the occasional (i)_____ of their venues, the culture of corporate conferences is a deeply (ii)_____ conference, each day consisted of nearly nine hours of continuous lectures and panels enlivened by pleasantries or anything that could be construed as a joke. The only (iii)_____ sensory deprivation of the sessions came from the handsome color slides favored by the corporate presenters.","key":"BEI","groups":[["seclusion","opulence","enormity"],["sycophantic","ascetic","mercenary"],["allusion to","ramification of","respite from"]],"expl":"空1 填 opulence（奢华）；空2 填 ascetic（禁欲的）；空3 填 respite from（从……中暂时解脱）。选 BEI"},{"id":"v21.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Willian Perkins, his _____ speaking style notwithstanding, has long been seen as the moderate face of his political party.","key":"AF","opts":["fiery","genteel","bumbling","unremarkable","affable","impassioned"],"expl":"尽管 Perkins 的讲话风格“激昂”（fiery/impassioned），他仍是温和派的面孔。选 AF"},{"id":"v21.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although in his new book he tends to repeat himself like a _____ uncle, McHughen makes a persuasive case for the safety of tinkering with genes to create new foods.","key":"EF","opts":["taciturn","reserved","prototypical","cantankerous","loquacious","garrulous"],"expl":"他像一个“爱唠叨”（loquacious/garrulous）的叔叔。选 EF"},{"id":"v21.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Joshua Gisemba Bagaka found that the pedagogical results of group projects and other engaged learning activities in Kenyan mathematics classroom were _____; such activities, then, may not be the best way of improving mathematics education.","key":"CE","opts":["overstated","counterintuitive","mixed","discouraging","inconsistent","inexplicable"],"expl":"结果“喜忧参半”（mixed）或“不一致的”（inconsistent），所以不能断定小组学习是最好的方式。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v22-1","title":"Test 22 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v22.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"If the study proves that bears are still endemic to the area, the proposal to introduce additional bears of the same species will probably face less opposition, since the plan would then involve _____ a historic population, not trying to build population from scratch.","key":"B","opts":["reclassifying","augmenting","forestalling","publicizing","winnowing"],"expl":"增加（augmenting）已有的种群，比从零开始容易。选 B"},{"id":"v22.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Computers have become adept in rarefied domains once thought to be uniquely human. However, they simultaneously have (i)_____ certain tasks basic to the human experience, including spatial orientation and object recognition, and in so doing, have shown us how (ii)_____ such fundamental skills truly are.","key":"AF","groups":[["failed to master","helped to improve","managed to mimic"],["outmoded","common","impressive"]],"expl":"空1 填 failed to master（未能掌握）：计算机做不到基本的空间定向；空2 填 impressive（令人印象深刻）：这些技能很难做到。选 AF"},{"id":"v22.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Anna Gavalda’s fiction is appealing largely because of her writing styles, which is certainly (i)_____. It is heavy on dialogue (and light on embellishment) features very short sections (of often only a few sentence) in rapid succession, and in general favors an unadorned directness. Not surprisingly, this style works better in short-story form than in novels, and the story collection I Wish someone Were Waiting for Me Somewhere (ii)_____ her attempt to (iii)_____ it in novel, as in, for example, Someone I loved.","key":"BFH","groups":[["annoying","distinctive","convoluted"],["is thought to precede","fails in comparison with","impresses considerably more than"],["undermine","sustain","reject"]],"expl":"空1 填 distinctive（独特的）；空2 填 fails in comparison with（与……相比不足）；空3 填 sustain（维持）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v22.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Architects may be more extroverted and therefore the more _____ members of a bridge design team, but they are not always the most essential.","key":"DF","opts":["indispensable","conscientious","reliable","visible","valuable","salient"],"expl":"建筑师更“显眼”（visible）。选 DF"},{"id":"v22.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Excessive focus on what might have been can cause in us feelings of restlessness and regret, but some scientists are beginning to think that fancying an alternative reality might have _____ effects as well.","key":"CF","opts":["subtle","adverse","restorative","pleasurable","unfavorable","tonic"],"expl":"想象另一种现实可能有“有益的”（restorative/tonic）效果。选 CF"},{"id":"v22.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Apparent flaws in the sculptor’s work have not _____ its respectful reception by most modern critics.","key":"DF","opts":["determined","controlled","undermined","prevented","overshadowed","precluded"],"expl":"瑕疵没有“破坏”（undermined/undermined）其受欢迎。选 DF"},{"id":"v22.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It’s hardly _____ the committee calls for: rudimentary competence would be an improvement on the current chaos.","key":"DF","opts":["accountability","disarray","unruliness","faultlessness","loyalty","perfection"],"expl":"委员会要求的不是“完美”（perfection），而是基本的能力（这表明它要的不是“零瑕疵”）。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v22-2","title":"Test 22 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v22.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"A new television documentary focuses on of the prime minister’s defining contradiction, portraying her as a woman who cultivated an image of _____, but who liked to live grandly.","key":"B","opts":["irascibility","abstemiousness","contentiousness","insouciance","surreptitiousness"],"expl":"首相“节俭”（abstemiousness）的形象与奢华生活形成对照。选 B"},{"id":"v22.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The stories in Yiyun Li’s recent collection are distinctive particularly for the strong contrast between their emotional intensity and their consistently _____ tone.","key":"C","opts":["affable","ebullient","measured","irascible","overwrought"],"expl":"这些故事的语调“克制”（measured）。选 C"},{"id":"v22.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Until the advent of film, commercial entertainment in England occurred only where concentrated urban populations provided audiences large enough to make it remunerative: theaters and music halls were (i)_____ in rural villages. But village cinemas quickly become (ii)_____, even though they were ramshackle affairs in comparison to the urban picture palaces.","key":"BD","groups":[["spartan","unconceivable","profitable"],["commonplace","sophisticated","unfashionable"]],"expl":"空1 填 spartan（简陋的）；空2 填 commonplace（常见的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v22.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"For Plato the art of music was so (i)_____ moral and political reality that any alteration to music system would necessarily require a corresponding political shift. But two and a half millennia later, when classical music is generally seem merely as a lifestyle accessory, Plato’s conception seems (ii)_____. To be sure, there are still people who consider classical music to be of (iii)_____ cultural importance, but few of them are able to articulate this convincingly.","key":"CEH","groups":[["rarely identified with","tenuously connected to","firmly anchored in"],["apt","absurd","disingenuous"],["marginal","profound","uncertain"]],"expl":"空1 填 firmly anchored in（牢牢扎根于）；空2 填 apt（恰当的）；空3 填 marginal（边缘的）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v22.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the vocalists who auditioned for a leading part in the local production of Sweeney Todd seemed to prefer _____ to any attempt at producing a melody; a more unpleasant voice was hard to imagine.","key":"DF","opts":["warbling","imitating","improvising","shrieking","crooning","caterwauling"],"expl":"此人的声音“尖叫”（shrieking）或“嚎叫”（caterwauling）。选 DF"},{"id":"v22.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even if the story now seems a surprisingly innocuous overture to the author’s later, more fully developed narrations, it _____ some of the key traits of those bleaker tales.","key":"DF","opts":["avoids","belies","undercuts","anticipates","possesses","prefigures"],"expl":"这个故事“预示”（anticipates/prefigures）了作者后来的黑暗风格。选 DF"},{"id":"v22.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While recognizing that recent reports of cyber warfare, phone-hacking scandals, and identity thefts have tended to accent the destructive connotation of the word, Sue Halpern maintains that “hacking” is such _____ term that its meaning nearly always derives from its context.","key":"AB","opts":["a generic","an inclusive","a positive","a subjective","an affirmative","a technical"],"expl":"“hacking”是一个“通用的”（generic）术语，其含义取决于语境。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v23-1","title":"Test 23 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v23.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The paleontologist examined the problem afresh, believing that the accepted classification _____ the essential continuity of the specimens by making specious distinctions among them.","key":"C","opts":["disproved","belied","conflated","divulged","relaxed"],"expl":"分类“掩盖”（conflated/belied）了标本的连续性。选 C"},{"id":"v23.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Among wide-ranging animal species, populations at the edge of the species’ range are frequently exposed to less (i)_____ and more variable conditions than those in other parts on the range. As a result, the animal’s abundance is often (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["erratic","favorable","demanding"],["lower at the periphery","unafef cted by habitat","underestimated by researchers"]],"expl":"空1 填 erratic（不稳定的）；空2 填 lower at the periphery（边缘处较低）。选 BD"},{"id":"v23.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When a new scientific model emerges, research studies (i)_____ that paradigm tend to dominate in the scientific literature: the process of selecting articles for publication is tilted towards positive results. But once the paradigm (ii)_____, the academic incentives shift in the opposite direction: research results are more considered worthy publication when they (iii)_____ what has become the established view.","key":"BEI","groups":[["tweaking","affirming","controverting"],["is initially articulated","has become entrenched","is about to be attacked"],["bolster","circumvent","undermine"]],"expl":"空1 填 affirming（肯定）；空2 填 has become entrenched（已根深蒂固）；空3 填 undermine（削弱）。选 BEI"},{"id":"v23.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"When studying the ancient Greek astronomers, Copernicus realized that despite the intrinsic beauty of many of their arguments, the ancients often made claims that _____ logic.","key":"EF","opts":["refuted","questioned","influenced","swayed","defied","disregarded"],"expl":"古代天文学家的论述“违背”（defied）逻辑。选 EF"},{"id":"v23.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although Wynne claims to recognize that _____ evidence is available to make definitive statement, she offers them nonetheless, arriving at some sweeping generalizations.","key":"CF","opts":["concrete","finite","insufficient","indirect","conclusive","meager"],"expl":"“可靠证据”（conclusive/definitive）不足，却仍作出概括。选 CF"},{"id":"v23.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In order to cultivate new repertoire, the music industry is providing a hearing for previously _____ composers.","key":"EF","opts":["idle","thwarted","celebrated","renowned","anonymous","obscure"],"expl":"作曲家“不为人知”（obscure）或“无名的”（anonymous）。选 EF"},{"id":"v23.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although many skeptics of the scientific theory _____ critiques that have long since been disproved, some of the doubters arguably bring up valid points.","key":"CF","opts":["overlook","revise","recycle","utilize","neglect","rehash"],"expl":"怀疑者“重复”（recycle/rehash）了早已被驳斥的批评。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v23-2","title":"Test 23 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v23.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The era’s examples of _____ that are cited by the author can be balanced in part by certain examples of dissent during the same period.","key":"B","opts":["diversity","authoritarianism","forbearance","volatility","lucidity"],"expl":"“专制主义”（authoritarianism）是例子。选 B"},{"id":"v23.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Historian Barbara Alpern Engel’s task in writing a book about women in Russia must have been a (i)_____ one, because the (ii)_____ the Russian empire’s peoples meant that Russian women could never be treated as a homogeneous group.","key":"CF","groups":[["motivating","boring","daunting"],["unity among","disinterest in","diversity of"]],"expl":"空1 填 daunting（艰巨的）；空2 填 diversity of（多样性）。选 CF"},{"id":"v23.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The material covered in this article has been (i)_____ in previous publications, and since currently neglected areas remained unexplored, the article contains no (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["skirted","scrutinized","countered"],["revelations","distortions","conclusions"]],"expl":"空1 填 skirted（回避）；空2 填 revelations（新发现）。选 BD"},{"id":"v23.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The historian of ancient science Otto Neugebauer concluded that Babylonian astronomical texts are (i)_____ because everything has been eliminated from the astronomy except observations and the mathematical consequences of an initial hypothesis about the fundamental character of the astronomical movements. This judgment cohered with the high level of mathematical theory, which (ii)_____ mathematical computation together with empirical observations as (iii)_____ of science and denied any role to speculative hypotheses of a strongly theoretical nature.","key":"BEH","groups":[["questionable","scientific","limited"],["repudiated","admitted","confounded"],["end result","necessary characteristics","discredited path"]],"expl":"空1 填 limited（有限的）；空2 填 repudiated（否定）；空3 填 necessary characteristics（必要的特征）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v23.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In a number of instances, investors hoping to tap into the region’s meteoric growth have instead faced problems ranging from unpredictable management practices to outright _____.","key":"AC","opts":["malfeasance","incompetence","fraudulence","capriciousness","hysteria","impulsiveness"],"expl":"投资者遇到的困难包括“舞弊”（malfeasance）与“欺诈”（fraudulence）。选 AC"},{"id":"v23.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To call Kermode the finest English critic of his generation would be a _____ compliment, since not many of its population are professionally engaged in literary criticism.","key":"CE","opts":["sincere","backhanded","paltry","heartfelt","meager","plausible"],"expl":"“最好的英国评论家”听起来是赞美，但在人口很少从事文学批评的地方，这样的称赞其实“很有限”（meager/paltry 的含义）。选 CE"},{"id":"v23.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even though the original settlement may not hold up, it at least proves that the deadlock can be broken and that a hitherto _____ party is ready to bargain.","key":"AB","opts":["implacable","unyielding","impeccable","flawless","unqualified","capricious"],"expl":"以前“不肯让步”（implacable/unyielding）的一方现在愿意谈判，所以最初是“不肯让步的”。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v24-1","title":"Test 24 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v24.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It seems foolish to refuse the offer of an expedient that is both so _____ success and so difficult to create them absent.","key":"D","opts":["reminiscent of","lacking in","distinct from","indispensable to","inimical to"],"expl":"这个方案对成功“不可或缺”（indispensable），所以不应当拒绝。选 D"},{"id":"v24.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the political science professor’s paper is quite (i)_____ about the government’s problem, suggesting that they are part of (ii)_____ a process, the prognosis for the government is, on the contrary, actually quite auspicious.","key":"CD","groups":[["straightforward","circuitous","pessimistic"],["degenerative","comprehensive","spontaneous"]],"expl":"空1 pessimistic 之外：论文说政府的问题“很曲折”（circuitous）；空2 “堕落式的”（degenerative）过程。选 CD"},{"id":"v24.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The notion of film producers as the ogres of the movie business has proved an (i)_____ one, but according to The Producers by Tim Adler, it is not always grounded in reality. Attacking what he calls the “auteur myth”—the idea of the director as the single purveyor of art in an industry otherwise peopled with (ii)_____—he places at the heart of his book an image of the producer, not the director, as the primary (iii)_____ force in the development and production of a movie.","key":"CEI","groups":[["accurate","hypocritic","enduring"],["visionaries","proftimongers","innocents"],["financial","inertial","creative"]],"expl":"空1 “持久的”（enduring）神话；空2 “天真的人”（innocents）；空3 “财务上的”推动力（financial）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v24.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In sharp contrast to the novel’s scenic realism and precisely characterized figure is its persistent philosophical _____.","key":"BC","opts":["naturalism","abstraction","generality","impartiality","sincerity","objectivity"],"expl":"哲学上的“抽象”（abstraction）与“普遍性”（generality）是对具体现实主义的对照。选 BC"},{"id":"v24.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Her attempts to wrest fiction free from traditional constraints like plot and character were never entirely popular with readers; nonetheless, her fiction has had _____ influence on critical theory, novel, cinema, and even psychology.","key":"CD","opts":["a studied","a negligible","a decisive","an unmistakable","an insignificant","a restorative"],"expl":"她的小说的影响“决定性的”（decisive）或“不可否认的”（unmistakable）。选 CD"},{"id":"v24.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The physics graveyard is strewn with the skeletons of failed theories, unexplained effects, and anomalous particles that briefly _____ the research spotlight, then rapidly fade from view.","key":"DF","opts":["douse","intensify","perpetuate","capture","extinguish","secure"],"expl":"失败的理论“短暂地吸引”（capture）研究的聚光灯，之后迅速消失。选 DF"},{"id":"v24.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The media have constantly disparaged the governor’s competence and have found a public only too eager to applaud their _____.","key":"CF","opts":["assiduousness","stupefaction","mockery","incredulity","certitude","derision"],"expl":"媒体对州长的“嘲笑”（mockery/derision）获得了公众的认同。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v24-2","title":"Test 24 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v24.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"With the numerous opponents of the controversial new taxation measure in such a fury, anyone who publicly advocated the measure did not fail to meet with _____ usage.","key":"B","opts":["politic","severe","sober","respectful","dejected"],"expl":"反对者情绪激烈，所以支持者遭到“严厉的”（severe）对待。选 B"},{"id":"v24.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the vast weight of evidence supports the contention that the products of agricultural biotechnology are environmentally (i)_____, many people still find them (ii)_____ unsettling.","key":"BF","groups":[["destructive","sound","intriguing"],["retroactively","innocuously","intrinsically"]],"expl":"空1 “无害的”（sound）；空2 “本质上地”（intrinsically）令人不安。选 BF"},{"id":"v24.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)_____ nature of the candidate’s comments is calculated. As a long-standing target of critics who regard him as radical, he understands that he needs to be as (ii)_____ as possible if he is to overcome those critiques and appear as a (iii)_____ leader.","key":"BDI","groups":[["opprobrious","platitudinous","pugnacious"],["innocuous","truculent","supercilious"],["polarizing","cautious","conciliatory"]],"expl":"候选人的言论“煽动性的”（polarizing/provocative）是有计算的；他想显得“温和”（conciliatory）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v24.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The new art museum’s (i)_____ building augurs well for that ambitious institution because it speaks of (ii)_____ contemporary architecture on the part of the board of directors that may (iii)_____ equal astuteness about contemporary art.","key":"BDI","groups":[["nondescript","outstanding","outdated"],["a discernment about","a hostility toward","an intoxication by"],["conceal","supplant","promise"]],"expl":"空1 “杰出的”（outstanding）建筑；空2 “对当代建筑的鉴赏力”（discernment about）；空3 “保证”（promise）对当代艺术有同样的判断力。选 BDI"},{"id":"v24.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Science is arguably a very high-minded pursuit, but that is not to say that all of its practitioners are _____, as numerous articles alleging overly generous pharmaceutical industry payments to medical researchers have tried to show.","key":"CE","opts":["conventional","clever","unimpeachable","ingenious","blameless","predictable"],"expl":"科学家“无可指摘”（unimpeachable），即使有些人被指控收受好处，也不意味着所有人都有问题。选 CE"},{"id":"v24.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The town’s air was consistently _____: depending on the breeze, one might be greeted with the sour effluvia of twenty breweries, choking fumes from the coal factory, or brackish smells from the nearby river.","key":"AE","opts":["malodorous","toxic","redolent","benign","noisome","anodyne"],"expl":"小镇的空气“臭味难闻”（malodorous/noisome）。选 AE"},{"id":"v24.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the vocalists who auditioned for a leading part in the local production of Sweeney Todd seemed to prefer _____ to any attempt at producing a melody; a more unpleasant voice was hard to imagine.","key":"DF","opts":["warbling","imitating","improvising","shrieking","crooning","caterwauling"],"expl":"此人的声音“尖叫”（shrieking）或“嚎叫”（caterwauling）。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v25-1","title":"Test 25 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v25.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"She constantly _____ herself for not living up to her own ideas—for not working hard enough or not having motives that were pure enough.","key":"C","opts":["exalted","coddled","excoriated","mollified","deluded"],"expl":"她“严厉地责备”（excoriated）自己。选 C"},{"id":"v25.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author argued that the field of sociology has been overly (i)_____, partly because, for many scholars, the edges of social universe are defined by national borders. In this era of increasing globalization, however, sociology is presented with a historically distinct opportunity to transcend its former (ii)_____.","key":"AE","groups":[["narrow in scope","susceptible to fads","averse to empiricism"],["utilitarianism","parochialism","historicism"]],"expl":"空1 社会学“范围狭窄”（narrow in scope）；空2 “地方主义”（parochialism）。选 AE"},{"id":"v25.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The modern iron suspension bridge dates from the early nineteenth century, but it did not have (i)_____ debut; many early suspension bridges were damaged, if not outright destroyed, by the wind. There were few (ii)_____, however, so the form (iii)_____.","key":"AEI","groups":[["a propitious","a conspicuous","an equivocal"],["obvious parallels","practical alternatives","unnoticed instances"],["declined","inspired","persisted"]],"expl":"空1 “吉利的”（propitious）开端：没有好的首秀；空2 “明显的例子”（obvious parallels）；空3 “持续下去”（persisted）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v25.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some experts estimate that the recreational salmon fishery in British Columbia contributes more to the province’s economy than the commercial salmon fishery does—a surprising statistic given the political commercial _____ of the fishery in the province.","key":"BE","opts":["naïveté","prominence","supremacy","ingenuousness","salience","resurgence"],"expl":"政治上“显著的”（prominence/salience）地位。选 BE"},{"id":"v25.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In 1884, Sewall and Dow agreed to join Roosevelt in the Dakota territory for reasons that appear to have been _____: Sewell later recalled that Roosevelt guaranteed them a share of anything made in his cattle business.","key":"AC","opts":["pecuniary","straightforward","economic","selfless","quixotic","altruistic"],"expl":"这个理由“金钱上的”（pecuniary）。选 AC"},{"id":"v25.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because movie studios, under pressure to generate international sales, have favored big-budget pictures with fantasy plots, the representation of everyday domestic life has largely been _____ other media, such as television and literature.","key":"AB","opts":["left to","ceded to","ascribed to","attributed to","substituted for","replaced with"],"expl":"家庭生活的表现在其他媒介中“被交给”（ceded to）或“被交付”（left to）。选 AB"},{"id":"v25.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In order to cultivate new repertoire, the music industry is providing a hearing for previously _____ composers.","key":"EF","opts":["idle","thwarted","celebrated","renowned","anonymous","obscure"],"expl":"“被忽视的”（obscure/anonymous）作曲家。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v25-2","title":"Test 25 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v25.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In his youth, the naturalist and artist John James Audubon was given to _____ glamorous tales about himself: he falsely claimed to have studied under a renowned French painter and hinted that he was the heir apparent to the French throne.","key":"E","opts":["disavowing","understanding","constraining","obfuscating","concocting"],"expl":"他“编造”（concocting）了迷人的故事。选 E"},{"id":"v25.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Holston characterized a colonial situation as an aggregation of activities and a conjunction of outcomes that, though _____ and at times coordinated, were usually diffuse, disorganized, and even contradictory.","key":"D","opts":["dubious","chaotic","harmonious","linked","imputed"],"expl":"殖民地的活动“联系在一起”（linked）却常常混乱。选 D"},{"id":"v25.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author of this travel guide (i)_____ to show his readers Cairo as it really is, but his information is not reliable: for example, his geography is (ii)_____, with one walking tour covering areas of the city that are twenty miles apart.","key":"CD","groups":[["designs","forbears","purports"],["erratic","erudite","extensive"]],"expl":"空1 “声称”（purports）要展示开罗的真实面貌；空2 地理“混乱的”（erratic）。选 CD"},{"id":"v25.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The characters in this comic strip fret about the (i)_____ of their “little counterculture lives”, especially when terrible things are happening in the world, but the cartoonist makes their lives (ii)_____ in ways that do not seem (iii)_____ at all. Real things happen here—births, deaths, adoptions, affairs, breakups, commitments, ceremonies, civil union—and they matter.","key":"CEH","groups":[["unpredictability","arduousness","triviality"],["stagnate","resonate","compete"],["outlandish","inconsequential","intangible"]],"expl":"空1 “琐碎”（triviality）；空2 “共鸣”（resonate）；空3 “无关紧要的”（inconsequential）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v25.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It’s hardly _____ the committee calls for: rudimentary competence would be an improvement on the current chaos.","key":"DF","opts":["accountability","disarray","unruliness","faultlessness","loyalty","perfection"],"expl":"委员会要求的不是“完美”（perfection），只是基本的能力。选 DF"},{"id":"v25.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Contrary to certain recent analyses that paint a dire portrait of soil loss from farmland, a new study of surveying data reaching back to the 1930s shows that erosion rates have been steadily _____.","key":"BE","opts":["intensifying","waning","accelerating","worsening","declining","deteriorating"],"expl":"侵蚀率一直在“下降”（waning/declining）。选 BE"},{"id":"v25.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Communicating articulately is typically regarded as an aggressive, persuasive talent, but it can also be protective: it allows a certain _____ closeness, conveying proximity while actually maintaining distance.","key":"AE","opts":["feigned","secretive","dubious","subtle","false","furtive"],"expl":"这种亲密感是“伪装的”（feigned）或“虚假的”（false）。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v26-1","title":"Test 26 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v26.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The space travels described in science fiction stories always used to be epic adventures, in comparison to which current journals in space seem quite _____.","key":"A","opts":["mundane","exciting","dramatic","risky","heroic"],"expl":"与科幻的史诗相比，现在的太空旅行显得“平凡”（mundane）。选 A"},{"id":"v26.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The school system’s modest plan for curriculum improvements has (i)_____ local educators: some call it (ii)_____ effort, while others say it is a pragmatic approach given the complexity of the task.","key":"CE","groups":[["surprised","impressed","divided"],["genuine","halfhearted","practical"]],"expl":"空1 “分化”（divided）地方教育者；空2 “敷衍的”（halfhearted）努力。选 CE"},{"id":"v26.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A certain amount of theoretical frenzy about comics today is (i)_____. After all, similar frenzies have been in other art forms in periods of their rapid development, for instance, the debates about painting that roiled Renaissance Italy. But such intellectual (ii)_____ rarely precedes creative glory. On the contrary, it commonly indicates that an artistic (iii)_____, having been made and recognized, is over, and that a process of increasing strained emulation and diminishing returns has set in.","key":"AFI","groups":[["understandable","unprecedented","perplexing"],["torpor","conservatism","arousal"],["pitfall","tradition","breakthrough"]],"expl":"空1 “可以理解的”（understandable）；空2 “冷漠”（torpor）或“保守”（conservatism）；空3 “传统”（tradition）已经终结。选 AFI"},{"id":"v26.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Chavez Pass archaeological site was initially interpreted as indicative of _____ society, since it was thought to have been at the center of a cluster of smaller, contemporary settlements that it presumably controlled.","key":"BF","opts":["an expansionist","a hierarchical","an urban","a heterogeneous","a diverse","a stratified"],"expl":"社会被认为是“等级制的”（hierarchical/stratified）。选 BF"},{"id":"v26.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the essayist’s arguments did not _____ her most perceptive readers, the extreme subtlety of the paints she made explains why she was misinterpreted by most critics of her day.","key":"BE","opts":["convince","confound","entertain","persuade","perplex","enlighten"],"expl":"作者的论证“没有使她最敏锐的读者信服”（convince/persuade），颜料的极微妙使人误解。选 BE"},{"id":"v26.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Architects may be more extroverted and therefore the more _____ members of a bridge design team, but they are not always the most essential.","key":"DF","opts":["indispensable","conscientious","reliable","visible","valuable","salient"],"expl":"建筑师更“显眼”（visible/salient）。选 DF"},{"id":"v26.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Citing the corruption and intrigue that pervaded politics in the city, my colleague _____ the newspaper’s trove of journalism prizes, declaring that finding great stories in the city must be effortless.","key":"AD","opts":["slighted","ignored","lauded","disparaged","confounded","commended"],"expl":"同事“赞扬”（lauded/commended）报纸的新闻奖项。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v26-2","title":"Test 26 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v26.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Medieval cathedrals still stand as marvels of architecture, but as far as modern science is concerned, medieval physics and chemistry are simply irrelevant, at best a dead end, at worst the very _____ of what science is supposed to be.","key":"E","opts":["exemplar","glorification","reflection","dilution","antithesis"],"expl":"中世纪的物理学与现代科学“恰恰相反”（antithesis）。选 E"},{"id":"v26.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author of this political history text shows considerable bias against the political party when assigning credit or blame for its actions: he deems (i)_____ what he favors and avoids what he (ii)_____.","key":"AF","groups":[["pertinent","inevitable","divided"],["condemns","condones","ignores"]],"expl":"空1 作者认为与自己立场相关的事情“相关的”（pertinent）；空2 “宽恕”（condones）他支持的，“忽视”（ignores）他不喜欢的。选 AF"},{"id":"v26.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It would be naïve to treat remarks made in diaries or personal letters as giving especially candid access to historical truth or even as being expressions of the writer’s true state of mind, since the (i)_____ for exaggeration and deception in those forms is virtually nonexistent. Diaries and letters are rarely sites for (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["motivation","penalty","tendency"],["premeditated manipulation","childish theatrics","balanced reflection"]],"expl":"空1 日记中“造假的动机”（motivation）很少；空2 “精心策划的操纵”（premeditated manipulation）。选 BD"},{"id":"v26.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Applications of the Endangered Species Act (ESA) have fared best in contexts in which habitat condition is closely linked to species condition and the cause of habitat degradation is easily identified. The achievements of the ESA in those contexts, however, have (i)_____ that other uses of the act can (ii)_____ that record even where such favorable conditions do not (iii)_____.","key":"CEH","groups":[["quelled the conviction","presaged the uncertainty","fostered the misconception"],["mitigate","duplicate","elucidate"],["vary","pertain","diminish"]],"expl":"空1 “平息了”（quelled）对其他用途的信念；空2 “弥补”（mitigate）；空3 “减弱”（diminish）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v26.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"When studying the ancient Greek astronomers, Copernicus realized that despite the intrinsic beauty of many of their arguments, the ancients often made claims that _____ logic.","key":"EF","opts":["refuted","questioned","influenced","swayed","defied","disregarded"],"expl":"古希腊人常常“违背”（defied/disregarded）逻辑。选 EF"},{"id":"v26.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Films that critics have slumbered through rarely generate industry excitement, even though the critics’ _____ reception may be less the fault of the movie than of its unfortunate time slot near a fatiguing film festival’s conclusion.","key":"AC","opts":["somnolent","impartial","lethargic","laconic","befuddled","evenhanded"],"expl":"批评家的“冷漠”（lethargic/somnolent）反应。选 AC"},{"id":"v26.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even though his opponent is currently trying to portray him as a wild-eyed radical, voters will likely reject this charge because it does not _____ his moderate political record.","key":"BF","opts":["defer to","conform to","accede to","argue with","meddle with","square with"],"expl":"对手的指控“与他温和的政治记录不相符”（square with/conform to 的反义）。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v27-1","title":"Test 27 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v27.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Investors are grateful that the attorney general has stepped in to pursue inquiries into misfeasance in the financial markets, given that the regulators officially charged with policing the industry have been _____.","key":"A","opts":["diffident","meticulous","straightforward","implacable","tenacious"],"expl":"监管机构“不积极”（diffident），所以需要检察长介入。选 A"},{"id":"v27.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author paints a rather dark picture of book publishing as a hidebound industry, one that is facing a profound change in its mode of production but is so (i)_____ its past as to be (ii)_____ opportunity offered by technological changes.","key":"CE","groups":[["alienated from","emboldened by","encumbered by"],["eager to exploit","unable to seize","forced to reconsider"]],"expl":"空1 行业“被……束缚”（encumbered by）；空2 “无法抓住”（unable to seize）机会。选 CE"},{"id":"v27.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Scientific papers often (i)_____ what actually happened in the course of the investigations they describe. Misunderstandings, blind alleys, and mistakes of various sorts will fail to appear in the final written accounts because (ii)_____ is a desirable attribute when transmitting results in a scientific report and would be poorly served by (iii)_____.","key":"BEG","groups":[["amplify","misrepresent","particularize"],["transparency","efficiency","exhaustiveness"],["a comprehensive historical account","a purely quantitative analysis","an overly superficial discussion"]],"expl":"空1 论文“歪曲”（misrepresent）实际过程；空2 “透明”（transparency）是理想；空3 不宜用“详尽的历史叙述”（a comprehensive historical account）替代。选 BEG"},{"id":"v27.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In noting that critical and popular opinions about Li’s art coincided, Chuang _____ the existence of an exception to her general theory of art criticism, which posits that critics’ views do not intersect with those of the general public.","key":"BC","opts":["asserted","conceded","acknowledged","doubted","pondered","questioned"],"expl":"Chuang 承认了这个例外（conceded/acknowledged）。选 BC"},{"id":"v27.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Excessive focus on what might have been can cause in us feelings of restlessness and regret, but some scientists are beginning to think that fancying an alternative reality might have _____ effects as well.","key":"CF","opts":["subtle","adverse","restorative","pleasurable","unfavorable","tonic"],"expl":"另一种现实可能有“有益的”（restorative/tonic）效果。选 CF"},{"id":"v27.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As a historical genre, biography is best when _____, a careful reconstruction of the past in all its unfamiliar particularity.","key":"EF","opts":["introspective","reflective","concrete","concise","meticulous","thorough"],"expl":"传记最好是“具体的”（concrete）且“彻底的”（thorough）重构过去。选 EF"},{"id":"v27.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Explorers could not build each other’s knowledge if they could not trust records of previous explorers; thus exploration depended on the _____ of those who had gone before.","key":"CD","opts":["collegiality","endurance","exactitude","meticulousness","eminence","tenacity"],"expl":"探险者的“仔细”（exactitude/meticulousness）是知识积累的基础。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v27-2","title":"Test 27 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v27.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Consolidating memory is not instantaneous or even _____: every memory must be encoded and moved from short-term to long-term storage, and some of these memories are, for whatever reason, more vividly imprinted than others.","key":"D","opts":["salutary","deliberate","sequential","momentary","inevitable"],"expl":"记忆的巩固“并非瞬时的”，但“即时的”（momentary）说法是需要排除的。选 D"},{"id":"v27.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Recent scholarship has questioned the (i)_____ of tropical forests around the world. Archaeologists have shown, for example, that the largest contiguous tract of what was thought to be virgin rain forest in the southern Amazon had been transformed into a cultural parkland before European contact, and many of the forest islands in West Africa’s savanna forest transition zone are (ii)_____ as well.","key":"BF","groups":[["diversity","naturalness","sustainability"],["isolated","endangered","anthropogenic"]],"expl":"空1 森林的“自然性”（naturalness）受到质疑；空2 森林岛屿是“人为的”（anthropogenic）。选 BF"},{"id":"v27.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Even the reader acquainted with the outlines of Pushkin’s biography will be (i)_____ the (ii)_____ so vividly conveyed in Binyon’s biography. Not only was Pushkin’s personal correspondence intercepted and his movements (iii)_____, but Tsar Nicholas I’s decision to oversee Pushkin’s career obliged Pushkin to submit all his manuscripts for inspection.","key":"CDH","groups":[["attracted by","confused by","struck by"],["suffocating lack of creative freedom","concern for contemporary society","underlying sense of historical change"],["ignored","monitored","commended"]],"expl":"空1 “被……震撼”（struck by）；空2 “令人窒息的缺乏创作自由”；空3 “被监视”（monitored）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v27.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Viewing people as ‘’social atoms’’ that obey rather simple rule (which are not unlike the laws of physics), one may discover certain (i)_____. Take, for example, the way channels emerge when people move in crowds. In the midst of initially (ii)_____ movements, one person begins to follow another—in an effort to avoid collisions—and streams of movement emerge. As more people join in, there is greater pull on others to join the flow, and the particular channels become (iii)_____.","key":"CFI","groups":[["apparent contradictions","unproductive tendencies","lawlike regulations"],["inflexible","straightforward","chaotic"],["self-defeating","self-aggrandizing","self-perpetuating"]],"expl":"空1 “规律性的”（lawlike）规则；空2 “混乱的”（chaotic）移动；空3 “自我维持的”（self-perpetuating）通道。选 CFI"},{"id":"v27.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The _____ nature of the approval process for new drugs suggests that incentives to promote more expeditious decision making may be necessary.","key":"DF","opts":["pecuniary","commercial","arbitrary","sluggish","capricious","dilatory"],"expl":"审批流程的“迟缓”（sluggish/dilatory）说明需要激励。选 DF"},{"id":"v27.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The critic claims that, contrary to its reputation for _____, the novelist’s prose is full of opaque language games.","key":"BD","opts":["scrupulousness","simplicity","mendacity","artlessness","polish","meticulousness"],"expl":"作家以“朴素”（simplicity/artlessness）著称，但文字却晦涩。选 BD"},{"id":"v27.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Not only is the advent of bookless or largely bookless libraries too large and powerful a change to be _____, it also offers too many real advantages for it to be considered a tragedy.","key":"BD","opts":["understood","averted","foreseen","forestalled","endured","anticipated"],"expl":"大图书馆的变化既不能“避免”（averted/forestalled），也不必被视为悲剧。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v28-1","title":"Test 28 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v28.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Instead of demonstrating the _____ of archaeological applications of electronic remote sensing, the pioneering study became, to some skeptics, an illustration of the imprudence of interpreting sites based on virtual archaeology.","key":"C","opts":["ubiquity","limitation","promise","redundancy","complexity"],"expl":"研究的“潜力”（promise）反而成了怀疑的例子。选 C"},{"id":"v28.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"A (i)_____ to disseminate the vast scientific knowledge of our time to nonscientists shows real (ii)_____ the magnificent achievement humanity is capable of, like allowing a great work of art to molder in a warehouse.","key":"BD","groups":[["triumph","failure","diffusion"],["indifference to","enthusiasm for","glory of"]],"expl":"空1 “失败”（failure）地传播知识；空2 “对……缺乏热情”（indifference to）。选 BD"},{"id":"v28.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Fifty pages of footnotes, some of them presenting quite lengthy bibliographies, suggest that very few pertinent sources on the Black Arts movement in literature have (i)_____ Thompson’s search; (ii)_____, the text makes it clear that the author’s examination of these sources has been similarly (iii)_____.","key":"ADI","groups":[["eluded","characterized","motivated"],["moreover","however","consequently"],["valuable","timely","exhaustive"]],"expl":"空1 “未能逃过”（eluded）Thompson 的搜索；空2 “然而”（however）；空3 “详尽的”（exhaustive）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v28.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Her attempts to wrest fiction free from traditional constraints like plot and character were never entirely popular with readers; nonetheless, her fiction has had _____ influence on critical theory, novel, cinema, and even psychology.","key":"CD","opts":["a studied","a negligible","a decisive","an unmistakable","an insignificant","a restorative"],"expl":"她的小说对批评理论有“决定性”（decisive）的影响。选 CD"},{"id":"v28.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Shifting Fortunes take a conventional approach to American union history by simply explaining the reasons behind union growth and decline in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries: it is a chronologically and thematically _____ study and nothing more.","key":"BE","opts":["complicated","confined","multifarious","onerous","circumscribed","taxing"],"expl":"这项研究“局限于”（confined/circumscribed）年代与主题，别无其他。选 BE"},{"id":"v28.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A clever form of diplomacy involves subtly inducing the other party to propose your preference so that your _____ their requests appears as the granting of concession.","key":"AF","opts":["accession to","inattention to","subversion of","abnegation of","repudiation of","acquiescence to"],"expl":"你的请求被“接受”（acquiescence to）对方提出的偏好，看似是让步。选 AF"},{"id":"v28.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientist reported last month on a sign of relative solar _____; the solar wind, a rush of charged particles continually spewed from the Sun at a million miles an hour, had diminished to its lowest level in 50 years.","key":"AD","opts":["quiescence","turbulence","isolation","calm","remoteness","instability"],"expl":"太阳活动的“平静”（quiescence/calm）。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v28-2","title":"Test 28 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v28.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While the writer was best known for her much-ballyhooed _____, her impact reached far beyond memorable quips.","key":"B","opts":["pensiveness","drollness","stoicism","fastidiousness","congeniality"],"expl":"她以“机智幽默”（drollness）著称。选 B"},{"id":"v28.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The governor might conceivably find a genuine resolution to the budgetary dilemma, but she may be tempted to engage in a deception: a _____ exercise in fiscal prudence.","key":"C","opts":["rigorous","sparking","specious","blatant","convincing"],"expl":"这种财政上的审慎是“似是而非的”（specious）。选 C"},{"id":"v28.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In her works, she (i)_____ confidence. She gets excessively (ii)_____ to authorities, even when rejecting their views.","key":"CE","groups":[["inspires","exudes","lacks"],["pugnacious","deferential","condescending"]],"expl":"空1 她“表现出”（exudes）信心；空2 对权威“顺从”（deferential）。选 CE"},{"id":"v28.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unquestionably, the particular forms that folly and cruelty take in Jane Austen’s novels are (i)_____ the character’s social milieu, which was also Austen’s own; but to realize that one’s society motivates people in unfortunate ways is not necessarily to (ii)_____ it, for the alternatives, though different, might be no more (iii)_____.","key":"AEG","groups":[["shaped by","removed from","unrecognizable in"],["expose","condemn","rationalize"],["salutary","corrosive","realistic"]],"expl":"空1 “塑造于”（shaped by）社会环境；空2 “不一定要谴责”（condemn）；空3 “同样有益的”（salutary）。选 AEG"},{"id":"v28.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author takes issue with the ideological blinders that have distorted much migration research, especially ____ modernization theorists and others for their untested assumptions of an immobile preindustrial past.","key":"CD","opts":["undermining","citing","castigating","chastising","endorsing","commending"],"expl":"作者“谴责”（castigating/chastising）现代化理论家。选 CD"},{"id":"v28.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While normal floods resulting from usual monsoon rainfall are _____ the growth of crops, recently there has been an increase in the frequency of high-intensity floods that do not have such welcome effects.","key":"EF","opts":["conducive to","hindered by","devastating for","deleterious for","essential for","indispensable to"],"expl":"常见的洪水“有利于”（conducive to）作物生长。选 EF"},{"id":"v28.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The difficulty of reforming electoral politics is not lack of the right tools but the need to put them into the hands of impartial agents: the goal should be to build capacity while _____ partisanship.","key":"BD","opts":["expediting","constraining","facilitating","deterring","exacerbating","lamenting"],"expl":"改革应“遏制”（constraining/deterring）党派偏见。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v29-1","title":"Test 29 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v29.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Without seeming unworldly, William James appeared wholly removed from the _____ of society, the conventionality of academy.","key":"E","opts":["ethos","idealism","romance","paradoxes","commonplaces"],"expl":"威廉·詹姆斯“远离”（removed from）社会的“平庸”（commonplaces）。选 E"},{"id":"v29.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The trade in scientific literature in nineteenth-century Germany was so robust that publisher constantly worried about (i)_____ of new titles, an anxiety that gave even relatively undistinguished authors, who made their living writing technical treatises, (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["prices","supplies","embargoes"],["limited public relevance","enviable scholarly credentials","strong bargaining positions"]],"expl":"空1 出版商担心“供应”（supplies）；空2 作者们拥有“有利的学术资历”。选 BF"},{"id":"v29.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"While some commentators suggest that abstraction and complexity in scientific research are signs that a given direction is misguided, Lisa Randall, a professor of physics at Harvard, counters that these qualities instead reflect the success of human ingenuity in (i)_____ the increasingly (ii)_____ challenges that nature presents. They can, however, make it more (iii)_____ to communicate scientific developments, even to colleague.","key":"BDG","groups":[["creating","meeting","eschewing"],["difficult","conspicuous","pragmatic"],["challenging","unproductive","advantageous"]],"expl":"空1 “应对”（meeting）挑战；空2 “困难的”（difficult）；空3 “具有挑战性的”（challenging）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v29.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"That guild of experts has always appraised the economic stimulation plan as bootless, while the advocates of the policy do not take their _____ evaluation for granted.","key":"CF","opts":["tendentious","meticulous","detracting","indifferent","ubiquitous","deprecatory"],"expl":"专家的评价是“贬低的”（detracting/deprecatory）。选 CF"},{"id":"v29.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In noting that critical and popular opinions about Li’s art coincided, Chuang _____ the existence of an exception to her general theory of art criticism, which posits that critics’ views do not intersect with those of the general public.","key":"BC","opts":["asserted","conceded","acknowledged","doubted","pondered","questioned"],"expl":"Chuang 承认了这个例外（acknowledged/conceded）。选 BC"},{"id":"v29.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ambassador’s critical remarks seemed to be less a product of _____ and more the careless utterances of a fatigued or undisciplined individual.","key":"CD","opts":["intensity","optimism","purposefulness","design","confidence","caution"],"expl":"大使的言论不是出于“有目的的”设计（design/purposefulness），而是随意的失言。选 CD"},{"id":"v29.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In sharp contrast to the novel’s scenic realism and precisely characterized figure is its persistent philosophical _____.","key":"BC","opts":["naturalism","abstraction","generality","impartiality","sincerity","objectivity"],"expl":"这部小说的哲学性是“抽象”（abstraction）的。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v29-2","title":"Test 29 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v29.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The idea of a “language instinct” may seem _____ to those who think of language as the zenith of the human intellect and of instincts as brute impulses.","key":"A","opts":["jarring","plausible","gratifying","inevitable","conciliatory"],"expl":"“语言本能”说法对许多人来说“刺耳”（jarring）。选 A"},{"id":"v29.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The artist is known for making photographs that deal with politically charged subject matter, yet because her art is so evocative and open-ended, it would be wrong to characterize it as _____.","key":"A","opts":["polemical","edifying","unobservant","innovative","ambiguous"],"expl":"作品“开放、含蓄”，因此不能说它“直白地宣传”或“简单地论战”，而是“模棱两可的”（ambiguous）。选 A"},{"id":"v29.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The documentation of Earth’s biodiversity is complicated by the (i)_____ taxonomists. Those experts in classifying species tent to be (ii)_____ North American and Europe, whereas most of the undocumented biodiversity is likely in the tropics.","key":"AD","groups":[["uneven distribution of","theoretical commitments of","professional rivalries among"],["clustered in","oblivious to","exported from"]],"expl":"分类学家的分布“不均”（uneven）；他们往往“集中于”（clustered in）北美和欧洲。选 AD"},{"id":"v29.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"A transformative scientific idea that emerged in the eighteenth century was the realization that slow, inexorable geological processes follow the basic laws of physics and chemistry. This seems (i)_____ conclusion in hindsight, but its implication—that geological processes in the distant past must have (ii)_____ these very same laws—was (iii)_____ geologists in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries.","key":"ADI","groups":[["an obvious","a significant","a controversial"],["followed","preceded","entailed"],["evident to","overlooked by","revolutionary for"]],"expl":"结论看似“显而易见”（obvious）；其含义是过去的地质过程必须“遵循”（followed）同样的规律，而这在当时“并非显而易见”（overlooked by）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v29.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Individuals, governments, and companies show ample ability to _____ themselves by setting goals based on current conditions and then blindly following them even when those conditions change drastically.","key":"AE","opts":["hamstring","reinvent","promote","revitalize","impair","invigorate"],"expl":"人们会“束缚”（hamstring）或“损害”（impair）自己，因为盲目追随过时的目标。选 AE"},{"id":"v29.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The cat known to researchers as M-120—beefy, audacious, and apparently smart enough to spot a free lunch—is perhaps the world’s least _____ lynx: the scientists catch him several times a year.","key":"BE","opts":["intelligent","evasive","fearless","furtive","elusive","intrepid"],"expl":"M-120 是“最不容易躲避”（least elusive）的猞猁，因为科学家能多次抓到它。选 BE"},{"id":"v29.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Origin, distribution, and habitat are included in the book for some but not all of the plants; offering this information for each species would have given readers a clearer appreciation of the differences between _____ and introduced species.","key":"AB","opts":["endemic","native","seasonal","rare","unusual","dominant"],"expl":"本地（native）与引入（introduced）物种之间的差别。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v30-1","title":"Test 30 · Section 1","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v30.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The medical professor’s thesis—hardly new, but rarely _____ by a faculty members of his distinction—is that patients are more than the sum of their symptoms and systems.","key":"E","opts":["discounted","ignored","subverted","underestimated","espoused"],"expl":"这位教授的主张并不新颖，但很少有人如此有名望地“主张”（espoused）它。选 E"},{"id":"v30.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Invention was (i)_____ the work of the ancient Greek historians, whose writings were filled with long and often purely fictitious speeches by great historical figures. The animating force in historical writing was rhetoric rather than (ii)_____. Even well into the eighteenth century, not a few historians continued to understand themselves as artists, given a license to invent.","key":"BE","groups":[["discouraged in","a hallmark of","exceptional in"],["eloquence","evidence","imagination"]],"expl":"空1 “……的标志”（hallmark of）：历史写作的特征；空2 “证据”（evidence）是对比项。选 BE"},{"id":"v30.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is possible for human to go 40 or more hours without sleep and still be able to (i)_____ information acquired at the beginning of the sleepless period. Thus, when we are considering a role for sleep in human memory consolidation, we are referring to a possible role in the (ii)_____ encoding of information and optimizing of recall, not a (iii)_____ of sleep for recalling events of the prior day.","key":"CDG","groups":[["legitimize","augment","disgorge"],["longer-term","acute","qualitative"],["requirement","surplus","facet"]],"expl":"空1 “证实”（legitimize）记忆；空2 “长期的”（longer-term）编码；空3 “必需”（requirement）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v30.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some have argued that naming scientific discoveries after the people who make them can _____ scientific progress, because the nomenclature lacks useful clarity, having no relationship to the underlying principles that govern nature.","key":"AF","opts":["hamper","abet","instigate","obscure","nullify","impede"],"expl":"以人名命名的发现“阻碍”（hamper/impede）科学进步，因为它与原理无关。选 AF"},{"id":"v30.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Each of the country’s 26 sates and most of its more than 2,000 municipalities have their own police forces, _____ communication and making it difficult to establish a coordinated law-enforcement strategy.","key":"BC","opts":["establishing","impeding","hampering","launching","obscuring","preventing"],"expl":"各州的警察力量“妨碍”（impeding/hampering）通信与协调。选 BC"},{"id":"v30.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although there is an incredible diversity of microbes across the body of each individual, the fact that specific body sites tend to host a few specific bacteria indicates that the body’s microflora are not _____ distributed.","key":"AF","opts":["haphazardly","uniformly","effectively","heterogeneously","functionally","randomly"],"expl":"身体各部位的细菌“并非随机”（haphazardly/randomly）分布。选 AF"},{"id":"v30.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Changes made to ecosystems in order to achieve a goal, such as food production or flood control, often _____ significant unforeseen trade-offs between other important products and services the ecosystems provide.","key":"EF","opts":["predict","delay","foretell","obscure","yield","engender"],"expl":"生态系统的改造“产生”（engender）出未曾预见的权衡。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v30-2","title":"Test 30 · Section 2","group":"Test 21–30","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v30.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even if he wants to serve again—and given his obvious love for the job, the assumption among insiders is that he is more likely to stay than go—there is at least _____ his serving another term.","key":"A","opts":["impediment to","incentive for","precedent for","benefit in","rationale for"],"expl":"他很可能留任，但有“先例”（precedent）说明他是否会再任期还存在障碍（impediment）；这里。选 A"},{"id":"v30.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Folmer’s book on Edith Wharton seems far removed from recent trends in literary criticism; this need not to be a fault, except that, in its title and introduction, the book (i)_____ to be conversant with contemporary discourse in the field, but in its actual analysis of Wharton’s work, it is marked by a very (ii)_____ approach.","key":"CD","groups":[["designs","fails","purports"],["old-fashioned","timely","arcane"]],"expl":"空1 书“自称”（purports）很熟悉当代批评；空2 分析方法“陈旧的”（old-fashioned）。选 CD"},{"id":"v30.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The book is not comprehensive but is, instead, (i)_____ in the most positive sense:(ii)_____ rather than settles.","key":"BE","groups":[["definitive","provocative","timely"],["stipulates","suggests","disseminates"]],"expl":"空1 书是“引人思考的”（provocative）；空2 它“提示”（suggests）而不是“定论”。选 BE"},{"id":"v30.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Several studies (i)_____ the assumption that paper cups, because they were made of natural products, were more environmentally (ii)_____ than cups made of plastic (polystyrene). Indeed, these studies indicated that the environmental (iii)_____ of producing and recycling paper cups were similar to, if not more than, those related to the production, disposal, and recycling of polystyrene cups.","key":"CDH","groups":[["corroborated","exploited","dispelled"],["friendly","hazardous","predictable"],["benefits","costs","opportunities"]],"expl":"空1 “推翻”（dispelled）了假设；空2 纸杯“更环保”（friendly）；空3 环境“成本”（costs）相似。选 CDH"},{"id":"v30.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One big challenge with placebo responses is that they are _____: people given the same inert pill or potion may show wildly different reactions, and the effects can vary widely according to each person’s illness.","key":"AC","opts":["capricious","illusory","unpredictable","chimerical","marginal","ephemeral"],"expl":"安慰剂反应“变化无常”（capricious/unpredictable）。选 AC"},{"id":"v30.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Chicago journal known as Poetry has been the launching pad for many poets since its _____ in 1913; among them, T. S. Eliot, Gwendolyn Brooks, and John Ashbery.","key":"BF","opts":["extraction","foundation","partnership","employment","revival","inception"],"expl":"该刊物自 1913 年的“创办”（inception/foundation）。选 BF"},{"id":"v30.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although most land snails are _____, the giant African snail is a notable exception; it can be 15 inches long and weigh 2 pounds.","key":"DF","opts":["gargantuan","juvenile","functional","diminutive","responsive","minuscule"],"expl":"大多数陆地蜗牛“很小”（diminutive/minuscule），非洲大蜗牛是例外。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v31-1","title":"Test 31 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v31.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Many creative photographers were delighted to find in instant photography a mode that encouraged them to stop viewing photography as _____ and start viewing it as something they could handle with spontaneity, even derision.","key":"A","opts":["sacrosanct","ephemeral","malleable","egalitarian","autonomous"],"expl":"摄影不再被视为“神圣不可侵犯的”（sacrosanct），而是可以随意处理的东西。选 A"},{"id":"v31.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author clearly supports the causes he writes about, but he is more a narrator than (i)_____. Some say he should have included more (ii)_____, but he is wise to let the fact speak for themselves. They are complex enough to prompt many kinds of interpretation, and he would bog down the complicated tale if he tried to adjudicate all of their competing claims.","key":"BE","groups":[["a reporter","an advocate","an adversary"],["statistical data","analysis of events","detailed description"]],"expl":"空1 作者是“辩护者”（advocate）而不是“记者”；空2 “详细的描述”（detailed description）。选 BE"},{"id":"v31.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Schechter is atypically (i)_____ the film version of Stephen King’s horror novel The shining because the qualities for which the majority of other critics have approved it (its artful camera work and so on) get in the way of narrative and render the story less, rather than more, (ii)_____ than other films of the same genre. This is not (iii)_____ view, and we must be grateful to Schechter for putting it forward.","key":"AFG","groups":[["unimpressed with","confused by","enamored of"],["heartbreaking","comical","terrifying"],["a commonplace","a superior","an unfamiliar"]],"expl":"空1 作者“不赞赏”（unimpressed with）；空2 影片“令人恐惧”（terrifying）；空3 这不是“常见的”（commonplace）观点。选 AFG"},{"id":"v31.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As the biography makes plain, the scientist led _____ sort of life, rarely remaining in one place for long.","key":"CE","opts":["an enigmatic","an idiosyncratic","an itinerant","a cautious","a peripatetic","a circumspect"],"expl":"科学家过着“游走的”（itinerant/peripatetic）生活。选 CE"},{"id":"v31.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is a revelation on almost every page of this book, and the author’s prose is _____ in the best possible way: blunt, sweet, off-kilter, and often quite funny.","key":"DF","opts":["eloquent","austere","somber","awkward","solemn","ungainly"],"expl":"作者的文笔“笨拙的”（awkward/ungainly）却很有趣。选 DF"},{"id":"v31.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The potential reduction in water lost from the proposed reservoir from evaporation is _____ inconsequential: even the minimum projected reduction would save enough water to furnish the needs of a Denver-sized municipality.","key":"CE","opts":["nearly","comparatively","scarcely","rarely","hardly","relatively"],"expl":"减少的水量“几乎”（nearly/hardly）微不足道。选 CE"},{"id":"v31.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"_____ the notion that attention is a limited resource, scientists have found lots of evidence that drivers with cell phones drives slower and are more apt to miss important details than drivers who drive solely on the road.","key":"BD","opts":["controverting","buttressing","questioning","bolstering","perpetuating","refuting"],"expl":"科学研究“驳斥”（refuting/controverting）了注意力资源有限的观点。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v31-2","title":"Test 31 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v31.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some ethicists worry that a deeper understanding of the brain may be tantamount to _____; if we discover that free will is an illusion of neural circuitry, how will we hold people responsible for their actions?","key":"E","opts":["vindication","proscription","ministration","valediction","exculpation"],"expl":"对大脑的深入理解可能等同于“开脱责任”（exculpation）。选 E"},{"id":"v31.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Of all her works, this play is the most dependent on the dramatic conventions of the author’s day: it was both the least _____ of her plays and the most commercially successful.","key":"A","opts":["experimental","popular","formulaic","lucrative","contemporary"],"expl":"这部剧作是“最依赖惯例的”（formulaic）。选 A"},{"id":"v31.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The controversy about Alexander the Great’s personality derives from the fact that our sources are (i)_____, all eyewitness accounts having perished. What remains is, at best, (ii)_____ (one history, for instance is based largely on the now-lost memoirs of Alexander’s alleged half-brother, Ptolemy) and at worst, highly unreliable.","key":"BD","groups":[["outdated","inadequate","abstruse"],["secondhand","repetitious","deceptive"]],"expl":"空1 史料“不足”（inadequate）；空2 资料多为“转述”（secondhand）。选 BD"},{"id":"v31.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Firebaugh and Beck contend that economic development improves the overall well-being of people within developing countries. However, other scholars emphasize the (i)_____ of this view, empirically demonstrating that while economic development does in fact contribute to the well-being of the population of developing countries, the magnitude of development’s positive effects on well-being has (ii)_____. In other words, these scholars suggest that (iii)_____ economic development and human well-being is taking place in developing countries.","key":"CFG","groups":[["falsity","arbitrariness","limitation"],["been greatly underestimated","not yet been measured","decreased over time"],["a decoupling of","an inversion of","a decline in"]],"expl":"空1 这一观点的“局限”（limitation）；空2 影响“未被充分估计”（greatly underestimated）；空3 “经济发展与福祉的脱钩”（decoupling of）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v31.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although a dedicated reader of the book can _____ a brief of chronology of Chappell’s life, the book is nevertheless not a real biography of Chapelle.","key":"BF","opts":["mass","obtain","overlook","excuse","forgo","glean"],"expl":"读者能够“获取”（glean/obtain）大概的年表。选 BF"},{"id":"v31.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In their quest for kinder cutting, physicians increasingly rely on endoscopic surgery, replacing large scalpels and clamps with cameras and _____ tools that snake into the body through tiny holes.","key":"AD","opts":["flexibility","rigidity","magnitude","suppleness","enormity","precision"],"expl":"内窥镜手术使用的是“精密的”（precision）与“柔性的”（flexibility）工具。选 AD"},{"id":"v31.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The university’s once _____ department of economic history has lost prestige and transmogrified into a department of management and marketing.","key":"AE","opts":["respected","slighted","pretentious","gigantic","venerable","snubbed"],"expl":"曾经“受尊敬的”（respected/venerable）系科。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v32-1","title":"Test 32 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v32.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Carmen’s affection for her sister, though not _____, was plainly too great to permit a painless departure.","key":"D","opts":["unsteady","ambivalent","careless","unbounded","noticeable"],"expl":"Carmen 对妹妹的感情“没有限制”（unbounded）。选 D"},{"id":"v32.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Making loans and fighting poverty are normally two of the least glamorous pursuits around, but remarkably enough put the two together, and you have an economic innovation that has become not just (i)_____ but downright (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["popular","pointless","dangerous"],["chic","unfathomable","sensible"]],"expl":"空1 “流行”（popular）；空2 “时髦”（chic）。选 AD"},{"id":"v32.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The research on otters’ environmental requirements is surprisingly (i)_____. One reason for this has to do with the estimation of how much they use different areas. Doing so may be (ii)_____ in some kinds of terrain, such as Shetland where the Eurasian otters are active in daytime and have clear individual markings. There it is possible to identify the individuals over stretches of coast of a few kilometers and to see what kinds of coast they use. However, the field conditions are (iii)_____.","key":"CEI","groups":[["straightforward","controversial","difficult"],["quite problematic","relatively simple","largely unnecessary"],["routine","deceptive","exceptional"]],"expl":"空1 研究“困难”（difficult）；空2 “相当成问题”（quite problematic）；空3 “特殊情况”（exceptional）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v32.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Travel writers have a special burden of forming _____ story—that is, one with a beginning, middle, and end—out of the unformed moments that make up the act of traveling.","key":"BE","opts":["a compelling","a coherent","an original","a serious","an orderly","an innovative"],"expl":"游记作者要形成“连贯的”（coherent）故事。选 BE"},{"id":"v32.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are many ways in which rat brains and human brains are _____. Indeed, rat brains are often used as generalized models for all mammalian brains, including our own.","key":"BD","opts":["identical","analogous","mysterious","comparable","adaptable","inexplicable"],"expl":"老鼠的大脑与人脑“相当”（comparable）。选 BD"},{"id":"v32.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Space is often referred to as the final frontier, as the only realm of which humankind has still to gain substantial understanding, yet the ocean realm is another vast area about which our knowledge is _____.","key":"DF","opts":["erroneous","confusing","frustrating","rudimentary","delusive","sketchy"],"expl":"海洋知识仍然“粗浅”（rudimentary/sketchy）。选 DF"},{"id":"v32.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The occasional minor errors, while annoying, do not _____ the basic scholarship or the valuable contribution of this book.","key":"EF","opts":["support","uphold","expose","explain","vitiate","impair"],"expl":"小错误“不会损害”（vitiate/impair）学术价值。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v32-2","title":"Test 32 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v32.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The science of astronomy was begun by amateurs and today remains dependent on their contributions, which are incisive by virtue of being _____ by the a priori assumptions that often vitiate the work of professional research scientists.","key":"B","opts":["characterized","unencumbered","supported","contradicted","inspired"],"expl":"业余天文学家的研究“未受束缚”（unencumbered）。选 B"},{"id":"v32.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The genius of the scientific method is that it (i)_____ the dictum of Aristotle that the goal of science is knowledge of the ultimate cause of things. True science, we now know, advances human knowledge by (ii)_____ ultimate causes and focusing instead on the testing of empirical hypotheses.","key":"BD","groups":[["qualifies","jettisons","afrfi ms"],["ignoring","predicting","confirming"]],"expl":"空1 科学“放弃”（jettisons）了“终极原因”的目标；空2 科学通过“预测”（predicting）来推进知识。选 BD"},{"id":"v32.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The meandering journey across the soundscape of the Internet can be (i)_____. Listening to music in this medium often generates anxiety fulfillment: no sooner has one experience begun than the thought of what else is out there intrudes. Putting an old-fashioned disk and letting it play to the end restores a measure of (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["liberating","taxing","educational"],["choice","boredom","sanity"]],"expl":"空1 “令人解放的”（liberating）与“令人疲惫的”（taxing）；空2 从“选择”（choice）转向完整播放带来的安宁。选 BF"},{"id":"v32.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"In this single volume, Kenny aims to survey for the general reader all of ancient philosophy; understandably, space in such a book is (i)_____, and he is not to be faulted for minor omissions. However, Kenny would have added significantly to his book’s value had he more effectively (ii)_____ the influence of ancient philosophy on the subsequent tradition. As it is, newcomers to the subject will have little (iii)_____ the afterlife enjoyed by ancient philosophy in the period 1600-1750.","key":"AEG","groups":[["at a premium","hard to fill","taken for granted"],["overlooked","signaled","prevented"],["sense of","devotion to","aversion to"]],"expl":"空1 篇幅“珍贵”（at a premium）；空2 作者“未能说明”（overlooked）影响；空3 新手对古代哲学的“后世”（afterlife）缺乏认识（sense of）。选 AEG"},{"id":"v32.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In American art the line between the good and the goods is not a hard-and-fast boundary, for in a commercial society the membrane that separates spirit and store is always _____.","key":"AC","opts":["porous","clogged","permeable","unwavering","steady","imaginary"],"expl":"商业社会中艺术与商品之间的界限是“可渗透的”（porous/permeable）。选 AC"},{"id":"v32.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the four microclimates, observed over the three years, show very similar overall trends, suggesting spatial _____ in the rock surface temperature regime, relative humidity and surface wetness data show clear differences.","key":"DE","opts":["invariability","superiority","perception","homogeneity","resemblance","immutability"],"expl":"四个小气候的整体趋势相似，表明空间上的“同质性”（homogeneity）。选 DE"},{"id":"v32.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because chemistry’s position as one of the natural sciences has long seemed _____, historians have generally treated the foundation of chemical professorship as an inevitable component of the progression of universities.","key":"AF","opts":["manifest","impregnable","relevant","predictable","germane","self-evident"],"expl":"化学作为自然科学“不言自明”（self-evident）的地位。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v33-1","title":"Test 33 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v33.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The maps in this volume are meant not as guides but as _____: they are designed to make the reader think anew about the city.","key":"D","opts":["adornments","references","truisms","provocations","valedictions"],"expl":"地图的作用是“挑衅”（provocations）读者的思考。选 D"},{"id":"v33.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Proponents of international regulation of environmental issues have always struggled against scientific uncertainty and economic hostility, two obstacles which, form a political standpoint, often have been closely related, as economic hostility toward environmental regulation for economic reasons have (i)_____ the considerable uncertainty underlying most environmental challenges to (ii)_____ of environmental regulation.","key":"CE","groups":[["resolved","gainsaid","exploited"],["exaggerate the efcfi acy","downplay the legitimacy","question the fallibility"]],"expl":"空1 经济敌意“削弱”（gainsaid）了不确定性；空2 “降低……的合法性”（downplay the legitimacy）。选 CE"},{"id":"v33.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many popular musicians have (i)____ new digital technologies that allow them unprecedented control over their music. These musicians use computers to (ii)_____ and modify their songs, resulting in a level of musical precision often unattainable naturally. Of course, though, as is often the case with new technologies, some traditionalists (iii)_____ these developments.","key":"AFG","groups":[["incorporated","synthesized","alleviated"],["energize","delineate","recast"],["balk at","revel in","retaliate"]],"expl":"空1 “采用”（incorporated）新技术；空2 “重塑”（recast）歌曲；空3 传统主义者“反对”（balk at）这些发展。选 AFG"},{"id":"v33.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Her apparent _____ her background and ancestry seems unconceivable in an age when people tend to think of themselves to exhaustion.","key":"CE","opts":["rejection of","deference to","unfamiliarity with","dishonesty with","ignorance of","fixation on"],"expl":"她对自己的出身“不熟悉”（unfamiliarity with）。选 CE"},{"id":"v33.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For parents, the pleasure of letting children choose which book to read aloud together is not always _____: I well remembered my inner groans when my child would constantly pick my least favorite book from the shelf.","key":"DF","opts":["intangible","enduring","impalpable","unalloyed","ephemeral","unqualified"],"expl":"不总是“没有杂质的”（unalloyed）乐趣。选 DF"},{"id":"v33.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In Schaller’s contradictory introduction to the book, she alternately applauds and _____ humankind’s role in animal conservation.","key":"CF","opts":["authorizes","endorses","denounces","discloses","relates","lambasts"],"expl":"作者在“谴责”（denounces/lambasts）人类的角色。选 CF"},{"id":"v33.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The company is so old-fashioned and opposed to innovation that it can seem downright _____.","key":"AC","opts":["antediluvian","flighty","archaic","chauvinistic","capricious","patronizing"],"expl":"这家公司“古老”（archaic/antediluvian）。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v33-2","title":"Test 33 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v33.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Neuroscientists are excited by technological progress that facilitates brain mapping, the most _____ of them comparing their growing abilities to tremendous advances that led to unimaginable success of the Human Genome Project.","key":"B","opts":["rigorous","sanguine","punctilious","unorthodox","sophisticated"],"expl":"最“乐观的”（sanguine）是把大脑绘图与人类基因组计划相比。选 B"},{"id":"v33.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many scholars have argued that the United States Supreme Court usually (i)_____ public opinion in its decisions because it fears that it will (ii)_____ if does not; when it does depart from public opinion, it whips up political maelstroms.","key":"BD","groups":[["comments on","hews to","overrides"],["lose public support","mitigate public anger","create public indifference"]],"expl":"空1 法院“遵循”（hews to）舆论；空2 担心会“失去公众支持”（lose public support）。选 BD"},{"id":"v33.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Campus-wide discussion on academic integrity can be (i)_____ by the fact that faculty and students tend to define cheating in (ii)_____ ways. Even when they concur on what cheating means, faculty and students often assign different levels of severity to specific violations. These differences can serve as a major (iii)_____ the creation of a commonly accepted set of standards of integrity that are consistently applied to all academic work within the campus community.","key":"CDH","groups":[["expedited","obscured","hampered"],["disparate","conventional","rigid"],["indictment of","impediment to","metaphor for"]],"expl":"空1 讨论被“妨碍”（hampered）；空2 定义“不一的”（disparate）；空3 “障碍”（impediment to）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v33.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Compared to Earth over most of its 4 to 6-billion-year history, the world we live in today is quite (i)_____. Of course, it is human nature to regard the world that we are used to as (ii)_____. The oceans, prairies, and mountain chains—even the air we breathe—seem the norm and therefore (iii)_____.","key":"BEG","groups":[["bountiful","atypical","stable"],["invaluable","permanent","corrupted"],["eternal","precious","endangered"]],"expl":"空1 地球现在“并非典型”（atypical）；空2 我们习惯的世界被视为“永恒”（permanent）；空3 “永恒的”（eternal/precious）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v33.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The central idea of the worldview known as “consilience” is that all tangible phenomena are based on material process that are ultimately reducible, however long and _____ the sequences, to the laws of physics.","key":"CE","opts":["facile","ethereal","tortuous","superficial","convoluted","protracted"],"expl":"无论序列多么“曲折”（tortuous/convoluted）或“持久”（protracted）。选 CE"},{"id":"v33.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although evolutionary psychologists do not seem quite as imperialist in their intellectual ambitions as their sociobiologist forebears of the 1970s, they tend, in some critics’ view, to be no less _____ in their claims.","key":"BD","opts":["abashed","arrogant","impetuous","hubristic","narcissistic","diffident"],"expl":"进化心理学家同样“傲慢”（arrogant/hubristic）。选 BD"},{"id":"v33.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the company still loses the occasional lawsuit, the litigation threat that once seemed so _____ has become quite manageable.","key":"AF","opts":["burdensome","pedestrian","sporadic","mundane","promising","onerous"],"expl":"诉讼威胁“沉重”（burdensome/onerous）。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v34-1","title":"Test 34 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v34.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The science community’s perennial lament over inadequate budgets has come to seem increasing _____, because government support for science and engineering has never been greater.","key":"E","opts":["vital","hopeless","poignant","condescending","disingenuous"],"expl":"对预算不足的抱怨“虚伪”（disingenuous）。选 E"},{"id":"v34.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In aquatic environments, the herbicide atrazine is more likely to (i)_____ developing amphibians when it is highly diluted than when it is much more concentrated, a new study suggests. Although counterintuitive, the finding is (ii)_____ some past research on atrazine and studies showing that other hormonally active compounds are most damaging at trace concentrations.","key":"BE","groups":[["supplant","kill","circumvent"],["unanticipated given","consistent with","undiminished by"]],"expl":"空1 “杀死”（kill）；空2 与其他研究“一致”（consistent with）。选 BE"},{"id":"v34.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Leo Tolstoy wrote many works of nonfiction and professed (i)_____ these explorations of ethics and religion compared with his novels and short stories. The fiction writer in him, however, was hard to (ii)_____. Handi Murdd is a short novel with the breadth and power of an epic, with vivid characterization and intense storytelling that sweep the reader away. While the reader senses the moral concerns of the tale’s creator, the novel is a far cry from the (iii)_____ of Tolstoy’s nonfiction.","key":"ADG","groups":[["a preference for","an aversion to","an indifference toward"],["suppress","identify","incite"],["didacticism","fluidity","creativity"]],"expl":"空1 作者“偏爱”（a preference for）小说；空2 “识别”（identify）作家；空3 与说教“迥然不同”（didacticism）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v34.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The concept of increasing complexity of organisms has _____ history among evolutionary biologists, and yet many laypeople would unhesitatingly say that the pattern applies to the history of life on Earth.","key":"DF","opts":["an illustrious","a sordid","a curious","a contentious","a distinguished","a fraught"],"expl":"进化复杂性的概念“引起争议”（contentious）。选 DF"},{"id":"v34.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The story lines of silent dramas may often have been _____, yet within those basic narrative outlines, the true artists among silent-film actors could express emotional shadings that have no analogue in spoken language.","key":"DE","opts":["implausible","incredible","conventional","elemental","rudimentary","confusing"],"expl":"默片故事情节“传统”（conventional）。选 DE"},{"id":"v34.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The candidate seeks to depict his opponent as being _____, as one who is simply unable to make a decision and stand his ground.","key":"AE","opts":["inconstant","cowardly","opportunistic","petty","capricious","spiteful"],"expl":"候选人把对手描绘成“反复无常”（inconstant）。选 AE"},{"id":"v34.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Given the _____ of solid case studies of environment degradation, this new study adds very little to our knowledge of the field.","key":"BC","opts":["erroneousness","plethora","surfeit","inaccuracy","rigor","outcome"],"expl":"环境退化的研究“大量”（plethora/surfeit）存在。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v34-2","title":"Test 34 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v34.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In modern times, friendship has become a _____ relationship: a form of connection in terms of which all are understood and against which all are measured.","key":"C","opts":["conciliatory","mercenary","paradigmatic","contentious","supplementary"],"expl":"友谊成为“典范式的”（paradigmatic）关系。选 C"},{"id":"v34.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even those observers who are the most _____ about genetic privacy issues would have to concede that genetic discrimination is rare: there have only been two cases of any notoriety.","key":"A","opts":["sanguine","zealous","candid","objective","apathetic"],"expl":"最“乐观的”（sanguine）观察者也承认歧视罕见。选 A"},{"id":"v34.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"If newspaper consumers are concerned about more than (i)_____ and prefer to read news that is consistent with their beliefs, then (ii)_____ is not a journalistic flaw, but, rather, a cultivated feature. In a competitive news market, producers can use slant to differentiate their products and stave off price competition.","key":"BD","groups":[["politics","accuracy","expense"],["bias","sensationalism","inconsistency"]],"expl":"空1 “政治”（politics）；空2 “偏见”（bias）。选 BD"},{"id":"v34.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Twenty years ago, when the book was first published, most reviewers dismissed the author’s predictions as (i)_____. Sometimes people (ii)_____ their errors: those same reviewers today, comparing the predictions with actual events, acknowledge how (iii)_____ the author was.","key":"CEH","groups":[["insightful","judicious","alarmist"],["persevere in","recognize","complicate"],["mistaken","prescient","pessimistic"]],"expl":"空1 当初被认为“危言耸听”（alarmist）；空2 “承认”（recognize）错误；空3 “有先见之明”（prescient）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v34.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although his original mission was a failure, Russian botanist Michael Friedrich Adams achieved an unexpected _____ when he found, by chance, the carcass of a woolly mammoth.","key":"CE","opts":["conclusion","upheaval","triumph","bombshell","success","venture"],"expl":"意外的“成就”（triumph/success）。选 CE"},{"id":"v34.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The medical researchers replied to the charge that their proposed new treatment was _____ by demonstrating that it in fact observed standard medical practices.","key":"CF","opts":["deleterious","untested","unorthodox","expensive","intricate","unconventional"],"expl":"对治疗的指控被驳斥为“不标准”（unorthodox）？。选 CF"},{"id":"v34.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because experience had convinced her that Hector was both self-seeking and avaricious, she rejected the possibility that the motivation behind his donation had been wholly _____.","key":"EF","opts":["redundant","frivolous","egotistical","ephemeral","altruistic","benevolent"],"expl":"Hector 的动机“完全是利他的”（altruistic/benevolent）。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v35-1","title":"Test 35 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v35.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In one theory, as people learn things throughout the day, connections between neurons get strengthened, but during sleep then all synapses are weakened, tenuous connections are _____ and only the strongest bonds could remain.","key":"E","opts":["reinforced","reproduced","replaced","stimulated","severed"],"expl":"弱的连接被“切断”（severed）。选 E"},{"id":"v35.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The irony of digital networking is that it can produce more (i)_____ than did the geographical confinement it supposedly transcended. As human interactions become (ii)_____ physical location, people are less likely to have regular dealings with others who do not share the same values and outlooks.","key":"AE","groups":[["provincialism","diversity","materialism"],["more determined by","less contingent on","less insensitive to"]],"expl":"空1 数字网络带来更多的“地方主义”（provincialism）；空2 人际互动不再“依赖”（contingent on）地点。选 AE"},{"id":"v35.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Keith Haring’s cartoonish art became even more (i)_____ than Andy Warhol’s much-reproduced soup cans when, in 1986, he opened his own store, the Pop Shop, to sell licensed Haring merchandise. The public loved the souvenirs; the critics (ii)_____ what they saw as his betrayal of artistic integrity. Haring claimed that these critics misunderstood his (iii)_____ to take art beyond galleries and museums, and thus to give a wider audience the opportunity to experience art.","key":"AEI","groups":[["commercial","traditional","expert"],["fostered","decried","anticipated"],["failed plan","financial need","sincere efof rt"]],"expl":"空1 Haring 的作品变得更“商业化”（commercial）；空2 批评者“痛斥”（decried）；空3 他的“真诚意图”（sincere effort）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v35.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Far from _____ innovations, as the patent system was designed to do, the patenting of concepts such as gene sequences gives individuals and corporations a legal choke to hold over ideas that should be useful to all.","key":"AE","opts":["spurring","recognizing","codifying","acknowledging","fostering","cataloging"],"expl":"专利制度应“促进”（spurring/fostering）创新，而不是阻碍。选 AE"},{"id":"v35.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The 1840s were _____ time for young women beginning to study science, particularly astronomy, in 1847 Maria Mitchell discovered the Nantucket comet, the first of several important astronomical discoveries of the era.","key":"AF","opts":["a favorable","an awkward","a perilous","a hazardous","an improbable","an auspicious"],"expl":"1847 年，年轻女性研究天文学的时代是“有利的”或“吉利的”（favorable/auspicious）。选 AF"},{"id":"v35.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To keep the museum’s admission lines moving, security inspections are considerably _____.","key":"CD","opts":["thorough","annoying","cursory","casual","irritating","methodical"],"expl":"为了保证队伍流动，安检被“草率地”（cursory/casual）进行。选 CD"},{"id":"v35.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The evil of class and race hatred must be eliminated while it is still _____ state; otherwise, it may grow to dangerous proportions.","key":"CF","opts":["an amorphous","an overt","a rudimentary","a threatening","an independent","an embryonic"],"expl":"仇恨在“萌芽”（embryonic/rudimentary）阶段就应被消除。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v35-2","title":"Test 35 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v35.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"One baffling aspect of the novel is its capacity to generate emotional power from a plot that lacks the most elementary _____: readers must accept not an occasional coincidence, but a continuous stream of them.","key":"E","opts":["synergy","continuity","naivety","premise","credibility"],"expl":"小说缺少最基本的“可信性”（credibility）：读者必须接受连续的巧合。选 E"},{"id":"v35.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The mood of the times is no longer one of (i)_____ over our scientific achievements. Doubts and worries beset technical and scientific specialist, as well as the public at large. I do not consider such worries (ii)_____, though they are often based on intuitive feeling rather than on strictly logical arguments.","key":"BD","groups":[["widening skepticism","uncritical joy","false humility"],["unfounded","sacrosanct","foreordained"]],"expl":"空1 “日益增长的怀疑”（widening skepticism）；空2 这些担忧“没有根据”（unfounded）。选 BD"},{"id":"v35.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Britain’s deteriorating economy after 1945 was (i)_____ by politicians who favored the manufacturing sector over the service sector: rather than attempting to (ii)_____ the decline of manufacturing, they should have promoted service industries.","key":"AE","groups":[["mishandled","bolstered","forestalled"],["augment","arrest","escalate"]],"expl":"空1 政治家“处理不当”（mishandled）；空2 “阻止”（arrest）制造业的衰落。选 AE"},{"id":"v35.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Even though intelligence may be quite (i)_____, and even though scientists may have made frustratingly (ii)_____ progress in understanding it, many experts on intelligence still think that the potential (iii)_____ of the quest to understand intelligence make it worth continuing. For instance, a brain-based understanding of intelligence may help teachers design strategies for educating children more effectively.","key":"CDH","groups":[["useful","neglected","complex"],["little","rapid","extensive"],["intellectual impediments","practical values","financial rewards"]],"expl":"空1 智力很“复杂”（complex）；空2 进展“缓慢”（little）；空3 “实践价值”（practical values）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v35.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many people remember a time when cutting-edge architects, who are these days treated like celebrities, had _____ relationship with the public: for much of the 1960s, big new buildings in cities were often cause for hostility, not celebration.","key":"AB","opts":["an antagonistic","an inimical","an autocratic","a symbiotic","an indifferent","an apathetic"],"expl":"1960 年代的建筑与公众是“对立”（antagonistic）的关系。选 AB"},{"id":"v35.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is surprising to see such a child that is at his sixteenth manifest a great measure of _____, for he delivers too cogent, brilliant a speech among adults.","key":"AB","opts":["maturity","precociousness","convolution","nefariousness","naïveté","ingenuousness"],"expl":"一个十六岁的孩子展现出“早熟”（precociousness）。选 AB"},{"id":"v35.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"People from one community always take each other as _____ since they automatically classify the others as their family line.","key":"DE","opts":["acquaintance","consort","neighborhood","kinfolk","relative","patron"],"expl":"同一社区的人把彼此看作“亲属”（kinfolk）。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v36-1","title":"Test 36 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v36.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Since many African farmers face a soil fertility problem, providing funding for fertilizer seems _____; closer examination of the data raises some troubling questions, however.","key":"C","opts":["imprudent","expensive","unimpeachable","modern","worrisome"],"expl":"为化肥提供资金“看似不言而喻”（unimpeachable），但数据带来疑问。选 C"},{"id":"v36.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The politician’s record while in office, though (i)_____, hardly accounts for her high standard three decades later—a standing all the more (ii)_____ because of continuing assaults on her reputation during those years.","key":"BD","groups":[["bewildering","admirable","unappreciated"],["unusual","regrettable","persistent"]],"expl":"空1 “令人钦佩的”（admirable）政绩；空2 “持续的”（persistent）诽谤。选 BD"},{"id":"v36.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"While the Prime Minister’s long-standing reputation for (i)____ practical power may (ii)_____ his recently stated willingness to devolve real power to regional assemblies and local governments, it certainly does not (iii)_____ his doing it.","key":"AFI","groups":[["centralizing","overseeing","exploring"],["render inevitable","be based on","raise doubts about"],["require","allow","preclude"]],"expl":"空1 “集权的”（centralizing）实际权力；空2 “并不排除”（raise doubts about）；空3 “不允许”（preclude）他去做。选 AFI"},{"id":"v36.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The juxtaposition of fertile alluvial soils originating in the Andes with the infertile inland soils of central Amazon Basin is one example of _____ of the soil conditions that can be found in the tropics.","key":"BD","opts":["intractability","heterogeneity","incompatibility","disparateness","instability","fragility"],"expl":"不同土壤条件的并存体现了“异质性”（heterogeneity）。选 BD"},{"id":"v36.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although most scientists hold that quantum theory and the theory of general relativity ought to be intimately connected, the theories have remained stubbornly _____.","key":"BD","opts":["consistent","unlinked","self-contradictory","estranged","arbitrary","congruent"],"expl":"两种理论“彼此隔绝”（estranged/unlinked）。选 BD"},{"id":"v36.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One big challenge with placebo responses is that they are _____: people given the same inert pill or potion may show wildly different reactions, and the effects vary widely according to each person’s illness.","key":"AC","opts":["capricious","illusory","unpredictable","chimerical","marginal","ephemeral"],"expl":"安慰剂反应“变化无常”（capricious/unpredictable）。选 AC"},{"id":"v36.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The _____ of biographies of antebellum capitalists is particularly striking in contrast with the abundance of life stories of industrialists in later eras.","key":"DF","opts":["brevity","banality","utility","paucity","triteness","dearth"],"expl":"对资本家传记的“缺乏”（paucity/dearth）。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v36-2","title":"Test 36 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v36.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Having regarded Marcus relationship to their boss as entirely _____, Jo was flabbergasted when Marcus publicly made clear his objections to some changes the boss was introducing.","key":"B","opts":["professional","sycophantic","prosaic","dissident","collegial"],"expl":"Jo 以为 Marcus 与老板的关系“完全是公事公办的”（professional）。选 B"},{"id":"v36.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although it is not uncommon for journalists to portray political inexperience on the part of public officials as an (i)_____, it was nevertheless surprising when members of the press treated the new senator’s obvious (ii)_____ as an extraordinary virtue.","key":"AF","groups":[["advantage","impediment","exception"],["nonchalance","acumen","naiveté"]],"expl":"空1 “优势”（advantage）；空2 “天真”（naiveté）。选 AF"},{"id":"v36.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Wolosky claims that Ella Wheeler Wilcox joined other women poets such as Julia Ward Howe, Frances Harper, and Charlotte Perkins Gilman in critiquing materialism and possessive individualism. Wolosky’s description (i)_____ the poetry of Gilman, Howe, and Harper, but it is not entirely (ii)_____ in the case of Wilcox, who hardly (iii)_____ the materialism of her time. Rather, Wilcox seems to have embraced the amassing of private property.","key":"ADI","groups":[["fits","conflates","misinterprets"],["apt","puzzling","uncommon"],["reflected","countenanced","impugned"]],"expl":"空1 描述“符合”（fits）Gilman 等人；空2 对 Wilcox “不太适用”（apt 的反义）；空3 “反映”（reflected）或“默许”（countenanced）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v36.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"What she disliked in the fictions of some of her peers was the excessive (i)_____. In her novel, by contrast, she was marked by a (ii)_____: she always (iii)_____.","key":"AEG","groups":[["explicitness","deviousness","divergence"],["ebullience","reticence","introspection"],["keeps some details undisclosed","ends the book with a bleak note","draws on unusual sources"]],"expl":"空1 “直白”（explicitness）；空2 “克制”（reticence）；空3 “保留某些细节不公开”。选 AEG"},{"id":"v36.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"He was one of the most powerful chess players over and one of the most _____; at the height of his fame he all but dropped out of chess, entering into a self-imposed exile.","key":"AE","opts":["perplexing","creative","troubled","infuriating","enigmatic","imaginative"],"expl":"他“神秘”（enigmatic）且“困扰”（troubled）。选 AE"},{"id":"v36.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A small degree of _____ is always desirable in a published diary. A sense of authenticity is seldom worth the diarist’s questionable grammar or careless phrasing.","key":"BD","opts":["characterization","emendation","documentation","revision","substantiation","individualization"],"expl":"日记出版时“修订”（emendation/revision）应该适度。选 BD"},{"id":"v36.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In his heyday, Sonny Bono’s role in public was _____: he was an accomplished lyricist, a mayoral success story, delegate from Palm Springs, and the husband of an internationally acclaimed vocalist.","key":"AB","opts":["protean","versatile","pedestrian","prominent","circumscribed","illustrious"],"expl":"Bono 的角色“显赫”（prominent/illustrious）且多面（versatile）。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v37-1","title":"Test 37 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v37.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some ambitious lawyers are willing to work on Supreme Court cases without charge in an effort to gain _____; they believe that this increased cachet will help them succeed in the future.","key":"C","opts":["wisdom","certitude","prestige","integrity","humility"],"expl":"通过无偿工作获取“声望”（prestige）。选 C"},{"id":"v37.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Contrary to those who fear the impact of invasive species on native plants, the biologists contend that the threat posed to biodiversity by nonnative species is often (i)_____. For instance, a study of garlic mustard, a nonnative plant now thriving in Minnesota’s oak forests, found that garlic mustard abundance in forest plots was not (ii)_____ the number of other plant species there.","key":"CE","groups":[["subtle","uniform","exaggerated"],["consistent with","related to","sustained by"]],"expl":"空1 威胁被“夸大”（exaggerated）；空2 与其他物种数量“不相关”（not related to）。选 CE"},{"id":"v37.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"To pay for the extra spending under this international poverty plan, each American would have to contribute less than the cost of buying a premium cup of coffee once a week. But financial aid is not (i)_____, and even if the funding recommended here were to (ii)_____, the grandest objectives may well remain unfulfilled. Nonetheless, carefully targeted aid can reward responsible governments, (iii)_____ individual initiative, and alleviate suffering. Many will think that’s worth of a cup of coffee.","key":"BFI","groups":[["an impediment","a panacea","a malady"],["be insufcfi ient","recede","materialize"],["obviate","temper","encourage"]],"expl":"空1 援助“不是万能药”（panacea 的反义 impediment）；空2 “不足”（insufficient）；空3 “鼓励”（encourage）个人主动性。选 BFI"},{"id":"v37.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Criticized for decades of overproduction in their signature line of derivative goods, Rectangle Record has satiated the market with a _____ of repackaged old CDs, which interferes with its ability to innovate and produce new albums.","key":"BD","opts":["dearth","glut","deficiency","surfeit","abundance","profusion"],"expl":"过剩（glut/surfeit）的重新包装的 CD。选 BD"},{"id":"v37.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"His political view, harking back to the turmoil in the 1934, is a _____ with no bearing on the present.","key":"DF","opts":["prototype","pretense","paradigm","relic","contradiction","vestige"],"expl":"他的政治观点是“遗迹”（relic）。选 DF"},{"id":"v37.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As a critic, Nelson is noteworthy for her _____: rather than presenting fully formed pronouncements, she is willing to let us watch as she works out her ideas.","key":"BD","opts":["generosity","humility","integrity","modesty","eloquence","rhetoric"],"expl":"Nelson 的“谦逊”（humility/modesty）在于展示思考过程。选 BD"},{"id":"v37.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although in the mid-1970s nuclear power seemed poised for a still greater role in energy supply, in fact the _____ of its prestige had already begun.","key":"BE","opts":["evaluation","waning","defense","undermining","ebbing","vindication"],"expl":"核能的声望在“衰落”（waning/ebbing）。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v37-2","title":"Test 37 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v37.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The author’s unfortunate predilection for mannered turns of phrase and complicated metaphors had a tendency to _____ her work’s straightforward themes.","key":"D","opts":["propitiate","accentuate","augment","occlude","presage"],"expl":"作者的修辞“遮蔽”（occlude）了作品的主题。选 D"},{"id":"v37.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The company’s steering committee, reluctant to be held any specific commitments, released a strategic plan that was deliberately _____.","key":"E","opts":["unpopular","repetitive","stringent","inflexible","nebulous"],"expl":"委员会不愿作出具体承诺，因而计划“模糊”（nebulous）。选 E"},{"id":"v37.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"So, perhaps the lesson is that rather than wanting their monarchy to (i)_____ its modernized Scandinavian counterparts, the British public cherishes it most when it is most (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["commend","discount","emulate"],["egalitarian","anachronistic","regal"]],"expl":"空1 “效仿”（emulate）北欧；空2 英国君主制在最“帝王般的”（regal）时最受珍视。选 CE"},{"id":"v37.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Parker’s model of human affairs reflects (i)_____ outlook, in stark contrast to the generally (ii)_____ premises that her colleagues in the economics department adopt in their work. Accordingly, her conclusions (iii)_____ theirs.","key":"ADI","groups":[["a sanguine","an introspective","a technical"],["pessimistic","theoretical","distinctive"],["are somewhat more accessible than","are not so sunny as","diverge markedly"]],"expl":"空1 “乐观的”（sanguine）；空2 “悲观的”（pessimistic）；空3 “与之截然不同”（diverge markedly）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v37.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The women's rights movement has been mostly _____ in the Middle East, but it is likely that activists will be newly galvanized by the political upheavals currently sweeping the region.","key":"BE","opts":["subverted","quiescent","interminable","bootless","abeyant","feckless"],"expl":"妇女权利运动在中东“平静”（quiescent/abeyant）。选 BE"},{"id":"v37.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Beatified by the Catholic Church in 1765, Italian cleric Ludovico Sabbatini is _____ each year on the day of his death, June 1.","key":"DE","opts":["pledged","evoked","deified","venerated","honored","christened"],"expl":"Sabbatini 每年被“尊崇”（venerated/honored）。选 DE"},{"id":"v37.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"What they see in Jimenez is the one candidate capable of decisive leadership, in stark contrast to Diaz, whose team in office has been marred by _____.","key":"CD","opts":["defensiveness","corruption","irresolution","vacillation","belligerence","pugnacity"],"expl":"对手团队执政期间的“犹豫不决”（vacillation/irresolution）。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v38-1","title":"Test 38 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v38.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Gladys took a _____ approach to problem solving, so when the committee needed ideas on how to create more low-cost public transportation, she suggested they study what worked well in other cities with similar needs.","key":"B","opts":["benign","pragmatic","compliant","rarefied","dogmatic"],"expl":"Gladys 的解决问题的方法是“务实的”（pragmatic）。选 B"},{"id":"v38.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Convinced of the gravity of her poetry, Voigt must have found the reviews of her most recent collection (i)_____ reading: one amused reviewer thought that it was unrecognizable as poetry but decidedly (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["tempting","depressing","thrilling"],["inspiring","irritating","diverting"]],"expl":"空1 诗集的评论让她感到“令人沮丧的”（depressing）；空2 “令人愉快的”（diverting）。选 BF"},{"id":"v38.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"To many newspapers readers now, this book published in 1953 is (i)_____. It is filled with references to some people whose ideas seemed (ii)_____ at that time, but are rarely viewed as (iii)_____ persons now.","key":"BDI","groups":[["refreshingly inspired","somewhat dated","excessively angry"],["unfashionable","dutiable","important"],["ignoble","prolific","seminal"]],"expl":"空1 “略显过时”（somewhat dated）；空2 “不时髦”（unfashionable）；空3 “开创性的”（seminal）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v38.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The research informing Gregory’s book on vegetarianism in Victorian England appears to be _____, with a great deal of revealing detail on display and more than a third of the text taken up with footnotes.","key":"CF","opts":["uneven","excessive","exhaustive","mixed","inconsistent","comprehensive"],"expl":"研究“详尽”（exhaustive/comprehensive）。选 CF"},{"id":"v38.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"He was a man of few words, _____ around all but his closest friends.","key":"AD","opts":["laconic","garrulous","ascetic","taciturn","tempestuous","ambiguous"],"expl":"他“沉默寡言”（taciturn/laconic）。选 AD"},{"id":"v38.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are many insights in the essay collected in Observations on modernity, but they are embedded in a dense English translation of a dense German original that may make many of them ______ to most readers.","key":"BF","opts":["vapid","inaccessible","sagacious","banal","distressing","opaque"],"expl":"这些见解对读者“晦涩难懂”（inaccessible/opaque）。选 BF"},{"id":"v38.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is not unusual for American eduction leaders to hold up another nation as a model for school reform: in the mid-nineteenth century, such figures _____ the professionalism and structure of the Prussian school system.","key":"CE","opts":["envied","imitated","hailed","augmented","acclaimed","enhanced"],"expl":"美国教育界称赞普鲁士的学校体系（hailed/envied/acclaimed）。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v38-2","title":"Test 38 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v38.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In the final scene of the movie, the character exhibits an almost unbelievable ______, remaining imperturbable in the face of intense and immediate physical danger.","key":"D","opts":["cunning","endurance","arrogance","sangfroid","percipience"],"expl":"角色“镇定自若”（sangfroid）。选 D"},{"id":"v38.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author’s best-selling book on Virginia Woolf is not (i)_____ treatment of her subject; on the contrary, it presents (ii)_____ portrait of the novelist, faults and all.","key":"AD","groups":[["an idealized","a comprehensive","a compelling"],["an unflinching","a slapdash","an erudite"]],"expl":"空1 不是“理想化的”（idealized）；空2 “毫不留情的”（unflinching）肖像。选 AD"},{"id":"v38.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Nordhaus predicts that in the future we will increasingly be (i)_____ ecological problems like global warming rather than (ii)_____ them. We may, for example, make some headway in limiting emissions that contribute to warming, but much of our work will be in adapting to ecological problems and alleviating their effects.","key":"AD","groups":[["managing","analyzing","transcending"],["solving","addressing","mitigating"]],"expl":"空1 “应对”（managing）生态问题；空2 “减轻”（mitigating）影响。选 AD"},{"id":"v38.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Compared with, say, the precision of a skein of geese winging its way across the autumn sky in a V formation, the seasonal marches of grazers across the Serengeti seem (i)_____, and at times even (ii)_____. But, in fact, years of careful observation by scientists have shown that there is (iii)_____ those migrations of zebras, wildebeests, and Thomson’s gazelles.","key":"AFI","groups":[["disorganized","purposeful","massive"],["illusionary","overwhelming","chaotic"],["feats a tendency toward aggression in","an undeniable grandeur to","a definite order to"]],"expl":"空1 迁徙“看似”混乱（chaotic）；空2 “错觉般的”（illusionary）；空3 有“确定的秩序”（a definite order to）。选 AFI"},{"id":"v38.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In her career as an editor, she pruned and shaped many a writer’s _____ prose into crisp lucidity.","key":"AC","opts":["wayward","transparent","errant","urbane","elegant","incisive"],"expl":"她把作家“不成熟的”（wayward/errant）文字修改为清晰的文字。选 AC"},{"id":"v38.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Philby secretly loathed the host of the party that he was attending, but it seemed _____ to say so publicly.","key":"BF","opts":["recondite","tactless","clever","malign","deft","impolitic"],"expl":"公开表态“不合时宜”（impolitic）。选 BF"},{"id":"v38.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In American Indian art, the supposed distinction between modern and traditional was fabricated by critics, and when artists have control over interpretation of their own work, the distinction appear, happily, to have been _____.","key":"AC","opts":["eliminated","reinforced","put to rest","intensified","recognized","established"],"expl":"这种区分被“消除”（eliminated）或“放下”（put to rest）。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v39-1","title":"Test 39 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v39.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"As the release of the annual report drew near, it was clear that more than a few employees suspected the company was on the verge of bankruptcy; the belief was _____ throughout the organization.","key":"C","opts":["omniscient","abject","pervasive","estimable","specious"],"expl":"员工“普遍”（pervasive）怀疑公司将破产。选 C"},{"id":"v39.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The contemporary trend whereby fashion designers flout mainstream tradition is unique only in its (i)_____; earlier fashion designers experience the same (ii)_____ impulse, albeit in a less extreme form.","key":"BE","groups":[["subversiveness","intensity","culpability"],["indiscriminate","iconoclastic","temperate"]],"expl":"空1 “颠覆性”（subversiveness）；空2 “偶像破坏的”（iconoclastic）。选 BE"},{"id":"v39.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A bird’s feathers would seem to be a (i)_____ design for protecting a bird from attack by microscopic organisms. They create a warm, moist space next to the skin that could be an ideal incubator for spores. Wild birds rarely (ii)_____ skin diseases, however. The chemicals in the sebum include an array of antibacterial and antifungal agents that allow the bird’s skin to (iii)_____.","key":"CDG","groups":[["perfect","typical","poor"],["contract","overcome","notice"],["stay healthy","become irritated","recover quickly"]],"expl":"空1 “完美的”（perfect）设计；空2 “感染”（contract）皮肤病；空3 “保持健康”（stay healthy）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v39.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite the general _____ of Roman archaeological studies toward the major cities and their monuments, archaeology has contributed much to a better understanding of rural developments in Roman territory.","key":"EF","opts":["openness","indifference","hostility","animus","bias","orientation"],"expl":"罗马考古研究的“偏向”（bias/orientation）于大城市。选 EF"},{"id":"v39.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Our mass media are much more fascinated by bad ideas or the failure of good ones than by successes: we drown in bad news—tales of how things went wrong--but we have only the most _____ discussion on how they might go right.","key":"DF","opts":["incisive","tantalizing","trenchant","cursory","illusory","perfunctory"],"expl":"媒体对如何“成功”的讨论只是“肤浅”（cursory/perfunctory）的。选 DF"},{"id":"v39.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A few decades ago the idea of animal morality would have been met with _____; however, recent research suggests that animals not only act altruistically but also have the capacity for empathy, forgiveness, trust, and reciprocity.","key":"AE","opts":["derision","resentment","dismissal","conviction","ridicule","certainty"],"expl":"动物道德曾被“嘲笑”（derision/ridicule）。选 AE"},{"id":"v39.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"At first, most of the famous fairy tales seem so implausible and so irrelevant to contemporary life that their _____ is hard to understand.","key":"BE","opts":["universality","persistence","appeal","ephemerality","survival","transience"],"expl":"童话的“持久”（persistence/survival）吸引力。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v39-2","title":"Test 39 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v39.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The automation of many of the functions performed at the factory, although initially inspiring _____ in many of the company’s employees, has had none of the deleterious effects forecast either within and beyond the organization.","key":"E","opts":["indifference","optimism","ambition","arrogance","trepidation"],"expl":"自动化最初引起的是“忧虑”（trepidation）。选 E"},{"id":"v39.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Memory-prompt technology such as online birthday reminders does more than enhance our recall abilities; it induces us to (i)_____ ever more behaviors to automated processes. Witness the (ii)_____ a program that allows us to create computer greeting cards for the entire year in one sitting.","key":"AE","groups":[["delegate","ascribe","liken"],["controversy over","popularity of","sophistication of"]],"expl":"空1 把行为“委派”（delegate）给自动化程序；空2 程序的“流行”（popularity）。选 AE"},{"id":"v39.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"While people complain about their hectic lives and demanding schedules, one might be justified in suspecting that they are being somewhat (i)_____: compulsive busyness seems to be, for many, a source of (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["disingenuous","guarded","dilatory"],["pride","despair","irritation"]],"expl":"空1 “不诚实的”（disingenuous）；空2 “自豪”（pride）。选 AD"},{"id":"v39.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Evidence has been accumulating since the 1930s that reducing an animals energy intake below its energy expenditure extends the life span and delays the (i)_____ of age-related diseases in rats, dogs, fish, and monkeys. Such results have inspired thousands of people to (ii)_____ in the hope of living longer, healthier lives. They have also led to a search for drugs that (iii)_____ the effects of calorie restriction without the pain of actually going on a diet.","key":"BEH","groups":[["diagnosis","onset","treatment"],["eat healthier foods","put up with constant hunger","take vitamin supplements"],["undermine","mimic","delay"]],"expl":"空1 “发病”（onset）；空2 “节食”（eat healthier foods 之类）；空3 “模仿”（mimic）热量限制的效果。选 BEH"},{"id":"v39.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because archaeology explores the most profound changes in human history by means of a grossly incomplete record; it has invited the sort of bold, imaginative interpretation in which speculation too easily becomes _____ evidence.","key":"CD","opts":["replaced by","constrained by","untethered from","divorced from","substituted for","constricted by"],"expl":"推测“脱离”（divorced from/untethered from）证据。选 CD"},{"id":"v39.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"During the eighteenth century, improvements in their material circumstances did not necessarily mean expanded independence for women elite families and, arguably, the social conventions of gentility _____ more of their time and energy.","key":"CE","opts":["provided","justified","demanded","granted","exacted","rationalized"],"expl":"社会习俗“要求”（exacted/demanded）女性付出时间与精力。选 CE"},{"id":"v39.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For certain economists, “pure” economic theory, that is, economic theory _____ a specific social structure, is impossible, much like a concept of anatomy that investigates no specific species.","key":"BD","opts":["attuned to","abstracted from","derived from","divorced from","sensitive to","analyzed in"],"expl":"“纯粹”的理论是“抽象”（abstracted from）特定社会结构的。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v40-1","title":"Test 40 · Section 1","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v40.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Like all general models, island biogeography theory is _____ reality, capturing just a few important elements of a system while ignoring many others.","key":"E","opts":["an adjunct to","an improvement on","a mirror of","a corollary to","a simplification of"],"expl":"所有模型都是现实的“简化”（simplification）。选 E"},{"id":"v40.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The reclusive clergyman may have lived and died in melancholy, but this doesn’t seem to have (i)_____ his genius in any way. On the contrary, we find ourselves wondering whether his genius wasn’t (ii)_____ in some mysterious way by his mood.","key":"BD","groups":[["influenced","hampered","triggered"],["served","controlled","identified"]],"expl":"空1 “并未妨碍”（hampered 的反义）；空2 其情绪“影响”（influenced）了他的天才。选 BD"},{"id":"v40.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although Uruk in southern Mesopotamia has been (i)_____ as being both the first city and the model for later cones, at least two sites in northern Mesopotamia have yielded clear evidence of urbanization long before the existing evidence from Uruk, and other discoveries indicate that some of the (ii)_____ early urbanism were invented not in southern Mesopotamia but in the north. These findings have led some archaeologists to (iii)_____ a serious reconsideration about when and where the first cities arose.","key":"CDI","groups":[["established","contested","presented"],["defining features of","derivative aspects of","traditional theories about"],["evaluate","ignore","propose"]],"expl":"空1 “确立”（established）；空2 “本土的”（traditional）；空3 “提出”（propose）重新思考。选 CDI"},{"id":"v40.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The professor’s habitual air of _____ was misleading front, concealing amazing reserves of patience and a deep commitment to his students’ learning.","key":"BF","opts":["cordiality","irascibility","disorganization","conviviality","diffidence","exasperation"],"expl":"他的“易怒”（irascibility 的反义）掩盖了耐心；实际上是“易怒”之外的“烦躁”（exasperation）。选 BF"},{"id":"v40.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Rebecca West’s book Black Lamb and Grey Falcon is a singularity _____ achievement, 1,100 pages that meld the genres of travel narratives, autobiography, historical analysis, and philosophical meditation.","key":"CE","opts":["evanescent","petty","polymathic","incongruous","encyclopedic","fleeting"],"expl":"这部著作是“百科全书式的”（encyclopedic/polymathic）成就。选 CE"},{"id":"v40.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"She expected her book to be _____, but in fact few of her readers disagreed with its premise that street art, long considered a mere sideshow entertainment, deserved to be regarded as high art.","key":"AE","opts":["controversial","dramatic","impressive","acclaimed","provocative","popular"],"expl":"这本书引起的讨论“颇具争议”（controversial/provocative）。选 AE"},{"id":"v40.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Researchers have recorded around 60 separate behaviors for worker honeybees, a number that seems to _____ the achievements of many mammals: even the versatile bottlenose dolphin only performs about twice the number a worker honeybee manages.","key":"BE","opts":["approximate","eclipse","reflect","compound","outdo","echo"],"expl":"蜜蜂的行为数量“超过”（outdo/eclipse）许多哺乳动物。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v40-2","title":"Test 40 · Section 2","group":"Test 31–40","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v40.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The restaurant often experience a decline in business after holiday seasons, for potential customers attempt to be more _____ to balance out their former celebratory indulgences.","key":"A","opts":["abstemious","loyal","unsophisticated","blithe","indolent"],"expl":"节日之后人们会更“节制”（abstemious）。选 A"},{"id":"v40.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The museum’s compelling new architectural exhibition looks at eleven projects around the world that have had major (i)_____ impacts despite modest budgets. It is part of (ii)_____ in the museum’s architecture and design department, which in the past has championed architecture’s artistic value over its real-world consequences.","key":"AE","groups":[["social","aesthetic","critical"],["an emphasis on theory","a shift in philosophy","a rejection of pragmatism"]],"expl":"空1 “社会”（social）影响；空2 “实用主义的转向”（shift in philosophy）。选 AE"},{"id":"v40.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Partly because of Lee’s skill at synthesizing (i)_____ trends drawn from many fields of study, her theories appeared to present, with uncanny aptness, ideas already (ii)_____ in the minds of her contemporaries.","key":"CF","groups":[["superseded","irrelevant","emergent"],["discredited","well established","half-formulated"]],"expl":"空1 “新兴的”（emergent）趋势；空2 “已经确立的”（well established）想法。选 CF"},{"id":"v40.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The motives of many major investors in Pop Art have arguably been to a large extent, (i)_____. These collectors demonstrate and enhance their power over the art market by establishing seemingly arbitrary works of art as priceless. This phenomenon reveals that (ii)_____ is not (iii)_____ of truth or beauty, but simply a trick of investment capital.","key":"CDG","groups":[["visionary","ambiguous","self-aggrandizing"],["value","virtuosity","originality"],["a product","an inversion","a limitation"]],"expl":"空1 “自我抬高”（self-aggrandizing）；空2 “价值”（value）；空3 “产品”（a product）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v40.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite its best efforts to stimulate sales, the bookselling business remains far from _____, for it has high fixed costs in wages and rent, and falling prices make these ever harder to spur.","key":"BD","opts":["effective","healthy","innovative","robust","stingy","parsimonious"],"expl":"书店生意远非“稳健”（robust/healthy）。选 BD"},{"id":"v40.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Every illness is a story, and when Annies began it was characterized by the kinds of _____ details that mean nothing until seen in hindsight.","key":"BF","opts":["salient","unexceptional","conspicuous","suggestive","abundant","nondescript"],"expl":"“不起眼的”（unexceptional/nondescript）细节。选 BF"},{"id":"v40.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"People’s decisions about childbearing depend on innumerable personal consideration and societal factors, yet even knowing this, demographers are often _____: their projections of birth rates frequently turn out to be embarrassingly at odds with reality.","key":"BF","opts":["sanguine","flummoxed","inconsistent","overconfident","heartened","confounded"],"expl":"人口学家常常“困惑”（flummoxed/confounded）。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v41-1","title":"Test 41 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v41.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Needing an advocate who would be both precise and succinct, they rejected McLintock, whose inveterate _____ would automatically preclude meeting those requirements.","key":"E","opts":["punctiliousness","concision","cautiousness","imperturbability","prolixity"],"expl":"冗长（prolixity）与要求的精确简洁相反，正是会妨碍达标的习惯。选 E"},{"id":"v41.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It can be (i)_____ to read Margaret Fuller’s travel writing, as she produced accounts of her travel that (ii)_____ conventions of bourgeois travel narrative, often capitulating to the most well-worn clichés of the genre at precisely the moments when she sought most energetically to cast them off in favor of some new, more passionate mode of discernment.","key":"AE","groups":[["frustrating","enlightening","exciting"],["challenged","conformed to","established"]],"expl":"空1 frustrating（难以阅读）；空2 conformed to（遵循旧游记惯例），与后文“落入俗套”呼应。选 AE"},{"id":"v41.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Human-caused disturbances, such as habitat destruction and the introduction of nonnative species, are among the leading causes of plant and animal population declines. Most populations are affected by a combination of adverse human pressures, each of which is in itself insufficient to (i)_____ a population crash. Therefore, studies of population declines that (ii)_____ individual factors and thus (iii)_____ potential interactions may lead to improper management of declining species.","key":"BEH","groups":[["delay","trigger","ofsf et"],["integrate","focus on","ignore"],["exaggerate","overlook","anticipate"]],"expl":"空1 trigger（引发）；空2 focus on（只关注单一因素）；空3 overlook（忽视潜在的相互作用）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v41.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The brain has become, for many people, _____ the biological machinations of the self, and the self-knowledge promised by neuroscience has ignited a hunger to understand how new findings weigh in on age-old questions.","key":"AB","opts":["tantamount to","synonymous with","implicated in","divorced from","detached from","subservient to"],"expl":"tantamount to（等同于）与 synonymous with（与……同义）都符合“大脑等同于自我的生物机制”。选 AB"},{"id":"v41.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although scientific progress leads to constant revision of ideas, one observation that has remained _____ over the years is that there are a lot of insects in the world: some 950,000 species have been identified.","key":"AC","opts":["robust","significant","strong","perplexing","confounding","obscure"],"expl":"robust / strong 表示“持续稳固”，与“经年未变”呼应。选 AC"},{"id":"v41.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"We do not always use words in accordance with their dictionary definitions, for meaning often fluctuates with context: that does not mean, however, that we are completely _____ in how we use language.","key":"BE","opts":["rote","unconstrained","irrational","unpredictable","free","methodical"],"expl":"不是完全 unconstrained（不受约束）或 free（自由）地使用语言。选 BE"},{"id":"v41.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Today the chair of task force in charge of revising the psychiatric diagnostic manual is _____ post—people work for years to position themselves as candidates—but in the early 1970s, descriptive psychiatry was a backwater.","key":"AE","opts":["a coveted","an arduous","a taxing","a lucrative","an enviable","an influential"],"expl":"空缺处需要“令人渴望的”职位，coveted / enviable 符合语境。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v41-2","title":"Test 41 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v41.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Baker set a new standard for explaining difficult art in language the public could understand; consequently, her books remain exemplars of _____ in art-historical analysis.","key":"C","opts":["fashion","rigor","lucidity","erudition","grandiosity"],"expl":"lucidity（清晰）与“让公众能理解”的说明方式一致。选 C"},{"id":"v41.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)_____ to disseminate the vast scientific knowledge of our time to nonscientists shows real (ii)_____ the extent of achievements humanity is capable of, like allowing a great work of art to molder in a warehouse.","key":"AF","groups":[["failure","plan","willingness"],["pretentious regarding","sympathy toward","indifef rence to"]],"expl":"空1 failure（失败）；空2 indifference to（对……漠不关心），与“让杰作在仓库中蒙尘”呼应。选 AF"},{"id":"v41.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unlike the elected branches of the United States government, where making personal connection with citizens is (i)_____ and almost (ii)_____ political efficacy, the United States Supreme Court continues to maintain that its members should communicate with the public almost exclusively through formal opinions—and even then through ceremonial rituals that date back to the nineteenth century.","key":"BD","groups":[["frowned upon","rampant","disregarded"],["a requirement for","a detriment to","an irrelevance to"]],"expl":"空1 rampant（普遍）；空2 a requirement for（政治效能的必要条件）。选 BD"},{"id":"v41.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Movement from bottom to top, from poor to rich, was rare, even movement from poor to middle class was (i)_____. Statistical analysis of trends in occupation, income, and property ownership, Thernstrom wrote, “yielded rather (ii)_____ conclusions about social mobility in nineteenth-century America.” So we might expect Thernstrom to be suspicious now of claims that differences in class could be (iii)_____ if only the public schools did a better job.","key":"AEI","groups":[["an anomaly","a cinch","a conjecture"],["multifaceted","pessimistic","unsophisticated"],["distinguished","misapprehended","obliterated"]],"expl":"空1 an anomaly（罕见的例外）；空2 pessimistic（悲观的）；空3 obliterated（抹平）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v41.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The astronomer admits that his interpretation of so-called Population III stars is _____ at present since no one has yet done any real calculations to see if it holds up under closer scrutiny.","key":"BD","opts":["spurious","speculative","predictive","conjectural","fabricated","implausible"],"expl":"speculative / conjectural 都表示“推测性的”，作者尚未经过计算验证。选 BD"},{"id":"v41.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Excessive focus on what might have been can cause in us feelings of restlessness and regret, but some scientists are beginning to think that fancying an alternative reality might have _____ effects as well.","key":"CF","opts":["subtle","adverse","restorative","pleasurable","unfavorable","tonic"],"expl":"restorative（恢复性的）与 tonic（补益的）描述正面效果，与“遗憾与不安”形成对比。选 CF"},{"id":"v41.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The territory’s tradition of simple and low taxes, combined with a comparatively easygoing government, has earned it the _____ of its citizens and is widely seen as a main reason for its stunning rise to prosperity.","key":"EF","opts":["opprobrium","vituperation","attention","dismissal","approbation","adulation"],"expl":"approbation（赞许）与 adulation（崇拜）都是正面评价，与“繁荣的主因”一致。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v42-1","title":"Test 42 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v42.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The macromolecule RNA is common to all living beings, and DNA, which is found in all organisms except some bacteria, is almost as _____.","key":"C","opts":["mercurial","amorphous","ubiquitous","manifest","exiguous"],"expl":"ubiquitous（无处不在）：DNA 几乎与 RNA 一样普遍存在。选 C"},{"id":"v42.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Argument may be an overly (i)_____ word to apply to the gossamer contrivance that is A Summer of Humming birds. In what seems a self-conscious (ii)_____ of its mascot the book flits from one subject or moment in history to another, following the various whims of its author.","key":"CE","groups":[["archaic","imprecise","robust"],["repudiation","emulation","misrepresentation"]],"expl":"空1 robust（“过度厚重”的词）与薄如蛛丝的作品形成反讽；空2 emulation（模仿其吉祥物的蜂鸟）。选 CE"},{"id":"v42.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"So (i)_____ is the reputation of the country's police for corruption and other forms of (ii)_____ that it has become a kind of tradition that every newly appointed police chief pledges to (iii)_____ the force.","key":"AFH","groups":[["persisted","paralyzing","unfounded"],["indolence","incompetence","criminality"],["contradict","reform","reward"]],"expl":"空1 persisted（持续存在）；空2 criminality（犯罪行为）；空3 reform（改革）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v42.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the parents do not think highly of the educational system “as a whole”, they fail to treat teachers with _____ equally.","key":"DF","opts":["consideration","veneration","lucubration","opprobrium","reverence","disdain"],"expl":"语境为负面，opprobrium（指责）与 disdain（轻蔑）符合“不尊重教师”的态度。选 DF"},{"id":"v42.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Economic growth has been identified as a _____ for poor countries to eradicate poverty, but this prescription also triggers great environmental concerns.","key":"AC","opts":["panacea","refuge","remedy","heaven","culprit","recipe"],"expl":"panacea（灵丹妙药）与 remedy（解决办法）都表示“解决贫困的手段”。选 AC"},{"id":"v42.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In mathematics, judgments about the validity of proofs are mediated by peer-reviewed journals; to ensure _____, reviewers are carefully chosen by journal editors, and the identity of scholars whose papers are under consideration are kept secret.","key":"CE","opts":["timelessness","originality","fairness","comprehensiveness","objectivity","novelty"],"expl":"空缺处为同行评审的目的，fairness（公平）与 objectivity（客观）是同伴评审的核心。选 CE"},{"id":"v42.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The sociologist argued that criminal behavior is an impermanent condition because it is the result of cyclical forces operating through _____ factors, not the manifestation of deeply rooted personal characteristics.","key":"AC","opts":["contingent","alarming","circumstantial","proliferating","unsustainable","intensifying"],"expl":"contingent（偶然的）与 circumstantial（环境性的）说明犯罪源于外部条件而非人格。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v42-2","title":"Test 42 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v42.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Notwithstanding that the _____ of local branch banks has been so much predicted, in most countries the number of branch banks has increased over the past decade.","key":"C","opts":["resurgence","proliferation","demise","profitability","reorganization"],"expl":"demise（消亡）与“预测分行将减少”相符，但实际数量却增长了。选 C"},{"id":"v42.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"As he has matured as a scholar, Felmar has come to see the merit of qualification. His conclusions, which early in his career he (i)______, are now often (ii)______.","key":"AD","groups":[["stated as absolutes","refused to reveal","backed up extensively"],["hedged","simplified","reiterated"]],"expl":"空1 stated as absolutes（以绝对化的方式陈述）；空2 hedged（加以限定）。选 AD"},{"id":"v42.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unlike the elected branches of the United States government, where making personal connection with citizens is (i)_____ and almost (ii)_____ political efficacy, the United States Supreme Court continues to maintain that its members should communicate with the public almost exclusively through formal opinions—and even then through ceremonial rituals that date back to the nineteenth century.","key":"BD","groups":[["frowned upon","rampant","disregarded"],["a requirement for","a detriment to","an irrelevance to"]],"expl":"同 v41.2.3：空1 rampant；空2 a requirement for。选 BD"},{"id":"v42.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The wealthy donor was known for his annual acts of (i)_____ throughout the community, but even more (ii)_____ was the fact that he was willing to get his hands dirty and serve the needy through hard physical labor as well as through (iii)_____ and gifts.","key":"CDH","groups":[["quality","legacy","largesse"],["laudable","inexpressible","disquieting"],["efof rt","endowments","handiwork"]],"expl":"空1 largesse（慷慨馈赠）；空2 laudable（值得称赞）；空3 endowments（捐赠）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v42.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"British critics covering African American musicians performing in London in the 1910s had little idea how to distinguish what was authentic African American music from what was _____, but they knew such a distinction existed.","key":"DF","opts":["eclectic","genuine","derivative","spurious","legitimate","specious"],"expl":"spurious（伪造的）与 specious（似是而非的）对应“非真正的”音乐。选 DF"},{"id":"v42.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Any antimatter in our part of the universe is necessarily _____ because of the overwhelming preponderance of ordinary matter, by which antimatter is quickly annihilated.","key":"AF","opts":["short-lived","nebulous","scarce","concrete","substantial","ephemeral"],"expl":"short-lived / ephemeral 都表示“短暂的”，因反物质会迅速湮灭。选 AF"},{"id":"v42.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are great _____ in countries’ greenhouse gas emissions, especially in per capita terms: while the United States and China are similar in aggregate emissions, United States per capita emissions are a huge multiple of China’s.","key":"BE","opts":["distortions","disparities","fluctuations","advances","variances","vacillations"],"expl":"disparities（差距）与 variances（差异）描述各国排放量的不平等。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v43-1","title":"Test 43 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v43.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"By the early nineteenth century, education in the United States had become _____ affair: almost every town provided free schools for young children, and many were in the process of building high schools.","key":"B","opts":["an analytical","a civic","a contested","a trivial","an exclusive"],"expl":"civic（公民的）：学校是公共事业，与“每个城镇都提供免费学校”一致。选 B"},{"id":"v43.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The description of humans as having an internal clock is not a (i)_____. Or rather, it is—you do not have a tiny watch in your cerebellum—but it also refers to (ii)_____, a specialized bundle of cells that regulates cyclical processes.","key":"CF","groups":[["euphemism","cliché","metaphor"],["an elusive psychological phenomenon","a standard literary trope","a real biological feature"]],"expl":"空1 metaphor（隐喻）；空2 a real biological feature（真实的生物特征）。选 CF"},{"id":"v43.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"(i)_____ have often shrilled that Australia’s Great Barrier Reef is dying, a result of agricultural runoff from the (ii)_____ Queensland coast. In truth, the preservation of the reef (iii)_____, a combination of active government intervention and the beneficial effects of responsible tourism.","key":"CEI","groups":[["Apologists","Optimists","Scaremongers"],["long-abandoned","over-farmed","well-preserved"],["is based on an impracticality","remains a matter of controversy","is something of a success story"]],"expl":"空1 scaremongers（散布恐慌者）；空2 over-farmed（过度耕作）；空3 is something of a success story（算是成功案例）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v43.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although people often describe the correct trajectory for a thrown or moving object, their efforts to explain that trajectory in terms of physics can reveal _____ understanding of the forces acting on the object.","key":"AD","opts":["a naïve","a subtle","a fallacious","an unsophisticated","a nuanced","a fresh"],"expl":"naïve / unsophisticated 都表示对力的理解浅显，与“解释可能暴露理解不足”呼应。选 AD"},{"id":"v43.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Appearing in the midst of so many equivocal comments, this unambiguous statement, whatever its intrinsic merit, plainly stands out as _____.","key":"AE","opts":["anomalous","arcane","irrelevant","superfluous","unusual","esoteric"],"expl":"anomalous（反常的）与 unusual（不寻常的）说明这一陈述在众多模棱两可的评论中格外突出。选 AE"},{"id":"v43.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For decades, Pluto seemed to be the mysteriously _____ planet: it was first thought to be about as large as Earth, but, subsequently, measurements had it smaller and smaller.","key":"CE","opts":["morphing","appearing","dwindling","orbiting","contracting","emerging"],"expl":"dwindling（缩小）与 contracting（收缩）描述冥王星不断变小的测量结果。选 CE"},{"id":"v43.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Science is arguably a very high-minded pursuit, but that is not to say that all of its practitioners are _____, as numerous articles alleging overly generous pharmaceutical industry payments to medical researchers have tried to show.","key":"CE","opts":["conventional","clever","unimpeachable","ingenious","blameless","predictable"],"expl":"unimpeachable（无可指摘的）与 blameless（无过错的）与“有人被指控过度收益”形成对比。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v43-2","title":"Test 43 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v43.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"His _____ character enables him to work with people who often hold sometimes even conflict views.","key":"D","opts":["choleric","intransigent","officious","irenic","prudent"],"expl":"irenic（平和的）与“能与持不同意见者共事”一致。选 D"},{"id":"v43.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author of this biography gives an accurate and (i)_____ account of the subject’s life story, but all the carefully assembled detail fails to compensate for the general lack of (ii)_____ in her writing.","key":"AF","groups":[["exhaustive","glib","selective"],["specificity","veracity","vivacity"]],"expl":"空1 exhaustive（详尽的）；空2 vivacity（活力），文风缺乏活力。选 AF"},{"id":"v43.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although she admitted that her airport expansion plan had recently collapsed, the governor (i)_____ the significance of the failure, pointing out that competing economic development proposals are now more (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["minimized","touted","acknowledged"],["tenuous","complicated","important"]],"expl":"空1 minimized（淡化）；空2 tenuous（不稳固的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v43.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Industry-sponsored scientific research on chemical safety often (i)_____. Media reports regularly imply that industry support of scientific work is alone sufficient to (ii)_____ that research. Even though the source of funding has been determined to be a less significant cause of bias than other factors, industry support suffices, in the minds of many people, to (iii)_____ the credibility of scientific work.","key":"BFH","groups":[["uncovers risks","elicits skepticism","promotes innovation"],["fund","vindicate","invalidate"],["adopt","vitiate","bolster"]],"expl":"空1 elicits skepticism（引发怀疑）；空2 invalidate（使无效）；空3 vitiate（损害）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v43.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Experiments show that it is shockingly easy to elicit a sense of _____ among a group of strangers: just tell them they’ll be working as a team, and they immediately start working as a team.","key":"DE","opts":["dominance","hierarchy","obedience","solidarity","camaraderie","optimism"],"expl":"solidarity（团结）与 camaraderie（同袍情谊）描述陌生人快速形成的群体感。选 DE"},{"id":"v43.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Typefaces, in one sense, are just like styles of shoes: they _____ because different people have different tastes and identities and because both creators and users value novelty for its own sake.","key":"CD","opts":["bemuse","converge","proliferate","abound","evolve","coincide"],"expl":"proliferate（激增）与 abound（大量存在）符合“因趣味多样而不断增多”的语境。选 CD"},{"id":"v43.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It’s a sign of John Dramani Mahama’s maturity as a writer that he is willing to consider his country’s future so _____: his memoir is appealingly honest, given to clear-eyed assessments rather than exaggerated accounts of achievements.","key":"BE","opts":["cheerfully","dispassionately","insightfully","evocatively","analytically","blithely"],"expl":"dispassionately（冷静客观地）与 analytically（分析性地）符合“清晰自省而非夸张”。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v44-1","title":"Test 44 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v44.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The jury's verdict was such a surprise that the populace rioted in the streets; nothing less than a reversal of the verdict could _____ them.","key":"A","opts":["mollify","emulsify","denigrate","petrify","disabuse"],"expl":"mollify（安抚）：只有推翻判决才能平息民众愤怒。选 A"},{"id":"v44.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Research into butterfly wings could have (i)_____ implications, since knowledge of their optical and thermal properties may be (ii)_____ controlling the behavior of computer chips, which likewise consist of finely structured thin film.","key":"CE","groups":[["ecological","aesthetic","technological"],["tantamount to","germane to","advance by"]],"expl":"空1 technological（技术层面）；空2 germane to（与……相关）。选 CE"},{"id":"v44.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Communal feeding is a remarkable behavioral aspect of this generally solitary animal. It is also a misunderstood behavior and one of the reasons is that Tasmanian devils have a bad reputation. Far from being a (i)____, communal devil feeding is (ii)_____ and purposeful, and is described as (iii)_____ behavior. The screaming and apparent fighting is an elaborate combination and variety of vocalizations and postures by which order is maintained.","key":"ADI","groups":[["free-for-all","rarity","necessity"],["structured","vicious","infrequent"],["innate","acquired","ritualized"]],"expl":"空1 free-for-all（混乱的争斗）；空2 structured（有组织的）；空3 ritualized（仪式化的）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v44.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The action in Zadie Smith’s novel On Beauty is mediated by an unabashedly _____ narrator who does not hesitate to inform us, as once upon a time the narrators of novels were wont to do, how we behave in general and how society usually works.","key":"BC","opts":["knowing","obtrusive","conspicuous","antiquated","mysterious","secretive"],"expl":"obtrusive（显眼的干扰）与 conspicuous（显眼的）描述叙述者过分露面。选 BC"},{"id":"v44.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since the data we have analyzed are so _____, it would be hazardous to draw a definite conclusion.","key":"DE","opts":["copious","overwhelming","abundant","meager","paltry","uncertain"],"expl":"meager（贫乏的）与 paltry（微不足道的）与“数据很少，难以下结论”呼应。选 DE"},{"id":"v44.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The phrase “bread and circuses” refers to early Roman politicians’ plans to _____ the votes of the poor by handing out cheap food and entertainment.","key":"CF","opts":["belie","surmount","secure","control","cherish","earn"],"expl":"空缺处为“赢取选票”，secure（获得）与 earn（赢得）都合适。选 CF"},{"id":"v44.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"They applaud the musicals of the 1930s and 1940s, whose plethora of stars, jokes, dances witty dialogue, and general gaiety make today’s offering seem _____ by comparison.","key":"AE","opts":["cheerless","vacuous","mirthful","insincere","gloomy","jovial"],"expl":"cheerless（无欢乐的）与 gloomy（阴郁的）描述今日作品相比之下的沉闷。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v44-2","title":"Test 44 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v44.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The inconspicuous location and lack of striking vistas that characterize the villa reflect the _____ aspect of its creator’s personality.","key":"D","opts":["volatile","grandiose","gregarious","self-effacing","imperious"],"expl":"self-effacing（自我隐藏的）与“不起眼的别墅”风格一致。选 D"},{"id":"v44.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"There are far too many (i)_____ in the report, such as incorrect date (albeit on (ii)_____ points), inconsistency between the text and related tables, and discrepancies between the citations and the references.","key":"CE","groups":[["unsupported generalizations","stylistic infelicities","little errors"],["numerous","minor","perplexing"]],"expl":"空1 little errors（小错误）；空2 minor（次要的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v44.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The physical (i)_____ seen in the remains of soldiers who fought in the fifteenth-century battle of Towton is unsurprising, given the (ii)_____ origins of the men who took the battlefield that day.","key":"CD","groups":[["decay","strength","diversity"],["disparate","unknown","controversial"]],"expl":"空1 diversity（多样性）；空2 disparate（来源各异的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v44.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Until now, old snapshots and home movies faded and crumbled and were eventually (i)_____. Only a few precious mementos were preserved and passed along. But as photography moves into the digital realm, family albums and home videos see capable of (ii)_____: our capacity to store them is, for all practical purposes, approaching the infinite. Is such a transformation a good thing? The natural world teaches us that (iii)_____ are vital to ecological health. Does a similar principle apply to communal memory?","key":"BEG","groups":[["archived","discarded","reproduced"],["transmission","immortality","revolution"],["death and decay","predator and prey","reproduction and renewal"]],"expl":"空1 discarded（被丢弃）；空2 immortality（永存）；空3 death and decay（死亡与衰败对生态至关重要）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v44.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It may not seem like a big deal for produce distributors to mix together soybeans from different farms, but a growing number of buyers are willing to pay a premium for soybeans the _____ of which is know: they like to know exactly where their food came from.","key":"DF","opts":["purity","output","heterogeneity","origin","yield","provenance"],"expl":"origin（来源）与 provenance（出处）指向“知道大豆来自何处”。选 DF"},{"id":"v44.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book reaffirms the idea that Africans on the continent have not stopped ______ or responding to their own creations; in fact, African creative agents have ushered in their own modern forms rooted in traditional ideas.","key":"EF","opts":["exposing","detecting","absorbing","noticing","generating","originating"],"expl":"空1 generating（生成）；空2 originating（起源），强调非洲人的创造性。选 EF"},{"id":"v44.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Flash floods are common in desert regions and were widespread before the evolution of trees and woodland soils; in contrast, flash floods are ______ in woodlands, where floodwaters, impeded by trees, form ponds.","key":"EF","opts":["overshadowed","redirected","obscured","precluded","mitigated","abated"],"expl":"空1 mitigated（缓解）；空2 abated（减弱）。洪水在林地中被减弱或缓和。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v45-1","title":"Test 45 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v45.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Since many prehistoric tools were made of materials, such as wood, bone, and antler, that tend to decay quickly, these archaeological specimens are _____ their stone counterparts.","key":"D","opts":["cruder than","derived from","found with","rarer than","similar to"],"expl":"rarer than（比……更稀少），木质等工具易腐，故留存下来的较少。选 D"},{"id":"v45.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The councilman was a highly respected, even (i)_____ member of society, so when he was accused of fraud, people were (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["venerated","obscure","unassuming"],["stunned","elated","gullible"]],"expl":"空1 venerated（受尊敬的）；空2 stunned（震惊）。选 AD"},{"id":"v45.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Not all paleontologists agree that connections between the continents were (i)_____ just after the extinction of the dinosaurs. Some hold the view that North America, Asia, and South America had (ii)_____ immediately following the dinosaur extinction, pointing to (iii)_____ between ancient kinds of mammals that existed on all three continents at this time in support of their argument.","key":"CEG","groups":[["significant","permanent","limited"],["lasting differences","extensive contacts","trivial likeness"],["similarities","intermediaries","hostilities"]],"expl":"空1 limited（有限的）；空2 extensive contacts（广泛接触）；空3 similarities（相似之处）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v45.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A formal floods resulting from usual monsoon rainfall are _____ the growth of plants, recently there has been an increase in the frequency of highly intensified floods that do not have such welcome effects.","key":"EF","opts":["conducive to","hindered by","devastating for","deleterious to","essential for","indispensable to"],"expl":"essential for / indispensable to 与“有益的洪水”呼应，表示对植物生长不可或缺。选 EF"},{"id":"v45.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Those who read Empson’s correspondence for the first time may be disappointed that so much of it is professional rather than personal, but the distinction in this case is _____: every letter bears the full stamp of Empson’s personality.","key":"BD","opts":["unambiguous","artificial","significant","spurious","clear-cut","unique"],"expl":"语境为“这一区别是人为的”，artificial / spurious 都表示不真实。选 BD"},{"id":"v45.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Analysis for the structural feather that were thought to _____ kinship between the two species prompted an investigation that dispelled that presumption and revealed that the two share a family history.","key":"AC","opts":["signify","underrate","point to","preclude","rule out","exaggerate"],"expl":"signify（表明）与 point to（指向）都表示暗示亲缘关系。选 AC"},{"id":"v45.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book captures the _____ of several politicians who spoke publicly of old-time virtues in order to mask private vices.","key":"BF","opts":["probity","dissemblance","opportunism","rectitude","ingenuousness","duplicity"],"expl":"dissemblance（掩饰）与 duplicity（两面三刀）描述“以旧德为幌子掩盖私恶”的政客。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v45-2","title":"Test 45 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v45.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"There are no _____ criteria of excellence in art: works that once were ignored or even reviled now fetch millions of dollars at auction, while those that were most highly praised in their day now languish in storage.","key":"D","opts":["subjective","dubious","transitory","immutable","uncontroversial"],"expl":"immutable（不变的）：艺术价值并非一成不变，故不存在不变的标准。选 D"},{"id":"v45.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The pupil had a reputation for obduracy, but the teacher found her to be, on the contrary, quite _____.","key":"C","opts":["zealous","astute","tractable","efficient","amusing"],"expl":"tractable（温顺的）与“以为她固执，实则很随和”形成对比。选 C"},{"id":"v45.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"(i)_____ may sound like the (ii)_____ novelty seeking, but in fact the latter can coexist with and balance that stick-to-it virtue strong-willed Victorians so promoted.","key":"CD","groups":[["Ambition","Creativity","Persistence"],["antithesis of","foundation for","precursor to"]],"expl":"空1 persistence（坚持）；空2 antithesis of（与……相反）。选 CD"},{"id":"v45.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Company historians tend to focus on either the company itself or company leaders, the latter being (i)_____ by writers who think (ii)_____ is important, the former favored by writers who think company heads are actually (iii)_____.","key":"CDH","groups":[["rehashed","misrepresented","preferred"],["leadership","organization","function"],["influential","interchangeable","uncontrolled"]],"expl":"空1 preferred（受偏爱的）；空2 leadership（领导力）；空3 interchangeable（可互换的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v45.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Baker was struck by the amount of _____ she saw at the renowned medical facility; for all their experience, the physicians could not seem to agree on the correct diagnosis for any given patient.","key":"AB","opts":["discordance","contention","quackery","nepotism","indecision","cronyism"],"expl":"discordance（不和）与 contention（争论）描述医生们无法达成诊断一致。选 AB"},{"id":"v45.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are great _____ in countries’ greenhouse gas emissions, especially in per capita terms: while the United States and China are similar in aggregate emissions, United States per capita emissions are a huge multiple of China’s.","key":"BE","opts":["distortions","disparities","fluctuations","advances","variances","vacillations"],"expl":"同 v42.2.7：disparities（差距）与 variances（差异）。选 BE"},{"id":"v45.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Church, Nussbaum, Waldman, and Wills have written very different books—Nassbaum and Wills range both farther and deeper—but each one of the four strives for _____, wanting to save us from the errors of partisans and zealots.","key":"BF","opts":["concision","evenhandedness","frankness","trustworthiness","succinctness","impartiality"],"expl":"evenhandedness（公正）与 impartiality（不偏不倚）描述作者避免偏见的目标。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v46-1","title":"Test 46 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v46.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because the critic thought that the mark of great literature was grandiosity and elegance not to be found in common speech, writers seeking his approbation _____ the vernacular.","key":"E","opts":["exploited","embraced","misapplied","considered","eschewed"],"expl":"eschewed（避开）：作家为获得批评家赞许而避开日常口语。选 E"},{"id":"v46.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Knowing how (i)_____ she was at work, her colleagues were surprised at her (ii)_____ throughout the dinner.","key":"BE","groups":[["dependable","diffident","diligent"],["timidity","assertiveness","punctiliousness"]],"expl":"空1 diffident（腼腆的）；空2 assertiveness（果断自信）。选 BE"},{"id":"v46.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Cynics will dismiss the race between Richard and Gorman as two equally dull candidates. However, the notion that the two leaders are (i)_____ does not meet them, for they are as different as can be. Richard is (ii)_____ and is fastidious of her appearance. So one could hardly accuse her of being either taciturn or (iii)_____.","key":"AEG","groups":[["interchangeable","uncritical","competent"],["condescending","loquacious","blunted"],["unkempt","reticent","adherent"]],"expl":"空1 interchangeable（可互换的）；空2 loquacious（健谈的）；空3 unkempt（不修边幅的）。选 AEG"},{"id":"v46.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Given that the department director was such a feeble contributor, sitting silently at important policy meetings and usually deferring to low-level aides, it was surprising that he had such a reputation for _____.","key":"BF","opts":["magnanimity","perspicacity","impartiality","detachment","benevolence","discernment"],"expl":"perspicacity（洞察力）与 discernment（识别力）与“毫无建树却有声誉”形成反差。选 BF"},{"id":"v46.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Between the late 1800s and early 1900s, various institutional structures emerged that set researchers in scientific fields apart as a professional class and moderated disputes by _____ some kinds of knowledge as real science.","key":"BF","opts":["differing","sanctioning","mischaracterizing","censuring","reprehending","endorsing"],"expl":"sanctioning / endorsing 都表示“认可”，把某些知识定为真正科学。选 BF"},{"id":"v46.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In Ramachandran’s opinion, it is perfectly acceptable to propose bold speculations about the brain, even if these speculations seem _____; as Ramachandran frequently remarks, science thrives on risky conjecture.","key":"AF","opts":["unfounded","premature","controversial","verifiable","testable","baseless"],"expl":"unfounded / baseless 都表示“没有根据”，但作者认为这种推测仍然可以接受。选 AF"},{"id":"v46.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Price knew about how to do people favors, sometimes just from kindness, but often out of _____.","key":"AD","opts":["self-interest","benevolence","magnanimity","opportunism","disinterest","mercy"],"expl":"self-interest（私利）与 opportunism（投机）是“出于利益”的动机。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v46-2","title":"Test 46 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v46.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Due to the many _____ in his committee presentation, Mark’s advisor suggested that he revise his work and practice in front of a mirror before presenting it to the entire department.","key":"C","opts":["facilities","jeremiads","gaffes","obloquies","exploits"],"expl":"gaffes（失言）与“在会议中频频出错，需要反复练习”一致。选 C"},{"id":"v46.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Fears that the recent sharp rise in oil prices is an indication that oil is running out appear to be (i)_____. The Middle East still contains vast oil supplies. Furthermore, even if new oil finds elsewhere have been (ii)_____ than in the past, substantial quantities of oil can be profitably stripped from tar and shale.","key":"BD","groups":[["contagious","unfounded","sagacious"],["less frequent","more accessible","less publicized"]],"expl":"空1 unfounded（无根据的）；空2 less frequent（较少的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v46.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The claim that large budget deficits significantly depress private investment and thereby hurt future wages and living standards is (i)_____; in reality, the (ii)_____ effects of budget deficits are tiny.","key":"AD","groups":[["fallacious","incomprehensible","incontrovertible"],["adverse","unforeseen","ameliorate"]],"expl":"空1 fallacious（谬误的）；空2 adverse（不利的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v46.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"People love to talk about their commutes to and from work: those with an easy commute tend to (i)_____, while those who hate their commute think and speak of it as a core affliction, like a chronic illness. Once you raise the subject, the testimonies pour out, and, if your ears are tuned to it, you begin overhearing commute talk everywhere. People who are normally (ii)_____ may, when describing their commutes, be unexpectedly(iii)_____ divulging the intimate details of their lives.","key":"CFG","groups":[["grumble","commiserate","gloat"],["inattentive","garrulous","circumspect"],["candid in","economical in","flustered about"]],"expl":"空1 commiserate（相互诉苦）；空2 garrulous（健谈的）；空3 candid in（坦率地）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v46.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Caricature can be revealing as well as amusing, and Ager’s novel is both: Ager’s delineation of class, ethnic, and generational struggle is exaggerated for comical effect, but it _____ nonetheless.","key":"AE","opts":["resonates","entertains","diverts","confuses","rings true","falls short"],"expl":"rings true（听起来真实可信）与 resonates（引起共鸣）都说明作品虽夸张却仍然真实。选 AE"},{"id":"v46.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the claim that no one knows what dark matter is remains _____, some scientists dispute the parallel assertion that dark matter has not been detected.","key":"BD","opts":["contentious","sound","questionable","unassailable","unverifiable","prominent"],"expl":"空缺处应为“仍有争议”的说法，questionable（有疑问的）与 unverifiable 语境不合，此处。选 BD"},{"id":"v46.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Benjamin Franklin’s reputation is so much one of appearing scientific investigation with commonsense empiricism that it is somewhat startling to realize how _____ the great experiment’s mentoring truly was.","key":"BD","opts":["reasonable","speculative","pragmatic","conjectural","careless","judicious"],"expl":"空缺处描述导师作用的性质，judicious（审慎的）与 pragmatic（务实的）相符。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v47-1","title":"Test 47 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v47.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Anthropologist Jane Goodall was _____ in her determination to anthropomorphize the animals she observed with such empathy, and so resisted her editors’ attempt to recast her descriptions in more dispassionate language.","key":"B","opts":["fickle","stalwart","solicitous","pretentious","whimsical"],"expl":"stalwart（坚定的）：她坚持赋予动物人性，拒绝编辑的修改。选 B"},{"id":"v47.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The small errors of fact in the work are not sufficient to allow one to (i)_____ Johnson’s main thesis, but their cumulative effect is to make the reader (ii)_____ of the quality of his research.","key":"AD","groups":[["dismiss","endorse","decipher"],["skeptical","credulous","appreciative"]],"expl":"空1 dismiss（忽视、不采信）；空2 skeptical（怀疑的）。小错误不足以否定主论点，但累积效果让读者怀疑研究质量。选 AD"},{"id":"v47.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A minor criticism of the book, which is (i)_____ an understanding of the difficulty of doing direct research in Hong Kong’s, is that So relied on secondary sources to tell the story of Hong Kong’s political development, with previous histories of the period (ii)_____ his research. Given So’s (iii)_____ many of the players in Hong Kong politics, it is surprising that he did not use interviews and other forms of direct research to delve further into the motivations, strategies, and tactics of participants.","key":"CFI","groups":[["attributable to","exacerbated by","tempered by"],["largely debunked by","obviating the need for","playing a large role in"],["deference to","estrangement from","proximity to"]],"expl":"空1 tempered by（被削弱）；空2 largely debunked by（被推翻，与“小批评”的语境相符）；空3 proximity to（与……接近）。选 CFI"},{"id":"v47.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In its few decades of existence, the field of technology assessment has undergone large changes: its original high ambitions to predict consequences of technology have been _____ if not discarded.","key":"EF","opts":["deferred","subverted","abandoned","relinquished","tempered","modulated"],"expl":"tempered（缓和）与 abandoned（放弃）：早期野心已被缓和甚至放弃。选 EF"},{"id":"v47.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Individuals interested in longevity have sought to fine-tune their bodies with all kinds of _____ diets: only raw foods; only plant; only the flesh, fruit, and nuts that prehistoric humans would have hunted and foraged.","key":"AD","opts":["eccentric","meager","salutary","proscriptive","trendy","exacting"],"expl":"proscriptive（规定性的）与 exacting（严苛的）描述饮食的限制性。选 AD"},{"id":"v47.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The baseball players performance during last nights game was impressive, although not _____; others have performed similar feats.","key":"BD","opts":["decisive","unexampled","significant","novel","outstanding","spectacular"],"expl":"unexampled（前所未有的）与“并非独一无二”形成对照。选 BD"},{"id":"v47.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The laboratory maze has grown ever less _____ since it was first invented instead of hoping to lose a rodent in a labyrinth; today’s scientists design mazes to elicit a few simple, easily measured behaviors.","key":"AD","opts":["intricate","extensive","effective","convoluted","useful","prevalent"],"expl":"intricate（复杂的）与 convoluted（错综复杂的）描述迷宫越来越简单。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v47-2","title":"Test 47 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v47.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Although New York exhilarated him, even at first Leger’s reaction to it was not _____: he was initially bothered by its stunning verticality.","key":"C","opts":["unspontaneous","unintentional","unqualified","unhopeful","uninterested"],"expl":"unqualified（无保留的）：Leger 并非毫无保留地喜欢纽约。选 C"},{"id":"v47.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Just as different human groups have different kinds of musical traditions, different groups of whales have different dialects evident in their songs, and it is possible for one group to influence the (i)_____ of another. It has been documented more than once that a group of whales will (ii)_____ its own tunes and adopt the new songs of an unfamiliar group.","key":"AE","groups":[["tastes","diversity","organization"],["create","abandon","perpetuate"]],"expl":"空1 tastes（音乐品味）；空2 abandon（放弃）。选 AE"},{"id":"v47.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Any number of mysteries to which individual scholars of Athenian history have devoted whole careers are addressed by Ober, and mostly successfully. This will cause some (i)_____ among scholars who have worked for years on a particular problem only to see another scholar suddenly (ii)_____ it.","key":"AF","groups":[["chagrin","complacency","hubris"],["prolong","exacerbate","resolve"]],"expl":"空1 chagrin（懊恼）；空2 resolve（解决）。选 AF"},{"id":"v47.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Recent proposals for fixing the climate have taken the form of large-scale geoengineering projects such as launching mirrors into space to reflect solar radiation away from Earth, undertakings that are vastly more (i)_____ than anything a nineteenth-century rainmaker could have cooked up. What is unclear, as one looks back at the history of weather modification research, is whether this resourceful ambition will be (ii)_____, or if, by contrast, it serves to make the scientific community’s (iii)_____ that much more devastating.","key":"BFH","groups":[["effective","enterprising","accessible"],["anticipated","challenged","productive"],["avidity","impotence","resignation"]],"expl":"空1 enterprising（有进取心的）；空2 challenged（被挑战）；空3 impotence（无力）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v47.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the group's street protests assumed an assertory uncompromising tenor, once admitted to the halls of power to begin formal lobbying, the group's leadership wisely chose to _____ the stridency of their rhetoric.","key":"DF","opts":["metamorphose","gild","wane","palliate","succor","damp"],"expl":"damp（抑制）与 palliate（缓和）都表示减弱激烈修辞。选 DF"},{"id":"v47.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"His own writing style was _____: colorful and tart in its choice of language, willing to run risks in its allusions, metaphors, and verbal juxtapositions, prone to irreverent conclusions designed to surprise or startle.","key":"BD","opts":["effusive","audacious","lyrical","striking","ornate","emotional"],"expl":"audacious（大胆的）与 striking（引人注目的）描述其风格。选 BD"},{"id":"v47.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Debate rages on between proponents of corporal punishment and the death penalty and their detractors, though even the most rabid supporter agrees that punishments must be _____ and the justice system evenhanded and thorough.","key":"AD","opts":["meet","clement","delimited","condign","tantamount","merciful"],"expl":"condign（应得的）与 meet（恰当的）描述惩罚应与罪行相称。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v48-1","title":"Test 48 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v48.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Discussions of impending water shortages are often couched in apocalyptic rhetoric, yet if the language is somewhat _____, the basic message is sound: water is indeed scarce and growing scarcer.","key":"E","opts":["abstract","complacent","ambiguous","unfamiliar","overblown"],"expl":"overblown（夸大的）与“虽有夸大，但基本信息正确”呼应。选 E"},{"id":"v48.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"He was a leader about whom the country’s people felt (i)_____: both (ii)_____ and reviling him.","key":"AF","groups":[["ambivalent","complacent","indifferent"],["ignoring","understanding","adulating"]],"expl":"空1 ambivalent（矛盾的）；空2 adulating（崇拜）。选 AF"},{"id":"v48.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Women in the mining towns of the American West were strictly stereotyped into neat categories of public and private, good and bad, but the 100 intrepid female prospectors in Zanjani’s book managed to (i)_____ those categories. In addition to providing documentation that demolishes the all-male version of prospecting, Zanjani uses the examples of her female loners to (ii)_____ some of the (iii)_____ generalizations about Euro-American women as uniformly nurturant and sociable pioneers.","key":"CDH","groups":[["inhabit","reveal","confound"],["puncture","invent","perpetuate"],["accurate","facile","unknown"]],"expl":"空1 confound（打破）；空2 puncture（刺破）；空3 facile（简单化的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v48.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Miller reminded his clients that labor relationship are inherently _____; the interests of business owners are diametrically opposed to those of employees.","key":"AD","opts":["adversarial","exploitative","mercenary","antagonistic","variable","changeable"],"expl":"adversarial（对立的）与 antagonistic（敌对的）描述劳资关系。选 AD"},{"id":"v48.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even the man was reserved in his speech, he thoroughly understood his mother, which made him far from _____ as people usually thought.","key":"BE","opts":["comprehensive","ingenuous","sophisticated","foolish","simple","sententious"],"expl":"ingenuous（天真的）：他并非看似的单纯。选 BE"},{"id":"v48.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Mark Messina’s book The Simple Soybean and Your Health exudes recognition much less unrestrained in the description of the soy's medical efficiency than its versatility, but the author cautions against soy to be a _____.","key":"AE","opts":["cure-all","solitude","efficacy","effectuality","panacea","placebo"],"expl":"空1 cure-all（万能药）；空2 panacea（灵丹妙药）。作者警告大豆不是万能的。选 AE"},{"id":"v48.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Three of the nation’s largest airlines could be operating under bankruptcy protection in coming weeks, analysts say, the latest sign of the industry’s ___ as it lurches through a historic transformation.","key":"AE","opts":["upheaval","exorbitance","affluence","peril","convulsion","opulence"],"expl":"peril（险境）与 upheaval（剧变）描述航空业的动荡。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v48-2","title":"Test 48 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v48.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The physical layout of the laboratory, although well adapted to the research being pursued when it was built, was not _____, making a thorough redesign necessary before a proposed new experimental program could be undertaken.","key":"E","opts":["compromised","imprecise","convoluted","ubiquitous","plastic"],"expl":"plastic（可塑的）：布局需要彻底重新设计，故并非可塑、可改造。选 E"},{"id":"v48.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Fables often endure due to their (i)_____, often telling one simple narrative, based around one character. This is both by design, because direct statements are more easily remembered than florid ones, and by accident, as fables are passed from teller to teller, (ii)_____ details fall away, leaving only the essential story.","key":"CD","groups":[["bombast","objectivity","simplicity"],["superfluous","requisite","apocryphal"]],"expl":"空1 simplicity（简洁）；空2 apocryphal（伪托的、非原始的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v48.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"There are something like 1,400 seed banks around the world, which guard samples of crop plants ranging from alfalfa to yams. But this agricultural archive is (i)_____ as a result of war, storms, scant money, and bad management, particularly in the world’s most (ii)_____ places.","key":"AE","groups":[["eroding","expanding","stabilizing"],["secure","turbulent","cosmopolitan"]],"expl":"空1 eroding（侵蚀）；空2 turbulent（动荡的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v48.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The limitations of human attention cause us to miss much of what goes on around us. The real problem here is that we are often (i)_____ these limitations: we think that we see the world as it really is, but our ostensibly reliable visual experience (ii)_____ striking mental (iii)_____.","key":"BDI","groups":[["impatient with","unaware of","distracted by"],["belies","unifies","dispels"],["feats","images","lapses"]],"expl":"空1 unaware of（未意识到）；空2 belies（掩盖、与……相矛盾）；空3 lapses（失误）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v48.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Agencies responsible for protecting natural resources too often issue permits allowing exploitation of those resources, a process that remains _____ given that agencies have become experts at masking their decisions in the scientific terms.","key":"CE","opts":["controversial","exacting","obscure","onerous","opaque","misleading"],"expl":"opaque（不透明的）与 obscure（模糊的）描述决策被科学术语掩盖。选 CE"},{"id":"v48.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The recent exhibition on Dadaism is nothing if not _____, for the visual arts are currently awash in Dadaist gestures and gambits of one variety or another.","key":"BE","opts":["sensational","timely","daunting","ill-advised","opportune","misguided"],"expl":"timely（及时的）：达达主义展览恰逢潮流。选 BE"},{"id":"v48.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Ascorbate readily oxidizes in aerated aqueous solutions, and the PH of such solutions, in part, _____ the rate of oxidation, since the higher the PH, the greater the rate of oxidation.","key":"AD","opts":["determines","accelerates","consolidates","governs","compounds","stabilizes"],"expl":"governs（决定）与 determines（决定）：pH 决定氧化速率。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v49-1","title":"Test 49 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v49.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Within the field of emotional intelligence research, disagreements remain about whether emotional intelligence can be learned and strengthened or is _____ characteristic.","key":"B","opts":["an expressed","an inborn","an invented","a cultivated","a perceptible"],"expl":"inborn（天生的）与“能否后天培养”形成对照。选 B"},{"id":"v49.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Recent years have seen a disheartening string of revelations in which everyday items once considered (i)_____ are found to contain (ii)_____ chemicals.","key":"BF","groups":[["ubiquitous","innocuous","insalubrious"],["benign","complex","baneful"]],"expl":"空1 ubiquitous（无处不在的）；空2 baneful（有害的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v49.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Most advocates of space exploration by the United States would not explicitly associate spaceflight with (i)_____, yet that belief, Launius and McCurdy write, is among the roots of arguments (ii)_____ human spaceflight. Throughout United States history there has been (iii)_____ —seek utopia—on the frontier, and many space advocates have used that notion to make their case for exploring and settling space.","key":"CFH","groups":[["entertainment","irrationality","utopia"],["questioning","analyzing","prompting"],["a hostile region fit only for the","the ideal location for one to better","a paradise corrupted by European"]],"expl":"空1 utopia（乌托邦）；空2 prompting（促使）；空3 the ideal location for one to better（理想之地，可以让人变得更好）。选 CFH"},{"id":"v49.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Consuming 25 to 35 percent of their body weight each day, sea otters are not only _____ but highly specialized eaters, organizing themselves into groups that zero in on specific kinds of prey.","key":"AE","opts":["prodigious","undiscriminating","fastidious","picky","voracious","omnivorous"],"expl":"voracious（贪婪的）与 prodigious（惊人的）描述海獭的食量，并且是专一的捕食者。选 AE"},{"id":"v49.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The concept of the Hellenistic period in ancient history has proved useful but also _____, with scholars disagreeing on the dates when the period began and ended.","key":"AB","opts":["slippery","elusive","fruitless","deceptive","futile","compelling"],"expl":"slippery（难以把握的）与 elusive（难以捉摸的）描述历史分期争议。选 AB"},{"id":"v49.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The current _____ of repackaged music under Miles Davis’ name might prompt any reasonable person to conclude that the recording vault has been plundered bare.","key":"AD","opts":["glut","revival","hodgepodge","surfeit","modicum","dearth"],"expl":"glut（过剩）与 surfeit（过量）描述重新打包发行的音乐泛滥。选 AD"},{"id":"v49.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"People enjoy listening to the governor’s inspiring speeches, and his eloquence lulls his adversaries into underestimating his ______, the tempered steel beneath the sleek suits.","key":"AB","opts":["tenacity","resolve","resourcefulness","kindness","compassion","frankness"],"expl":"tenacity（韧性）与 resolve（决心）是“钢铁般的”内在品质。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v49-2","title":"Test 49 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v49.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The cognitive flexibility of successful fictional detectives is often _____ by their cultural ambivalence: detectives’ intellectual acumen, it seems, exists in direct proportion to their uneasy place in society.","key":"D","opts":["amplified","highlighted","spurred","matched","negated"],"expl":"matched（相称）：智识敏锐与社会地位不安相互对应。选 D"},{"id":"v49.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The scientist’s motivation for (i)_____ a ban on the food addictive cannot be called (ii)_____. He himself had a patent for the substitution for the addictive food.","key":"AD","groups":[["advocating","opposing","conceding"],["altruistic","solemn","effective"]],"expl":"空1 advocating（倡导）；空2 altruistic（无私的）。科学家自己有专利，所以动机不能被称为无私。选 AD"},{"id":"v49.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Since the field of quantum mechanics is often considered to be (i)_____, it was surprising to find it attracts so much (ii)_____ interest.","key":"AF","groups":[["abstruse","unconventional","interdisciplinary"],["cursory","technical","general"]],"expl":"空1 abstruse（深奥的）；空2 technical（技术性的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v49.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"To get funding and tenured positions, medical researchers have to get their work published in well-regarded journals, where rejection can climb above 90 percent. Not surprisingly, the studies that tend to make the grade are those that make (i)_____ claims. But while coming up with such (ii)_____ claims is relatively easy, getting the data to bear them out is another matter. When studied rigorously, the great majority of these claims (iii)_____.","key":"BFG","groups":[["well-supported","eye-catching","small-scale"],["practical","orthodox","striking"],["yield contradictory evidence","require extensive analysis","support conventional beliefs"]],"expl":"空1 eye-catching（引人注目的）；空2 striking（惊人的）；空3 yield contradictory evidence（得出相反证据）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v49.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Ancient cave painters explored every surface, and although they bypassed certain walls that to us seem just as suitable for decoration as ones they chose, the placement of the art apparently wasn’t _____.","key":"BF","opts":["inconsequential","capricious","strenuous","undisclosed","arduous","impulsive"],"expl":"capricious（随意的）与 inconsequential（无关紧要的）描述壁画位置并非随意选择。选 BF"},{"id":"v49.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although many skeptics of the scientific theory _____ critiques that have long since been disproved, some of the doubters arguably bring up valid points.","key":"CF","opts":["overlook","revise","recycle","utilize","neglect","rehash"],"expl":"空缺处为“重提已被推翻的批评”，rehash（重提旧说）符合。选 CF"},{"id":"v49.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the employees’ union and company management, entering into contract negotiations, both issued statements encouraging _____, acrimony between the two sides continued unabated.","key":"DE","opts":["pertinacity","compromise","patience","civility","comity","steadfastness"],"expl":"civility（文明）与 comity（礼让）是劳资双方应呼吁的态度。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v50-1","title":"Test 50 · Section 1","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v50.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Barry was a skilled _____: though his arguments were completely flawed, they were clever-sounding enough to deceive everyone who heard them.","key":"A","opts":["sophist","scholar","quibbler","doctrinaire","pedant"],"expl":"sophist（诡辩家）：论证有漏洞却听起来巧妙。选 A"},{"id":"v50.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"There has been great enthusiasm in the United States for reducing fossil fuel dependence by increasing production of biofuels from crops such as corn and switchgrass, but this (i)_____ about biofuel’s potential should be (ii)_____ by a realistic appraisal of the costs and challenges of biofuel production.","key":"BD","groups":[["forbearance","exuberance","obduracy"],["tempered","delineated","exacerbated"]],"expl":"空1 exuberance（热情）；空2 tempered（缓和）。选 BD"},{"id":"v50.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"As the study of the foundation of western Shanghai reveals, there was a sense of elegance in the refined, simple lines that characterized the entire row, bereft of the exuberant, emphatic, assertive, ornament that constituted the latest British architectural fashion, which expressed its detestation of Plalladianism and neoclassicism—London’s Regent Street then being regarded as abhorrent—calling it the product of a (i)_____ “shopocracy”. The (ii)_____ of Western architectural taste—oscillating between simplicity and ornamental (iii)_____—must have bemused Chinese observers who had long accepted that both approaches were valid and could co-exist.【 GRE】","key":"ADI","groups":[["superficial","quintessential","disdained"],["impermanence","eternality","subtlety"],["profundity","modesty","exuberance"]],"expl":"空1 superficial（肤浅的）；空2 impermanence（易逝）；空3 exuberance（繁复装饰）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v50.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As a way of _____ the negative impacts of overdependence on a single export product—crude oil, the Nigerian government passed legislation in 1999 intended to revitalize the moribund solid minerals sector.","key":"BD","opts":["assuming","checking","disguising","stemming","downplaying","shouldering"],"expl":"stemming（遏制）与 checking（抑制）描述减轻单一出口的负面影响。选 BD"},{"id":"v50.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"After many years of feeling _____ by his seniors managers, Clark was becoming hopeful of advancement.","key":"BC","opts":["vilified","stymied","hindered","aggrieved","circumvented","overlooked"],"expl":"stymied（受阻）与 hindered（受阻碍）。选 BC"},{"id":"v50.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even before she went to art school, Veronica found the standard design categories _____: she didn’t understand why designing buildings and designing tables should require different sensibilities.","key":"BE","opts":["provocative","limiting","stimulating","confusing","confining","exhilarating"],"expl":"confining（束缚的）与 limiting（限制的）描述传统设计分类的局限。选 BE"},{"id":"v50.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Upon realizing that the indicators of a stressful situation can be extremely _____, the psychologist reconsidered her claim that a reliable way of reducing stress is to recognize stressful situations and then avoid them.","key":"BE","opts":["acute","exiguous","persistent","overstated","tenuous","unrelenting"],"expl":"tenuous（薄弱的）：压力的指示器可能很不可靠。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v50-2","title":"Test 50 · Section 2","group":"Test 41–50","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v50.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Reading chunks of Shapiro’s verse in one sitting, it must be said, exposes the _____ nature of his writing: scads of poems are too glancing to strike a nerve, scarcely worth a second reading.","key":"A","opts":["jejune","esoteric","corrosive","finicky","indiscreet"],"expl":"jejune（幼稚、浅薄的）描述诗作缺乏深度。选 A"},{"id":"v50.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"According to Dr. Edith Widder, measuring the level of pollutants in sediment provides a more accurate and robust indication of an estuary's health than does measuring the level of chemicals in the water, since pollution in water is (i)_____, but pollution in sediment is (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["declining","manageable","transient"],["significant","persistent","detectable"]],"expl":"空1 transient（短暂的）；空2 persistent（持久的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v50.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"As the pace of the trial (i)_____, the wait at the beginning of the day became less interminable, and the attorneys’ requests to suspend proceeding for private conferences with the judge, almost invariably granted early on, were routinely (ii)_____.","key":"CD","groups":[["slowed","materialized","accelerated"],["rebufef d","repeated","recounted"]],"expl":"空1 accelerated（加快）；空2 repeated（重复）。选 CD"},{"id":"v50.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"During the Harlem Renaissance, Alain Locke (i)_____ the first flourishing of a self-consciously racial art movement in America and was widely credited with providing the philosophical basis for its emergence. His importance as a critic of African America art and as an art theorist is (ii)_____ if controversial, yet he has received (iii)_____ attention for his unique insight into the broad forces that shaped American modernism and cultural nationalism in the visual arts.","key":"BDI","groups":[["forestalled","presided over","seethed over"],["undisputed","misleading","questionable"],["undeserved","meticulous","insufcfi ient"]],"expl":"空1 presided over（主持、见证）；空2 questionable（有争议的）；空3 undeserved（不应得的）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v50.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To call Kermode the finest English critic of his generation would be a _____ compliment, since not many of its population are professionally engaged in literary criticism.","key":"CE","opts":["sincere","backhanded","paltry","heartfelt","meager","plausible"],"expl":"backhanded（似褒实贬的）：精英数量稀少，这样的赞美有讽刺意味。选 CE"},{"id":"v50.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In sharp contrast to the novel’s scenic realism and precisely characterized figure is its persistent philosophical _____.","key":"BC","opts":["naturalism","abstraction","generality","impartiality","sincerity","objectivity"],"expl":"abstraction（抽象性）与 generality（概括性）与“写实”形成对照。选 BC"},{"id":"v50.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Estimating demographic parameters in marine mammals is challenging, often requiring many years of data to achieve sufficient precision to _____ biologically meaningful change.","key":"CF","opts":["effect","tolerate","discern","envisage","withstand","detect"],"expl":"discern（识别）与 detect（探测）：需要多年数据才能辨别变化。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v51-1","title":"Test 51 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v51.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The painter’s problem, like that of an author whose early literary masterpiece exhausts the themes it embodies, is how to _____ his first highly acclaimed efforts with works of comparable significance and presence.","key":"E","opts":["combine","illuminate","realize","amend","follow"],"expl":"follow（延续）：如何让第二部作品与第一部处于同等水平。选 E"},{"id":"v51.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Managers who categorically squelch insights from low-tiered employees run the obvious hazard of (i)_____ creativity; conversely, these very same managers are more likely to (ii)_____ any ideas that flow down from the top brass.","key":"BD","groups":[["fomenting","smothering","sparking"],["unquestioningly embrace","arbitrarily denounce","conditionally approve"]],"expl":"空1 smothering（扼杀）；空2 unquestioningly embrace（不加质疑地接受）。选 BD"},{"id":"v51.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Vaccine denial has all the hallmarks of a belief system that is not (i)_____. The notion that childhood vaccines are driving autism rates has been (ii)_____ by multiple epidemiological studies. Yet the true believers are (iii)_____, critiquing each new study that challenges their views, and rallying to the defense of disgraced researchers whose work was retracted.","key":"AFH","groups":[["amenable to refutation","susceptible to fashion","open to criticism"],["resuscitated","documented","upended"],["indignant","persistent","phlegmatic"]],"expl":"空1 amenable to refutation（可以被反驳）；空2 upended（推翻）；空3 indignant（愤怒的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v51.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Governments are often willing to pay the direct costs of preparing for emergencies that may never happen: they make room in their budgets to prepare for _____ but unlikely events.","key":"AD","opts":["plausible","anticipated","dangerous","conceivable","foreseen","unimaginable"],"expl":"plausible（合理可信的）与 conceivable（可以想象的）相对“不太可能”事件。选 AD"},{"id":"v51.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Sports stars are often _____ figures, regarded as representative of the city or country for which they compete.","key":"AF","opts":["totemic","iconoclastic","protean","idealized","irreverent","emblematic"],"expl":"emblematic（象征性的）与 totemic（图腾般的）描述体育明星代表城市。选 AF"},{"id":"v51.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The life of a secret agent is dangerous enough, but the life of a double agent is infinitely more ______: a single slip can send an agent crashing to destruction.","key":"BD","opts":["arduous","precarious","clandestine","perilous","covert","exhilarating"],"expl":"precarious（岌岌可危的）与 perilous（危险的）描述双重间谍的处境。选 BD"},{"id":"v51.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The writer’s assignment of the critic includes personal _____ such as jibes about his physical girth and style of delivery, and is not the better for it.","key":"AF","opts":["aspersions","commendations","falsehoods","fantasies","whims","slurs"],"expl":"slurs（侮辱）与 aspersions（诽谤）描述人身攻击。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v51-2","title":"Test 51 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v51.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The presidents’ cordial greeting may seem to be a small gesture of friendliness, but it is not without _____ in the heretofore stifled atmosphere of the society’s meetings.","key":"A","opts":["significance","impertinence","nostalgia","precedent","triviality"],"expl":"significance（重要性）：礼貌的问候在压抑氛围中有其意义。选 A"},{"id":"v51.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because reading on the Web entails quickly scanning and sorting through a deluge of information, many wonder if our level of engagement with the text (i)_____ or if the ability to read closely and carefully is one that can be (ii)_____ if we simply spend more time immersed in a book.","key":"AD","groups":[["irreparably compromised","tentatively disrupted","permanently restored"],["fully reactivated","further degraded","summarily disregarded"]],"expl":"空1 irreparably compromised（无法挽回地受损）；空2 further degraded（进一步退化）。选 AD"},{"id":"v51.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"From time to time, all scientific disciplines encounter observations that do not fit the theories of the day. At first such observations tend to be treated as (i)_____, but those scientists (ii)_____ them sometimes discover that they have to abandon established principles in order to account for the new findings.","key":"AE","groups":[["anomalies","discoveries","harbinger"],["averse to scrutinizing","willing to investigate","unable to acknowledge"]],"expl":"空1 anomalies（反常现象）；空2 willing to investigate（愿意调查）。选 AE"},{"id":"v51.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The perennial problem for critics of nineteenth-century novelist Charlotte Yonge is the relationship of her realism to her (i)_____. While admiring her complex psychological portraits and detailed descriptions of quotidian family life, readers since her own time have tended to fault her improbable manipulation of plot to teach a moral lesson. Indeed, many critics (ii)_____ her because of her willingness to (iii)_____.","key":"BDH","groups":[["pessimism","didacticism","eclecticism"],["dismiss","applaud","underestimate"],["squander suspense","sacrifice credibility","deflate pretension"]],"expl":"空1 didacticism（说教性）；空2 dismiss（否定）；空3 sacrifice credibility（牺牲可信度）。选 BDH"},{"id":"v51.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A priori mathematics, according to Galileo, does not _____ the need for observation, but mathematics does allow us to deduce unobservable properties and thus to penetrate further into the structure of nature than observation does.","key":"CE","opts":["address","acknowledge","obviate","diminish","displace","appreciate"],"expl":"obviate（免除）：先验数学并不能免除观察的必要性。选 CE"},{"id":"v51.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the peculiarities of humans is that we irrationally gravitate to the predictable and avoid risk, whatever the reasons for this _____, it is hardly a sound basis for dealing with complex, long-term problems.","key":"BD","opts":["eccentricity","predilection","vacillation","proclivity","wavering","cowardice"],"expl":"空1 predilection（偏好）；空2 proclivity 同义表示“倾向”。选 BD"},{"id":"v51.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"An abundance of nutrient-rich pollution in estuaries causes algae to _____, much as houseplants grow better when their soil contains added fertilizer.","key":"AB","opts":["abound","proliferate","stagnate","coalesce","collect","diversify"],"expl":"proliferate（过度增殖）：藻类因营养物而大量繁殖。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v52-1","title":"Test 52 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v52.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The purpose of accounts of the Amazons for their male Greek recorders was _____, to teach both male and female Greeks that all-female groups, formed by withdrawal from traditional society, are destructive and dangerous.","key":"B","opts":["deceptive","didactic","pre-cautious","vengeful","reflective"],"expl":"didactic（教诲性的）：Amazon 的记述是为了教育希腊人。选 B"},{"id":"v52.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"While in their consideration of the unique way athletics and academics are combined in United States universities, Markovits and Rensmann do not (i)_____ Gumbrecht’s idealizing vision of the compatibility of college athletics with the intellectual missions of institutions of higher learning, neither do they regard college athletics as (ii)_____: they believe that big-time sports have a rightful place in university life.","key":"AD","groups":[["fully endorse","intentionally recapitulate","entirely misconstrue"],["indispensable","venal","profitable"]],"expl":"空1 fully endorse（完全认同）；空2 indispensable（不可或缺的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v52.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The order applies to all Federal agency whose actions may affect the status of invasive species and requires agencies to identify such actions and to the extent practicable and permitted by law, and since invasive species severely reduce the number of native species and even (i)_____ their existence, the agency has determined and made public its determination that the benefits of such actions clearly outweigh the potential harm caused by invasive species; and that all feasible and (ii)_____ measures to (iii)_____ risk of harm of the introduction of invasive species will be taken in conjunction with the actions.","key":"BDI","groups":[["escalate","preclude","diminish"],["prudent","mawkish","braggart"],["remedy","counterbalance","minimize"]],"expl":"空1 preclude（排除）；空2 prudent（审慎的）；空3 minimize（最小化）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v52.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The stories of silent drama may often have been _____; yet, within those broad outlines, the true artists among silent-film actors could express shadings that had no immediate analogue in language.","key":"DE","opts":["implausible","incredible","conventional","elemental","rudimentary","confusing"],"expl":"conventional（程式化的）与 rudimentary（基础的）描述默片故事的惯常性。选 DE"},{"id":"v52.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the wild, no other mammal _____ individuals from another species: badgers do not tend hares, deer do not nurture baby squirrels, lions do not care for giraffes.","key":"BE","opts":["protects","fosters","aids","cajoles","adopts","coaxes"],"expl":"adopts（收养）与 fosters（抚育）都是“照料别物种幼崽”，此处。选 BE"},{"id":"v52.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Recent research runs counter to the long-cherished notion that a small drop in body temperature during and after surgery is either _____ or actually protects the patient by slowing metabolism and reducing the body’s demand for blood and oxygen.","key":"BC","opts":["beneficial","immaterial","inconsequential","preventive","prophylactic","redundant"],"expl":"beneficial（有益的）与 prophylactic（预防性的）描述体温下降的效果。选 BC"},{"id":"v52.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the northeastern United States, beaver populations had been critically reduced or even _____ in large areas at the end of nineteenth century; as a result, several states instituted prohibitions on beaver trapping.","key":"BC","opts":["diminished","extirpated","eliminated","devalued","weakened","underrated"],"expl":"extirpated（灭绝、根除）与 eliminated 都表示海狸数量在大片地区被消灭。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v52-2","title":"Test 52 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v52.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The often-cited parallels between human communities and insect colonies are _____: the cooperation found among social insects is essentially due to the insects genetic ties, while humans often collaborate with non-relatives.","key":"A","opts":["superficial","obvious","hackneyed","contradictory","uncanny"],"expl":"superficial（表面的）：蚁群合作源于亲缘，与人类合作不同，因此类比只是表面的。选 A"},{"id":"v52.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the years prior to the Civil War, Philadelphia’s African American press encourage readers to be vaccinated against smallpox. This journalistic campaign was initially (i)_____, appealing to readers sense of communal duty, and became even more (ii)_____ once the war started, as smallpox outbreaks began to occur on Philadelphia’s outskirts.","key":"AE","groups":[["hortatory","inefef ctive","widespread"],["controversial","urgent","inopportune"]],"expl":"空1 hortatory（劝诫性的）；空2 urgent（紧迫的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v52.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A hallmark of certain nineteenth-century mystery novels was the reform agenda of their authors, who ostensibly sought to expose economic injustice while depicting the seamy underside of urban life. In reality, however, these claims to a radical political agenda were often (i)_____ meant to give lurid thrillers the appearance of (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["authentic","complicated","disingenuous"],["escapist appeal","high-minded purpose","gripping suspense"]],"expl":"空1 disingenuous（不诚实的）；空2 high-minded purpose（崇高目标）。作者宣称的改革意图实为噱头。选 CE"},{"id":"v52.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Conventionally, the ultimate measure of a scientific work’s validity is how broadly and confidently its conclusions become accepted in the relevant field, which in turn (i)_____ the extent to which its findings are replicated and extended. However, establishing such validity, especially for a novel experimental finding, can take years, and what (ii)_____ replication or extension may be (iii)_____ for some time.","key":"AFH","groups":[["derives from","works against","leads to"],["justifies","impugns","constitutes"],["evident","disputed","touted"]],"expl":"空1 leads to（导致）；空2 constitutes（构成）；空3 disputed（有争议的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v52.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Laughter, like speech, is primarily a human faculty, although both functions may also exist in a more _____ form in lesser primates.","key":"CF","opts":["indispensable","crucial","primitive","intelligible","recognizable","rudimentary"],"expl":"rudimentary（初级的）与 primitive 都描述灵长类较原始的形式，人类的笑声与言语则是更完备的能力。选 CF"},{"id":"v52.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is normal for artists who achieve great acclaim during their lifetimes to be considered _____ shortly after their deaths, only to have their reputations restored by subsequent generations.","key":"BE","opts":["sacrosanct","outmoded","overrated","canonical","unfashionable","emblematic"],"expl":"outmoded（过时的）与 unfashionable 描述身后被贬低，后来又恢复声誉。选 BE"},{"id":"v52.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Human perception is not a direct consequence of reality but rather requires imagination, because the data that people encounter in their lives are never complete and always _____.","key":"AB","opts":["equivocal","ambiguous","apparent","clear","transient","contradictory"],"expl":"ambiguous（模糊的）与 equivocal 都表示感知数据不完整、含糊。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v53-1","title":"Test 53 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v53.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In the nineteenth century, geology became so respected among middle-class Britons that the science came to be seen as _____, a yardstick by which other disciplines measured their scientific rigor and imaginative power.","key":"E","opts":["accessible","derivative","pragmatic","empirical","paradigmatic"],"expl":"paradigmatic（典范的）：地质学成为其他学科衡量标准的典范。选 E"},{"id":"v53.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Though McDonough discusses (i)_____ the filmmaker’s aesthetic principles, it is the description of the (ii)_____, the very vulgarity of the director’s films, rather than McDonough’s learned discourses on the aesthetics of the film, that makes the book so entertaining.","key":"CF","groups":[["inaccurately","superficially","adroitly"],["subtle ingenuity","absolute discretion","flagrant crassness"]],"expl":"空1 superficially（表面地）；空2 flagrant crassness（明显的粗俗）。选 CF"},{"id":"v53.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Saul’s particular combination of intellectuality and vitality was not paradoxical; it was category-shattering. (i)_____ was, in a way, his very theme. Was ever a bookish soul so cracklingly unmediated, so (ii)_____ raw life? He was as vivid physically as he was mentally, almost perversely alert, completely at home in the world of matter, repulsed by (iii)_____.","key":"AEI","groups":[["energy","nostalgia","solitude"],["put off by","flush with","uninterested in"],["seriousness","sensuality","tedium"]],"expl":"空1 solitude（独处）；空2 flush with（充满）；空3 tedium（乏味）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v53.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Susanne Prediger argues that although rational decimals and fractions are mathematically equivalent, students generally deal with them in _____ ways, hence they are not cognitively equivalent.","key":"BE","opts":["variable","divergent","unique","cursory","dissimilar","superficial"],"expl":"divergent（分歧的）与 dissimilar 都表示学生处理两者的方式不同。选 BE"},{"id":"v53.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although Lemettais was _____ computer engineering, he lacked the spirit or enthusiasm to pursue it as a lifelong occupation.","key":"CF","opts":["fanatical about","adept at","indifferent to","diligent regarding","proficient in","apathetic about"],"expl":"indifferent to（漠不关心）与 apathetic about 都表示他缺乏热情。选 CF"},{"id":"v53.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In science, replicability comes with the idea that the pursuit of scientific truth should not be _____: researchers who make claims must allow others to test them empirically.","key":"CE","opts":["incomplete","settled","private","unfinished","insular","unerring"],"expl":"insular（封闭的）与 private 都指科学不应是私密的。选 CE"},{"id":"v53.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even the most hard-nosed critics could hardly deny that the novelist’s best books are _____: they are filled with energy, imagination, and something close to a white-hot inspiration.","key":"CE","opts":["inventive","engaging","spirited","compassionate","vigorous","warmhearted"],"expl":"spirited（充满活力的）与 vigorous 描述小说最好的作品。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v53-2","title":"Test 53 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v53.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"One might expect someone of such _____ views to have a comparably dour personality, but people who have worked with her talk about how she uses her considerable charm to convince people that she is right.","key":"D","opts":["forbearing","convoluted","felicitous","astringent","hyperbolic"],"expl":"astringent（严厉尖刻的）与“不苟言笑”的观点相符。选 D"},{"id":"v53.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In our daily lives, we often (i)_____ our separate identities: you can have one identity at work and another online, for example. Such (ii)_____ disappear in certain circumstances, however, resulting in a cross-pollination of our different selves.","key":"CF","groups":[["renounce","merge","compartmentalize"],["uncertainties","correlations","boundaries"]],"expl":"空1 compartmentalize（分隔）；空2 boundaries（界限）。选 CF"},{"id":"v53.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"If the candidate wins the election now that rivals within his own party have (i)_____ him in a campaign that was (ii)_____ without their help, he will be mightily indebted to these self-styled saviors.","key":"AD","groups":[["rallied","separated from","undermined"],["foundering","effective","improving"]],"expl":"空1 undermined（削弱）；空2 foundering（陷入困境）。选 AD"},{"id":"v53.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The difficulty for nineteenth-century advocates of the claim that forests helped regulate climate was that their argument (i)_____ historical anecdote and observations. Proving the forest-climate link through verifiable and experimental scientific means rather than observation was (ii)_____ for these individuals, a situation that eventually led to the link (iii)_____ justifications for forest conservation.","key":"CDI","groups":[["lacked","discounted","employed"],["problematic","unnecessary","straightforward"],["being revived in","dropping out of","losing out to"]],"expl":"空1 lacked（缺乏）；空2 problematic（有问题的）；空3 losing out to（输给）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v53.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Liam Clancy described the young Bob Dylan as a sponge, eagerly absorbing the possibilities life and culture might provide, and Dylan presents himself so in his memoir _____ in his intellectual and musical curiosity.","key":"AE","opts":["insatiable","devious","unique","pretentious","voracious","cunning"],"expl":"insatiable（永不满足的）与 voracious（贪婪的）描述求知欲。选 AE"},{"id":"v53.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Red Sea town of Aydhab presents scholars with _____: medieval records describe it as a major port for ships engaged in trade, yet today there is no trace of a viable harbor at the site.","key":"DF","opts":["an illusion","a contradiction","a chimera","a puzzle","an anachronism","a conundrum"],"expl":"空1 a contradiction（矛盾）；空2 a puzzle（谜题）。文献记载与现状矛盾，是待解之谜。选 DF"},{"id":"v53.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As clucks of disapproval about Americans’ political _____ have grown louder in recent years, many historians have looked for contrast to the decades before the Civil War as a time when Americans were enthusiastically engaged in politics.","key":"BF","opts":["zealotry","apathy","hypocrisy","partisanship","insincerity","passivity"],"expl":"zealotry（狂热）与 partisanship（党派偏见）；此处。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v54-1","title":"Test 54 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v54.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some species camouflage patterns may be _____, granting those species a higher chance of survival in a heterogeneous environment.","key":"A","opts":["plastic","subtle","singular","consistent","imitable"],"expl":"plastic（可塑的）：伪装图案可随环境变化。选 A"},{"id":"v54.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the popular conception, (i)_____ is inextricably tied up with (ii)_____: doing something truly creative, we are inclined to think, requires the freshness and energy of youth. Orson Welles made his masterpiece, Citizen Kane, at twenty-five, and Mozart wrote his breakthrough Piano concerto no.9 at twenty-one.","key":"BE","groups":[["progress","genius","destiny"],["serendipity","precocity","dedication"]],"expl":"空1 genius（天才）；空2 precocity（早熟）。选 BE"},{"id":"v54.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Methods were developed to remove distortions caused by either the research environment or the researcher. Such methods, especially with respect to the researcher, were considered to (i)_____ those (ii)_____ subjectivity whose unbridled expression was thought to otherwise (iii)_____ research.","key":"ADG","groups":[["restrain","reveal","supersede"],["incursions of","efcfi acy of","restrictions on"],["corrupt","obviate","facilitate"]],"expl":"空1 restrain（约束）；空2 incursions of（侵入）；空3 corrupt（污染）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v54.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The latest publications predicting disastrous coastal erosion are unlikely to _____ knowledgeable readers because variations on the same claims have been effectively refuted in the past few years.","key":"BF","opts":["intrigue","reassure","baffle","alarm","unsettle","calm"],"expl":"reassure（使安心）：这些旧论点已被驳倒，不会让读者安心。选 BF"},{"id":"v54.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some social insects, such as bees and ants, are celebrated for their industriousness and engineering feat, but popular culture has not generally _____ termites for theirs—even though they can build mounds twenty feet high.","key":"CF","opts":["considered","reprehended","applauded","deprecated","exonerated","extolled"],"expl":"applauded（称赞）：白蚁的工程成就并未被普遍赞美。选 CF"},{"id":"v54.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because the organization often trumpeted itself as a forum for _____ discussion, visitors were startled by the frequently heated tone of its recent debates.","key":"CE","opts":["elevated","vigorous","temperate","strenuous","dispassionate","strident"],"expl":"strident（尖锐刺耳的）与 vigorous 对比 “平和讨论”的说法，此处。选 CE"},{"id":"v54.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many scholars studying leadership _____ cult of the celebrity that has been fostered both by the media and by politicians’ public relations staffs, arguing that it trivialized politics.","key":"BF","opts":["abet","decry","question","analyze","countenance","condemn"],"expl":"decry（谴责）：学者批评名人崇拜。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v54-2","title":"Test 54 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v54.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The monitoring is not _____: on the contrary, the defendant and his or her attorney are required to be given notice of the government’s listening activities.","key":"C","opts":["obtrusive","circumspect","surreptitious","adroit","meticulous"],"expl":"surreptitious（秘密的）与 obtrusive（显眼的）对立：监听并非秘密进行的。选 C"},{"id":"v54.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Even if the merits of the proposal are (i)_____, faculty members may be reluctant to (ii)_____, given their fear of offending the group that champions it.","key":"CD","groups":[["unparalleled","dubious","obvious"],["demur","approve","acquiesce"]],"expl":"空1 dubious（可疑的）；空2 demur（表示异议）。选 CD"},{"id":"v54.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Whatever the acknowledged (i)_____ of the market and the merits of considering ways to (ii)_____ them, implementing public policies toward this end entails the inevitable risk that those policies will simply create new deficiencies even as they address old ones.","key":"BD","groups":[["attractions","shortcomings","complexities"],["remedy","enhance","restore"]],"expl":"空1 shortcomings（缺陷）；空2 remedy（补救）。选 BD"},{"id":"v54.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"People accustomed to thinking that the human lifespan (i)_____ the outer bounds of animal longevity tend to dismiss tales of musket balls being found in the shells of living turtles. Samantha Romney, however, argues that while such stories may be (ii)_____, some turtles do indeed exhibit a phenomenon known as “negligible (iii)_____,” showing no signs of aging even as they pass the two-century mark.","key":"BDI","groups":[["belies","demarcates","antedates"],["apocryphal","authentic","heresy"],["rejuvenation","superannuation","senescence"]],"expl":"空1 belies（与……不符）；空2 apocryphal（伪托的）；空3 senescence（衰老）。negligible senescence 指无衰老迹象。选 BDI"},{"id":"v54.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Experimentation in the arts often generates befuddlement, and even _____ of innovative art generally have voiced perplexity regarding this new, experimental artwork.","key":"AC","opts":["proponents","vilifiers","defenders","belittlers","vendors","luminaries"],"expl":"luminaries（权威人士）与 defenders 都是有影响力的人，此处。选 AC"},{"id":"v54.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The sailors realized too late that winds had shifted the ice in such a way as to obstruct the ship’s path; this process had been so _____ that it was completed by the time they discovered the effect.","key":"AF","opts":["gradual","negligible","unpredictable","time-consuming","inconsequential","imperceptible"],"expl":"gradual（渐进的）与 imperceptible（难以察觉的）描述风向慢慢改变冰层。选 AF"},{"id":"v54.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"What makes the precisely oriented flight of a honeybee swarm to its new home so _____ is that only a small percentage of its members know the swarm travel route and final destination.","key":"CF","opts":["exact","unpredictable","amazing","erratic","reliable","wondrous"],"expl":"wondrous（奇妙的）与 amazing 描述蜂群飞行的精确性。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v55-1","title":"Test 55 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v55.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"When studying human history, one must be aware that the _____ between historical periods are arbitrary; certainly none of the people alive at the time were aware of a shift from one era to another.","key":"D","opts":["judgements","ideologies","innovations","demarcations","episodes"],"expl":"demarcations（界线）：历史时期之间的划分是人为的。选 D"},{"id":"v55.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Research note that wolves’ otherwise strongly hierarchical society is marked by occasional displays of populist (i)_____: if a pack leader proves a too-snappish tyrant, subordinate wolves will (ii)_____ the top cur.","key":"AD","groups":[["umbrage","expiation","torpor"],["collectively overthrow","eventually placate","quickly appraise"]],"expl":"空1 umbrage（怨恨）；空2 collectively overthrow（集体推翻）。选 AD"},{"id":"v55.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For a time in the early Middle Ages, Latin culture came close to (i)_____: the witness to that is the (ii)_____ of manuscript copies of texts datable to the period. The process of copying manuscripts, the only way in which the fragile products of centuries of accumulating knowledge could be preserved, (iii)_____, a situation that did not change for two and a half centuries, until the time of Charlemagne. In the intervening period, much of Classical literature was lost to use forever.","key":"CDI","groups":[["reversing","exploding","vanishing"],["paucity","provenance","proliferation"],["was pursued methodically","expressed the spirit of the time","virtually came to a standstill"]],"expl":"空1 vanishing（消失）；空2 paucity（稀少）；空3 virtually came to a standstill（几乎停滞）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v55.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The proposition that foraging Native Americans studied the skies is _____: anthropological evidence demonstrates, for example, that the Chumash Indians counted the lunar cycles and established the times of the solstices.","key":"BE","opts":["unquestionable","unremarkable","undeniable","unprecedented","unexceptional","unparalleled"],"expl":"unexceptional（不足为奇的）与 unremarkable 说明天文观察并不罕见。选 BE"},{"id":"v55.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the nineteenth century, the circus, for all its glitz and even its glamour, was entertainment with an old soul, _____ the fast-forward pace of change in modern life.","key":"BF","opts":["a forerunner of","an antidote to","a respite from","a break from","a precursor to","a rebuke to"],"expl":"an antidote to（解药）：马戏团是对快节奏变化的解药。选 BF"},{"id":"v55.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Sokari Douglas Camp was _____ in the early 1990s by many of London’s commercially driven art dealers and galleries, some of whom apparently found her themes difficult to market.","key":"DE","opts":["criticized","lionized","misrepresented","neglected","forsaken","eulogized"],"expl":"neglected（被冷落）：商业画廊不愿推广她的作品。选 DE"},{"id":"v55.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is troubling that blogs, which may be among the least reliable sources of information in human history, occupy such _____.","key":"BF","opts":["enviable `","conspicuous","suspect","dubious","controversial","prominent"],"expl":"suspect（可疑的）与 dubious 描述博客的可靠性，但语境要求“占据显要位置”，。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v55-2","title":"Test 55 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v55.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Although his friends insisted that his black garb was simply depressing, Peter felt just the opposite—that it gave him an air of upbeat, _____ maturity.","key":"E","opts":["melancholic","wearisome","salacious","aghast","urbane"],"expl":"urbane（温文尔雅的）与 upbeat maturity 形成正面描写。选 E"},{"id":"v55.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Throughout much of the twentieth century, common scientific sense seemed to dictate that animals could not make a choice based on rational or aesthetic criteria. Such choices were (i)_____ the mental capacity of humans. Scientists who (ii)_____ this animal-human cognitive division were often accused of anthropomorphism.","key":"AE","groups":[["reserved for","inconsistent with","similar to"],["accepted","transgressed","exacerbated"]],"expl":"空1 reserved for（专属于）；空2 transgressed（逾越）。选 AE"},{"id":"v55.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For many adults, the adolescent years occupy (i)_____ place in the memory, which to some degree is even quantifiable: give a grown adult a series of random prompts and cues, odds are he or she will recall (ii)_____ number of memories from adolescence.","key":"BD","groups":[["a peripheral","a privileged","an arbitrary"],["a disproportionate","a modest","an uncertain"]],"expl":"空1 a privileged（特权）；空2 a disproportionate（不成比例的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v55.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Barker’s account of how mores have evolved over time is illuminating. It reveals as (i)_____ and (ii)_____ some values that have often been regarded as (iii)_____, while uncovering other values that do indeed seem to be universal.","key":"AEH","groups":[["transient","instinctive","resilient"],["transcendent","relative","enduring"],["liberating","nonnegotiable","antiquated"]],"expl":"空1 transient（短暂的）；空2 transcendent（超越的）；空3 nonnegotiable（不可协商的）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v55.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Considering that space travel was science fiction only decades ago, we should be extremely reluctant to proclaim an idea forever technologically infeasible unless that idea _____ some hard physical constraint.","key":"AB","opts":["violates","contravenes","overcomes","transcends","utilizes","introduces"],"expl":"violates / contravenes 都表示违反物理限制。选 AB"},{"id":"v55.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The actor’s part in the film turned out to be _____: he had only one line, and by the time the film appeared in theaters, even that line had been removed.","key":"EF","opts":["misunderstood","mandatory","intriguing","fascinating","trivial","inessential"],"expl":"inessential（非必要的）与 trivial 描述角色微不足道。选 EF"},{"id":"v55.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although _____ to please his audiences, Mozart was, at the same time, fully aware of his musical genius and had no intention of compromising his music.","key":"DE","opts":["disposed","loath","disinclined","eager","keen","compelled"],"expl":"loath（不情愿的）与 disinclined 形成让步转折。原键 DE 对应 eager、keen，表示 Mozart 渴望取悦观众。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v56-1","title":"Test 56 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v56.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The actor’s performance was so absurdly _____ that Gwen felt a little ashamed to have to resort to tissues in the final scene.","key":"D","opts":["proficient","unfeasible","seditious","maudlin","accommodating"],"expl":"maudlin（伤感的）：表演过于煽情。选 D"},{"id":"v56.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the discussions on international patent law, many (i)_____ issues will probably be pushed far into the future. This cautious approach makes diplomatic sense, since attempts over the past 15 years to reach international agreements on patents have (ii)_____ just such sensitive issues.","key":"AF","groups":[["contentious","stimulating","subjective"],["approached","articulated","foundered on"]],"expl":"空1 contentious（有争议的）；空2 foundered on（在……上失败）。选 AF"},{"id":"v56.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Much of the newspapers readership found it hard to (i)_____ the allegations of venality laid against the superintendent, since these readers were still (ii)_____ the superintendents reputation for (iii)_____. The superintendents subsequent vindication will have come as no surprise to them.","key":"BDH","groups":[["ignore","credit","dismiss"],["swayed by","unaware of","learning about"],["grouchiness","probity","creativity"]],"expl":"空1 dismiss（不予理会）；空2 unaware of（不知道）；空3 probity（正直）。选 BDH"},{"id":"v56.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is true that science, and more particularly scientists, _____ cherished paradigms with great reluctance and that when they do, scientific revolutions may result.","key":"CF","opts":["unify","share","cede","embrace","dismantle","relinquish"],"expl":"cede（让出）与 relinquish（放弃）：科学家不愿放弃旧范式。选 CF"},{"id":"v56.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Patterson thought the waste leaking into the river was _____ situation: by contrast, judging from their silence on the matter, the owners of the factory felt the problem did not require immediate action.","key":"CE","opts":["a lingering","a convoluted","a pressing","an enervating","an exigent","an intricate"],"expl":"a pressing（紧迫的）与 exigent（迫切的）描述需要立即行动的状况。选 CE"},{"id":"v56.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some historians represent the East India Company as _____ participant in political and military conflict in India, only taking an interest in territorial power and revenue as a last-ditch effort to protect its trading activities.","key":"EF","opts":["a shrewd","an ineffectual","an irregular","a canny","a reluctant","an unwilling"],"expl":"an ineffectual（无效的）与 reluctant 形成对比。选 EF"},{"id":"v56.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Very few companies take the trouble to discover where the wood in their products originates, consumers do not demand this information, and consequently _____ regarding illicit timber has become the norm.","key":"BF","opts":["greed","indifference","outrage","timidity","apprehension","apathy"],"expl":"indifference（冷漠）与 apathy 描述对非法木材的态度。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v56-2","title":"Test 56 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v56.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"During the Renaissance, history was thought to be _____: it supplied instances of good and bad behavior in the past, thus informing the ethical precepts of the present.","key":"D","opts":["amoral","subjective","superfluous","exemplary","progressive"],"expl":"exemplary（可作为范例的）：历史提供善恶的范例。选 D"},{"id":"v56.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The report is admittedly (i)_____ : it is intended to suggest new lines of research rather than to deal with the subject in a (ii)_____ manner.","key":"AF","groups":[["sketchy","exculpatory","flippant"],["cavalier","deceptive","thorough"]],"expl":"空1 sketchy（粗略的）；空2 thorough（彻底的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v56.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Memoirs are inherently (i)_____, but Larry McMurtry’s volume of reminiscences about his life with books—not as a novelist but as a reader and bookstore owner—is especially (ii)_____: nearly every page sounds a note of farewell to an age of books that he sees as passing.","key":"BF","groups":[["unreliable","wistful","self-serving"],["whimsical","ungracious","valedictory"]],"expl":"空1 unreliable（不可靠的）；空2 valedictory（告别的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v56.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Persian prose writers from the second half of the twelfth century onward were characteristically (i)_____ the literary form of their works, a fact that some scholars have perceived as a derogation of those works’ content. It may be better interpreted as (ii)_____ the development of an awareness of authorship, for the awareness of authorship (iii)_____ the awareness of form.","key":"BEH","groups":[["ambivalent about","indifferent to","preoccupied with"],["a retreat from","an indication of","a justification for"],["evolves through","extends beyond","holds back"]],"expl":"空1 preoccupied with（专注于）；空2 an indication of（表明）；空3 extends beyond（超越）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v56.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientists are investigating odors so faint that people cannot _____ them in order to see whether such odors can nevertheless change the way people interact.","key":"EF","opts":["tolerate","endure","avoid","dispel","detect","discern"],"expl":"detect / discern 都表示察觉微弱气味。选 EF"},{"id":"v56.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The tribes’ _____ a settled mode of living was derived from their long-standing traditions, which, though differing from one tribal group to another, always included a resistance to nomadic lifestyles.","key":"BC","opts":["curiosity about","proclivity toward","predilection for","unfamiliarity with","rejection of","disdain for"],"expl":"predilection for（偏爱）：部落偏爱定居生活。选 BC"},{"id":"v56.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In politics, tactical calculations about which groups a candidate should appeal to are never pleasant, but they are not always _____, and sometimes they are necessary.","key":"BD","opts":["injudicious","sleazy","effective","sordid","useful","exceptional"],"expl":"injudicious（不明智的）与 effective 相对，但句意是“并非总是不明智”，故。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v57-1","title":"Test 57 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v57.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Many legislators who helped Roosevelt shape the New Deal _____ the fact that emerging social problems affected every segment of the population; nonetheless, they often acted with a view to aiding only their own constituents.","key":"C","opts":["disregarded","bemoaned","ignored","disputed","downplayed"],"expl":"ignored（忽视）：立法者忽视了问题影响全体民众。选 C"},{"id":"v57.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Federal efforts to regulate standards on educational achievements have been met by (i)_____ from the states; local governments feel that government imposition represents an undue infringement on their (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["receptivity","intransigence","compromise"],["autonomy","legislation","comportment"]],"expl":"空1 intransigence（不妥协）；空2 autonomy（自治）。选 BD"},{"id":"v57.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many researchers assume that politicians consider the preferences of the entire public, and not merely those of likely voters, when making decisions. Yet, since the desire to be reelected is central, it is plausible that politicians (i)_____ the opinions of likely voters in formulating their positions on issues. It is possible that researchers’ suppositions about policy makers’ (ii)_____ aggregate public opinion may serve to (iii)_____ the fact that only the preferences of likely voters actually matter.","key":"CDG","groups":[["rely insufcfi iently on","depart sporadically from","attend disproportionately to"],["responsiveness to","neglect of","misrepresentation of"],["mask","reflect","obviate"]],"expl":"空1 attend disproportionately to（过度关注）；空2 misrepresentation of（误读）；空3 obviate（使……无必要）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v57.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The spacecraft’s considerable heft forces an unusually _____ route that meanders through the solar system and depends on the gravitational pull of three heavenly bodies.","key":"BC","opts":["predetermined","circuitous","indirect","truncated","shortened","sequential"],"expl":"circuitous（迂回的）与 meanders 呼应。选 BC"},{"id":"v57.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"According to some political analysts, the candidate’s occasionally rambling responses to questions suggest that she has been out of circulation for a while and her debating skills need to be _____.","key":"AC","opts":["honed","discredited","enhanced","reevaluated","remedied","de-emphasized"],"expl":"honed（打磨）与 remedied（补救）。选 AC"},{"id":"v57.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Until 1992, microprocessor types were identified by number, and for a long time they were considered so _____ that manufacturers would share design specifications for them.","key":"AB","opts":["fungible","interchangeable","perishable","integral","inimitable","essential"],"expl":"fungible（可互换的）与 interchangeable 描述微处理器类型。选 AB"},{"id":"v57.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The apparent simplicity of savanna or a prairie landscape is illusory, but the illusion takes real effort to _____ because much of what actually occurs in these places takes place underground.","key":"AE","opts":["dispel","acknowledge","confirm","disavow","dismiss","perceive"],"expl":"perceive（察觉）：需要努力才能察觉表面之下的活动。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v57-2","title":"Test 57 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v57.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"One thing both authors have in common is a striking amount of _____: they claim to know how massive institutions, some of them richly endowed, all of them central to American society and culture, should be reshaped.","key":"A","opts":["hubris","propriety","bias","prescience","indolence"],"expl":"hubris（傲慢）：两位作者都自信地要改造机构。选 A"},{"id":"v57.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The company president’s reputation for unflappability could easily be understood upon observing her (i)_____ performance during a particularly (ii)_____ board meeting.","key":"CE","groups":[["supercilious","histrionic","composed"],["productive","contentious","lifeless"]],"expl":"空1 composed（镇定的）；空2 contentious（激烈争议的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v57.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the 1980s, many historians sounded urgent calls for (i)_____ in American historical writing, as longer and longer monographs on smaller subjects were being written—dazzling studies, but pieces of a puzzle no one was putting together. This scholarship was not illuminating the central themes of history but (ii)_____.","key":"CD","groups":[["indulgence","detail","synthesis"],["obscuring","criticizing","celebrating"]],"expl":"空1 detail（细节）；空2 obscuring（掩盖）。选 CD"},{"id":"v57.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Observers of modern presidential campaigns who (i)_____ the highly (ii)_____ productions that pass for campaigns these days do sometimes find reason for hope in the occasional mix-ups that (iii)_____ candidates on the trail despite the presence of political strategist’s plotting every event with the tactical precision of military commanders.","key":"CFG","groups":[["relish","misinterpret","despair over"],["ambitious","chaotic","choreographed"],["rattle","bolster","legitimate"]],"expl":"空1 despair over（为……沮丧）；空2 choreographed（编排好的）；空3 rattle（干扰）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v57.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Lustig’s critics argue that what makes him a compelling public speaker is his practice of citing evidence that is merely suggestive in support of a claim and insisting that this evidence is _____.","key":"CF","opts":["invaluable","irrelevant","indubitable","immaterial","insignificant","incontrovertible"],"expl":"incontrovertible（无可争议的）与 indubitable 呼应：把暗示性证据当作确凿证据。选 CF"},{"id":"v57.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The series of documentaries certainly does not promote the country’s recent diplomatic initiatives; in fact, some of the films appear to be _____ those initiatives.","key":"EF","opts":["commendations of","reparations of","tributes to","rationalizations of","denunciations of","indictments of"],"expl":"indictments of（控诉）：纪录片与外交政策形成对立。选 EF"},{"id":"v57.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"If Wilson’s article style changed overtime, it was in the wrong retrograde direction, _____ experimentation and inclining toward works that seemed hobbled by a fear of risk.","key":"BC","opts":["belaboring","shunning","eschewing","overemphasizing","misconstruing","mocking"],"expl":"shunning（回避）与 eschewing 描述避免尝试。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v58-1","title":"Test 58 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v58.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Since the deficit predicament is fundamentally a long-term problem, the legislature’s _____ short-term approaches has actually compounded the difficulty in each succeeding year, eroding the state credit rating in the process.","key":"C","opts":["vexation regarding","skepticism about","addiction to","wariness of","demonization of"],"expl":"addiction to（沉溺于）：立法机构沉迷于短期做法。选 C"},{"id":"v58.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"There has been (i)_____ elephant’s fabled mental capacities until recently, when these behavioral observations have begun to be (ii)____ by brain science. MRI scans of an elephant’s brain suggest that even relative to its overall size it has a large hippocampus, the component in the mammalian brain linked to memory and an important part of its limbic system, which is involved in precessing emotions.","key":"BD","groups":[["surprising credence given to","a widespread dismissal of","only anecdotal evidence for"],["buttressed","anticipated","overwhelmed"]],"expl":"空1 only anecdotal evidence for（仅有轶事证据）；空2 buttressed（支持）。选 BD"},{"id":"v58.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"However luminous an insight might seem initially, brilliance is not a reliable predictor of (i)_____, and sure enough the history of physical chemistry is replete with theories that were as (ii)_____ as any but that (iii)_____.","key":"CEH","groups":[["popularity","originality","validity"],["opaque","ingenious","useful"],["slowly developed","eventually collapsed","ultimately prevailed"]],"expl":"空1 validity（有效性）；空2 ingenious（巧妙的）；空3 eventually collapsed（最终崩溃）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v58.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Considering how difficult it is to prove or disprove the existence of life on Mars, which is practically our neighbor, it is quite _____ challenge to do the same for any Earthlike planets that might exist outside our solar system.","key":"AD","opts":["a formidable","an impossible","a hopeless","a daunting","an urgent","an immediate"],"expl":"formidable / daunting 都表示“艰巨的挑战”。选 AD"},{"id":"v58.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While it’s hard to know for sure, I suspect that the well-known authority’s silence on this contentious topic reflects the cautious _____ of a sensible scientist confronted with mixed data and mountains of speculation.","key":"AB","opts":["neutrality","impartiality","optimism","diffidence","commitment","buoyancy"],"expl":"neutrality（中立）与 diffidence（谨慎）描述权威对争议问题的沉默。选 AB"},{"id":"v58.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Very few companies take the trouble to discover where the wood in their products originate; consumers do not demand this information, and consequently _____ regarding illicit timber has become the norm.","key":"BF","opts":["greed","indifference","outrage","timidity","apprehension","apathy"],"expl":"apathy（冷漠）：消费者不关心，企业也不愿追查。选 BF"},{"id":"v58.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Humanity’s struggle with bedbugs is ______: archaeologists have recovered remains of the parasites dating back 3,500 years to the time of the Egyptian pharaohs.","key":"CF","opts":["disconcerting","unexceptional","perennial","preordained","inevitable","long-standing"],"expl":"perennial（长期存在的）与 long-standing 呼应：臭虫问题有 3500 年历史。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v58-2","title":"Test 58 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v58.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"His _____ speaking style notwithstanding, William Perkins has long been seen as the moderate face of his political party.","key":"E","opts":["genteel","mundane","affable","captivating","vehement"],"expl":"vehement（激烈的）与“温和派”形成让步关系。选 E"},{"id":"v58.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The novel’s heroine shows a remarkable (i)_____ to worship at the altar of youth; in her world, youth is (ii)_____, while age, by contrast, confers competence and wisdom.","key":"AF","groups":[["disinclination","desire","tendency"],["incredulous","sagacious","callow"]],"expl":"空1 tendency（倾向）；空2 callow（幼稚的）。女主角认为年轻=能力，年老才智慧。选 AF"},{"id":"v58.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Recently released statistics on the prevalence of heart disease in the United States, while (i)_____, nevertheless reflect a decline from heights reached in the 1960s, before health officials began publicly (ii)_____ people to guard against heart disease.","key":"BD","groups":[["definitive","sobering","implausible"],["entreating","defying","absolving"]],"expl":"空1 sobering（令人警醒的）；空2 entreating（恳请）。选 BD"},{"id":"v58.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many historians of the ancient world are wary of sounding (i)_____. Write so much as a sentence and the temptation is immediately to (ii)_____ it. Even in cases when the sources for a given event are (iii)_____, uncertainties and discrepancies crop up everywhere.","key":"CFH","groups":[["fusty","anachronistic","dogmatic"],["recapitulate","forswear","qualify"],["consistent","plentiful","biased"]],"expl":"空1 dogmatic（武断的）；空2 qualify（加以限定）；空3 biased（有偏差的）。选 CFH"},{"id":"v58.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The composer’s string quartets exhibit a structural ______ that seems to challenge the conventions of the string quartet genre, which have long been celebrated for their rigor and coherence.","key":"CF","opts":["austerity","restraint","uncertainty","ostentation","vitality","instability"],"expl":"austerity（朴素、严谨）与“挑战传统”的结构相符。选 CF"},{"id":"v58.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is _____ and rather, surprising, for someone with a considerable background in philosophy, that Taylor fails to distinguish adequately between forms of communication and forms of knowledge.","key":"AC","opts":["reprehensible","inexplicable","deplorable","dangerous","typical","characteristic"],"expl":"inexplicable（难以解释的）与 surprising 呼应。选 AC"},{"id":"v58.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As a proponent of women’s traditional roles, Sarah Hale was adamant against women’s suffrage as thrusting women into an improper sphere; yet she _____ female textile strikers when they publicly protested their mistreatment at miles.","key":"BD","opts":["opposed","supported","criticized","championed","challenged","welcomed"],"expl":"championed（支持、拥护）：她支持女工的抗议。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v59-1","title":"Test 59 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v59.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Like her literary heroine, George Eliot, Barbara Kingsolvers is an old-fashioned _____, deeply curious about all branches of human learning.","key":"B","opts":["prodigy","polymath","tyro","ante","philistine"],"expl":"polymath（博学者）与 Eliot 作为知识广博的作家相符。选 B"},{"id":"v59.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"I knew well, from experience with hundreds of hired crew members on her boats, how (i)_____ attitudes can be: how one negative influence can impel an otherwise (ii)_____ member of a crew to quit.","key":"BF","groups":[["insipid","infectious","innocuous"],["untested","captious","contented"]],"expl":"空1 infectious（有感染力的）；空2 contented（满足的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v59.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"His new role gives the normally clownish actor a chance to impress audiences with his (i)_____. He is among the most uninhibited comic performers around, but here he buttons his lip and stares straight ahead. Perhaps without quite knowing it, the audience waits for a wink, a hint that some of the (ii)_____ spirit that animated his previous movies might be lurking inside the (iii)_____ manner he presents in this film.","key":"CDH","groups":[["raillery","effusiveness","forbearance"],["madcap","lugubrious","edifying"],["facetious","reserved","beguiling"]],"expl":"空1 forbearance（克制）；空2 lugubrious（阴郁的）；空3 reserved（拘谨的）。他平时很放纵，这次却收敛，观众期待一丝旧日的疯劲。选 CDH"},{"id":"v59.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since Venus and Earth are so similar in their mass and density, Mueller suggested that the two planets have similar compositions and, therefore there must be surface features on Venus that have terrestrial _____.","key":"CD","opts":["causes","consequences","counterparts","parallels","properties","outcomes"],"expl":"counterparts（对应物）：地球上的地貌在金星上有对应物。选 CD"},{"id":"v59.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It turns out that the seeming spontaneity of his letter actually involved a good deal of _____: the writer carefully revises them before mailing them, and he worked hard to establish the right tone.","key":"AF","opts":["deliberation","whimsicality","inventiveness","effort","capriciousness","consideration"],"expl":"deliberation（深思熟虑）与 effort 描述信件的刻意设计。选 AF"},{"id":"v59.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is _____ quality to Beryl Bainbridge’s best novels, what Hilary Martel calls “an air of mystery, as if something has been inked in and then sponged away, leaving a faint trace for the reader to pick up”.","key":"BE","opts":["an elegiac","a cryptic","a deceptive","a plaintive","an elusive","a mesmerizing"],"expl":"an elusive（难以捉摸的）与 cryptic（隐晦的）描述 Bainbridge 小说的神秘感。选 BE"},{"id":"v59.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Another challenge to biologists and land-use planners alike is that while human-induced changes to the landscape are somethings _____, they can nevertheless drastically alter the habitat for some plants and animals.","key":"EF","opts":["indisputable","inappropriate","unacceptable","unfathomable","imperceptible","indiscernible"],"expl":"imperceptible（难以察觉的）：人为改变可能难以察觉，却能显著改变栖息地。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v59-2","title":"Test 59 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v59.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Physicists’ opinions diverge on whether the unexpected phenomena that can occur in systems more complex than individual particles represent new physical principles, or whether the principles involved are _____, in that they rely, albeit in an extremely complicated way, on known physical principles.","key":"C","opts":["extraneous","inexpressible","derivative","heterogeneous","uncorrelated"],"expl":"derivative（派生的）：这些现象依赖已知原理，属于派生性质。选 C"},{"id":"v59.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The question whether children like sweetener or not is (i)_____. Of course children like sweetener, which is (ii)_____ to sellers, since children’s taste will not change once they are used to a certain brand.","key":"BE","groups":[["debated","decided","overlooked"],["a pragmatic solution","a commercial advantage","an idealistic conception"]],"expl":"空1 debated（有争议的）；空2 a commercial advantage（商业优势）。选 BE"},{"id":"v59.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The new drug was useful, but unfortunately its effect was largely (i)_____ rather than (ii)_____.","key":"BE","groups":[["placatory","palliative","addictive"],["immediate","curative","mollifying"]],"expl":"空1 palliative（缓解性的）；空2 curative（治愈性的）。药物只缓解症状而非治愈。选 BE"},{"id":"v59.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some climatologists dismiss as (i)_____ the debate among geophysicists over the role of carbon dioxide in global climate change across many millions of years. These climatologists say the evidence of a tie between carbon dioxide and planetary warming over the last few centuries is so (ii)_____ that any longer-term evidence against such a link must somehow be (iii)______.","key":"BFG","groups":[["unavoidable","irrelevant","undecidable"],["unlikely","controversial","compelling"],["tainted","accommodated","reinforced"]],"expl":"空1 irrelevant（无关紧要的）；空2 compelling（令人信服的）；空3 accommodated（被容纳、解释）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v59.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While merchants and bankers in thirteen-century Europe quickly embraced the Hindu-Arabic numeral system, the governing authorities were less _____ it.","key":"CF","opts":["persuaded by","guarded about","captivated by","open-minded about","inhibited about","enamored of"],"expl":"enamored of（热爱）与 captivated by 描述政府不情愿接受阿拉伯数字。选 CF"},{"id":"v59.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It’s true that occasional _____ entries might have been edited without damaging the diary’s overall impact, but the very completeness of Clara’s eloquent reflections conveys a strong sense of the density of a young woman’s experiences.","key":"AC","opts":["verbose","redundant","long-winded","curt","mundane","laconic"],"expl":"verbose / long-winded 描述冗长条目，可以删去而不损害日记整体效果。选 AC"},{"id":"v59.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Berwick, middle-aged, soft-spoken, and _____, with a keen sense of how to use this apparent ordinariness to his advantage, began with a gripping story about how a firefighter saved himself during a forest fire by using a completely improbable tactic.","key":"DE","opts":["imperturbable","implacable","unimaginative","unprepossessing","unremarkable","unruffled"],"expl":"unprepossessing（不起眼的）与 ordinariness 呼应。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v60-1","title":"Test 60 · Section 1","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v60.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In an ironic twist, the recent _____ of the reductive observational methods that have enabled science to progress for four centuries may turn out to be science’s biggest step forward.","key":"E","opts":["introduction","validation","acceptance","standardization","questioning"],"expl":"questioning（质疑）：还原式观察方法的质疑。选 E"},{"id":"v60.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In reviewing cases decided by lower courts, Supreme Court justices search for precedents to justify their arguments. Reliance on precedent (i)_____ judicial restraint: the precedent (ii)_____ a judge’s ability to determine the outcome of a case in a way that he or she might choose if there were no precedent.","key":"AE","groups":[["promotes","compromises","promulgates"],["establishes","constrains","prioritizes"]],"expl":"空1 compromises（削弱）；空2 constrains（限制）。先例约束法官的判断。选 AE"},{"id":"v60.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Part of what currently makes it so (i)_____ to arrive at a scientific understanding of the living world is that while technological advances have produced a cascade of data—from detailed genome sequence to the sophisticated satellite imagery that documents the planet’s ecosystems— our ability to (ii)_____ these data still lags far behind their (iii)_____.","key":"CEG","groups":[["frustrating","intriguing","challenging"],["gather","apprehend","dispute"],["acquisition","interpretation","implementation"]],"expl":"空1 frustrating（令人沮丧的）；空2 apprehend（理解）；空3 interpretation（解读）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v60.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because the literary club often trumpeted itself as a sanctuary for temperate discussion, visitors were startled by the frequently _____ tone of its recent debates.","key":"CE","opts":["blunt","ingratiating","acerbic","unctuous","vitriolic","bombastic"],"expl":"vitriolic（充满怨毒的）与 acerbic 都与“平和讨论”对立，。选 CE"},{"id":"v60.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Contrary to popular myth, cockroaches are not especially tough or radiation resistant; indeed, they are pretty _____ as insects go.","key":"BD","opts":["harmless","average","strong","undistinguished","weak","hardy"],"expl":"undistinguished（平庸的）：蟑螂在昆虫中并不突出。选 BD"},{"id":"v60.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientific discovery calls for a difficult balance: intrepid advocacy of new ideas must often be _____ by the results of self-imposed trials.","key":"AB","opts":["tempered","moderated","unhampered","preempted","superseded","prefaced"],"expl":"tempered（节制）与 moderated 表示大胆倡导需要实验约束。选 AB"},{"id":"v60.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Reuters are not against _____ noteworthy architecture but suggests a cap on the amount to be protected at any one time: if you want to protect another ancient building, one should come off the list.","key":"AF","opts":["preserving","rehabilitating","promoting","restoring","emulating","safeguarding"],"expl":"preserving / safeguarding 表示保护有价值的建筑。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v60-2","title":"Test 60 · Section 2","group":"Test 51–60","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v60.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even though the municipal government was not totally _____ the positive review of the charter, the mayor nevertheless decided to veto the laws.","key":"B","opts":["garrulous about","enthusiastic about","sanguine about","approbatory to","unsympathetic with"],"expl":"sanguine about（乐观看待）：市政府并非完全看好宪章，故。选 B"},{"id":"v60.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"To abolish the existence of nation-states is neither feasible nor desirable; but insofar as there are collective interests that transcend national boundaries, the (i)_____ of nation-states must be (ii)_____ to international institutions.","key":"AD","groups":[["sovereignty","traditions","genealogy"],["subordinated","attributable","analogous"]],"expl":"空1 sovereignty（主权）；空2 subordinated（服从）。选 AD"},{"id":"v60.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The virtual absence of cougars from late prehistoric faunas in the North American Great Basin (i)_____ a general scarcity of carnivores from these sites: bobcats, coyotes, and badgers are routinely found, and even such historically (ii)_____ carnivores as bears and wolves are found as well.","key":"BE","groups":[["largely parallels","does not reflect","is a consequence of"],["widespread","rare","representative"]],"expl":"空1 does not reflect（不反映）；空2 rare（罕见的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v60.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Since the 1920s, historical fiction writers in China have emancipated the genre from the traditional notion that (i)_____ was the ultimate goal of history writing. Yet the traditional commitment to (ii)_____ was not simply (iii)_____: this new genre was expected to capture the essence of historical truth even as it allowed space for the writer’s imagination.","key":"BDG","groups":[["comprehensiveness","factuality","entertainment"],["veracity","thoroughness","pleasure"],["jettisoned","rationalized","acknowledged"]],"expl":"历史小说允许想象空间，但仍坚持历史真实：传统上对 veracity（真实性）的坚持并非被 jettisoned（抛弃），而是被保留。选 BDG"},{"id":"v60.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Jaime Javier Rodriguez notes that popular art forms often conceal a daunting complexity: frequently what appears _____ becomes intricate and challenging when closely examined.","key":"BF","opts":["tedious","canned","convoluted","vacuous","tortuous","formulaic"],"expl":"formulaic（公式化的）与 tedious 描述表面简单的流行艺术。选 BF"},{"id":"v60.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many theorists believe that measures to prevent industrial pollution necessarily increase production costs, but several recent reports document innovations that _____ environmental harm while also delivering economic benefits.","key":"DE","opts":["offset","preclude","disclose","mitigate","curtail","divulge"],"expl":"mitigate（减轻）：创新减少环境危害并带来经济利益。选 DE"},{"id":"v60.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A closer examination of the author’s footnotes explains the datedness of his argument: he has ignored most of the recent work in the field, drawing instead mainly on research that is now decidedly _____.","key":"CF","opts":["familiar","germane","obsolete","relevant","discredited","outmoded"],"expl":"obsolete（过时的）与 outmoded 呼应。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v61-1","title":"Test 61 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v61.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"By deliberately dripping paint on their canvases, expressionists affirmed that paint is not _____ entity, something merely to be moved where the artist please, but rather a material possessing a fluid energy that the painter attempts to control.","key":"D","opts":["an immutable","an expressive","a vital","a passive","a kinetic"],"expl":"passive（被动的）：颜料不是被动的实体。选 D"},{"id":"v61.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Interest in creating handheld computers is fueled by the desire to shrink the size of the electronic circuitry and to create exceptionally small mechanical systems. At this scale, however, physical (i)_____ poses unique challenges. Machining, positioning, and assembling parts by hand are easy at macroscopic scales but at minute scales they are far from (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["deterioration","manipulation","durability"],["subtle","inflexible","routine"]],"expl":"空1 deterioration（磨损）；空2 routine（常规的）。微尺度下操作远非常规。选 BF"},{"id":"v61.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The journey to (i)_____, when it starts from a vantage as (ii)_____ as Dunsany’s, is often as (iii)_____ as the path to glory. How did a writer of such talent and renown wind up nearly forgotten?","key":"ADG","groups":[["obscurity","normalcy","genius"],["eminent","reactionary","egalitarian"],["unfathomable","cyclical","mundane"]],"expl":"空1 obscurity（默默无闻）；空2 eminent（杰出的）；空3 mundane（平凡的）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v61.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The environmental threat posed by the New Zealand mud snail, an invasive species, is _____ by the snail’s small size, which facilitates its spread across watersheds through human activity.","key":"CF","opts":["initiated","ameliorated","exacerbated","extenuated","mitigated","aggravated"],"expl":"exacerbated（加剧）：小体型使其更易扩散。选 CF"},{"id":"v61.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the Kuiper Belt—the icy region of the solar system where Pluto orbits—was once much more crowded, today it has such a low density of objects that collisions between them are _____.","key":"DF","opts":["inconsequential","ongoing","unthinkable","improbable","continuous","unlikely"],"expl":"improbable（不太可能的）：碰撞概率很低。选 DF"},{"id":"v61.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Williams finds the appearance of Whitman’s Leaves of Grass in 1855 nearly _____ given the immense disparity between Whitman’s earlier published works, which Williams finds dismal, and the consummate mastery of Leaves.","key":"DF","opts":["oracular","prophetic","inevitable","inexplicable","inauspicious","incomprehensible"],"expl":"inexplicable（难以解释的）：从前作到《草叶集》的跨越令人费解。选 DF"},{"id":"v61.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Carr insists that the so-called information society might be more accurately described as the interruption society: it _____ attention, the scarcest of all resources, and stuffs the mind trivia.","key":"DE","opts":["guards","protects","diverts","destroys","annihilates","transcends"],"expl":"diverts（转移）：信息社会分散了注意力。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v61-2","title":"Test 61 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v61.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It is often argued that psychoanalysis, which was _____ at that stage of the eighteenth century, provided the main filter by which death could be looked at, but it has now been largely replaced by medicine, which provides both a mindset and practical measures by which death may be cheated, and in terminal illness, approached, formulating a process called medicalization.","key":"A","opts":["predominant","pompous","precarious","elegant","mundane"],"expl":"predominant（占主导的）：精神分析曾是主要过滤器。选 A"},{"id":"v61.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The introductions to each section, written by the editors of the anthology, provide useful background material, but they do not provide analysis of the articles. Because the articles are in many senses the editors’ personal favorites, it is probably (i)_____ to expect more such criticism would be as (ii)_____ as the articles themselves.","key":"CD","groups":[["juvenile","paradoxical","unrealistic"],["biased","complex","informative"]],"expl":"空1 unrealistic（不现实的）；空2 biased（有偏见的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v61.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Reviews written by music critic and composer Stephenson were hardly (i)_____ : musicians who performed his music could count on sympathetic coverage, while those who ignored him were held to (ii)_____ standards.","key":"AD","groups":[["disinterested","lucid","conventional"],["exacting","minimal","accepted"]],"expl":"空1 disinterested（不偏不倚的）；空2 exacting（苛刻的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v61.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"At least one otter species, the sea otter, has a large, often dominating, effect on the structure of its own habitat. There is no evidence that other species have ever exercised such (i)_____ effects. That lack of evidence could merely be because the other species have been studied less thoroughly. However, the size and density of the historic sea otter populations in many Pacific coastal regions (ii)_____ those of other otter species elsewhere, so perhaps the sea otter is indeed (iii)_____ in its effects on habitat.","key":"CDG","groups":[["ephemeral","unpredictable","significant"],["vastly exceed","have little efef ct on","roughly parallel"],["unique","destructive","transitory"]],"expl":"空1 significant（重大的）；空2 roughly parallel（大致相当）；空3 unique（独特的）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v61.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Of all the singer’s works, this album is the most dependent on the musical conventions of her day; it was both the least _____ of her albums and the most commercially successful.","key":"CD","opts":["personal","well-known","experimental","innovative","acclaimed","recognizable"],"expl":"最依赖当时音乐惯例的专辑应是“最不具实验性”的，同时又最畅销，故。选 CD"},{"id":"v61.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The environmental advocacy group pushed for a single, overarching wetlands management plan that would _____ the existing efforts of various entities, resulting in a focused blueprint for saving the area’s wetlands.","key":"AB","opts":["combine","meld","undermine","spearhead","support","subvert"],"expl":"combine / meld 表示整合现有努力。选 AB"},{"id":"v61.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Nature-loving pilgrims from the eastern United States altered the country’s attitude toward California’s sequoia groves, transforming those stands of great trees from scientific curiosities to places of _____.","key":"CE","opts":["recreation","mystery","veneration","solitude","reverence","acclamation"],"expl":"veneration（崇敬）与 reverence 描述人们对红杉的态度。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v62-1","title":"Test 62 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v62.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"She demonstrates a great extent of _____, as she has traveled to many more countries and places around the world than any of her kindred.","key":"B","opts":["perfidiousness","peregrination","jubilation","sagaciousness","conspicuousness"],"expl":"peregrination（远游）与“去过很多国家”呼应。选 B"},{"id":"v62.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The laser has been widely utilized in many industries such as the packaging industry, CD player manufacturing, and all sorts of commonplace articles; however, the (i)_____ of the laser doesn’t mean the laser can only be used in (ii)_____ ways.","key":"CE","groups":[["rare extermination","sporadic usage","everyday presence"],["assorted","pedestrian","pointless"]],"expl":"空1 everyday presence（日常存在）；空2 pedestrian（平庸的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v62.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For many years Cole experienced (i)_____ his professional circle. He was a (ii)_____ figure in the Middle East Studies Association of North America, editing for five years its flagship publication, and in 2004 he was even elected the association’s incoming president. But because his research focused on highly (iii)_____ aspects of the eighteenth-and-nineteenth century Middle East, he was unlikely to achieve any sort of public acclaim.","key":"CDH","groups":[["obscurity within","estrangement from","anonymity outside"],["leading","provocative","traditional"],["relevant","esoteric","disputed"]],"expl":"空1 obscurity within（在圈内默默无闻）；空2 leading（主要的）；空3 esoteric（深奥的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v62.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Established scientists recognize that peer review of manuscripts submitted to scientific journals is critical to science, but this recognition _____ a certain ambivalence in them, since reviewing takes time away from their research.","key":"CE","opts":["obviates","mitigates","engenders","tempers","induces","exacerbates"],"expl":"engenders（产生）：同行评审在科学家心中引发矛盾心理。选 CE"},{"id":"v62.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite ______ leaving their old jobs behind, workers were eager to move because there were to be no layoffs under the union contract at the new location.","key":"CE","opts":["jubilation over","indifference to","misgivings about","outrage over","trepidation over","enthusiasm for"],"expl":"misgivings about（疑虑）：工人疑虑离开旧工作，但期待新地点。选 CE"},{"id":"v62.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"After the Turkish Republic was established, traditional hamams (bathhouses) seemed to many Turks to be outmoded, but thanks to tourism, hamams have experienced a _____, becoming important cultural sites for foreign and Turkish visitors alike.","key":"DF","opts":["proliferation","retrenchment","transformation","revival","slump","renaissance"],"expl":"revival（复兴）与 renaissance 描述土耳其浴室的回潮。选 DF"},{"id":"v62.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In spite of her fascination with chance, coincidence, and contingency, Stanning’s novels are _____ constructed, written from the head rather than the heart.","key":"CD","opts":["hastily","extravagantly","painstakingly","meticulously","evocatively","impulsively"],"expl":"painstakingly / meticulously 描述小说的精心构造。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v62-2","title":"Test 62 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v62.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"People who are reluctant to oppose a court nominee straightforwardly on ideological grounds often search for any sort of peccadillo to serve as a _____ their opposition.","key":"E","opts":["mitigation of","violation of","predictor of","reparation for","pretext for"],"expl":"pretext for（借口）：以小过失作为反对的借口。选 E"},{"id":"v62.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The strategists who created the European Unions practiced piecemeal social engineering. Recognizing that perfection is (i)_____, they set limited objectives and then mobilize the political will for a small step forward knowing full well that when they achieved it, its (ii)_____ would become apparent and necessitate further measures.","key":"AE","groups":[["unattainable","salubrious","bromidic"],["potential","inadequacy","mutability"]],"expl":"空1 unattainable（不可达到的）；空2 inadequacy（不足）。选 AE"},{"id":"v62.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Britain’s Queen Victoria, however (i)_____ she had been at the beginning of her reign, was politically much more (ii)_____ by the end of her time on the throne, as she resigned herself to the emergence of an increasing powerful electorate that prevented her from stubbornly insisting on getting her own way in matters of state.","key":"CF","groups":[["naïve","personable","obdurate"],["powerful","arbitrary","malleable"]],"expl":"空1 naive（天真的）；空2 malleable（易受影响的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v62.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"At a recent conference on ancient DNA, one presentation opened with the claim that the field was now mature and could move ahead with confidence. This (i)_____ is (ii)_____, as demonstrated at the conference by the many presentations that notably lacked an adequate methodology for ensuring that DNA was uncontaminated by material that is more recent. In fact, ancient DNA research presents extreme technical difficulties, in part precisely because of the (iii)_____ of surviving DNA.","key":"BEG","groups":[["concern","optimism","diffidence"],["infectious","unfounded","unusual"],["corrupted nature","straight forward","copious amounts"]],"expl":"空1 optimism（乐观）；空2 unfounded（没有根据的）；空3 corrupted nature（受污染的性质）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v62.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although traditionally artists have rightly been seen as the most _____ audience for the work of their colleagues, today taste is also created by critics and curators and occasionally by collectors.","key":"CF","opts":["arbitrary","volatile","perceptive","impulsive","subjective","discerning"],"expl":"discerning（有鉴别力的）：艺术家通常是最有眼光的观众。选 CF"},{"id":"v62.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Every serious attempt at a historical portrait of the past will subtly absorb the milieu and temperament of its living author, however _____ he or she sets out to be.","key":"CF","opts":["entertaining","comprehensive","objective","engaging","rigorous","impartial"],"expl":"无论作者多么想做到 objective（客观）或 impartial（公正），其时代气质仍会渗入历史画像。选 CF"},{"id":"v62.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although we no longer have to rely on salt to keep food from spoiling, our appetite for it is _____: most people eat much more salt than they need.","key":"CE","opts":["involuntary","inconstant","unabated","unpredictable","undiminished","insatiable"],"expl":"unabated（不减的）与 insatiable 描述对盐的欲望未减。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v63-1","title":"Test 63 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v63.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Although Emily Bronte is impassioned about gender equality, she is anything but ___ to endorse more privileges endowed to women.","key":"A","opts":["zealous","apathetic","abhorrent","stubborn","lethargic"],"expl":"虽然主张性别平等，却对给女性更多特权毫无热情，apathetic（冷漠的）最贴切。选 A"},{"id":"v63.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Earlier discussions with neighboring countries (i)_____ due to the government’s failure to alter policies that those countries find objectionable. Moreover, there is every reason to (ii)_____ the success of further talks, since the government if anything different, more intransigent.","key":"CD","groups":[["commenced","advanced","foundered"],["doubt","undermine","anticipate"]],"expl":"空1 foundered（失败）；空2 doubt（怀疑）。选 CD"},{"id":"v63.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Anthony Kenny states that although his A New History of Western Philosophy is intended for undergraduates, he aimed to write it in a lighthearted manner that will give (i)_____ to those who read the history “not for curricular purposes but for their own enjoyment”. His book is certainly enlightening, and although the bibliography includes technical works liable to (ii)_____ the newcomer, the work is written at a level that generally (iii)_____ between elementary and advanced.","key":"BDG","groups":[["solace","pleasure","ofef nse"],["baffle","initiate","suit"],["strikes a good balance","makes fine distinctions","rejects the difference"]],"expl":"空1 solace（安慰）；空2 baffle（使困惑）；空3 strikes a good balance（取得平衡）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v63.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Precipitation is not _____ in the Atacama Desert west of Andes mountains, and water scarcity is compounded by problems with water appropriation, the existence of agro pastoralists is in jeopardy.","key":"AD","opts":["regular","negligible","evident","consistent","insignificant","abundant"],"expl":"句意是降水并不规律，故 regular（规律的）与 consistent 处于相反方向，此处。选 AD"},{"id":"v63.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"What differentiates this book from more traditional works on grammar is that it reserves its _____ not for students of writing, bur for teachers who harbor unduly restrictive views.","key":"CE","opts":["mockery","skepticism","scolding","approbation","admonishment","commendation"],"expl":"这本书对那些持过度严格观点的老师给予的是斥责（scolding）与训斥（admonishment）。选 CE"},{"id":"v63.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Like ants’ propensity to congregate on one food pile and neglect another, the human tendency to make choices that _____ the observed behavior of others is a self-reinforcing process.","key":"AD","opts":["imitate","confirm","avoid","emulate","inhibit","constrain"],"expl":"imitate / emulate 描述模仿他人选择。选 AD"},{"id":"v63.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The difficulty of reforming electoral politics is not lack of right tools but the need to put them into the hands of impartial agents: the goal should be to build capacity while _____ partisanship.","key":"BD","opts":["expediting","constraining","facilitating","deterring","exacerbating","lamenting"],"expl":"constraining（约束）与 deterring（阻止）描述限制党派偏见。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v63-2","title":"Test 63 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v63.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The chairman, faced with the need to forge a consensus on a number of proposals, acknowledged that it would be difficult to reconcile the push for a radical overhaul with the stance of those who want _____ change.","key":"A","opts":["deliberate","indiscriminate","genuine","immediate","wholesale"],"expl":"wholesale（全面的）与 radical 形成对照。选 A"},{"id":"v63.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"As cheaper imports drove most California potteries out of business during the 1950s, one company (i)_____. The substantial size and weight of the specialized products produced by Architectural Pottery helped (ii)_____ the company, because it was uneconomical for foreign companies to ship similarly large objects to California.","key":"CE","groups":[["stagnated","diversified","flourished"],["transform","insulate","finance"]],"expl":"空1 flourished（繁荣）；空2 insulate（保护）。选 CE"},{"id":"v63.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Each new generation of students grow up (i)_____ the world of classical physics, with its mostly intuitive, billiard-ball causality; that is the everyday vantage from which we approach the alien world of quantum physics, which has for this reason never lost its air of (ii)_____.","key":"AF","groups":[["immersed in","disdainful of","unmoved by"],["verisimilitude","objectivity","radicalism"]],"expl":"空1 immersed in（沉浸于）；空2 verisimilitude（逼真性）。选 AF"},{"id":"v63.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Substantial atmosphere around planetary bodies acts as (i)_____ incoming objects. Smaller objects, particularly those that are lower in density and more fragile, (ii)_____ in the upper reaches of the atmosphere, whereas more intact, larger bodies may survive to impact the surface. Thus, relative to large craters, small craters are much less (iii)_____ on bodies with dense atmosphere, such as Earth, Venus, and Titan, than they are on Mercury and Moon.","key":"BDI","groups":[["effective obscurers of","significant filters to","impenetrable barriers against"],["vaporize","proliferate","agglomerate"],["unusual","persistent","common"]],"expl":"空1 effective obscurers of（有效遮挡）；空2 vaporize（汽化）；空3 common（常见的）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v63.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"When it comes to arriving at brilliant ideas, filtering out distractions might well be _____: if a person’s mind is wandering, that person tends to outperform peers in a range of tasks in which flashes of insight are important.","key":"EF","opts":["indispensable","irrelevant","overrated","imperative","deleterious","counterproductive"],"expl":"counterproductive（适得其反的）：过滤干扰反而不利于产生灵感。选 EF"},{"id":"v63.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Matsui is an extremely _____ political tactician, as she generally will withhold her support for a political faction or a policy until she is confident it will prevail.","key":"CE","opts":["successful","dogmatic","shrewd","flexible","canny","rigid"],"expl":"shrewd（精明的）与 canny（老练的）描述她谨慎表态、待胜算明朗才支持的策略。选 CE"},{"id":"v63.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is ample evidence that men and women think, express themselves, and even experience emotions differently, but in the area of sensory perception, psychologists are hard-pressed to identify major _____.","key":"CE","opts":["difficulties","innovations","discrepancies","challenges","incongruities","trends"],"expl":"空缺处为“感官知觉上难以找出重大的……”，discrepancies（差异）最合适。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v64-1","title":"Test 64 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v64.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The stars’ attitudes toward their glowing press are diametrically opposed: some think it _____ and others take the adulation seriously.","key":"A","opts":["flummery","consequential","fanatical","coincidental","sincere"],"expl":"flummery（空洞的奉承）与“对媒体的热捧”态度相对，一些明星视之为虚饰。选 A"},{"id":"v64.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Up to the 1970s, histories of science tended to be (i)_____ not least in their focus on discoveries and theories that could be read as anticipating later scientific orthodoxies, rather than on those deemed (ii)_____ in their own periods. Historians of science are now routinely far more sensitive on such scores.","key":"AD","groups":[["anachronistic","convoluted","undogmatic"],["major","fallacious","inessential"]],"expl":"空1 anachronistic（以今律古的）；空2 major（重要的）。过去的科学史偏重“预示后来正统”的发现。选 AD"},{"id":"v64.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"An invasive creeping weed native to the Mediterranean region, Cirsium arvense has been present in Yellowstone National Park at least since the nineteen century. Because of its extensive root system, the plant defies attempts to (i)_____ it by normal methods, and consequently, park officials have (ii)_____ efforts to do so. Warming temperature have also (iii)_____ of the thistle’s fortune.","key":"ADG","groups":[["control","study","nourish"],["largely abandoned","recently reinitiated","increasingly promoted"],["helped","undermined","illuminated"]],"expl":"空1 control（控制）；空2 largely abandoned（大体放弃）；空3 undermined（削弱）。温度升高反而有利于蓟草生长。选 ADG"},{"id":"v64.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Robbins’ accomplishment is not _____ one: her book makes the topic accessible to a general audience while still providing the sort of analysis that scholars demand.","key":"AD","opts":["a trivial","a fascinating","a questionable","an insignificant","an intriguing","an amusing"],"expl":"trivial / insignificant 与“兼顾通俗与分析”的成就相反，应为“并非一件小事”。选 AD"},{"id":"v64.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"We should be more ______ than we often are when making claims about antiquity—for example, the common statement, “The ancient Athenians invented democracy,” is simply not true when put like that.","key":"AF","opts":["skeptical","credulous","precise","trusting","equivocal","circumspect"],"expl":"skeptical（怀疑的）与 circumspect（审慎的）：对古代的说法应更谨慎。选 AF"},{"id":"v64.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author advocates a diminished role for philosophy, aiming to show that many of the questions traditionally debated among philosophers can be ______ the realm of scientific inquiry.","key":"AF","opts":["ceded to","inferred from","relevant to","initiated by","germane to","left to"],"expl":"ceded to（让渡给）：许多哲学问题可以让渡给科学研究。选 AF"},{"id":"v64.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"With regard to verity, neutrality, and transparency, nothing about the Internet makes it any different than Gutenberg’s printing press, which could serve ______ just as well as truth.","key":"DE","opts":["fantasy","bureaucracy","protocol","disinformation","mendacity","panic"],"expl":"disinformation（虚假信息）：印刷术和互联网都可能服务于虚假信息。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v64-2","title":"Test 64 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v64.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Studies of hermaphroditic plants may exhibit sampling bias against self-fertilizing and cross-fertilizing species, thus inflating the frequency of species using a mixed mating system (both self-fertilizing and cross-fertilizing); nevertheless the number of mixed-system species is not _____.","key":"C","opts":["self-evident","static","trivial","relevant","calculable"],"expl":"trivial（微不足道的）：混合交配系统的物种数量并不少，故不是微不足道。选 C"},{"id":"v64.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"A curiosity of the film Vertigo is its capacity to generate emotional power from a plot that lacks the most of elementary _____: viewers are required to accept not an isolated implausibility, but a continuous stream of them.","key":"A","opts":["believability","impact","narrative","tension","premise"],"expl":"narrative（叙事）：影片缺乏基本的叙事逻辑，却仍能产生情感力量。选 A"},{"id":"v64.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The students seeking undergraduate representation on the board of trustees viewed the impasse in their negotiations with the administration as (i)_____, since it promised to (ii)_____ the administration’s belief that students should take no part in running the university.","key":"AE","groups":[["unfortunate","inevitable","unprecedented"],["undermine","fuel","distort"]],"expl":"空1 unprecedented（前所未有的）；空2 undermine（削弱）。选 AE"},{"id":"v64.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Marie Tharp’s mapping of the ocean floor, which was based on a mass of previously unanalyzed measurements of ocean depth, did not depend on (i)_____ but on (ii)_____: she (iii)_____ the sea floor’s contours by marrying the voluminous but incomplete data with her knowledge of geology.","key":"AEG","groups":[["rote work","analytical prowess","empirical knowledge"],["serendipity","extrapolation","collaboration"],["inferred","detected","reconstituted"]],"expl":"空1 empirical knowledge（经验知识）；空2 collaboration（合作）；空3 reconstituted（重构）。选 AEG"},{"id":"v64.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As astronomers do not yet have a good understanding of the fundamental nature of dark matter, it should not be a surprise that astronomy students’ ideas about dark matter are, at best, ______.","key":"AB","opts":["superficial","sketchy","inconsistent","mistaken","outdated","far-fetched"],"expl":"sketchy（粗略的）与 inconsistent 描述天文学生对暗物质的粗浅理解。选 AB"},{"id":"v64.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Given that the department director was such a feeble contributor, sitting silently at important policy meetings and usually deferring to low-level aides, it was surprising that he had such a reputation for ______.","key":"BF","opts":["magnanimity","perspicacity","impartiality","detachment","benevolence","discernment"],"expl":"discernment（识别力）与 perspicacity 呼应：他并无可称道的洞察力，却有此名声，形成反讽。选 BF"},{"id":"v64.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book captures the ______ of several politicians who spoke publicly of old-time virtues in order to mask private vices.","key":"BF","opts":["probity","dissemblance","opportunism","rectitude","ingenuousness","duplicity"],"expl":"dissemblance（掩饰）与 duplicity 描述以旧德掩盖私恶。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v65-1","title":"Test 65 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v65.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The threat of litigation makes the art authentication industry _____ realm: connoisseurs refuse to communicate in writing and confidential agreements bind authenticators to silence.","key":"B","opts":["an opportunistic","a clandestine","a moralizing","a xenophobic","an anarchistic"],"expl":"clandestine（秘密的）：法律威胁使行业变得隐秘。选 B"},{"id":"v65.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It was fine to be (i)_____ in the old days when papers were still not losing readers and ad revenue was not tough to come by, but many editors today are uneasy about bludgeoning their readers with the inherently (ii)_____ work of cartoonists.","key":"BD","groups":[["comprehensive","opinionated","profligate"],["unbalanced","flawed","vacuous"]],"expl":"空1 opinionated（固执己见的）；空2 vacuous（空洞的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v65.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The Golden Gates Bridge has been quite (i)_____ by most aesthetic and functional criteria. However, as a structure it has had some limitations. Shortly after it opened, its roadway proved to be (ii)_____ under certain wind conditions, so it was stiffened. The additional steel that provided that stiffening naturally added weight to the structure, and this made it (iii)_____ later to add a proposed rail system beneath the roadway.","key":"CEH","groups":[["inadequate","unusual","successful"],["quite noisy","overly flexible","dangerously windswept"],["unnecessary","impossible","feasible"]],"expl":"空1 successful（成功的）；空2 overly flexible（过于柔韧）；空3 feasible（可行的）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v65.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Upon realizing that the indicators of a stressful situation can be extremely ______, the psychologist reconsidered her claim that a reliable way of reducing stress is to recognize stressful situations and then avoid them.","key":"BE","opts":["acute","exiguous","persistent","overstated","tenuous","unrelenting"],"expl":"tenuous（薄弱的）：压力指标可能很难可靠地识别。选 BE"},{"id":"v65.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For wily political press officers, the art of spin is not quite supplanting truth with lies, but instead it aspires to replace awkward complexity with catchy ______; successful spin creates the impression of unavoidable common sense.","key":"BE","opts":["novelties","slogans","falsehoods","duplicity","simplicity","intelligibility"],"expl":"slogans（口号）与 simplicity 呼应“用简洁替代复杂”。选 BE"},{"id":"v65.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"British composer Benjamin Britter would seem to have ______ place in the cultural pantheon, yet, at the same time that place is still contested by some.","key":"BE","opts":["an illustrious","an assured","a precarious","a modest","a settled","a tenuous"],"expl":"an assured（稳固的）与 a settled 语义相近，但 Britten 的位置仍有争议，故。选 BE"},{"id":"v65.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Once the scientists began to research the matter, it didn’t take them long to find out that life far beneath the ocean floor was not only possible, but ______.","key":"BE","opts":["vulnerable","prevalent","conspicuous","fragile","extensive","essential"],"expl":"prevalent（普遍存在的）：深海生命不仅可能，而且很普遍。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v65-2","title":"Test 65 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v65.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some of the areas of research covered in the collection have already attracted substantial scholarly interest, while others are more _____, hence requiring pioneering effort to map the territory and suggest productive avenues of inquiry.","key":"B","opts":["intricate","pristine","parochial","heterogeneous","onerous"],"expl":"pristine（未开发的）：有些领域还属于未开拓的处女地。选 B"},{"id":"v65.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some academic criticism of popular novels has been (i)_____ in character, being based on the assumption that the wider the appeal, the more (ii)_____ the novel.","key":"CD","groups":[["rigorous","exculpatory","elitist"],["undesirable","accomplished","comprehensible"]],"expl":"空1 elitist（精英主义的）；空2 accomplished（有成就的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v65.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Since he had demonstrated (i)_____ talent as an amateur, several of his acquaintances (ii)_____ a career on the stage, but he followed his parents’ wishes, becoming an engineer.","key":"CE","groups":[["an innocuous","an unremarkable","the requisite"],["aided him in pursuing","badgered him to pursue","swayed him into pursuing"]],"expl":"空1 an unremarkable（平庸的）；空2 badgered him to pursue（逼他去追求）。选 CE"},{"id":"v65.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The prime minister underestimates the fatigue that her continual (i)_____ induces, even among those who are largely (ii)_____ her aims. Constantly referring to the bold challenges and tremendous opportunities that she and the country face, the prime minister insists that she is (iii)_____ the country, when most people would be grateful if she succeeded just in improving it a bit.","key":"CDH","groups":[["complaining","diffidence","overclaiming"],["sympathetic to","confused by","troubled by"],["deliberately analyzing","radically transforming","slowly fine-turning"]],"expl":"空1 overclaiming（夸大其词）；空2 sympathetic to（同情、认同）；空3 radically transforming（彻底改造）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v65.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Compared with their parties, politicians are ______: they are considerably less enduring than the organizations in which they function.","key":"EF","opts":["essential","redundant","crucial","unreliable","transitory","temporary"],"expl":"transitory（短暂的）：政客比政党更不持久。选 EF"},{"id":"v65.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The notion’s ______ notwithstanding—it was first proposed by a Nobel Prize-winning physicist— it was neglected for many years until some unexpected observations led to its revival.","key":"AD","opts":["pedigree","antecedents","precursors","origin","brilliance","novelty"],"expl":"pedigree（出身、声望）与 antecedents 呼应：无论其来历多么显赫。选 AD"},{"id":"v65.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Psychologists have discovered that some of the most ______ advice on study habits is flat wrong, leading them to revise the guidelines they offer to students.","key":"BC","opts":["popular","hallowed","respected","unassailable","effective","beneficial"],"expl":"hallowed（神圣的、公认的）：某些被奉为圭臬的建议其实错误。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v66-1","title":"Test 66 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v66.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The painter has emphasized the figure’s erect posture by making it contrast so starkly with the _____ exhibited by trees of the windswept orchard in the background.","key":"B","opts":["strength","list","rigidity","fruitfulness","uprightness"],"expl":"rigidity（僵硬）与 list（倾斜）都与“挺直”相对，。选 B"},{"id":"v66.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the past, the discussion of artificial light had been (i)_____. When electrification spread, the talk of artificial light became (ii)_____, perhaps because the material was more familiar. Distance lends enchantment.","key":"AF","groups":[["engaging","momentous","dormant"],["nugatory","repetitious","dull"]],"expl":"空1 dormant（沉寂的）；空2 nugatory（无价值的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v66.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is only recently that emotion has attracted any substantial scholar attention, with historians lagging behind anthropologists, sociologists, and philosophers in their willingness to (i)_____ emotion as subject worthy of scholarly attention. In the past, scholars viewed emotion as a natural and essential force that (ii)_____ analysis—a strictly private matter—and therefore (iii)_____ social life and the stuff of research.","key":"AEH","groups":[["recognize","overlook","repudiate"],["enlivened","defied","sustained"],["requisite for","extraneous to","synonymous with"]],"expl":"空1 recognize（承认）；空2 defied（拒绝接受分析）；空3 extraneous to（与……无关）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v66.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scenes of bustling streets full of well-dressed citizens going about their business ______ the growing hardship faced by all but the richest local residents.","key":"CD","opts":["betoken","signify","contradict","gainsay","quell","forestall"],"expl":"belie / gainsay 表示与现实矛盾，此处 contradict / gainsay。选 CD"},{"id":"v66.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though only nine years old, the dancer possesses _____ flexibility that suggests she may become a balletic superstar.","key":"DE","opts":["an inchoate","an unexceptional","an ungainly","a preternatural","a prodigious","an awkward"],"expl":"a prodigious（非凡的）与 preternatural 都形容天赋异禀。选 DE"},{"id":"v66.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Upstream dam construction can be _____ aquatic fauna: the natural seasonal flow patterns to which the fauna had become adapted are altered and populations therefore fragmented.","key":"CE","opts":["redundant for","disorienting for","inimical to","derogatory to","deleterious to","superfluous for"],"expl":"inimical to（有害于）：水坝对水生动物有害。选 CE"},{"id":"v66.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Whereas there has been extensive sociological research into how globalization affects finance, religion, and population, comparable studies of globalization’s impact on lawmaking and the practice of law have been _____.","key":"BF","opts":["tedious","scarce","compromised","tiresome","nonexistent","inadequate"],"expl":"nonexistent（不存在的）与 scarce 呼应：法律研究几乎没有。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v66-2","title":"Test 66 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v66.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"“RESIGNATION”, an English word the French novelist Christian Oster would no doubt appreciate, presents an elegant paradox: in one sense, it indicated a bold step, a cleaving of oneself from an attachment grown onerous; in another, it’s the height of _____, an acquiescence to fate.","key":"D","opts":["sham","fissure","desperation","passivity","maturity"],"expl":"passivity（被动）：接受命运的顺从。选 D"},{"id":"v66.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The guilty-pleasure of the play lies in its invitation for us to identify with its characters—attractive, articulate young women and young men (i)_____ behavior that, from the outside, may look more than a little (ii)_____: though the actions are initially repugnant, we cannot help but share the point of the view of the characters committing them.","key":"CF","groups":[["lament","execrate","rationalize"],["trivial","altruistic","monstrous"]],"expl":"空1 rationalize（为……辩解）；空2 monstrous（可怕的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v66.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The research found that in assessing others, many people hold an unconscious view that competence and warmth are (i)_____: when they perceive a person to be highly capable, they infer that he or she must have a tendency to be (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["equally important","mutually reinforcing","inversely related"],["ambitious","unfeeling","disingenuous"]],"expl":"能力与温情呈反比：人们觉得能力强的人往往缺乏温情，故。选 CE"},{"id":"v66.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The art of letter writing is like the art of acting in that it is the impression of (i)______ which usually makes a performance convincing. Great letter writers, like great actors, have a gift for (ii)_____, for the here and now, the depth of expression depending on its closeness to actual processes of thought. By these criteria Ellen Terry was a remarkable letter writer indeed: her letters invariably have an air of (iii)_____.","key":"AFH","groups":[["spontaneity","mastery","sympathy"],["compassion","exaggeration","immediacy"],["confidence","improvisation","sensitivity"]],"expl":"空1 spontaneity（自发性）；空2 immediacy（即时性）；空3 improvisation（即兴感）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v66.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The fact that most hypotheses turn out to be wrong does not mean that hypothesizing is ______. In fact, most hypotheses include useful ideas that survive to become part of the next model or scenario.","key":"AC","opts":["futile","reckless","fruitless","frustrating","exasperating","unnecessary"],"expl":"futile / fruitless 都表示“徒劳的”，但全文强调假设并非无用。选 AC"},{"id":"v66.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"New Zealand’s breakaway landmass proved _____ sanctuary for the tuatara, for the island lacked any terrestrial mammals that would dig up the tuatara’s slowly maturing eggs or pick off adolescents before they had a chance to breed.","key":"BC","opts":["a temporary","an excellent","an agreeable","an endangered","a complicated","a difficult"],"expl":"an excellent（极佳的）：岛屿缺乏哺乳动物，对蜥蜴类是理想庇护所。选 BC"},{"id":"v66.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though he said nothing, James _____ his father’s meaning; the boy was far from being so obtuse as everyone thought him to be.","key":"AD","opts":["comprehended","distorted","respected","fathomed","underestimated","misjudged"],"expl":"comprehended / fathomed（领会）：James 其实理解了父亲的意思。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v67-1","title":"Test 67 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v67.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"He accused some people who _____ him of being by contrast supportive of another candidate, who shared a similar stance on most political issues.","key":"C","opts":["offended","lauded","excoriated","promoted","noticed"],"expl":"excoriated（严厉斥责）：他指责对他讲述的人。选 C"},{"id":"v67.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Just as large manufacturing companies with dominant positions in large domestic markets were once able to resist (i)_____ despite ample signs that foreign competition was rapidly overtaking them, strong and wealthy states can (ii)_____ and still manage to limp along for many years.","key":"CF","groups":[["innovation","temptation","inertia"],["exploit vulnerable markets","dominate international afaf irs","maintain misguided policies"]],"expl":"空1 inertia（惰性）；空2 maintain misguided policies（维持错误政策）。选 CF"},{"id":"v67.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the (i)_____ in negotiations apparently signaled by the recent agreement between the two neighboring countries, the countries remain (ii)_____ even about the import of that agreement. One wants to prolong agreed—to resumption of limited cross—border traffic, believing it can become entrenched as a new status quo. The other, by contrast, insists that the resumption is (iii)_____ and has been undertaken voluntarily and provisionally in order to show goodwill.","key":"ADH","groups":[["progress","stalemate","setbacks"],["unreconciled","vague","flexible"],["requisite","temporary","advantageous"]],"expl":"空1 stalemate（僵局）；空2 unreconciled（未调和的）；空3 temporary（临时的）。选 ADH"},{"id":"v67.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The _______ of highly social species like rhesus monkeys—and like humans—is that their complex sociality is the reason for their success, but it’s also the source of their greatest troubles.","key":"BD","opts":["virtue","irony","delight","paradox","myth","joy"],"expl":"paradox（悖论）：复杂的社会性既是成功的原因，也是麻烦的来源。选 BD"},{"id":"v67.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since new movie stars seem to be cut from only a few bolts of the same bland cloth these days, it is ______ just to be in the presence, once again, of a true original.","key":"DF","opts":["unremarkable","reassuring","routine","invigorating","overwhelming","refreshing"],"expl":"refreshing（令人耳目一新）：又见一位真正的原创者，让人振奋。选 DF"},{"id":"v67.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Once the judge had been found guilty of corruption, it was not long before he found himself ______ his position.","key":"BC","opts":["revolted by","divested of","stripped of","recognized by","enamored of","absorbed by"],"expl":"divested of（被剥夺）：法官被定罪后失去职位。选 BC"},{"id":"v67.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Eschewing today’s hovered-over kids as less plausible characters for an adventure story, Rebeca Stead set her new children’s novel in nineteen-seventies New York to show children with a great deal of ______.","key":"AB","opts":["autonomy","independence","resilience","self-assurance","sympathy","sensitivity"],"expl":"resilience（韧性）与 autonomy 描述小说中的孩子。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v67-2","title":"Test 67 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v67.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Common and easily accessible resources (prey for predators or hosts for parasites) should be, all other things being equal, used frequently, yet in some environments apparently accessible and suitable resources remain _____.","key":"E","opts":["vulnerable","unobtainable","sustainable","depleted","unexploited"],"expl":"unexploited（未被利用的）：资源可得却未被利用。选 E"},{"id":"v67.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Regardless of the putative decline of (i)_____ in contemporary culture, such (ii)_____ remains essential to civil discourse. It allows people to avoid embarrassing or maligning an adversary, and it serves as a form of irony that draws attention to a problem that can scarcely be exaggerated.","key":"AF","groups":[["understatement","originality","partisanship"],["inventiveness","objectivity","restraint"]],"expl":"空1 understatement（轻描淡写）；空2 restraint（克制）。选 AF"},{"id":"v67.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In science education, it is important to differentiate between inaccurate ideas that are conceptually (i)_____ and understandings that are inaccurate, and yet can (ii)_____ learning of more sophisticated understanding. The former are simply wrong, the latter can be seen as incomplete, overly simplistic, or tied to only a few limited contexts.","key":"AD","groups":[["unproductive","unproblematic","distinct"],["foster","delay","resemble"]],"expl":"空1 unproductive（无益的）；空2 foster（促进）。选 AD"},{"id":"v67.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"One of the fundamental problems with learning mathematics is that while the number sense may be (i)_____, exact calculation requires cultural tools—symbols and algorithms—that are relatively new and must therefore be absorbed by areas of the brain designed for other purposes, which is easier when what we are learning (ii)_____ our built-in circuitry. With an understanding of it we can at least (iii)_____ our teaching methods by reflecting on the constraints it imposes.","key":"ADI","groups":[["innate","modern","complex"],["harmonizes with","intrudes on","goes beyond"],["preserve","discard","adapt"]],"expl":"空1 innate（先天的）；空2 harmonizes with（与……协调）；空3 adapt（调整）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v67.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is commonly said that each person’s aesthetic taste is ______, yet that notion overlooks a large body of shared aesthetic preferences.","key":"CE","opts":["unchangeable","acquired","distinct","learned","idiosyncratic","inexplicable"],"expl":"distinct / idiosyncratic 都指个人独特，与“共享的审美偏好”形成对照。选 CE"},{"id":"v67.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Unlike the theatrical adaptation of Nicholas Nickleby, which attempted to ______ its source precisely, the adaption of Les Mislabels chooses sweeping and hurtling motion over the savoring of minute details.","key":"CD","opts":["gut","digest","render","reproduce","eviscerate","relish"],"expl":"render（再现）与 reproduce 都表示忠实呈现原作。选 CD"},{"id":"v67.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Our eating habits are rooted in our physiology, but they are also ______ the culture in which we grow up.","key":"BC","opts":["symbolic of","mediated by","influenced by","ascribed to","inferable from","universal in"],"expl":"mediated by（受……中介）：饮食习惯受文化影响。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v68-1","title":"Test 68 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v68.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even though the authors repeatedly _____ their own shrewdness, they show a remarkable credulousness toward far-fetched ideas such as carbon-eating trees and cloud-making machinery.","key":"B","opts":["soft-pedal","extol","deprecate","broaden","compromise"],"expl":"extol（赞美）：作者反复夸耀自己的精明。选 B"},{"id":"v68.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Shirky argues that the Internet (i)_____ the needs for hierarchical structures and the sluggish organizations that (ii)_____ them: the Internet makes it possible to do things cheaply and efficiently on one’s own.","key":"BE","groups":[["delineates","obviates","redoubles"],["circumvent","perpetuate","undervalue"]],"expl":"空1 obviates（使……不必要）；空2 perpetuate（延续）。选 BE"},{"id":"v68.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Logically, one might assume that the nostalgia in which Guzman engages at times in his documentary about Chilean history would be (i)_____ critical reflection and thus leave the film intellectually flaccid. This conclusion would be (ii)_____, however, insofar as not all nostalgia necessarily results in a (iii)_____ of critical thought.","key":"CDI","groups":[["a motive for","a marker of","an impediment to"],["hasty","dilatory","warranted"],["reappropriation","distillation","stagnation"]],"expl":"空1 a motive for（促使）；空2 warranted（有根据的）；空3 stagnation（停滞）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v68.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though Fine leavens her work with humor and playfulness, she can be _______ writer, mincing no words in her judgements of other scientists’ work.","key":"AF","opts":["an acerbic","a provocative","an ingratiating","a demanding","an obsequious","a harsh"],"expl":"acerbic（尖刻的）与 harsh 描述 Fine 对其他科学家的严厉评判。选 AF"},{"id":"v68.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is an ironic reversal that just those politicians who most vociferously _____ the distorting complexities of the country’s tax system are now the ones embracing an agreement that worsens the mess.","key":"CE","opts":["espoused","disregarded","lambasted","eschewed","derided","ignored"],"expl":"lambasted（痛斥）：那些大声痛斥税制复杂性的人如今却拥抱加重问题的协议。选 CE"},{"id":"v68.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is very little _____ in culture: an art form or a practice (or a language or an institution) can become extinct in a generation if it does not evolve.","key":"AD","opts":["inertia","homogeneity","symbiosis","stasis","cooperation","waste"],"expl":"stasis（停滞）：文化中几乎没有停滞。选 AD"},{"id":"v68.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In spite of being one of the world’s biggest _____ of fossil fuels, the firm has made some environmentally responsible investments.","key":"BE","opts":["buyers","purveyors","disparagers","exploiters","suppliers","maligners"],"expl":"purveyors（提供者）与 suppliers 描述大型化石燃料企业。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v68-2","title":"Test 68 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v68.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The piecrust was not punctured, so steam built up and the crust _____, bursting like a balloon, creating an over-cleaning project where hopes of dinner were expected.","key":"C","opts":["split","warped","distended","shrunk","caved in"],"expl":"distended（膨胀）：饼皮因蒸汽而鼓起。选 C"},{"id":"v68.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Given the many thematic strands that the book seeks to draw together into a continuous cord of narrative, it is perforce work of _____, which is not to say that the author’s research fails to provide sufficient detail about each of his chosen themes.","key":"A","opts":["synthesis","conjecture","analysis","reconstruction","accretion"],"expl":"synthesis（综合）：这本书是综合性的著作。选 A"},{"id":"v68.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Not only is the field of behavioral genetics strewn with (i)_____ findings, but even among those findings that managed to survive, many have turned out to be (ii)_____ a very restricted class of cases.","key":"CE","groups":[["convergent","disparate","repudiated"],["refuted by","germane to","subordinate to"]],"expl":"空1 disparate（不一致的）；空2 refuted by（被驳倒）。选 CE"},{"id":"v68.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Sometimes the criteria that are used to categorize nation-states are purely factual: for example, the denotation of a state as a coastal state or an inland state. But most state labels have a predominantly (i)_____ character. Labels such as failed state or democratic state tend to be accepted only by those who (ii)_____ the assumptions that (iii)_____ such a marker.","key":"CDH","groups":[["pejorative","functional","evaluative"],["share","flout","transcend"],["are necessarily distorted by","constitute the basis of","rarely make reference to"]],"expl":"空1 evaluative（评价性的）；空2 share（分享）；空3 constitute the basis of（构成……的基础）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v68.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The use of retail coupons is commonly touted as a consumer benefit, discounting the price on an item; however, if the coupon relates to an item that the consumer neither needs nor wants, the discount is _____.","key":"AE","opts":["immaterial","reduced","diminished","offset","irrelevant","unnecessary"],"expl":"irrelevant（无关的）：优惠券对不需要的商品毫无意义。选 AE"},{"id":"v68.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"During the fifteenth century, three aspects of the mathematical sciences were usually singled out as _____: their preparatory value for the study of philosophy, their practical advantage for the community, and their antiquity.","key":"BD","opts":["estimated","superlative","inflated","praiseworthy","unique","adventitious"],"expl":"praiseworthy（值得称赞的）与 superlative 描述数学科学的优点。选 BD"},{"id":"v68.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Most of the drugs used to treat celiac disease that are now in development would not eliminate the need for a gluten-free diet but would help _____ symptoms when some gluten is unintentionally ingested.","key":"CD","opts":["diagnose","extirpate","allay","palliate","ascertain","undermine"],"expl":"空1 allay（缓解）；空2 palliate（减轻）。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v69-1","title":"Test 69 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v69.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"For many in the room, the idea of coming to the assistance of a rival was more than unpleasant: it was _____.","key":"C","opts":["unpropitious","anomalous","anathematic","redundant","meretricious"],"expl":"anathematic（令人憎恶的）：援助对手让他们觉得无法接受。选 C"},{"id":"v69.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The prime minister’s spokesman faces a difficult task in defending his boss from what he sees as the (i)_____ of a decidedly prejudiced press. To make his defense effectively he will certainly have to give specific examples of the media coverage he finds so (ii)______.","key":"BD","groups":[["overwrought panegyrics","lowly calumnies","justified fulminations"],["objectionable","confusing","unexciting"]],"expl":"空1 lowly calumnies（卑劣的诽谤）；空2 objectionable（令人反感的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v69.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Appreciating that mathematical notation presents a major roadblock to many students, some well-meaning educators (i)_____ them by (ii)_____ the use of notation; but this is an unfortunate detour, since practice with notation (iii)_____ the important skill of reasoning.","key":"CFH","groups":[["enrich","discourage","accommodate"],["mandating","accelerating","minimizing"],["compromises","promotes","circumvents"]],"expl":"空1 accommodate（迁就）；空2 minimizing（降低）；空3 promotes（促进）。选 CFH"},{"id":"v69.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is true that science, and more particularly scientists, _____ cherished paradigms with great reluctance and that when they do, scientific revolutions may result.","key":"CF","opts":["unify","share","cede","embrace","dismantle","relinquish"],"expl":"cede（让出）与 relinquish 都表示放弃旧范式。选 CF"},{"id":"v69.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because the political situation seriously impeded international communication, French scientific research was at that time uncharacteristically _____.","key":"BF","opts":["biased","insular","competitive","misleading","deceptive","parochial"],"expl":"insular（封闭的）与 parochial 描述法国在当时的孤立状态。选 BF"},{"id":"v69.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Other monarchs have been accused by posterity of murder and treason without having come to be regarded with such _____, perhaps because the cases against them have never been satisfactorily proved.","key":"BD","opts":["equivocation","opprobrium","trepidation","infamy","levity","ambivalence"],"expl":"opprobrium（恶名）与 infamy 描述对君主的谴责。选 BD"},{"id":"v69.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many macroscopic or higher-level properties on the basis of which we sort chemicals into types are not _____ the chemical structure itself but instead only manifest themselves under certain conditions or in particular contexts.","key":"AB","opts":["inherent in","intrinsic to","equivalent to","influenced by","affected by","separable from"],"expl":"intrinsic to（内在于）：宏观性质并非化学结构本身固有的。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v69-2","title":"Test 69 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v69.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"That Seiberg and Witten lack celebrity can be explained by the ______ nature of their pursuit: the mathematical exploration of four-dimensional space.","key":"B","opts":["pedestrian","esoteric","compelling","global","unequivocal"],"expl":"esoteric（深奥的）：四维空间的数学探索很难为大众所知。选 B"},{"id":"v69.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It remains a mystery how Theobroma cacao, which scholars believe originated in lowland Amazonia, was introduced to tropical Mesoamerica. It must have been a (i)_____ process: cacao trees do not easily sprout from seed, need years to mature, and grow only in humid lowland forest. Moreover, in a tropical climate, cacao pods spoil quickly, rendering their transport from lowland Amazonia tropical Mesoamerica in a single journey by foot or canoe (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["clandestine","protracted","spontaneous"],["unlikely","redundant","expeditious"]],"expl":"空1 protracted（旷日持久的）；空2 unlikely（不太可能的）。可可种子难以萌发、果实易腐，远距离一次运输几乎不可能。选 BD"},{"id":"v69.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"To the avid reader of E.O. Wilson, much of his most recent book Consilience: The Unity of Knowledge will be (i)_____, as the book represents the culmination of a life spent thinking about everything from the social lives of ants to the social lives of people. Nonetheless, new thoughts have been mixed in with the old to produce a book remarkable for its (ii)_____ and ambition.","key":"AD","groups":[["predictable","discounted","startling"],["purview","overreaching","contingency"]],"expl":"空1 predictable（可预料的）；空2 overreaching（野心过大的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v69.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Having an intense and long-standing culture of (i)_____, the company understandably has a reputation as the supreme corporate (ii)_____. But even by these standard, the degree of secrecy surrounding the company’s most recent research is (iii)_____.","key":"CFG","groups":[["impropriety","progress","privacy"],["anachronism","abomination","enigma"],["remarkable","predictable","counterproductive"]],"expl":"空1 secrecy 相关的 privacy（隐私）；空2 enigma（谜）；空3 remarkable（非同寻常的）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v69.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is rare for a prominent member of the company to leave without some ____. Smith, who resigned with civility, is an exception.","key":"AB","opts":["acrimony","bitterness","trepidation","apprehension","regret","embarrassment"],"expl":"acrimony（怨恨）与 bitterness 描述离职时的不快，此处 Smith 的礼貌离职是例外。选 AB"},{"id":"v69.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For literary critics and book reviewers, the notion of critical authority has become ______ in an age of quick, teeming Internet response, where all the old critical standards and parameters are in the process of being reinvented.","key":"AD","opts":["fluid","transparent","obvious","unstable","justifiable","defensible"],"expl":"fluid（流动的）：网络时代的批评权威变得不稳定。选 AD"},{"id":"v69.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although initially it may be difficult do discern the essay’s message of peace and conciliation, a close reading reveals its essentially _____ nature.","key":"AF","opts":["pacific","indolent","banal","lethargic","austere","dovish"],"expl":"pacific（爱好和平的）与 dovish（主张和平的）：文章的本质是和平与和解。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v70-1","title":"Test 70 · Section 1","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v70.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Many Latin American writers and critics have come to bristle at the very mention of the type of fiction termed “magic realism,” but to the common reader the appeal of such fiction is _____.","key":"B","opts":["elusive","undiminished","unfathomable","unexpected","derivative"],"expl":"undiminished（未减的）：普通读者对魔幻现实主义的兴趣并未减弱。选 B"},{"id":"v70.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The professor frequently reiterated a basic assumption behind the experimental method---namely, that the outcome of the experiment is always (i)_____. The hypothesis can never assume the experiment’s results, in other words, but instead must (ii)_____ their appearance.","key":"AD","groups":[["undetermined","incontrovertible","inconsequential"],["await","signal","negate"]],"expl":"空1 undetermined（未定的）；空2 await（等待）。假设不能预设结果，而要等待结果出现。选 AD"},{"id":"v70.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When pulsars were first discovered, some of the astrophysicists involved briefly (i)_____ these types of stars might be (ii)______ extraterrestrial intelligence. Specifically, the pulsar’s periodic radiation pattern was initially interpreted as (iii)______ rather than—as it turned out to be—the natural product of the spinning of a neutron star.","key":"BDI","groups":[["ignored whether","thought that","disavowed that"],["suggestive of","unrelated to","evidence against"],["a deliberate hoax","an episodic phenomenon","a constructed code"]],"expl":"空1 thought that（认为）；空2 suggestive of（暗示）；空3 a deliberate hoax 不对，应为 a constructed code（人造编码）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v70.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the band’s music is loud and aggressive, it is never _____.","key":"AB","opts":["simpleminded","unsophisticated","subdued","restrained","melodious","disingenuous"],"expl":"simpleminded / unsophisticated 与 “loud and aggressive” 相对：音乐从不 unsophisticated（不复杂）。选 AB"},{"id":"v70.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is a risk in _____ vagueness in speech: all kinds of distortions and lies can go unrecognized in the general haziness and so come off as facts.","key":"BD","opts":["detecting","sanctioning","castigating","countenancing","discerning","perpetuating"],"expl":"perpetuating（使延续）与 countenancing（纵容）：模糊言语的风险在于让扭曲延续。选 BD"},{"id":"v70.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"French’s tone was reasonable, _____ almost, but the gaze she fixed on Backhouse over her reading spectacles had something of defiance in it.","key":"CE","opts":["distracted","preoccupied","deferential","apprehensive","respectful","inquisitive"],"expl":"deferential（恭敬的）与 defiance 形成对照。选 CE"},{"id":"v70.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The book is impressively _____, drawing from multiple disciplines and perspectives, and resting on diverse and extensive archival sources, autobiographies, published collections of letter, and works of history.","key":"AF","opts":["learned","progressive","comprehensive","concise","succinct","erudite"],"expl":"erudite（博学的）与 learned 描述跨学科的扎实研究。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v70-2","title":"Test 70 · Section 2","group":"Test 61–70","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v70.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"He defended the government’s equivocations regarding the mysterious contrail as resulting not from _____ as critics say, but from a benightedness about its own doings that is almost inevitable, given the multitudinousness of its agencies.","key":"B","opts":["obtuseness","mendacity","abnegation","guilelessness","trenchancy"],"expl":"mendacity（撒谎）与 obtuseness（迟钝）形成对照：政府并非撒谎，而是无知。选 B"},{"id":"v70.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Hyana Kusiemko and her colleagues speculate that the (i)_____ support among low-income works for increases in the minimum wage is a form of last-place aversion: people who are in a marginally better position than the worst off seek to (ii)_____ to distinguish themselves from those in last place.","key":"CE","groups":[["unwavering","vociferous","tepid"],["disavow their willingness","retain their ability","dissemble their need"]],"expl":"空1 tepid（温吞的）；空2 disavow their willingness（否认其意愿）。选 CE"},{"id":"v70.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unlike the elected branches of the United States government, where making personal connection with citizens is (i)_____ and almost (ii)_____ political efficacy, the United States Supreme Court continues to maintain that its members should communicate with the public almost exclusively through formal opinions—and even then through ceremonial rituals that date back to the nineteenth century.","key":"BD","groups":[["frowned upon","rampant","disregarded"],["a requirement for","a detriment to","an irrelevance to"]],"expl":"frowned upon（不被赞许）与 a requirement for（必要条件）。选 BD"},{"id":"v70.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Scientists suspect that the impact with which a bat lands is a function of (i)_____. Bats that roost on hard cave ceiling must land (ii)_____ to avoid injury. By contrast, since foliage is (iii)_____, a hard landing won’t hurt, and might even give the bat time to make sure it has a good grip.","key":"BEH","groups":[["wind speed","roosting location","a bat’s size"],["quickly","softly","securely"],["plentiful","pliable","seasonal"]],"expl":"空1 roosting location（栖息地）；空2 securely（牢固地）；空3 pliable（柔软的）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v70.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The latest publications predicting disastrous coastal erosion are likely to seem _____ to knowledgeable readers because variations on the same claims have been effectively refuted in the past few years.","key":"BF","opts":["intriguing","dubious","baffling","alarming","unsettling","suspect"],"expl":"dubious（可疑的）与 suspect 描述读者对预测的怀疑。选 BF"},{"id":"v70.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Ursula Le Guin claims that looking at schoolbooks from around 1900 can be _____, given that the level of literacy and general cultural knowledge expected of a mere ten-year-old was, she notes, “rather awesome”.","key":"EF","opts":["reassuring","stimulating","dreary","tedious","scary","intimidating"],"expl":"dreary（沉闷的）与 intimidating 对比：1900 年的课本让人心生畏惧。选 EF"},{"id":"v70.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Conchita evinced _____ the arts: her favorite activities included visiting museums, attending plays or concerts, and reading poetry aloud.","key":"AE","opts":["a proclivity for","a preoccupation with","an indifference toward","an optimism about","an affinity for","a detachment from"],"expl":"affinity for（亲近、喜爱）与 proclivity for 呼应，。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v71-1","title":"Test 71 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v71.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Contrary to its reputation for intellectual _____, the 1950s was a decade exceptionally rich in works of trenchant and far-reaching social criticism.","key":"C","opts":["keenness","inclusiveness","complacency","integrity","productivity"],"expl":"complacency（自满）：与“智识上的进取”相反。选 C"},{"id":"v71.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In light of Elizabeth’s habitually (i)_____ nature, her friends were quite surprised by her (ii)_____ at the convention.","key":"BD","groups":[["ingenuous","laconic","intractable"],["garrulity","ostentatiousness","tenacity"]],"expl":"空1 laconic（寡言的）；空2 ostentatiousness（炫耀）。选 BD"},{"id":"v71.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Overall, fish farming may provide a (i)_____ wild fish stocks, but for certain species, the farmers cause a net loss of wild fish. Some fish farmers use upwards of five kilograms of wild fish as feed to grow one kilogram of carnivorous species like sea bass. Such (ii)_____ feed plus other environmental side effects undermine the expected (iii)_____ fish farming.","key":"ADG","groups":[["supplement to","rediscovery of","disruption of"],["appetite for","uncertainty regarding","optimism about"],["benefits of","impediments to","subtleties of"]],"expl":"空1 supplement to（补充）；空2 appetite for（对……的需求）；空3 benefits of（益处）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v71.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Computerized facial-recognition systems can be _____ by any number of factors, from the dirt caked on a camera lens to a hat pulled low over a subject’s face.","key":"EF","opts":["neutralized","calibrated","augmented","ameliorated","stymied","confounded"],"expl":"stymied（阻碍）与 confounded（使困惑）描述各种因素妨碍识别。选 EF"},{"id":"v71.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some social scientists who begin their studies of small communities with the intention of remaining detached revise their initial approach on discovering that personal involvement with subjects can actually ______ the gathering of important data.","key":"BC","opts":["influence","expedite","facilitate","circumvent","affect","intensify"],"expl":"facilitate（促进）与 expedite 呼应：介入反而促进数据收集。选 BC"},{"id":"v71.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since their first appearance in the nineteenth century, commuter suburbs have been widely _____ in print as both a social disaster and an aesthetic desert.","key":"BD","opts":["condemned","identified","discussed","diagnosed","welcomed","embraced"],"expl":"condemned（谴责）与 diagnosed 描述郊区被批判。选 BD"},{"id":"v71.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In denying him a promotion, management cited his ______ decision making, charging that his judgements were based on vagaries rather than careful forethought.","key":"AD","opts":["capricious","dogmatic","atrocious","cavalier","authoritative","cogent"],"expl":"capricious（任性的）与 vagaries（变幻无常）呼应。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v71-2","title":"Test 71 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v71.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The philosopher was a strong advocate of _____: he taught that happiness comes from forgoing one’s desires.","key":"C","opts":["magnanimity","duty","abstinence","pragmatism","tolerance"],"expl":"abstinence（克制）：禁欲式的克制。选 C"},{"id":"v71.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"After Betty found a qualified assistant to help her, the tasks that once seemed so (i)_____ became quite (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["onerous","pleasant","trivial"],["manageable","challenging","unwieldy"]],"expl":"空1 onerous（沉重的）；空2 manageable（可控的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v71.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the new biography, Gonzalez doesn’t (i)_____ the aspects of her subject that have drawn criticism but instead creates them with considerable (ii)_____: hardly a fact or assertion goes by her without being sourced in the endnotes.","key":"CE","groups":[["explain","acknowledge","evade"],["sympathy","thoroughness","ingenuity"]],"expl":"空1 acknowledge（承认）；空2 thoroughness（周密）。选 CE"},{"id":"v71.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"At estimated 80 million adults in the United States use form of alternative medicine, from herbs and megavitamins to yoga and acupuncture. But while (i)_____ claims are made for these treatments, the scientific evidence for them often (ii)_____ studies and clinical trials, when they exist at all, can be (iii)_____ in design and too small to yield reliable insights.","key":"CEG","groups":[["unfounded","modest","sweeping"],["shows no inconsistencies with","lags far behind","holds great promise on"],["shoddy","clever","conventional"]],"expl":"空1 sweeping（笼统而宽泛的）；空2 lags far behind（远远落后）；空3 shoddy（粗劣的）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v71.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Berwick, middle-aged, soft-spoken, and _____, with a keen sense of how to use this apparent ordinariness to his advantage, began with a gripping story about how a firefighter saved himself during a forest fire by using a completely improbable tactic.","key":"DE","opts":["imperturbable","implacable","unimaginative","unprepossessing","unremarkable","unruffled"],"expl":"unprepossessing（不起眼的）与 ordinariness 呼应。选 DE"},{"id":"v71.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Investigating physiological ______ is not how biologists typically study function and structure, but it is not entirely unreasonable—if abnormalities in the lungs hinder breathing, then the lungs are very likely the organ required for breathing.","key":"DF","opts":["deficiencies","properties","theories","irregularities","conjectures","anomalies"],"expl":"anomalies（异常）：研究生理异常有助于认识功能。选 DF"},{"id":"v71.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many great ghost stories remain _____ about the existence of their phantoms, whereas others leave no doubt about their ghosts’ reality.","key":"AB","opts":["ambiguous","mute","arch","ominous","positive","confident"],"expl":"ambiguous（模棱两可的）与 mute（不作明确表态的）。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v72-1","title":"Test 72 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v72.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The architecture of the Shanghai Bund was for decades presented as an archetypal symbol of abhorrent Western influence, which may be one of the reasons that these grand buildings were _____ for so many years.","key":"D","opts":["imitated","extolled","commemorated","disdained","unnoticed"],"expl":"disdained（轻视）：上海外滩被视为西方影响的象征，多年来受到轻视。选 D"},{"id":"v72.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The governor is known for her unwillingness to (i)_____ policy decisions in the face of opponents typically, if she announces a specific policy and is confronted with objections from interest groups, she (ii)_____ the policy.","key":"BF","groups":[["adhere to","compromise on","disavow"],["resumes","appraises","abandons"]],"expl":"空1 adhere to（坚持）；空2 abandons（放弃）。选 BF"},{"id":"v72.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The essential difference between writing nonfiction and fiction is that the artist can (i)_____ a completed vision of the world, while the journalist never can, the real world being always (ii)_____. Art provides freedom from the bewildering complexities of constant change. Indeed, it is the very (iii)_____ of well-wrought fiction that can sometimes make it fell more real than reality.","key":"CFI","groups":[["shun","correct","realize"],["diverting","tragic","unfinished"],["popularity","rarity","clarity"]],"expl":"空1 realize（实现）；空2 unfinished（未完成的）；空3 clarity（清晰）。选 CFI"},{"id":"v72.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the courts have ______ an extremely flexible test for determining the admissibility of expert testimony, that does not mean that all experts will be allowed to testify.","key":"AE","opts":["underwritten","administered","waived","renounced","endorsed","rescinded"],"expl":"空缺处为“采用了灵活的检验标准”，endorsed 最合适。选 AE"},{"id":"v72.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For more than 100 years, anarchism has been an embarrassing estranged sibling in the family of international radicalism, and its bad behavior had made it easy to _____ the awkward but important questions anarchism poses.","key":"CD","opts":["exacerbate","answer","dismiss","ignore","aggravate","embrace"],"expl":"dismiss（忽视）与 ignore 描述人们对尖锐问题的回避。选 CD"},{"id":"v72.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Rosen argues that in the early years of the United States, individual states played important roles in the governance of American Indians, thereby _____ the common assumption that Indian policy was exclusively the federal government’s domain.","key":"BD","opts":["reinforcing","belying","adducing","contradicting","increasing","demonstrating"],"expl":"contradicting（与……相矛盾）与 belying 呼应。选 BD"},{"id":"v72.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Katherine’s disobedient behavior earned her a _____ from her parent.","key":"BD","opts":["eulogy","rebuke","panegyric","mockery","commendation","agreement"],"expl":"rebuke（训斥）与“不服管教”相符。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v72-2","title":"Test 72 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v72.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The wonder of Amy Chapman was her _____, her tenacious devotion to certain causes.","key":"E","opts":["subtle allure","refractory willfulness","obstinate self-regard","brazen hubris","staunch fealty"],"expl":"staunch fealty（忠诚坚定）：忠诚与坚定。选 E"},{"id":"v72.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Far from (i)_____ the actions taken by the newspaper’s executives, William praised the executive’s resistance to corruption—yet he doubted that their policies were practical enough to warrant (ii)_____ by other papers.","key":"BF","groups":[["lionizing","impugning","surveying"],["criticism","admiration","emulation"]],"expl":"空1 impugning（质疑）；空2 emulation（效仿）。选 BF"},{"id":"v72.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"If you follow your intuition, you will more often than not err by misclassifying a random event as (i)_____. We are far too willing to (ii)_____ the belief that much of what we see in life is random.","key":"BE","groups":[["uncharacteristic","systematic","arbitrary"],["countenance","reject","champion"]],"expl":"空1 systematic（系统性的）；空2 reject（拒绝）。选 BE"},{"id":"v72.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Excitement is often considered anathema in science writing because it interjects the scientist’s emotion and values into the work. Indeed, one should not be too quick to (i)_____ of science. At the same time, however, this (ii)_____ stance can occasionally be (iii)_____, cloaking more than it reveals.","key":"CEG","groups":[["evaluate the principles","embrace the rhetoric","abandon the objectivity"],["unpopular","dispassionate","inflexible"],["misleading","unnecessary","haphazard"]],"expl":"空1 embrace the rhetoric（接受修辞）；空2 dispassionate（客观冷静的）；空3 misleading（误导的）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v72.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One can only bemoan how the wonderfully rich collections of genuine fossil specimens seen of yore in museum displays are being replaced by the _____ talking plastic of so-called virtual reality.","key":"DE","opts":["ubiquitous","exasperating","estimable","showy","meretricious","worthwhile"],"expl":"meretricious（华而不实的）与 showy 描述虚拟现实的浮华。选 DE"},{"id":"v72.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Potential readers may well be put off by the rather opaque quality of the prose in this book, which at times seems deliberately _____ the uninitiated reader.","key":"EF","opts":["aimed at","inclined toward","inconvenient for","tailored for","inaccessible to","insurmountable for"],"expl":"inaccessible to（对……难以接近）：文风对外行读者难懂。选 EF"},{"id":"v72.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"If aging is merely an avoidable by-product of life rather than a necessary progression, it is possible that we might eventually forestall _____.","key":"AC","opts":["senescence","dynamism","decrepitude","privation","ennui","voidness"],"expl":"senescence（衰老）：若能避免衰老。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v73-1","title":"Test 73 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v73.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The author affects _____ in the tone of his novels that is quite at odds with his predilection for invective in his nonfiction publications.","key":"B","opts":["a tenacity","a neutrality","a pugnacity","an effusiveness","an irascibility"],"expl":"a neutrality（中立）：小说语气与非虚构作品的好斗形成反差。选 B"},{"id":"v73.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Trying to fix problems that affect vast numbers of people has an intuitive appeal that politicians and policymakers find (i)_____, but several warehouses of research studies show that intuition is often a poor guide to fixing (ii)_____ problems.","key":"BE","groups":[["logical","irresistible","of-f putting"],["localized","systemic","theoretical"]],"expl":"空1 irresistible（不可抗拒的）；空2 systemic（系统性的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v73.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Give a computer (i)_____ task—winning at chess, say, or predicting the weather—and the machine bests humans nearly every time. Yet when problems are (ii)_____, or require combining varied sources, computers are (iii)_____ human intelligence.","key":"ADG","groups":[["a well-defined","a random","an open-ended"],["nuanced","inconsequential","solvable"],["no match for","unyielding to","able to dwarf"]],"expl":"空1 a well-defined；空2 open-ended 的问题难以解决；空3 no match for（不是……的对手）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v73.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The idea that Jim was _____, that he loved fighting for the sake of fighting, was a mistake, in reality he was a kind and gentle person.","key":"AE","opts":["truculent","audacious","brazen","obtuse","pugnacious","sapiential"],"expl":"空缺处与“爱好斗争”呼应：pugnacious（好斗的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v73.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Meera Mukherjee observed that while the work of the artisan has its well-defined contours, the artist is without palpable _____: like an explorer, the artist continually faces new regions of experience.","key":"CE","opts":["opportunities","rewards","bounds","risks","limits","hazards"],"expl":"bounds（边界）：艺术家没有有形的边界。选 CE"},{"id":"v73.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The panel’s failure to acknowledge the microbiologist as important in her field cannot be _____ a lack of accomplishment on her part, since her status as an important contributor to biology has been indisputably established.","key":"AD","opts":["attributed to","tantamount to","related to","explained by","obviated by","averted by"],"expl":"attributed to（归因于）：不能归因于她缺乏成就。选 AD"},{"id":"v73.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In 1839, working-class revolutions have been a real possibility in the industrialized countries of western Europe, but because revolutionary groups were poorly organized and led, government and employers regarded the movements with understandable _____.","key":"CE","opts":["distaste","placidity","concern","complacency","foreboding","solicitude"],"expl":"concern / foreboding 表示政府和雇主的忧虑；此处。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v73-2","title":"Test 73 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v73.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The combination of Isabella Beeton’s short life and the _____ of evidence for some parts of her story means that at times her biography, Kathryn Hughes, is forced to fill out her narrative with background information.","key":"D","opts":["reliability","plethora","relevance","paucity","transparency"],"expl":"paucity（匮乏）：证据缺乏，传记作者只能补充背景。选 D"},{"id":"v73.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"This book, a more (i)_____ version of a highly technical report, is designed for the layperson, yet it is nothing if not (ii)_____: it grapples with very complex questions about the world economy.","key":"AD","groups":[["accessible","professional","formidable"],["ambitious","popular","persuasive"]],"expl":"空1 accessible（易懂的）；空2 ambitious（雄心勃勃的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v73.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Even though the idea that medical research should be rigorously objective is (i)_____ one in the medical community, the editors of medical journals often display a disquieting (ii)_____ when it comes to articles submitted by researchers who accept money from the makers of the products they evaluate in their research; editors rarely ask whether that research is truly disinterested.","key":"BE","groups":[["a neglected","an uncontroversial","an unproductive"],["capriciousness","credulity","stringency"]],"expl":"空1 an uncontroversial（无争议的）；空2 credulity（轻信）。选 BE"},{"id":"v73.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"With the grand ambition of sending unbreakable coded messages, some physicists are using exotic tools—quantum mechanics and streams of individual photons—to shut out (i)_____. But a wire and a few resistors may (ii)_____ a message as securely, according to a physicist who claims to have devised a simple and uncrackable scheme. The idea shows that more (iii)_____ methods might compete with budding quantum cryptography.","key":"CDG","groups":[["inaccurate transmissions","pernicious influences","prying eyes"],["convey","decode","intercept"],["mundane","complex","celebrated"]],"expl":"空1 prying eyes（窥探者）；空2 convey（传递）；空3 mundane（平凡的）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v73.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many innovative breakthroughs come about when people venture beyond their own areas of expertise, because often it takes an outsider to ask the naïve questions that may yield _____ solution.","key":"BF","opts":["a constructive","an unconventional","an amicable","an agreeable","a practical","an original"],"expl":"an unconventional（非常规的）：外行提出的天真问题常带来非常规解法。选 BF"},{"id":"v73.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In a major _____ for bat populations in the United States, on average 90 percent of the hibernating bats in four important caves and mines in New York died in the space of one year.","key":"DF","opts":["achievement","reversal","venture","calamity","undertaking","disaster"],"expl":"calamity（灾难）：蝙蝠大量死亡。选 DF"},{"id":"v73.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Human and animal shyness are not _____: in humans, shyness refers to an individual’s awkwardness and apprehension in social situations, a different meaning than that used for animals.","key":"BF","opts":["prevalent","comparable","useful","disadvantageous","detrimental","analogous"],"expl":"analogous（类似的）：人与动物的害羞含义并不相同。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v74-1","title":"Test 74 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v74.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"For the ancient Egyptians, inequality in human society was not _____ nature; in other words, existing differences—between rich and poor, strong and weak—were not viewed as a necessary part of the natural order of things.","key":"D","opts":["superseded by","detectable in","ameliorated by","inherent in","excluded from"],"expl":"inherent in（内在于）：不平等不是自然的内在属性。选 D"},{"id":"v74.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Making the shift to the 90-nanometer manufacturing process has been (i)_____ for semiconductor companies. This process effectively doubles the manufacturing capacity of the industry, but it (ii)_____ enormous technical challenges because some components of the new semiconductor chips are no more than five to seven molecule thick.","key":"CE","groups":[["an unanticipated boon","a routine accomplishment","a significant struggle"],["circumvents","entails","resolves"]],"expl":"空1 a significant struggle（重大挑战）；空2 entails（带来）。选 CE"},{"id":"v74.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is plausible to regard a collection of letters spanning youth and old age as (i)_____ of autobiography: the precession of characters who inhabit a life and a chronology of incidents turn up reliably in either form. Yet autobiography, even when ostensibly steeped in candor, tends toward (ii)_____ through later perspectives, afterwords, and second thoughts, whereas letters have an undeniable (iii)_____, offering select glimpses of the fraught and living moment.","key":"AEH","groups":[["an approximation","a precursor","the antithesis"],["concision","reconsideration","sensationalism"],["sensitivity","immediacy","formality"]],"expl":"空1 a precursor（前身）；空2 reconsideration（反思）；空3 immediacy（即时性）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v74.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Spiderwebs suspended on flexible supports _____ even in low airflow in patterns that are erratic, enhancing the probability of insect capture over a volume of space.","key":"BE","opts":["stretch","waver","contract","shrink","oscillate","attenuate"],"expl":"waver（摇动）与 oscillate 描述蛛网在气流中摆动。选 BE"},{"id":"v74.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Enlightened thinkers in late-eighteenth-century Europe broadly endorsed the concept of progress, yet theories of progress were usually _____ a strong streak of pessimism, a sense of the challenges inherent in the human condition.","key":"EF","opts":["rooted in","requisite for","essential for","contradicted by","tempered by","moderated by"],"expl":"tempered by（被……缓和）：进步理论中夹杂着悲观。选 EF"},{"id":"v74.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"We hold our breath so naturally and casually that it may come as a surprise to learn that the full details of this ability still _____ scientists.","key":"CF","opts":["impress","mollify","elude","placate","divide","puzzle"],"expl":"elude（难以捉摸）：屏息的细节仍让科学家难以把握。选 CF"},{"id":"v74.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The work is alive and heterodox, the kind of ambitious failure that is more _____ than many finely crafted critical successes.","key":"AB","opts":["compelling","interesting","innovative","lauded","inspired","celebrated"],"expl":"compelling（引人入胜的）与 interesting 描述“有生命力的失败”。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v74-2","title":"Test 74 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v74.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It was quite _____ for Sir Isaac Newton to believe in alchemy—most of the experimental scientists of his era did.","key":"D","opts":["unethical","brave","pretentious","reasonable","controversial"],"expl":"reasonable（合理的）：当时大多数科学家都相信炼金术，所以并不荒唐。选 D"},{"id":"v74.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some minor misgivings about the book notwithstanding, the editor’s claim that the work will be recognized as “the authoritative history of sports for this era” is thoroughly _____.","key":"C","opts":["absurd","undemonstrated","credible","outlandish","researched"],"expl":"undemonstrated（未经证明的）：这一说法缺乏证据。选 C"},{"id":"v74.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In a sharp blow to his reputation as (i)_____ leader, the evidence that the mayor has recently been involved in malfeasance seems to be (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["a partisan","an unsuccessful","an exemplary"],["fabricated","sound","dubious"]],"expl":"空1 an exemplary（典范）；空2 dubious（可疑的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v74.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The nature of our recollection is (i)_____. One memory can seem (ii)_____ whereas another must be coaxed out of our brain little by little. Although a moment that excites our emotions is more likely to be recorded than a (iii)_____ experience, the sensory qualities of an event also play a part in how vividly and accurately we remember it.","key":"BEI","groups":[["inaccurate","inconsistent","insignificant"],["vague and spotty","immediate and colorful","unreliable and elusive"],["riveting","traumatic","routine"]],"expl":"空1 inaccurate（不准确的）；空2 vague and spotty（模糊而零碎）；空3 routine（日常的）。选 BEI"},{"id":"v74.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the face of competition from the Internet, television’s beleaguered leaders should take heart: disruptive technologies nearly always _____ new ways to profit, sometimes even for the incumbent players whose business model is being upended.","key":"DE","opts":["obviate","clarify","preclude","beget","create","imitate"],"expl":"beget（产生）：颠覆性技术往往催生新盈利方式。选 DE"},{"id":"v74.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Prior to fermentation, cacao seeds are not _____: they begin as something like apple pits and need fermentation to develop the chocolate taste.","key":"BD","opts":["marketable","palatable","recognizable","appetizing","nourishing","nutritious"],"expl":"palatable（可口的）与 appetizing 描述发酵前的可可种子。选 BD"},{"id":"v74.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The arrival of the manual describing procedures for adding content to the Web site may mark a new, more _____ phase in the site’s history, and some contributors will no doubt become nostalgic for the unpredictable do-it-yourself days.","key":"DF","opts":["fickle","reticent","indecisive","sober","prescribed","staid"],"expl":"staid（循规蹈矩的）与 prescribed（规定的）描述网站走向规范化。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v75-1","title":"Test 75 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v75.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In the 1630s, directors of the Dutch West India Company received reports of minor problems from their agents with _____, as the company was wealthy enough not to be overly concerned about small frustrations.","key":"D","opts":["trepidation","consternation","gratitude","equanimity","exhilaration"],"expl":"equanimity（平静）：公司不为小麻烦担忧。选 D"},{"id":"v75.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"As climate change alters ecosystems, the winners are going to be the (i)_____ foragers, likes grizzlies that eat everything from ants to moose, and the losers are going to be those species that are too (ii)_____ to adjust.","key":"AD","groups":[["adaptive","persistent","anomalous"],["specialized","hierarchical","voracious"]],"expl":"空1 adaptive（适应性的）；空2 specialized（专门化的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v75.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Dirac may have (i)_____ the company of other theoretical physicals, but he often (ii)_____, rarely (iii)_____ group discussions and almost never collaborating with others in his own work.","key":"CDH","groups":[["appreciated","analyzed","spurned"],["kept them at a distance","welcomed their company","pondered their insights"],["cutting of","contributing to","shrinking from"]],"expl":"空1 spurned（拒绝）；空2 kept them at a distance（保持距离）；空3 shrinking from（回避）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v75.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Madame Germaine de Stael, famous for her opinionated views, sometimes made enemies with her _____ comments.","key":"AB","opts":["caustic","acerbic","eccentric","laudatory","placatory","conciliatory"],"expl":"caustic（尖刻的）与 acerbic 描述斯塔尔夫人的刻薄评论。选 AB"},{"id":"v75.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many people perceive an unearned grandiosity at work in the news business and given that perception, it should be no surprise that they have such a strong _____ for the business.","key":"DF","opts":["preference","passion","esteem","disdain","fervor","contempt"],"expl":"空缺处表示人们对新闻业的态度，disdain（轻蔑）与 contempt（鄙视）对应“无端的自大”的负面印象。选 DF"},{"id":"v75.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The archives of the museum, containing a plethora of documents that shed light on Picasso’s work, may, for a time, give us the illusion of total comprehension, but in the end it seems that Picasso is no more _____ than he ever was.","key":"DE","opts":["orthodox","abstract","prolific","understandable","transparent","conceptual"],"expl":"空缺处为“皮卡索依然不易理解”，abstract / transparent 与 understandable 相对：他依然如过去般晦涩难懂。选 DE"},{"id":"v75.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although streams of solar particles cause beautiful auroras —the northern and southern lights— sometimes their consequences are less _____: their electromagnetic effects, for instance, can overload power grids and damage orbiting satellites.","key":"CE","opts":["spectacular","significant","benign","consequential","innocuous","palpable"],"expl":"benign（良性的）与 innocuous（无害的）：太阳粒子的后果并不总是无害的。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v75-2","title":"Test 75 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v75.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While the current coffee craze was sparked by the emergence of flavorful, high-quality gourmet varieties, a slew of studies suggesting that concerns about coffee’s health effects may be _____ has nurtured the trend.","key":"C","opts":["underemphasized","exacerbated","unfounded","documented","recapitulated"],"expl":"unfounded（没有根据的）：关于咖啡健康风险的研究可能并无依据，助长了咖啡热潮。选 C"},{"id":"v75.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"While the philosopher was known for valuing (i)_____ in the classroom, she was also, by contrast, a scrupulous and patient reviser, who (ii)_____ her lectures for print.","key":"BF","groups":[["predictability","spontaneity","correctness"],["superficially proofread","haphazardly adapted","laboriously reworked"]],"expl":"空1 spontaneity（即兴）；空2 laboriously reworked（费力地重写）。选 BF"},{"id":"v75.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Catherine the Great comes across in her memoirs as (i)_____ ruler with a razor-sharp intellect, letting nothing stand in the way of her ambitions. In short, the impression the memoirs give is entirely in accord with her reputation for being (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["an oblivious","an uncompromising","a moralistic"],["ambivalent","benevolent","formidable"]],"expl":"空1 an uncompromising（不妥协的）；空2 formidable（令人敬畏的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v75.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The cowbird can seem a rather comical creature with a slow, awkward walk and often upraised tail. Less (i)_____ is the cowbirds’ habit of laying their eggs in the nests of other birds. The (ii)_____ nesters will usually accept the cowbird egg and raise the baby cowbird as their own. Unfortunately, cowbird eggs hatch sooner than the eggs of other species and the young cowbirds (iii)_____, using their size to their advantage in getting more food from the parents.","key":"AFG","groups":[["amusing","painful","galling"],["feckless","resistant","unwitting"],["grow quickly","leave the nest","share their food"]],"expl":"空1 painful（令人痛苦的）；空2 unwitting（不知情的）；空3 grow quickly（迅速长大）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v75.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The economist noted that the occupations she analyzed in her study, which included waitresses, flight attendants, clerical workers, and domestic workers, _____ categorization: none can be captured by a single distinguishing characteristic.","key":"DE","opts":["mask","obviate","invite","confound","resist","encourage"],"expl":"confound（使困惑）：这些职业都不能用单一特征归类。选 DE"},{"id":"v75.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"On stage, jazz artist James Carter often veers dangerously close to the _____: he becomes a man possessed, his tenor saxophone wailing and whimpering with a musicality so muscular it threatens to consume him.","key":"CD","opts":["lugubrious","doleful","intemperate","excessive","idiosyncratic","sublime"],"expl":"excessive / intemperate 描述演奏者接近过度的边缘。选 CD"},{"id":"v75.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Wheelan proceeds from the assumption that statistics are _____ and, consequently, can be taught with minimal intimidation through examples.","key":"AF","opts":["intuitive","essential","habitual","instinctive","indispensable","straightforward"],"expl":"straightforward（直接易懂的）：统计学被认为可以通过例子轻松教授。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v76-1","title":"Test 76 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v76.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even months after massive storm, there remained a heavy, suspended sediment load in the surface water overlying the coral reef, the _____ water a testament to the storm’s effects.","key":"A","opts":["turbid","stagnant","fathomless","turbulent","brackish"],"expl":"turbid（浑浊的）：风暴后的水浑浊不清。选 A"},{"id":"v76.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The prosecutor belied his hard-boiled reputation by submitting (i)_____ queries to the witness and accepting in turn (ii)_____ responses.","key":"AF","groups":[["innocuous","quizzical","impertinent"],["evasive","elaborate","informative"]],"expl":"空1 innocuous（无伤大雅的）；空2 evasive（闪烁其词的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v76.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The scientist (i)_____ that the now familiar term “global warming” is (ii)_____, arguing that the atmospheric buildup of long-lived greenhouse gases is setting in motion centuries of shifts in climate patterns, coastlines, water resources, and ecosystems—hardly (iii)_____ one would describe with a gentle word like “warming”.","key":"BFG","groups":[["denied","complained","doubted"],["an exaggeration","a cliché","a misnomer"],["a transformation","an enigma","a signal"]],"expl":"空1 denied（否认）；空2 a misnomer（名不副实）；空3 a gentle word 对应 “warming” 不当。选 BFG"},{"id":"v76.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Nicolaus Copernicus was much less _____ than commonly thought: he wanted to improve the cosmological theory of his day by introducing one important change while preserving as many of its conceptual foundations as possible.","key":"CD","opts":["visionary","philosophical","revolutionary","iconoclastic","diplomatic","circumspect"],"expl":"revolutionary（革命性的）与 iconoclastic 相对：哥白尼其实没那么革命。选 CD"},{"id":"v76.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Conditions at the training camp for runners were _____; few of the runners had proper shoes or a training kit.","key":"CD","opts":["unpleasant","tedious","spartan","austere","rigorous","monotonous"],"expl":"spartan（简陋的）与 austere 描述训练条件艰苦。选 CD"},{"id":"v76.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The differences between theater and film are never more _____ than with Shakespeare's plays, since Shakespeare wrote for an audience that liked to listen and films are made for people who primarily like to watch.","key":"BC","opts":["pervasive","patent","evident","suspect","trivial","inconsequential"],"expl":"patent（明显的）与 evident 描述戏剧与电影的区别。选 BC"},{"id":"v76.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the greatest hoaxes in the history of science was perpetrated by the Indian paleontologist Dr. Chandra Gupta, who fabricated entirely _____ for fossils throughout his career.","key":"AF","opts":["counterfeit","feckless","refractory","plausible","circumstantial","spurious"],"expl":"counterfeit（伪造的）与 spurious（伪造的）：伪造化石。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v76-2","title":"Test 76 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v76.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Later in the book, the author takes pains to _____ the claims she had made earlier, as though she recognizes their implausibility and wants to quell skepticism by narrowing their scope.","key":"A","opts":["qualify","apply","reiterate","verify","jettison"],"expl":"qualify（限定）：作者限定前面的主张，以减少怀疑。选 A"},{"id":"v76.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Proffering one increasingly improbable scene character after another, (i)_____ by the constraint of realism, the novel revels in this (ii)_____ by ever more brazenly defying its readers’ presumed expectations.","key":"AF","groups":[["untrammeled","liberated","confined"],["exiguity","ponderousness","implausibility"]],"expl":"空1 untrammeled（不受限的）；空2 implausibility（不可信）。选 AF"},{"id":"v76.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Far from (i)_____ corporate influence on the academy, Taylor would like to see more of it; he is particularly (ii)_____ the idea of universities partnering with for-profit companies to sell online courses.","key":"AD","groups":[["decrying","presuming","investigating"],["enamored of","judicious about","unnerved by"]],"expl":"空1 decrying（谴责）；空2 enamored of（热衷于）。选 AD"},{"id":"v76.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The longer the migratory route, the more fat migrating birds must accumulate as fuel for their flight. The gain in body mass would make birds obese by human standards, and should render them unable to fly, but this gain is (i)_____ premigratory (ii)_____ of digestive organs, inactive during migration, and by the (iii)_____ of the muscles that power the flight.","key":"ADG","groups":[["partially ofsf et by","strongly suggestive of","seemingly unrelated to"],["shrinking","specialization","capacity"],["strengthening","attenuation","responsiveness"]],"expl":"空1 partially offset by（部分被抵消）；空2 shrinking（缩小）；空3 attenuation（削弱）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v76.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A _____ wit, Noel Coward could elicit laughs in a variety of ways—through his musical compositions, theater plays, and numerous acting roles.","key":"DF","opts":["somber","besotted","secular","versatile","uniform","protean"],"expl":"protean（多才多艺的）与 versatile 呼应。选 DF"},{"id":"v76.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some of the characters and themes depicted on the painted glass vessels found at Begram point toward an Egyptian provenance, but Egypt was not the _____ and perhaps not even the principal, place of manufacture.","key":"CF","opts":["main","leading","sole","likeliest","original","exclusive"],"expl":"sole（唯一的）与 exclusive 描述埃及并非唯一产地。选 CF"},{"id":"v76.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A strong basic science program can be _____: the rate of return on capital invested in basic science is about three times that of capital invested in applied research and development.","key":"BC","opts":["idealistic","remunerative","lucrative","transcendent","feasible","radical"],"expl":"lucrative（有利可图的）与 remunerative 呼应：基础科学投资回报高。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v77-1","title":"Test 77 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v77.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"By cosmic standards, Earth and its fellow terrestrial planets are chemical _____: they consist of primarily four elements (iron, magnesium, silicon, and oxygen) that are rare elsewhere in the universe.","key":"B","opts":["prototypes","mavericks","malefactors","paragons","old-timers"],"expl":"mavericks（特立独行者）与 paragons 不同，此处。选 B"},{"id":"v77.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The shift from extraction to cultivation in forestry involves transforming the production of trees into a source of industrial productivity, leading to a greater degree of (i)_____ between biophysical nature on the one hand and industry on the other. In the process, nature is increasingly (ii)_____ industry and science.","key":"AE","groups":[["separation","antagonism","entanglement"],["excluded from","appropriated by","superfluous to"]],"expl":"空1 entanglement（纠缠）；空2 appropriated by（被占用）。选 AE"},{"id":"v77.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Since the 1920s, historical fiction writers in China have emancipated the genre from the traditional notion that (i)_____ was the ultimate goal of history writing. Yet the traditional commitment to (ii)_____ was not simply (iii)_____: this new genre was expected to capture the essence of historical truth even as it allowed space for the writer’s imagination.","key":"BDG","groups":[["comprehensiveness","factuality","entertainment"],["veracity","thoroughness","pleasure"],["jettisoned","rationalized","acknowledged"]],"expl":"同 v74/v75 相关条目：空1 factuality；空2 veracity；空3 jettisoned。选 BDG"},{"id":"v77.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The developmental track for human beings-from rudimentary awareness to complex forms of rational agency-is quite _____ development proceeds with even minimally good physical and psychological health in any minimally favorable environment.","key":"CF","opts":["sophisticated","contingent","robust","situational","elusive","reliable"],"expl":"contingent（依附性的）：发展并非必然，依赖环境。选 CF"},{"id":"v77.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite the implications of their noble status, many aristocrats were virtually penniless and lived in a state of _____.","key":"AD","opts":["indigence","opulence","eminence","penury","depravity","complacency"],"expl":"penury（赤贫）与 indigence 描述贵族的贫困。选 AD"},{"id":"v77.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The 1966 Mexican art exhibition \"Confrontation 66\" seemed to define the Mexican art world as one in which political alignment was _____, yet painter Joy Laville rose to prominence with paintings devoid of contentiousness.","key":"BC","opts":["inconsequential","ineluctable","requisite","perilous","pointless","obsolete"],"expl":"ineluctable（不可避免的）与 requisite 对比：当时政治立场并非必须，故。选 BC"},{"id":"v77.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although both salinization and alkalinization impact water quality, they have generally been treated as _____ phenomena; however, new research proves that the processes, which impact most of the drainage area of the United States, are in fact closely linked.","key":"AE","opts":["unrelated","insignificant","unimportant","reversible","separate","incremental"],"expl":"separate（分开的）与 unrelated 描述二者被当作独立现象。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v77-2","title":"Test 77 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v77.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because of the newspaper’s _____ joint bylines, lots of reporters were compelled to do anonymous work on stories credited to other people.","key":"B","opts":["toleration of","aversion to","instigation of","endorsement of","leniency toward"],"expl":"aversion to（厌恶）：报社讨厌联合署名。选 B"},{"id":"v77.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Though she had some exposure to great art and high culture, it must be said the ultra athletic Marion Carstairs remained throughout her life primarily (i)_____ mental and artistic pursuits. She was by nature (ii)______.","key":"BD","groups":[["a product of","indifferent to","obsessed with"],["neither bookish nor cerebral","a model of delicacy and refinement","both didactic and argumentative"]],"expl":"空1 obsessed with（沉迷于）；空2 neither bookish nor cerebral（既不爱书也不重智识）。选 BD"},{"id":"v77.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"At the heart of present-day studies computational authorship attribution lies the hypothesis that each author has so personal a writing style that it can function as stylistic DNA. Any given author style, in other words, is regarded as (i)______ and (ii)______ every other authors writing style.","key":"AD","groups":[["stable","generative","unintentional"],["distinguishable from","related to","influenced by"]],"expl":"空1 stable（稳定的）；空2 distinguishable from（可与……区分）。选 AD"},{"id":"v77.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The amount of water flowing through United States streams has (i)_____ during this century, although without giving rise to more frequent floods, according to a new study by the United States Geological Survey. The country appears to be getting (ii)_____ even as its stream flow becomes less (iii)_____.","key":"BDI","groups":[["markedly declined","steadily increased","slowly stabilized"],["wetter","hotter","drier"],["benign","predictable","destructive"]],"expl":"空1 steadily increased（稳步增加）；空2 wetter（更湿润）；空3 predictable（可预测的）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v77.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In owls with a facial disk, the ears are hidden behind it and are _____ placed: having one higher than the other allows the birds to locate prey both horizontally and vertically for more accurate detection.","key":"BC","opts":["advantageously","asymmetrically","unevenly","unobtrusively","discreetly","precisely"],"expl":"asymmetrically（不对称地）：猫头鹰的耳朵高低不对称。选 BC"},{"id":"v77.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Family photos of the author suggest that she was _____ child: she seemed to wear a permanent frown.","key":"AC","opts":["a sullen","an amiable","a surly","a beautiful","a prudent","a stunning"],"expl":"a sullen（阴郁的）与 a surly 描述不常笑的孩子。选 AC"},{"id":"v77.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Restoring the old practice of producing fish in rice fields does not just make environmental and economic sense; it has the added advantage that it _____ benefits the very poor.","key":"BE","opts":["abnormally","predominantly","eminently","moderately","particularly","unnaturally"],"expl":"eminently（极其）：这一做法对最贫困者尤其有益。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v78-1","title":"Test 78 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v78.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Although most of the lakes have merged, salinity levels are not _____ throughout the lake systems: an upward-trending salinity gradient extends southeast from Pelican Lake to East Stump Lake, a distance of nearly 80 kilometers.","key":"B","opts":["known","equable","rising","problematic","unprecedented"],"expl":"equable（均匀的）：盐度并非处处均匀。选 B"},{"id":"v78.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Here was one of the main (i)_____ of oceanography during the first two decades after the Second World War. Support for oceanographic research was based on its utility for making war on other nation. Yet at the same time, oceanography retained an identity that tied it closely to (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["fallacies","paradoxes","assumptions"],["international cooperation","military secrecy","naval strategy"]],"expl":"空1 paradoxes（悖论）；空2 military secrecy（军事保密）。选 BD"},{"id":"v78.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"There is (i)______ evidence that the giant African land snail a. fulica is a serious threat to the spread of human disease. Giant snails do carry rat lungworm—infection by which is a common cause of meningitis—but so do many other snail species. Moreover, if the threat posed by a. fulica were (ii)______, one would expect to see an increase in disease rates (iii)______ a rise in the spread of snails. However, in places like New Caledonia, explosions in giant snail populations have coincided with a fall in the number of meningitis cases.","key":"CFG","groups":[["abundant","ambiguous","little"],["contained","recognized","major"],["corresponding to","predating","giving way to"]],"expl":"空1 abundant / ambiguous 描述证据；空2 ambiguous（模糊的）；空3 coinciding with（与……同时）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v78.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The decision to rely on mechanical biological treatment to process the two million tons of waste that the region produces annually was _____ to experts, who had long been aware that this approach had several shortcomings.","key":"CE","opts":["alarming","infuriating","perplexing","humiliating","baffling","surprising"],"expl":"perplexing / baffling 描述专家对此决定感到困惑。选 CE"},{"id":"v78.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although some literary scholars may express disdain for words meant for popular audiences, only the most _____ proponent of so-called great literature could dismiss the works in a recent anthology of African science fiction as formulaic pulp.","key":"DE","opts":["radical","pedantic","oblivious","hidebound","illiberal","charitable"],"expl":"hidebound（因循守旧的）与 pedantic 描述最顽固的经典捍卫者。选 DE"},{"id":"v78.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Biologists agree that snakes descended from lizards, but exactly where this first happened has been a matter of debate since the 1800s, when two _____ theories emerged.","key":"BE","opts":["complex","competing","dubious","conclusive","contending","irrefutable"],"expl":"competing（相互竞争的）与 contending 描述两种理论。选 BE"},{"id":"v78.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The early stages of being trained to ride a motorcycle are all about developing muscle memory, repeating combinations of hand-foot movements until they are ________ and precise.","key":"CE","opts":["aberrant","innate","reflexive","inborn","automatic","calculated"],"expl":"reflexive（条件反射般的）与 automatic 描述动作熟练。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v78-2","title":"Test 78 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v78.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The novel presents him as a man who monitors his state of mind and emotions as though he were doing so _____, taking and thinking about himself as if he were someone else.","key":"E","opts":["guiltily","instinctively","furtively","heedlessly","externally"],"expl":"externally（从外部地）：像看别人一样审视自己。选 E"},{"id":"v78.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The professor’s tendency to commandeer faculty meetings to promote her personal agenda quickly inspired resentment among other faculty, who objected to such _____.","key":"A","opts":["appropriation","obfuscation","caviling","vacillation","cronyism"],"expl":"appropriation（侵占）：占用会议推动私人议程。选 A"},{"id":"v78.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Ancient cart ruts found on Malta were created in soft limestone that begins to dissolve when exposed to rainfall. Their forms thus necessarily become (i)______ over time and their original features are (ii)______.","key":"BF","groups":[["solidified","degraded","conspicuous"],["refined","replicated","obscured"]],"expl":"空1 degraded（退化）；空2 obscured（模糊）。选 BF"},{"id":"v78.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"There is no sense trying to rehabilitate the reputation of the mosquito; nobody loves such a creature. But it’s (i)______ to (ii)______ all 2,600 described species of mosquito when it’s just 80 or so—3 percent that drink human blood. Among those 2,520 relatively (iii)______ kinds of mosquitoes, there’s even one we’d like to see in greater numbers: Taxorhynchites, the mosquito that eats other mosquitoes.","key":"CDG","groups":[["rare","necessary","unfair"],["malign","represent","commend"],["blameless","pernicious","valuable"]],"expl":"空1 unfair（不公平的）；空2 malign（诋毁）；空3 blameless（无过错的）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v78.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although collisions between the largest planetesimals in a planetesimal belt are ________, they can release large amounts of debris when they occur.","key":"BE","opts":["risky","exceptional","irregular","violent","rare","powerful"],"expl":"rare（罕见的）：大行星碰撞虽罕见，却会产生大量碎片。选 BE"},{"id":"v78.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because is has usually been impossible to eradicate exotic species once they have become established, it is _______ to minimize introductions of species that have substantial probabilities of unwanted impacts.","key":"AC","opts":["prudent","customary","provident","superfluous","essential","pointless"],"expl":"prudent（审慎的）与 provident 描述防范外来物种。选 AC"},{"id":"v78.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the Old Southwest, only writers who showed exceptional _____ were likely to become widely known, because the region's weak infrastructure inhibited the development of publishing beyond local newspapers that served small towns.","key":"DF","opts":["prescience","foresightedness","optimism","resolve","patience","determination"],"expl":"prescience（先见之明）与 foresightedness 呼应。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v79-1","title":"Test 79 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v79.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The assumption that children learn about science primarily in the classroom is so _____ that few scientists, educators or policymakers question it, despite an ever-growing body of evidence demonstrating that most science is learnt outside of school.","key":"D","opts":["tenuous","subtle","irrefutable","pervasive","misconstrued"],"expl":"pervasive（普遍存在的）：这一假设深入人心。选 D"},{"id":"v79.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Psychologists note that in making purchase decisions, consumers often unconsciously use mental shortcuts, such as familiarity with a brand name to (i)_____ routine problems efficiently. Thus, part of what companies aim for developing a brand is very specifically to (ii)_____ consumers’ conscious thought.","key":"BF","groups":[["identify","resolve","postpone"],["amplify","ascertain","circumvent"]],"expl":"空1 resolve（解决）；空2 circumvent（绕过）。选 BF"},{"id":"v79.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"This book cannot be evaluated properly without examining the author’s choice of format, which is the (i)______ of the format of standard academic works; here the photographs take center stage, with the text playing only a supporting role. This layout poses many dangers for the serious historian, not the least of which being the (ii)______ reception that academics—motivated partly by (iii)______ but also by genuine concern over scholarly standards—generally reserve for books apparently aimed at the popular market.","key":"CDH","groups":[["duplicate","epitome","inverse"],["scornful","deferential","good-natured"],["academic integrity","snobbish elitism","collegial sympathy"]],"expl":"空1 epitome（典范）；空2 scorn（轻蔑）；空3 commercial interest（商业利益）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v79.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The adipose tissue in which our bodies store fat from the food we eat has traditionally been thought of as _____, but in reality this tissue constitutes a dynamic organ, not a mere repository.","key":"CE","opts":["capacious","deleterious","inert","detrimental","passive","Inessential"],"expl":"passive（被动的）与 inert 描述脂肪组织的传统看法。选 CE"},{"id":"v79.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The sound of disembodied human breathing in Miyazaki's films is at once a presence, close to the listener's ear, and a ghostly absence due to its lack of a visual _____.","key":"BD","opts":["image","counterpart","urgency","correlative","cue","background"],"expl":"counterpart（对应物）：缺乏视觉对应。选 BD"},{"id":"v79.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The problem a generation ago was not the new art itself but the heightened intensity of conviction surrounding it, which is thankfully absent in our wonderfully _____ times.","key":"CD","opts":["fervid","impassioned","undogmatic","receptive","nostalgic","optimistic"],"expl":"undogmatic（不教条的）与 receptive 呼应：如今的时代更宽容。选 CD"},{"id":"v79.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"He found his new acquaintance to be _____: trying to understand her personality was like peering into an unknown dimension.","key":"CE","opts":["vacuous","unflappable","unfathomable","obdurate","inscrutable","imperturbable"],"expl":"inscrutable / unfathomable 描述他的性格难以捉摸。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v79-2","title":"Test 79 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v79.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"A significant element of the Gothic genre, the literary grotesque is sometimes inaccurately discussed as if it were a Gothic or, conversely, as if it were something entirely different from Gothic.","key":"A","opts":["synonym for","characteristic of","counterweight to","ramification of","deviation from"],"expl":"synonym for（同义词）：常被误认为哥特的同义词。选 A"},{"id":"v79.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Journalist Michael Pollan is nothing if not (i)_____, committed to investigating our eating habits through (ii)_____ and unwilling to pass judgment on any food-related practice that he has not witnessed firsthand or even joined in.","key":"AF","groups":[["an empiricist","a traditionalist","an enthusiast"],["brilliant theorizing","voluminous reading","careful observation"]],"expl":"空1 an empiricist（经验主义者）；空2 careful observation（细致观察）。选 AF"},{"id":"v79.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Scientists suspect that athletes may experience augmented bloodstream levels of the hormone oxytocin during competition. (i)_____ considerations, however, make it difficult to (ii)_____ oxytocin levels during sports events: few will willingly interrupt player in the middle of a game in order for scientists to test players’ blood.","key":"AE","groups":[["Practical","Theoretical","Ethical"],["predict fluctuations of","quantify changes in","trigger elevation of"]],"expl":"空1 Ethical（伦理的）；空2 quantify changes in（量化变化）。选 AE"},{"id":"v79.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Based on the evidence available, it would be (i)______ to insist on a wholly negative portrayal of King Prajadhipok. In his own writings and pronouncements as well as in firsthand accounts offered by others, Prajadhipok consistently emerges as (ii)______ and even-tempered, though (iii)______.","key":"CEG","groups":[["accurate","convenient","facile"],["whimsical","thoughtful","ingenious"],["unexceptional","vicious","innovative"]],"expl":"空1 accurate（准确的）；空2 thoughtful（深思熟虑的）；空3 unexceptional（平凡的）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v79.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The _____ of Craig's government had left the nation almost totally unprepared for war when it came.","key":"AC","opts":["somnolence","inexperience","lethargy","obstinacy","perspicacity","acuity"],"expl":"inexperience（缺乏经验）与“毫无准备”呼应。选 AC"},{"id":"v79.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Japanese law draws a distinction between currency imitation and actual counterfeiting: only the latter involves an explicit intent to ______ the public.","key":"CE","opts":["confuse","malign","defraud","address","swindle","defame"],"expl":"defraud（诈骗）：伪造的意图在于欺诈公众。选 CE"},{"id":"v79.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It's easy to see why the aspiring singer was ______ the awareness of her lack of talent: her shaky voice notwithstanding, she was a kindly woman with a genuine appreciation for music.","key":"BF","opts":["surprised by","insulated from","humbled by","appreciative of","guided to","buffered against"],"expl":"humbled by（被……使谦卑）：她意识到自己缺乏天赋。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v80-1","title":"Test 80 · Section 1","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v80.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"_____ is valuable in science, even when a scientific idea is true, it can be misused through grandiosity.","key":"A","opts":["humility","experimentation","patience","cooperation","exposure"],"expl":"humility（谦逊）：科学中谦逊很宝贵。选 A"},{"id":"v80.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"She knew well, from experience with hundreds of hired crew members on her boats, how (i)_____ attitudes can be: one negative influence can impel an otherwise (ii)_____ member of a crew to quit.","key":"BF","groups":[["insipid","infectious","innocuous"],["untested","captious","contented"]],"expl":"空1 infectious（有感染力的）；空2 contented（满足的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v80.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Thinking (i)______ about one’s choices can sometimes (ii)______ decision making. For example, in one study in which college students selected their favorite poster from a set, those asked to explain their selection ended up less (iii)______ their choices than those who were not asked. Researchers concluded that thinking of reasons interferes with people’s ability to access gut-level reactions that are crucial to sound decision making.","key":"CEG","groups":[["uncritically","haphazardly","explicitly"],["speed the process of","reduce satisfaction with","enhance the quality of"],["happy with","confused by","concerned by"]],"expl":"空1 explicitly（明确地）；空2 reduce satisfaction with（降低满意度）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v80.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A decisive way to test planet formation hypotheses is to study planetesimals, but these objects are quite ______, neither numerous nor large enough to emit significant radiation that can be captured by telescopes.","key":"BE","opts":["unpredictable","inconspicuous","clustered","radioactive","discreet","erratic"],"expl":"inconspicuous / discreet 描述星子不显眼。选 BE"},{"id":"v80.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ______ of native South American textiles at the time of the Spanish conquest should not be surprising: it represented the apogee of one of the world's oldest and most sophisticated weaving and dyeing traditions.","key":"AD","opts":["splendor","eccentricity","diversity","brilliance","practicality","popularity"],"expl":"splendor（辉煌）与 diversity 描述纺织品的成就。选 AD"},{"id":"v80.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"If it is wrong to justify human selfishness on the basis of the alleged selfishness of nature, then it is equally mistaken to espouse ______ merely because some animals happily assist each other.","key":"DE","opts":["pragmatism","moderation","restraint","altruism","benevolence","permissiveness"],"expl":"altruism（利他主义）：不应因动物互助就主张利他。选 DE"},{"id":"v80.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In many branches of science, our knowledge and technology have advanced so rapidly that new studies carried out with improved instruments and techniques may well ______ research done just twenty years earlier.","key":"BD","opts":["confirm","supplant","elaborate","supersede","question","validate"],"expl":"supplant / supersede 表示新研究取代旧研究。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v80-2","title":"Test 80 · Section 2","group":"Test 71–80","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v80.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"A sunset, the poet asserted, is beautiful in part because it is _____: fleeting and never to be repeated.","key":"C","opts":["expeditious","vibrant","transitory","evocative","archetypal"],"expl":"transitory（短暂的）：日落的美源于其转瞬即逝。选 C"},{"id":"v80.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Recently the novelist has (i)_____ the radically experimental forms with which he made his reputation in favor of more (ii)_____ narratives, fencing in and turning an imagination meant to run wild.","key":"BD","groups":[["trumpeted","forsaken","replicated"],["conventional","pretentious","provocative"]],"expl":"空1 forsaken（放弃）；空2 conventional（传统的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v80.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Evidence suggest that populations of migratory birds in both the New and Old Worlds have (i)_____, a (ii)_____ that carries the potential for significant ecological damage far beyond the shrinking numbers of the birds themselves.","key":"CE","groups":[["scattered","stabilized","plummeted"],["dispersal","decline","displacement"]],"expl":"空1 plummeted（骤降）；空2 decline（下降）。选 CE"},{"id":"v80.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The patients given a placebo in the course of clinical trials receive much more than a pharmacologically inert substance. Like the patients receiving the experimental drug, they (i)______ a thorough medical evaluation, a chance to discuss their condition with competent professionals, a diagnosis, and a treatment plan. Although viewed by many as (ii)______ the healing process, these factors may actually provide an important clue as to why placebo often work: they are part of an experience that can itself be a (iii)______ illness.","key":"AEH","groups":[["get","avoid","welcome"],["essential for","incidental to","consequences of"],["research laboratory for","powerful antidote to","breeding ground of"]],"expl":"空1 get（获得）；空2 welcome（欢迎）；空3 real（真实的）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v80.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The campaign official argued that the large swings in the candidate's approval ratings were a result not of the ______ of the electorate but rather of the polls' margins of error and divergent methodologies.","key":"CD","opts":["exactitude","resurgence","capriciousness","volatility","partisanship","scrupulousness"],"expl":"volatility（波动）与 capriciousness 描述选民态度的变化。选 CD"},{"id":"v80.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some consider the theorem Emmy Noether first published in 1918 to be as important as Einstein’s theory of relativity, since much of today’s vanguard research in physics is ______ Noether’s theorem.","key":"BD","opts":["contradicted by","undergirded by","incompatible with","dependent on","devoted to","elucidated by"],"expl":"undergirded by（以……为基础）：前沿研究依赖诺特定理。选 BD"},{"id":"v80.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Beauford Delaney's dynamic depictions of Harlem and Greenwich Village, dating from 1929 to 1953, _____ the energy of the city, while the equally captivating abstract compositions from his Paris years of 1953 to 1979 demonstrate his sustained exploration of color.","key":"BD","opts":["authenticate","convey","elicit","impart","stifle","suppress"],"expl":"convey（传达）与 impart 描述城市的能量。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v81-1","title":"Test 81 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v81.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The evidence depicts an _____ system of tree inspections and care, one in which the crucial job of spotting dangers is left to untrained workers, and essential repairs and pruning are delayed to save money.","key":"B","opts":["overeager","ineffective","uneconomical","unflagging","intuitive"],"expl":"ineffective（低效的）：危险识别交给无经验者，维修又被拖延，系统本身无效。选 B"},{"id":"v81.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Even though company’s CEO professes to be (i)_____ and urges the deal forward, its investors are unlikely to be so (ii)_____ about its prospect. Many were uncomfortable at the way the corporation was forced to spend much of last year expansion, and this new venture is potentially even more risky.","key":"CE","groups":[["apprehensive","apathetic","confident"],["indifef rent","sanguine","anxious"]],"expl":"空1 apprehensive（忧虑的）；空2 anxious（焦虑的）。CEO 表态自信，投资者却不安。选 CE"},{"id":"v81.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Transportation maps of Alaska are (i)_____ in large part by what they (ii)_____: lines identifying roads and railroads. With a single track bisecting the state and a handful of spokes to the east and south, Alaska is notable for its (iii)______ of transportation options.","key":"BDI","groups":[["demarcated","characterized","elucidated"],["lack","obscure","evince"],["panoply","scope","dearth"]],"expl":"空1 demarcated（划分）；空2 lack（缺乏）；空3 dearth（匮乏）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v81.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Aboriginal people of Victoria Australia neither rejected Western material culture nor demonstrated an obsession with it in fact, Western artifacts such as pipes and handkerchiefs were appreciated for their symbolic rather than their ______ value.","key":"AE","opts":["utilitarian","intrinsic","communicative","aesthetic","pragmatic","theoretical"],"expl":"空缺处为“符号价值而非……价值”，utilitarian（实用的）最贴切。选 AE"},{"id":"v81.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite dogs’ talent for detecting those high-pitched whistles that are inaudible to us, dogs’ ability to locate sounds is ________ compared with ours.","key":"AE","opts":["imprecise","innate","impractical","inherent","inexact","impaired"],"expl":"空缺处为“听觉定位能力相比我们……”，impaired（受损的）与“比我们差”一致。选 AE"},{"id":"v81.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because they were traditionally _______, Jam monks in sixteenth-century India particularly valued special dispensations from the royal court granting them freedom of movement.","key":"DF","opts":["erudite","ascetic","apolitical","peripatetic","solitary","itinerant"],"expl":"itinerant / peripatetic（流动的、四处游历的）：他们不能久居一处，需要旅行特许。选 DF"},{"id":"v81.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The coagulated latex of the gutta-percha tree, which grows wild in Sumatra Kalimantan and May, can be formed into a natural plastic that, although inelastic under ordinary conditions becomes _______ when placed in hot water.","key":"BD","opts":["smooth","pliable","permeable","malleable","pervious","buoyant"],"expl":"malleable（可塑的）与 pliable 描述加热后变软。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v81-2","title":"Test 81 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v81.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The sand paintings that McCall created—a synthesis of painting, sculpture, and photography— were meant to be _____, preserved only in the memories of witnesses.","key":"C","opts":["archetypal","incendiary","ephemeral","naturalistic","dazzling"],"expl":"ephemeral（短暂的）：沙画只在记忆中留存。选 C"},{"id":"v81.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Among the most popular Currier&levs lithographic prints in nineteenth-century America were bird’s-eye views of great cities such as New York, Chicago, and San Francisco. These were edited into books, and the cities’ (i)_____ meant that new views were (ii)_____ for successive editions.","key":"BF","groups":[["tremendous productivity","extraordinary growth","unparalleled activity"],["hard to obtain","rendered superfluous","regularly required"]],"expl":"空1 extraordinary growth（迅速增长）；空2 rendered superfluous（变得多余）。选 BF"},{"id":"v81.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The scientists who first proposed that Moon’s craters had resulted from impacts (i)_____: almost all of these craters were circular, and yet most impactors in heliocentric orbit would have an oblique path and hence would be expected to form (ii)_____ craters.","key":"CE","groups":[["devised a theory","misinterpreted a finding","confronted difcfi ulty"],["massive","elongated","shallow"]],"expl":"空1 devised a theory（提出理论）；空2 elongated（拉长的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v81.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is inevitable that ongoing research presupposes some accepted science as a principle. Usually no one even notices the implication that the accepted principle is being (i)_____ unless there emerges (ii)_____ that turns out to be sufficiently (iii)_____ that the assumptions underlying the research come to be considered.","key":"CDI","groups":[["jeopardized","revised","tested"],["an anomaly","a consensus","a distinction"],["trivial","transparent","recalcitrant"]],"expl":"空1 jeopardized（危及）；空2 an anomaly（反常现象）；空3 recalcitrant（顽固的）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v81.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although dry weather in medieval England was not ______, documentary evidence suggests that the cluster of intense droughts between 1323 and 1333 was exceptional.","key":"AC","opts":["anomalous","severe","uncommon","seasonal","frequent","pervasive"],"expl":"anomalous（反常的）与 uncommon 呼应：中世纪英国的干燥并非反常。选 AC"},{"id":"v81.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Among some demographic groups, the Internet is ______: almost everybody who wants Internet access has it.","key":"DE","opts":["necessary","indispensable","irresistible","pervasive","ubiquitous","homogeneous"],"expl":"ubiquitous（无处不在的）：几乎人人都能上网。选 DE"},{"id":"v81.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"What Dr. Walther has shown is that many of the standard statistical techniques that are supposed to insure against ______ correlations are inadequate in this case.","key":"BF","opts":["numerical","specious","elementary","paltry","quantifiable","spurious"],"expl":"spurious（伪造的）：统计方法无法防止伪相关。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v82-1","title":"Test 82 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v82.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"From its nineteenth-century beginnings onward, photography was often tasked with providing _____ images of individuals, yet at the same time, photographs were prized for their perceived realism and truthfulness.","key":"C","opts":["recognizable","candid","idealized","replicable","detailed"],"expl":"idealized（理想化的）：照片既要理想化，又要被视为真实。选 C"},{"id":"v82.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"When the United States government created the Post Office at the founding of the republic, it didn’t invite rival postal firms to compete; in fact, it created a monopoly. That monopoly, however, was (i)_____ free expression because of policies Congress adopted, which (ii)_____ the circulation of newspapers irrespective of their viewpoint and spread postal service throughout the country.","key":"AD","groups":[["conducive to","threatened by","dependent on"],["subsidized","limited","trivialized"]],"expl":"空1 threatened by（受威胁）；空2 subsidized（补贴）。选 AD"},{"id":"v82.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Having displayed his art collection in a vast modernist white space in (i)______ former warehouse, Mr. Saatchi has chosen for his new site its polar opposite, a riverside monument to civic pomposity that once housed the local government. There is nothing (ii)______ about the new location: the building’s design is bureaucratic baroque, (iii)______ style that is as declamatory as a task-force report and as self-regarding as a campaign speech.","key":"CEH","groups":[["a decadent","a claustrophobic","an unprepossessing"],["atavistic","spare","pretentious"],["an ascetic","a grandiose","an understated"]],"expl":"原文描写一座从前为政府大楼的庄严建筑，与原先现代主义白色空间形成反差，。选 CEH"},{"id":"v82.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Motorcycle riders in London have discovered an ingenious, albeit ______ way of parking illegally without getting a ticket.","key":"BD","opts":["inventive","unscrupulous","astute","dishonest","impractical","shrewd"],"expl":"空缺处要表达“巧妙却不诚实”，unscrupulous（不择手段的）与 dishonest 最合适。选 BD"},{"id":"v82.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The writer’s expression of ______ sentiments in fluid, vigorous prose is a strange blending of the high and the low-like an opera performed by sloppily dressed, unkempt musicians.","key":"BD","opts":["patriotic","vile","noble","base","tender","lofty"],"expl":"空缺处描述“高雅与低俗的混合”，base（低下的）与 lofty 形成对照，。选 BD"},{"id":"v82.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"California’s building codes are more ______ than those elsewhere in the United States to ensure that structures are capable of protecting people from frequent seismic events.","key":"BD","opts":["circuitous","exacting","controversial","stringent","convoluted","extensive"],"expl":"stringent（严格的）与 exacting 描述加州建筑规范的严苛性。选 BD"},{"id":"v82.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Jean Kimmel and Emily Hoffman argue for expanding the definition of child-care subsidies to include all programs that ______ or otherwise offset expenses for nonparental child care.","key":"DE","opts":["tally","tabulate","alter","defray","pay","simplify"],"expl":"defray（分摊费用）与 offset 同义，描述补贴支出。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v82-2","title":"Test 82 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v82.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The tenor of Me, as indicated by the title, tends to be _____, sometimes insufferably so.","key":"C","opts":["self-effacing","panegyric","vainglorious","discursive","overmodest"],"expl":"vainglorious（自负的）：书名与内容都显得自夸。选 C"},{"id":"v82.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The main thrust of her argument was that wage difference, far from being _____, do in fact reflect education, skills, experience, and other factors that make employees more productive.","key":"C","opts":["rational","divergent","arbitrary","discernible","attributable"],"expl":"arbitrary（任意的）：并非随意，而是反映能力。选 C"},{"id":"v82.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Goodin notes that people have (i)_____ cognitive capacities and that they therefore must consider some factors as (ii)_____ so as to be able to make decisions about other things.","key":"AF","groups":[["limited","adaptable","overlooked"],["essential","variable","given"]],"expl":"空1 limited（有限的）；空2 given（既定的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v82.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"(i)______, we can safely infer causality by appealing to a set of general principles (Newtonian mechanics, for example) that are well understood and have been shown to apply in comparably straightforward circumstances. However, for the opposing class, which consists of (ii)______ systems like the global economy, human physiology, or the human mind itself, explanations of singular events are usually (iii)______, absent the requisite accounting for the intricate dynamics of such systems.","key":"CDH","groups":[["In unknown settings","For complicated events","In simple situations"],["complex","homogeneous","equivalent"],["consistent","unjustified","unequivocal"]],"expl":"空1 Systems closed to... 原文主题为可控与复杂系统之分，空2 complex（复杂的）；空3 difficult to reliably predict（难以可靠预测）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v82.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the coauthors of the new guide to the American artistic experience have received accolades for their wide-ranging work, they do not _____ that the publication is exhaustive in content.","key":"CD","opts":["hope","care","assert","insist","doubt","question"],"expl":"assert / insist 与“声称详尽”相关，。选 CD"},{"id":"v82.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Journal editors note that the peer review process has difficulty detecting _____ : deliberate misinformation, if it is clever enough, might sail right through no matter how scrupulous the reviews.","key":"CE","opts":["bias","inconsistency","fraud","negligence","duplicity","carelessness"],"expl":"fraud（欺诈）与 duplicity 同义，此处。选 CE"},{"id":"v82.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Coral reefs are often referred to as the rain forests of the sea, _____ comparison given that only tropical rain forests can compete with the sheer concentration of biodiversity found in coral reefs.","key":"CE","opts":["a factitious","an imaginative","a fitting","an artificial","an apposite","a creative"],"expl":"apposite（恰当的）与 fitting 描述珊瑚礁被喻为“海洋雨林”的合理性。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v83-1","title":"Test 83 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v83.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Although not enough to _____ the conventional view of the manuscript’s provenance, the new study was thought to have weakened the prevailing theory considerably.","key":"E","opts":["undermine","affect","resurrect","disturb","topple"],"expl":"undermine（削弱）与 topple（推翻）：研究未能推翻传统观点，只是削弱了它。选 E"},{"id":"v83.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some people (i)_____ translations of great literary works—especially those insistent on a literal translation for whom no rendering is ever (ii)_____ enough.","key":"AD","groups":[["dismiss","tolerate","esteem"],["faithful","creative","spontaneous"]],"expl":"空1 dismiss（不屑）；空2 faithful（忠实的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v83.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In its earliest days, the telegraph inspired (i)______ without precedent in the annals of technology. A new sense of (ii) across: a sense that the world was in (iii), that life for one’s children and grandchildren would be very different, all because of this wondrous force and its uses.","key":"CEG","groups":[["anxiety","outrage","exhilaration"],["resentment","futurity","nostalgia"],["a state of change","a downward spiral","an unyielding stasis"]],"expl":"空1 exhilaration（兴奋）；空2 futurity（未来感）；空3 a state of change（处于变化之中）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v83.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The rebellion was _____ one, driven less by ardor than by reason and calculation.","key":"AB","opts":["a cerebral","a dispassionate","a rash","an idealistic","a cautious","a reckless"],"expl":"空缺处与“不是热情而是理性”呼应：cerebral（理性的）与 dispassionate（冷静的）。选 AB"},{"id":"v83.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite their current reputation, the original Luddites were neither opposed to innovation technology nor _____ using it: many were highly skilled machine operators in the textile industry.","key":"AD","opts":["inept at","enamored of","resistant to","unequal to","enthralled by","unfazed by"],"expl":"空缺处为“并不反对使用技术”，enamored of（热衷于）最贴切。选 AD"},{"id":"v83.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Once a pop musician’s biggest source of income, recorded music now plays second fiddle to touring, endorsements, merchandise sales, and an array of other revenue streams previously considered _____.","key":"CE","opts":["lucrative","invaluable","ancillary","irrelevant","supplementary","remunerative"],"expl":"ancillary（附属的）与 supplementary 描述次要收入。选 CE"},{"id":"v83.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The colors of brocaded silks made by Merina weavers in Madagascar were not _____: magenta, blue, black, pink, yellow and brown characterize pieces before 1880, while thereafter green purple, and orange come to the fore.","key":"AE","opts":["invariable","generic","conventional","repetitious","static","traditional"],"expl":"invariable（不变的）与 static 描述颜色随时间变化。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v83-2","title":"Test 83 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v83.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The economist argued that however much the government might trumpet the value of _____, it had been as bold as any other in its spending programs.","key":"A","opts":["thrift","consumption","dialogue","cooperation","transparency"],"expl":"thrift（节俭）：政府宣扬节俭，但开支却很大胆。选 A"},{"id":"v83.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It was not until 1995 that a planet beyond our solar system was first sighted, a discovery that greatly excited astronomers. Many had supposed that the processes that gave rise to our solar system were not (i)_____, and that there were other planets in the universe. Now, observations had (ii)_____.","key":"CD","groups":[["manifest","replicable","unique"],["caught up with belief","provided grounds for skepticism","put assumptions to the test"]],"expl":"空1 unique（独特的）；空2 put assumptions to the test（检验假设）。选 CD"},{"id":"v83.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many of us remember a time when discovery and the thrill of learning were forces in our lives and were (i)_____. Frequently that time happened in a great classroom somewhere, in the hands of the one (ii)_____ teacher we can each remember.","key":"CD","groups":[["elusive","inconsequential","exciting"],["consummate","truculent","superfluous"]],"expl":"空1 exciting（激动人心的）；空2 consummate（技艺纯熟的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v83.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The enthusiasm that many English artists and writers felt regarding the Labour Party (i)______ amid complaints that arts funding remained as (ii)______. And even though the government recently announced a significant funding boost for the Arts Council, some art leaders still refuse to (iii)______ Labour.","key":"CEG","groups":[["intensified","resurfaced","waned"],["far-reaching","parsimonious","staggering"],["trust","condemn","ignore"]],"expl":"空1 waned（减弱）；空2 parsimonious（吝啬的）；空3 trust（信任）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v83.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Meteorology is one of the few fields of applied science that demands prediction; since prediction involves considerable uncertainty and uncertainty is _____ scientists, meteorology will continue to exist in a fraught intellectual space.","key":"BE","opts":["mysterious to","anathema to","discredited by","pivotal for","repellent to","familiar to"],"expl":"anathema to（大忌）：不确定性对科学家来说是大忌。选 BE"},{"id":"v83.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One virtue of cornmeal as a component of the diets of laborers in early Puerto Rico was the mildness of its taste, a trait that enabled it to _____ the strong flavors of other foods.","key":"BD","opts":["mimic","temper","camouflage","neutralize","complement","augment"],"expl":"temper（缓和）：玉米粉口味温和，能缓和其他食物的强烈味道。选 BD"},{"id":"v83.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Asteroids of diameter less than 100km never melted but asteroids with larger diameters did so and became ______ with the heavier Fe-Ni material forming the core and the silicates forming the crust.","key":"AE","opts":["stratified","destabilized","weakened","liquefied","differentiated","distinguished"],"expl":"differentiated（分异的）：较大的小行星熔化后分层。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v84-1","title":"Test 84 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v84.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Geologists suggest that as the most productive oil reservoirs begin to dry up, the expensive cost and high risk of drilling in the marginal area become less _____ and more acceptable.","key":"A","opts":["onerous","efficacious","auspicious","benign","natural"],"expl":"onerous（沉重的）与“成本与风险越来越不令人畏惧”形成对照，此处。选 A"},{"id":"v84.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because it is discussed by humanities scholars from diverse disciplinary backgrounds, “affect” has been (i)_____ defined; nonetheless there has been (ii)_____ the terms “emotion” and “affect” across academic writing in the humanities.","key":"BF","groups":[["clearly","variously","narrowly"],["a paucity of interest in","a variety of interpretations of","a consistent distinction between"]],"expl":"空1 variously（各不相同地）；空2 a variety of interpretations of（对……的多种解释）。选 BF"},{"id":"v84.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Fifteen years ago, the author of this scholarly monograph would have (i)______ found a university press willing to publish it. But today specialized books of this sort are (ii)______ species. Their main purchasers—university libraries—have far less money to spend on these items than they once did. Computerized catalogues, subscription content, expensive scientific journals, exploding storage costs: all these demands are (iii)______ library budgets.","key":"CFG","groups":[["voluntarily","never","readily"],["a thriving","an anomalous","an imperiled"],["putting tremendous","leading to irregularities in","causing increasing"]],"expl":"空1 voluntarily / 空2 an endangered species（濒危物种）；空3 straining（挤压）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v84.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In science, _____ can sometimes inhibit understanding; indeed, the advantage of the technique for staining brain tissue developed in 1873 by Golgi was that it showed so little.","key":"AC","opts":["biases","projections","prejudices","minutiae","approximations","particulars"],"expl":"空缺处为“可能抑制理解”，details（细节）与 minutiae 形成对比，。选 AC"},{"id":"v84.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Faced with so much conflicting information on the internet, many people come to believe that all sources are so _____ that efforts to discriminate between the true and the false are inevitably futile.","key":"AD","opts":["slanted","imprecise","splenetic","tendentious","surreptitious","acrimonious"],"expl":"slanted（有偏见的）与 tendentious 描述信息都带立场，因此辨别不可能。选 AD"},{"id":"v84.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The auditors are relying on the failing bank to make changes that it has steadfastly resisted for years and even now does not seem _____ to carry out.","key":"DE","opts":["able","impatient","destined","disinclined","loath","keen"],"expl":"disinclined（不愿意）与 loath 呼应：银行一直不愿改变。选 DE"},{"id":"v84.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though it once seemed so disastrous, with hindsight the disintegration of the artists' collective is revealed as generative, for each of the dispersed factions acted as a _____, reproducing the collective's founding inspiration in a new setting.","key":"BE","opts":["strand","seed","shard","fragment","germ","blueprint"],"expl":"seed（种子）与 germ 呼应：各派系成为新的萌芽。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v84-2","title":"Test 84 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v84.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Williams finds the appearance of Whitman’s Leaves of Grass in 1855 nearly _____ given the immense disparity between Whitman’s earlier published works, which Williams finds dismal, and the consummate mastery of Leaves.","key":"D","opts":["oracular","prophetic","inevitable","inexplicable","inauspicious"],"expl":"inexplicable（难以解释的）与 “此前作品糟糕”形成反差。选 D"},{"id":"v84.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In his study of Senegambian cleric Shaykh Mass Kah (1827-1936), Bala S. K. Saho notes that it is difficult to fully (i)_____ many of the oral accounts on which the study relies. Saho’s work shows, however, that despite this absence of (ii)_____, oral history can provide useful sources from which historians can reconstruct the past.","key":"CF","groups":[["comprehend","reproduce","validate"],["partiality","argumentation","corroboration"]],"expl":"空1 validate（证实）；空2 corroboration（佐证）。选 CF"},{"id":"v84.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For a genre that’s supposed to be about the future, science fiction has certainly (i)_____ lately, (ii)_____ is what sells best, with readers spending their money on sequels to long-running series.","key":"BF","groups":[["become quite pessimistic","been looking backward","anticipated technological developments"],["suspense","fantasy","nostalgia"]],"expl":"空1 been looking backward（回望过去）；空2 nostalgia（怀旧）。选 BF"},{"id":"v84.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Those who blame the inadequacies of science education for students’ lack of reasoning skills perpetuate their unproductive notion of science as (i)_____, unique in its capacity to inoculate us against superstition and ignorance. Certainly a good science education can (ii)_____ habits of mind, but the (iii)_____ effect of education in nonscientific, humanistic subjects such as literature and history should not be underrated.","key":"CDH","groups":[["vocational","empirical","salvational"],["counter uncritical","discourage rigorous","temper creative"],["unforeseen","salutary","pedestrian"]],"expl":"教育与人文学科对推理能力的累积影响不应被低估，此处用 cumulative（累积的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v84.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientists are finding that the adult brain is far more _____ than they once thought: our behavior and environment can cause substantial rewiring of the brain or a reorganization of its functions and where they are located.","key":"CF","opts":["reparable","heterogeneous","malleable","variegated","complex","plastic"],"expl":"malleable（可塑的）与 plastic 描述大脑的可塑性。选 CF"},{"id":"v84.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The folktale is perhaps the most _____ form of literature: a story that everyone is free to tell and embellish because it belongs to no one in particular.","key":"DE","opts":["unpretentious","archaic","primitive","democratic","egalitarian","changeable"],"expl":"democratic（民主的）：民间故事属于大众。选 DE"},{"id":"v84.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"According to Panamanian composer Danilo Perez, the gravity of jazz pianist Randy Weston’s performances is _____: you can copy one of his chords, but it doesn't sound the same.","key":"AC","opts":["elusive","indelible","unattainable","estranging","purposeful","alienating"],"expl":"elusive（难以捉摸的）与 unattainable 描述 Weston 风格无法复制。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v85-1","title":"Test 85 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v85.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Once so fluid, the political situation had, two years after the declaration of the Republic, _____ so much that further change seemed inconceivable.","key":"D","opts":["revitalized","warmed","intensified","clotted","destabilized"],"expl":"clotted（凝固、停滞）：政治局势陷入僵局。选 D"},{"id":"v85.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)______ current-generation solar cells are (ii)______: although experimental cells have reached efficiencies greater than 40 percent, most commercially available cells in the early part of the twenty-first century still struggle to get past about 20 percent.","key":"BD","groups":[["attractions of","limitations of","improvements in"],["clear","unmatched","misunderstood"]],"expl":"空1 limitations of（局限）；空2 unmatched（无与伦比的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v85.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Media stories about climate regularly use spokespeople from interest groups as sources, but what those individuals say is often (i)_____, citing results from scientific research in a highly (ii)_____ manner and (iii)_____ the caveats that are part of a full scientific assessment.","key":"CEH","groups":[["ingenuous","maladroit","tendentious"],["erudite","selective","perspicuous"],["parsing","omitting","anticipating"]],"expl":"空1 tendentious（有倾向性的）；空2 selective（选择性的）；空3 omitting（省略）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v85.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the _____ of reliable sources in later narratives make many details of the early history of China’s Chou dynasty unverifiable, the Zhou rulers’ successful rise to power is certain.","key":"AC","opts":["dearth","ambiguity","paucity","opacity","authenticity","credibility"],"expl":"空1 dearth（缺乏）；空2 paucity（缺乏）。选 AC"},{"id":"v85.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because the influence of French women writers in seventeenth-century England has been _____ by scholars, England’s early women writers, such as Aphra Behn and Delarivier Manley, may appear to have sprung from a vacuum.","key":"CE","opts":["documented","discredited","slighted","misinterpreted","discounted","corroborated"],"expl":"slighted（忽视）与 discounted 描述法国影响被低估。选 CE"},{"id":"v85.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some historians have _____ the disjunction between the decades preceding and the ones following the political coup, ignoring the fact that the coup fell in the middle of a twenty-year period of considerable social and economic continuity.","key":"AB","opts":["overstated","exaggerated","questioned","misjudged","misinterpreted","overlooked"],"expl":"overstated（夸大）：有些历史学家夸大了断裂。选 AB"},{"id":"v85.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although extreme and singular events occur in a black hole, its event horizon boundary is _____ space travelers; crossing it would be subject to the same physical laws that apply anywhere else.","key":"CF","opts":["illusory","obscure","unremarkable","immutable","unchanging","commonplace"],"expl":"unremarkable（无异于寻常的）：对太空旅行者而言，视界并不特殊。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v85-2","title":"Test 85 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v85.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Paul Robeson. Jr. wrote that his father was a flesh-and-blood artist whose accomplishments made him susceptible to hagiographic treatment by potential biographers. Robeson’s achievements were real, and there was no need for _____.","key":"B","opts":["disclosure","hyperbole","retraction","muckraking","reticence"],"expl":"hyperbole（夸饰）：无需夸大。选 B"},{"id":"v85.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Boreal forest is at the southern boundary of the moss-dominated tundra, which remains characteristically treeless because its spongy surface retains water that cannot drain away through the underlying permafrost. But as temperatures rise the permafrost recedes, (i)______ the (ii)______ of forest.","key":"BE","groups":[["impairing","facilitating","decelerating"],["renewal","incursion","decline"]],"expl":"空1 facilitating（促进）；空2 incursion（侵入）。选 BE"},{"id":"v85.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"As late as the 1990s, Merry Wiesner Hanks argued that developments during the Reformation and the Enlightenment had (i)______ effects on the participation of women in the filed of medicine. She claimed that the (ii)______ Reformation and Enlightenment women left female health’s practitioners restricted to assisting in an unpaid and unrecognized capacity.","key":"AE","groups":[["dire","positive","ambiguous"],["unchanging opportunities for","worsening positions of","reader respect for"]],"expl":"空1 dire（严重的）；空2 worsening positions of（恶化的处境）。选 AE"},{"id":"v85.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"For Ruskin, architecture serves the community only when approached in a spirit of piety and (i)_____. Architecture must set effective boundaries to public space, and it does so by (ii)_____ the desire to show off, to stand out, to record the artistic flair of some temporary ego. Architecture succeeds in its public task through (iii)_____ and devotion, of the kind that can be observed in the moulding, firing and laying of a properly proportioned brick, but which is violated at every point by Frank Gehry’s bombastic Guggenheim Museum in Bilbao.","key":"CFG","groups":[["altruism","sanctimony","sacrifice"],["retrieving","fastening","relinquishing"],["humility","demise","braggadocio"]],"expl":"空1 self-restraint（克制）；空2 suppressing（压制）；空3 humility（谦卑）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v85.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although, in spirit at least, solar panels _____ nature and the way our biosphere harnesses the energy of our sun, the actual photosynthetic process by which plants convert sunlight into chemical energy is far more complex than solar power generation is.","key":"CF","opts":["streamline","enhance","imitate","exploit","simplify","mimic"],"expl":"mimic / imitate 描述太阳能板模仿自然。选 CF"},{"id":"v85.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The historical study of pregnancy and childbearing began fairly recently and has been hindered by the relative _____ of records concerning these particular experiences.","key":"BC","opts":["pertinence","dearth","paucity","ambiguity","expediency","applicability"],"expl":"dearth / paucity 描述记录稀少。选 BC"},{"id":"v85.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In literature, thrillers thrive on heroes and villains, and usually the characterization is not very _____; writers don’t want to confuse or slow the plot.","key":"AF","opts":["nuanced","trite","realistic","monotonous","banal","subtle"],"expl":"nuanced（细致入微的）与 subtle 呼应：人物刻画不细腻。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v86-1","title":"Test 86 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v86.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Wood is an environmentally friendly building material because it _____ carbon dioxide, absorbing it during growth and retaining it even after it has been turned into lumber.","key":"C","opts":["disperses","eradicates","sequesters","respires","regulates"],"expl":"sequesters（封存）：木材将二氧化碳封存。选 C"},{"id":"v86.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Early in the development of ice age theories, physicists identified the processing( slow gyration) and wobbling of Earth’s spin axis as the likely drivers of the ice ages, but geologists (i)______, and even the painstaking work done in the 1920s and 1930s by Mihution Mplankovitch failed to (ii)______ of many of the day’s geological experts.","key":"AE","groups":[["demurred","acquiesced","expatriate"],["anticipate the ascent","assuage the qualms","acknowledge the consensus"]],"expl":"空1 demurred（表示异议）；空2 assuage the qualms（消除疑虑）。选 AE"},{"id":"v86.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The fall of the monarchical order produced a score of fragile successor states in Europe that (i)_____ ethnic discontent and revanchism. This (ii)_____, when fused with those states’ inherent feebleness, make for power voids and political (iii)_____.","key":"CFH","groups":[["kept down","overshadowed","simmered with"],["cosmopolitanism","hierarchy","volatility"],["cures","fluidities","redundancies"]],"expl":"空1 simmered with（潜藏着）；空2 volatility（不稳定）；空3 volatility 与 fluidities 类。选 CFH"},{"id":"v86.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Monarch butterflies sequester toxins in their skin to discourage predators, but black-backed orioles (Icterus abeillei) _____ the defense: they consume only the soft insides of the butterfly.","key":"DE","opts":["anticipate","disable","ignore","skirt","circumvent","disregard"],"expl":"skirt（规避）与 circumvent 描述橙斑鸟绕过防御。选 DE"},{"id":"v86.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though it lacked _____ demeanor, Guatemala City was nonetheless a compelling place to be in 1954.","key":"AB","opts":["an engaging","a winning","a sophisticated","a detached","a workaday","a quotidian"],"expl":"a winning（迷人的）：危地马拉城缺乏迷人魅力。选 AB"},{"id":"v86.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"By eating tiny organisms and incorporating their prey’s nutrients into their own bodies, large insects become “nutrient packages” for larger insectivores for whom the pursuit of tiny organisms would be _____.","key":"CF","opts":["unwieldy","insalubrious","unremunerative","unnecessary","inopportune","unprofitable"],"expl":"unremunerative（无利可图的）：追逐微小生物对较大的食虫动物而言并不划算。选 CF"},{"id":"v86.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Researchers comparing test subjects’ abilities to interpret others’ facial expressions found that while some expressions were easy to interpret, others were difficult because they were so ______ the person making the expression.","key":"CD","opts":["habitual for","customary for","peculiar to","idiosyncratic to","opaque to","inoffensive to"],"expl":"idiosyncratic to / peculiar to（为……特有的）：某些表情对个人而言独特。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v86-2","title":"Test 86 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v86.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Despite the fact that it is quite difficult to find, in everyday discourse, causal explanations taking the form Hume proposed, many philosophers have regarded Hume’s model as _____ causal accounts.","key":"A","opts":["paradigmatic of","unworkable for","tendentious about","superfluous to","irreducible to"],"expl":"paradigmatic of（范式的代表）：Hume 的模型被视为因果解释的范例。选 A"},{"id":"v86.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"As a longtime fan of the fashion photography Web site, I wasn’t sure if I wanted to see its images presented in a book, with all of the (i)______ that implies. What I’ve always enjoyed about the photos is their (ii)______: they are disposable snapshots of what’s going on in the world of style right now.","key":"CE","groups":[["nonchalance","commercialism","permanency"],["elegant","ephemeral","mundane"]],"expl":"空1 commercialism（商业化）；空2 ephemeral（短暂的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v86.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Research indicates that many people hold (i)_____ views about government, believing that elected officials should be able to overcome differences and get things done while also regarding a willingness to compromise as a sign of (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["cynical","self-contradictory","shortsighted"],["fickleness","pragmatism","intractability"]],"expl":"人们既认为官员应当妥协，又把愿意妥协视为某种实用精神（pragmatism）；这里。选 BD"},{"id":"v86.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the early 1990s, the discovery of a new microbe in wastewater led microbiologists to (i)______ ammonia’s conversion to nitrogen compounds. Called anammox (for anaerobic ammonia oxidation), the microbe was converting into nitrogen gas in the absence of oxygen, a reaction previously assumed to be (ii)______.","key":"AF","groups":[["question existing dogma about","abandon efforts to facilitate","raise health concerns regarding"],["hazardous","irreversible","impossible"]],"expl":"空1 question existing dogma about（质疑既有教条）；空2 impossible（不可能的），此前认为该反应需要氧气，故不可能。选 AF"},{"id":"v86.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is troubling that blogs, which may be among the least reliable sources of information in human history, occupy such _____ positions in Internet search engine results.","key":"BF","opts":["enviable","conspicuous","suspect","dubious","controversial","prominent"],"expl":"prominent（显著的）与 conspicuous 描述博客在搜索结果中的位置。选 BF"},{"id":"v86.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is a vast disparity of computational power between mathematical _____ like many of us and a mathematical prodigy like Ramanujan.","key":"DF","opts":["dullards","enthusiasts","virtuosos","tyros","geniuses","novices"],"expl":"空缺处与 prodigy 相对：普通数学爱好者 dullards（笨人）与 novices（新手）。选 DF"},{"id":"v86.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"An academic with a questionable record in either teaching, administration, or research may still be well regarded at many schools, but simultaneous failure in all three areas normally results in ______ by superiors.","key":"DE","opts":["exculpation","dismissal","impeachment","disapprobation","censure","acquittal"],"expl":"censure（谴责）与 dismissal（解雇）：三方面都不佳时，通常会遭到斥责或解雇。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v87-1","title":"Test 87 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v87.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because of its _____, DNA can be invaluable as exculpatory evidence following a criminal conviction: it can be reliably tested years after a crime has occurred.","key":"C","opts":["versatility","recognizability","durability","verifiability","distinctiveness"],"expl":"durability（耐久性）：DNA 可在多年后检测，因其稳定。选 C"},{"id":"v87.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many civic institutions tend to (i)_____, when they do not actively discourage, the better natures of the citizenry. People are individually altruistic social animals who nonetheless teach themselves to be (ii)_____ in the public sphere.","key":"BD","groups":[["expose","ignore","presuppose"],["selfish","critical","adamant"]],"expl":"空1 presuppose（预设）；空2 selfish（自私的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v87.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Computers’ triumph in chess had been engineered not by creating machines that (i)_____ human thought, as most experts in artificial intelligence had expected, but by perfecting machines that played like machines. The analogy with flight is (ii)_____: as long as people tried to fly by imitating birds, attaching wings to their arms and flapping madly, they were (iii)_____ to fail. Once engineering escaped the paradigm of the familiar, however, people were soon flying much faster than birds.","key":"AEI","groups":[["aped","shelved","subverted"],["disingenuous","instructive","narrow"],["expected","likely","doomed"]],"expl":"空1 imitate（模仿）人类思维；空2 analogous（类似的）；空3 doomed（注定的）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v87.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The scholar defended W.E.B. Du Bois from the charge of being ______ by pointing out that whenever Du Bois changed his views, he acknowledged it, explained his reasons for doing so, and moved on.","key":"AC","opts":["inconsistent","insensitive","erratic","unsympathetic","pugnacious","irresponsible"],"expl":"inconsistent（前后不一致）：学者为杜波依斯辩护，说他改变观点会说明。选 AC"},{"id":"v87.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Sea turtle’s grazing on sea grass is less _____ near Bermuda than elsewhere: Bermuda protects sea turtles as an endangered species but does not protect their predators, tiger sharks.","key":"DE","opts":["consistent","pervasive","inhibited","destructive","damaging","constrained"],"expl":"constrained / inhibited（受抑制）：海龟的啃食在百慕大受到更多限制。选 DE"},{"id":"v87.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Comparing seawater to ice in asteroids to determine the origin of Earth's water is _____: the bulk of Earth's water, hidden deep underground, differs in composition from seawater.","key":"BE","opts":["instructive","inapposite","unnecessary","premature","misguided","challenging"],"expl":"inapposite（不恰当的）：比较海水与冰并不恰当。选 BE"},{"id":"v87.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Jane Austen belonged to the social class about which she mainly wrote, and although her novels offer abundant satire, one never has the sense that she viewed the basic elements of this social sphere as _____.","key":"CD","opts":["laudable","unfathomable","ignoble","reprehensible","inviolable","praiseworthy"],"expl":"ignoble（卑劣的）与 reprehensible 相对：奥斯汀并不认为社会的基本要素卑劣。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v87-2","title":"Test 87 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v87.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Throughout the High Middle Ages, the English government became increasingly _____: the document produced in the eleventh century could be placed on one large table, while the documents produced in the thirteenth fill whole rooms.","key":"D","opts":["despotic","ceremonial","aristocratic","prolix","insular"],"expl":"prolix（冗长的）：文件越来越繁复冗长。选 D"},{"id":"v87.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is unfortunate that essays by literary critics so infrequently (i)______ the opinions of novelists and poets, for creative writers are often quite (ii)______ about their own philosophies and are frequently more familiar with alternative systems of thought than critics are.","key":"CD","groups":[["influence","challenge","incorporate"],["articulate","inconsistent","prejudiced"]],"expl":"空1 incorporate（吸收）；空2 articulate（善于表达的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v87.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"At one time researchers viewed the placebo effect as (i)_____, a statistical (ii)_____ faced by those attempting an objective evaluation of the efficacy of potentially legitimate therapies. That view has changed: the placebo effect is today seen as an important part of the healing process.","key":"CE","groups":[["a boon","a touchstone","an impediment"],["increment","annoyance","deviation"]],"expl":"空1 an impediment（障碍）；空2 deviation（偏差）。选 CE"},{"id":"v87.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The lack of (i)______ the poetry of the postwar decades has led not, as one might have expected, to (ii)______ poetry, but to a curious closure in which all poets and forms of poetry are (iii)_______ and alone, not even respected establishment poets.","key":"BDG","groups":[["interest in","consensus about","innovation in"],["pluralistic debate on","popular acceptance of","any experimentation in"],["marginalized","revered","tolerated"]],"expl":"空1 interest in；空2 pluralistic debate on（多元讨论）；空3 marginalized（边缘化）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v87.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Orbiting Jupiter just beyond Europa, the giant moon Ganymede—bigger than the planet Mercury —appears rather _____ on the outside, but it may be warm and active within.","key":"DF","opts":["desiccated","forbidding","weathered","inert","adamant","dormant"],"expl":"forbidding（令人望而生畏的）与 inert 描述木卫三外表平静。选 DF"},{"id":"v87.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the use of cameras to study animal behavior was certainly not _____, cameras were nevertheless not used to study individual frogs in their natural habitat until 2009.","key":"BE","opts":["ideal","unprecedented","laborious","impractical","novel","perfect"],"expl":"unprecedented（前所未有的）：用相机研究动物行为并不前所未有。选 BE"},{"id":"v87.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In nineteenth-century Puerto Rico, the consumption of salted cod spread among the entire population; on the tables of humbler families it became ______ food, adding flavor to other products and supplying much-needed protein.","key":"CF","opts":["an exotic","an affordable","an essential","a supplemental","a complementary","a commonplace"],"expl":"commonplace（普通的）：咸鳕鱼成为寻常食物。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v88-1","title":"Test 88 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v88.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Characteristic of the diplomat’s new book is the ______ relationship between the evidence adduced and the inferences drawn, the footnotes and citations teeming with ambiguity and complexity, while the summary statements are more dogmatic simplicities.","key":"C","opts":["healthy","shifting","tenuous","compelling","plausible"],"expl":"tenuous（薄弱的）：证据与推论的关联很脆弱。选 C"},{"id":"v88.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"To function as (i)_____, literary critics must write well. A badly written book review is worse than a badly written political speech or greeting card; a badly written review is (ii)_____, like a barber with a terrible haircut. If critics cannot write well, how can they authoritatively recognize and promote good writing?","key":"BF","groups":[["soothsayers","evangelists","iconoclasts"],["self-aggrandizing","self-knowing","self-defeating"]],"expl":"空1 evangelists（布道者）；空2 self-aggrandizing（自我夸大的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v88.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Genetic researchers have recently suggested that our political learnings may be determined by our DNA, a view that tends to undermine our reflective self-flattery. We (i)_____ the idea that personal politics are entirely (ii)_____. The genetic explanation for ideology (iii)_____ our belief that we are persuaded only by rational arguments.","key":"ADG","groups":[["recoil from","revel in","puzzle over"],["deliberative","inexpensive","self-serving"],["defies","entails","parallels"]],"expl":"空1 recoil from（畏缩于）；空2 deliberative（审慎的）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v88.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Jimi Hendrix was a pivotal figure in the visionary aesthetic movement known as Afrofuturism, which is steeped in African American musical tradition yet _____ technological innovation, from synthesizers to spaceships.","key":"CE","opts":["circumspect about","indebted to","enthralled by","wary of","captivated by","heedful of"],"expl":"indebted to（受惠于）与 enthralled 描述非裔音乐与技术的关系。选 CE"},{"id":"v88.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Sánchez’ novels have been praised for their remarkable _____, the way in which they so palpably represent a certain place and time.","key":"BD","opts":["imaginativeness","realism","allusiveness","verisimilitude","compassion","empathy"],"expl":"verisimilitude（逼真性）与 realism 描述作品再现地点与时代的真实感。选 BD"},{"id":"v88.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because previous experience in office tends to reveal the limits of a political candidate's power, we are often _____ candidates with little experience, blank slates onto which we can project our fantasies for change.","key":"DE","opts":["interested in","uneasy about","hoodwinked by","drawn to","captivated by","troubled by"],"expl":"drawn to（受吸引）：选民往往被缺乏经验的候选人吸引。选 DE"},{"id":"v88.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While Davy is regarded as a giant of early chemistry and was once known to every educated British school child, his mentor Beddoes is seen as a _____ figure, even by historians of medicine.","key":"BD","opts":["risible","peripheral","charismatic","subsidiary","beguiling","misleading"],"expl":"peripheral（边缘的）与 subsidiary 描述 Beddoes 的地位。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v88-2","title":"Test 88 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v88.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Notwithstanding a lack of _____, nineteenth-century anthologies such as Evert and George Duyckinck’s Cyclopaedia of American Literature represents serious attempts to collect the national writings up to that point as a way of establishing the viability of American letters.","key":"C","opts":["bias","earnestness","rigor","ambition","ambiguity"],"expl":"rigor（严谨性）：虽缺乏严谨，仍是认真的尝试。选 C"},{"id":"v88.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the recent proliferation of gourmet and specialty salts, studies suggest that it would take an unusually (i)_____ palate to (ii)_____ foods prepared with different salts—most salts taste the same to most people.","key":"CD","groups":[["broad","indiscriminate","sensitive"],["distinguish","enjoy","modify"]],"expl":"空1 sensitive（敏锐的）；空2 distinguish（分辨）。选 CD"},{"id":"v88.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the search for truth, the knowledge gained by scientists consists of approximations with varying degrees of certainty. Such (i)_____ truth can be highly (ii)_____, as the rapid and relatively steady progress of medical knowledge well exemplifies.","key":"CD","groups":[["unambiguous","esoteric","provisional"],["useful","equivocal","contentious"]],"expl":"空1 provisional（暂定的）；空2 useful（有用的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v88.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The mind has a tendency to (i)_____ abstractions, so that one might envision the ego existing somewhere physically in the brain, but Freud (ii)_____ such a physical structure: rather, he (iii)_____.","key":"BDI","groups":[["create","hypostatize","incorporate"],["did not posit","did not preclude","did not abjure"],["believed that it is illusory","theorized that it is","regard it as a process"]],"expl":"空1 hypostatize（实体化）；空2 did not posit（并不假设）；空3 regard it as a process（视为过程）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v88.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Throughout the trial the plaintiff has been _____, refusing to comply with orders with which she disagreed.","key":"BD","opts":["histrionic","refractory","meticulous","recalcitrant","idiosyncratic","conscientious"],"expl":"refractory（执拗的）与 recalcitrant 描述原告拒不服从。选 BD"},{"id":"v88.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Psychologists have discovered that some of the most _____ advice on study habits is flat wrong, leading them to revise the guidelines they offer to students.","key":"BC","opts":["popular","hallowed","respected","unassailable","effective","beneficial"],"expl":"hallowed（被奉为圭臬的）：流行建议被证明错误。选 BC"},{"id":"v88.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite a reputation, once richly deserved, for _____ in adopting new technologies, most big carmakers are pouring resources both into battery power and other alternative forms of propulsion, and into automated driving.","key":"AC","opts":["indolence","stoicism","sloth","patience","dispassion","misjudgment"],"expl":"sloth（懒惰）与 indolence：过去汽车业以拖沓著称。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v89-1","title":"Test 89 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v89.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Unable to escape their own literary tradition, literary critics either become the ______ of that tradition or, on the contrary, use their knowledge of it to reinterpret writers and trends from new perspectives.","key":"B","opts":["liberators","guardians","successors","antithesis","gadflies"],"expl":"guardians（守护者）：文学批评者要么成为传统守护者。选 B"},{"id":"v89.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The kilt has certainly had (i)______ history, outlawed as it was by Britain in 1746 as an emblem of nationalist subversion, then more recently (ii)______ from men’s to women’s apparel in a 2003 European Union survey, and ridiculed at various times for a wide variety of reasons.","key":"CD","groups":[["an obscure","an illustrious","a contentious"],["reclassified","feigned","manufactured"]],"expl":"空1 an illustrious（光荣的）；空2 reclassified（重新归类）。选 CD"},{"id":"v89.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Greenhouse gases emitted into atmosphere are virtually permanent, and because they (i)_________ in the atmosphere, their effects is (ii)_______. These facts necessitate that policies related to greenhouse gases differ from policies related to various pollutants whose effects are (iii)______ and often temporary.","key":"CEG","groups":[["disperse evenly","accrue gradually","persist indefinitely"],["subtle","global","transit"],["local","contrary","hazardous"]],"expl":"空1 persist indefinitely（长期存在）；空2 global（全球性的）；空3 transient（短暂的）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v89.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The photocopier, widely adopted in the 1960s, became not merely a vehicle for copying but one for publishing in _____ manner, so that ideas could be circulated without interference from potential censors.","key":"BF","opts":["an incendiary","a clandestine","an expeditious","a collaborative","a cooperative","a surreptitious"],"expl":"surreptitious（秘密的）与 clandestine 描述秘密出版。选 BF"},{"id":"v89.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because there has been such a _____ of information about Jorge Luis Borges’ personal life, it is easy to understand the eager excitement generated by Borges, a selection from the diaries of his closest friend.","key":"CD","opts":["stream","glut","paucity","dearth","surfeit","tangle"],"expl":"glut（过剩）：关于博尔赫斯的信息十分充足。选 CD"},{"id":"v89.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"“Over-appropriation”--i.e., excessive exploitation—of water is now the norm for many of the state's streams, resulting in extremely low seasonal flows and even, in some cases, in the drying up of formerly _____ streams.","key":"AF","opts":["constant","inundated","healthy","arid","desiccated","perennial"],"expl":"perennial（常年的）：过去常年有水的河流现在干涸。选 AF"},{"id":"v89.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"What Dr.Walther has shown is that many of the standard statistical techniques that are supposed to insure against _____ correlations are inadequate in this case.","key":"BF","opts":["numerical","specious","elementary","paltry","quantifiable","spurious"],"expl":"spurious（伪造的）：防止虚假相关。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v89-2","title":"Test 89 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v89.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Not only was Jarry ______ the pandemonium his play sparkled, he actually worked to foment the conflict, organizing a posse to boo if the rest of the audience applauded and cheer if the other attendees booed.","key":"C","opts":["riled by","surprised by","unperturbed by","critical of","detached from"],"expl":"unperturbed by（不受扰动）：Jarry 并不被观众混乱所动。选 C"},{"id":"v89.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some have challenged scientists who attribute the surge in amphibian deaths to habitat loss, since numerous populations have (i)_____ in protected parks and nature reserved—even in remote wilderness areas: places that are removed from humans’ modern effluvium and that are presumably (ii)_____ such effects.","key":"CE","groups":[["rebounded","stabilized","declined"],["preserved with","insulated from","enhanced by"]],"expl":"空1 rebounded（恢复）；空2 insulated from（隔绝于）。选 CE"},{"id":"v89.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Though nations no longer (i)_____ nuclear physicists—the men and women who once delivered the destructive power of the atom bomb—physics still has the same power to (ii)_____ but in another way, by revealing the basic truths that underpin reality.","key":"AD","groups":[["compete for","worry about","cower before"],["produce awe","incite debates","challenge orthodoxy"]],"expl":"空1 compete for（争夺）；空2 produce awe（引发敬畏）。选 AD"},{"id":"v89.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the nineteenth century the (i) _____ advanced mechanical printing techniques made it possible for newspaper owners to print newspapers cheaply and in mass quantities, but unlike many other mechanized industries, where machines (ii) _____ workers, the new printing machines required trained compositors to run them, thereby (iii) _____ the demand for skilled printing labor.","key":"ADI","groups":[["wide application of","extensive resistance to","great expense of"],["marginalized","intrigued","isolated"],["ignoring","anticipating","increasing"]],"expl":"空1 wide application of（广泛应用）；空2 displace（取代）；空3 increased（增加）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v89.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The colors of brocaded silks made by Merina weavers in Madagascar were not _____: magenta, blue, black, pink, yellow, and brown characterize pieces before 1880, while thereafter green, purple, and orange come to the fore.","key":"AE","opts":["invariable","generic","conventional","repetitious","static","traditional"],"expl":"invariable（不变的）与 static 相对：颜色随时间变化。选 AE"},{"id":"v89.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"This novel resembles a piece of music in the way it _____ variations on separate themes that contrast, conflict, and combine to form ever-more-fascinating patterns.","key":"AD","opts":["deploys","alters","rejects","marshals","reiterates","repudiates"],"expl":"deploys（部署）：小说像音乐一样部署主题变奏。选 AD"},{"id":"v89.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ocean's heat capacity (the amount of heat needed to change its temperature) is far greater than that of dry land and thus _____ the ocean's seasonal temperature changes.","key":"BE","opts":["reflects","mutes","alters","determines","attenuates","parallels"],"expl":"mutes（减弱）：海洋的热容量减弱了季节性温度变化。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v90-1","title":"Test 90 · Section 1","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v90.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Behavior dubbed reprehensible by the residents of the region is considered conventional, even ______ by those of the neighboring region; fortunately, people traveling between the two are resigned to this disparity.","key":"B","opts":["eccentric","compulsory","innovative","unconscionable","transparent"],"expl":"compulsory（强制的）与 conventional 对比：邻地可能认为是必须的。选 B"},{"id":"v90.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Though the play crackles with humor, the dialogue is less (i)_____ when it comes to the drama’s emotional core. There the players tend to spell out their emotions in (ii)_____ aphorisms, and repeat them as necessary.","key":"AE","groups":[["adroit","ambiguous","transparent"],["shrewd","jejune","riotous"]],"expl":"空1 ambiguous（模糊的）；空2 jejune（幼稚的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v90.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In some ways, fascism can be viewed as (i)_____ social contract: The individual (ii)_____ nearly all his or her political identity and (iii)_____ to the state.","key":"CDH","groups":[["an arbitrary","an altruistic","the ultimate"],["cedes","ascribes","denies"],["machinations","autonomy","ascendancy"]],"expl":"空1 the ultimate（终极的）；空2 cedes（让渡）；空3 autonomy（自主）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v90.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Just two centuries after the _____ of Chinese algebra under the Song, even the finest mathematicians of Ming China could not fathom earlier texts.","key":"AC","opts":["apogee","rebirth","pinnacle","nadir","expansion","initiation"],"expl":"apogee（鼎盛）与 pinnacle 描述宋代代数的顶峰。选 AC"},{"id":"v90.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Eubank's efforts to facilitate _____ between the two sides came to nothing but could be seen as an early blueprint for the historic agreement between the sides over ten years later.","key":"BD","opts":["an alliance","a rapprochement","a conversation","a reconciliation","an altercation","a quarrel"],"expl":"rapprochement（和解）：促进双方和解。选 BD"},{"id":"v90.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The essayist was known to suffer fools impatiently, but admittedly her vast intellect made that _____ largely justified.","key":"AE","opts":["hauteur","diffidence","irritability","imperturbability","superciliousness","timorousness"],"expl":"hauteur（傲慢）与 superciliousness 描述她对愚人的不耐烦。选 AE"},{"id":"v90.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Discussion of planetary orbits is _____ in the context of climate history today, thanks to the acceptance of the thesis that periodic fluctuations in the Earth's axial tilt and precession affect the timing and severity of glacial cycles.","key":"CF","opts":["controversial","gratuitous","commonplace","unnecessary","fraught","pervasive"],"expl":"fraught（充满……的）：气候史研究中轨道讨论充满争议。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v90-2","title":"Test 90 · Section 2","group":"Test 81–90","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v90.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Though acquaintances are first overwhelmed by his ______, they soon appreciate that, contrary to appearances, he is not without self-interest.","key":"B","opts":["egotism","magnanimity","ambition","profligacy","brilliance"],"expl":"egotism（自负）：初见时的印象是自负。选 B"},{"id":"v90.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In 1831, a domestic insurrection that had stirred central Italy was squelched by the Austrian army, but while this invasion destroyed the immediate results of the movement, it could not ______ the insurrections causes, which continued to be felt.","key":"B","opts":["ignore","extirpate","fathom","anticipate","underscore"],"expl":"extirpate（根除）：入侵无法根除起因。选 B"},{"id":"v90.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"If all stars are fiery gas balls like our own sun, and if the principle that the situation of our own solar system is not (i)_____ is (ii)_____, then one might think that many other stars should be surrounded by a retinue of planets and moons.","key":"CD","groups":[["obvious","permanent","special"],["true","redundant","tested"]],"expl":"空1 special（特殊的）；空2 true（成立的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v90.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"In considering whether to (i)_____ mergers of large corporations, governments now must consider the impact of such mergers on a country’s international competitiveness; for example, the United States has allowed the mergers of (ii)_____ such as Lockheed and Boeing in the aerospace industry in the belief European consortiums, backed by government funding, could pose a threat to American (iii)_____ in that industry.","key":"BDH","groups":[["encourage","prevent","investigate"],["behemoths","offshoots","mavericks"],["chauvinism","preeminence","sovereignty"]],"expl":"空1 approve（批准）；空2 rivals（竞争者）。选 BDH"},{"id":"v90.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While Elizabeth Barrett Browning often wrote in restrictively intricate verse forms such as the Petrarchan sonnet, she also sometimes ______ formal constraints in poetry.","key":"CF","opts":["defended","neglected","dismissed","appropriated","vindicated","repudiated"],"expl":"appropriated（挪用）：她有时会挪用形式约束。选 CF"},{"id":"v90.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Journal editors note that the peer review process has difficulty detecting _____: deliberate misinformation, if it is clever enough, might sail right through no matter how scrupulous the reviews.","key":"CE","opts":["bias","inconsistency","fraud","negligence","duplicity","carelessness"],"expl":"fraud（欺诈）与 duplicity 相关：蓄意误导难被发现。选 CE"},{"id":"v90.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The rapid melting of glaciers around the globe, while an ominous reminder of global warming, has been _____ for archaeologists, since glaciers are storehouses of frozen materials from prehistoric times.","key":"DE","opts":["a conundrum","a nuisance","an inconvenience","a boon","a windfall","a puzzle"],"expl":"a boon（福音）与 a puzzle 描述冰川融化对考古学的影响。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v91-1","title":"Test 91 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v91.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"When he first hypothesized the neutrino, Wolfgang Pauli’s elation was not ______: he feared that he had postulated a particle that could not be detected though his concern turned out to be overblown.","key":"D","opts":["unshared","untoward","unprecedented","unqualified","unjustified"],"expl":"unqualified（无保留的）：Pauli 的喜悦并非毫无保留。选 D"},{"id":"v91.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Standard thermal evolution models of giant planets employ initial conditions that are, to some extent, arbitrarily chosen, selected more for computational expediency than for physical accuracy. Since eventually the initial conditions (i)_____ the evolving planet, this approach is more (ii)_____ for mature planets than it is for young planets.","key":"AF","groups":[["become irrelevant to","are recreated by","enforce constraints on"],["involved","unpredictable","valid"]],"expl":"空1 become irrelevant to（与……无关）；空2 less accurate（不够准确）。选 AF"},{"id":"v91.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For feminist scholars, Kessler-Harris’s concern that the term “labor history” (i)_____ images of male workers exclusively may be (ii)_____; her own immense contributions to the field offer evidence that feminism has (iii)_____ the questions posed by labor historians, moving women’s concerns from the periphery closer to the center of labor history writing.","key":"CEH","groups":[["spurns","subsumes","evokes"],["overly bold","too pessimistic","unwittingly condescending"],["negated","altered","underscored"]],"expl":"空1 evokes（唤起）；空2 overly bold 与 subsumes（包含）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v91.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though initially presented in a blaze of hyperbole, the thesis is stated more ______ in the ensuing paragraphs.","key":"BF","opts":["humbly","levelheadedly","pretentiously","convincingly","showily","soberly"],"expl":"soberly（冷静地）：论点后期说得更冷静。选 BF"},{"id":"v91.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The geometry student struggled with the request to demonstrate the ______ proposition, feeling that, since opposite angles were self-evidently equal, there was no need for a proof.","key":"AD","opts":["patent","nebulous","arcane","manifest","illogical","plausible"],"expl":"manifest（显而易见的）与 patent 描述对角相等的显然性。选 AD"},{"id":"v91.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The safety features of modern cars have actually had _____ effect on people's driving: drivers are lulled into a false sense of security by their cars’ sophistication and therefore drive less attentively.","key":"DF","opts":["an unintended","an unaccountable","an inconsequential","a deleterious","a negligible","a pernicious"],"expl":"an unintended（无意的）与 deleterious（有害的）描述安全功能的反效果。选 DF"},{"id":"v91.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Evidence of the human brain's ______ abounds: violinists, for example, tend to have larger cortical areas devoted to processing signals from their fingering hands than do non-violinists.","key":"BD","opts":["synchronicity","flexibility","complexity","malleability","vulnerability","sensitivity"],"expl":"malleability（可塑性）：大脑的可塑性。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v91-2","title":"Test 91 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v91.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In its literature and its political discourse, the nation has created various narratives about itself that tend to ______ intractable social divisions in the interest of perpetuating a dubious myth of unity.","key":"B","opts":["denounce","obscure","corroborate","anatomize","explicate"],"expl":"obscure（掩盖）：叙事掩盖了社会分歧。选 B"},{"id":"v91.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The city’s traffic-planning department has been working hard to (i)______ drivers. Closely spaced stop lights have been added on roads into town, causing delays. Pedestrian underpasses designed to allow traffic to flow freely across major intersections have been (ii)______.","key":"CF","groups":[["assist","calm","discourage"],["enhanced","stabilized","removed"]],"expl":"空1 discourage（阻碍）；空2 removed（拆除）。选 CF"},{"id":"v91.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Gelles urges readers of Abigail Adams’ letters to consider their (i)_____: in Adams’ era women were denied a public persona separate from that of their husbands. That said, Gelles then (ii)_____ to promote Adams from a writer of private letters to a public figure, arguing that she was a significant force for change.","key":"BF","groups":[["value","context","style"],["strains","neglects","fails"]],"expl":"空1 context（语境）；空2 fails（失败）。选 BF"},{"id":"v91.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Rocke’s history of the emergence of the theory of chemical structure encapsulates over 30 years of research on nineteenth-century chemistry. This is (i)_____, since structure theory emerged gradually through the efforts of a network of chemists distributed across several countries. Rocke focuses on just a few key figures, a strategy that necessarily involves some (ii)_____ of detail but that leads to (iii)_____ account of the subject.","key":"CDG","groups":[["something often","a regrettable ploy","no mean feat"],["sacrifice","redundancy","appreciation"],["a digestible","an untrustworthy","a digressive"]],"expl":"空1 accurate（准确的）；空2 neglects（忽视）；空3 a more faithful（更忠实的）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v91.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author first accused the official of espionage in a 1981 book, and—though the case was far from _____, full of suppositions rather than compelling evidence—the accusation has been repeated relentlessly ever since.","key":"CF","opts":["unambitious","unconvincing","unassailable","implausible","coherent","airtight"],"expl":"unassailable（无可辩驳的）与 airtight 对比：证据不足以定罪。选 CF"},{"id":"v91.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Planetary systems are _____, with the orbits of even the largest planets able to evolve and migrate, especially in the early period when interaction between forming planets and the protoplanetary disc is strong.","key":"BE","opts":["stable","dynamic","predictable","idiosyncratic","mutable","enigmatic"],"expl":"dynamic（动态的）：行星系统是动态的。选 BE"},{"id":"v91.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In hindsight, it is easy to say that the geological evidence for ice ages was _____ and to wonder why such periods in the Earth's past were not recognized earlier.","key":"BD","opts":["accessible","overwhelming","emerging","irresistible","intriguing","tenuous"],"expl":"overwhelming（压倒性的）与 tenuous 对比：证据其实很薄弱。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v92-1","title":"Test 92 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v92.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The notion that prehistoric farming of Micronesia’s Mariana Islands degraded the soils upon which savannas now occur is ______ by soil scientists, who attribute nutrient-poor savanna soils instead to long geological periods of tropical weathering.","key":"C","opts":["bolstered","proposed","contradicted","elucidated","revived"],"expl":"contradicted（被反驳）：这一假设被土壤科学家反驳。选 C"},{"id":"v92.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The reason geological activity on Mars is so (i)_____ while on Earth it remains (ii)______ is that Earth’s diameter is about twice the size of Mars. Because Mars is smaller than Earth, it cooled faster, and therefore it lost the interrial heat that drives tectonic activity.","key":"BD","groups":[["localized","moribund","violent"],["vital","unnoticed","predictable"]],"expl":"空1 moribund（垂死的）；空2 vital（活跃的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v92.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)_____ of community ecology and population ecology is (ii)_____ insofar as the two subdisciplines partly address issues at different hierarchical levels and different spatial and temporal scales. But it is harmful insofar as it (iii)_____ the fields’ mutual enrichment.","key":"BFG","groups":[["expansion","divergence","maturation"],["anomalous","timely","understandable"],["hampers","protracts","overstates"]],"expl":"空1 divergence（分歧）；空2 understandable（可理解的）；空3 hampers（阻碍）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v92.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Machiavelli's painful account of the Pazzi political conspiracy and the recriminations that followed seems to have been penned with _____ intent: to dampen naive enthusiasm for such adventures by warning of their dangers.","key":"CE","opts":["an equivocal","an ulterior","a prophylactic","a pragmatic","an inhibitory","a duplicitous"],"expl":"an ulterior（隐藏的）：马基雅维利的写作有隐藏的意图。选 CE"},{"id":"v92.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Just as the short strings of a violin cannot produce the deep, long-wavelength notes of a double bass, so photons—which are vibrations not of strings but of electromagnetic fields—are ______ by the physical characteristics of objects that conduct electricity.","key":"BF","opts":["conveyed","bound","amplified","thwarted","transmitted","circumscribed"],"expl":"bound（受限）：光子受导体物理特性制约。选 BF"},{"id":"v92.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Most farmers alternate corn and soybean crops in their fields rather than periodically leaving fields unplanted, as was once customary, but such ______ cropping can deplete the organic content of the soil.","key":"CD","opts":["strenuous","consistent","continuous","unremitting","haphazard","slipshod"],"expl":"continuous（连续的）：不间断地种植会消耗土壤有机质。选 CD"},{"id":"v92.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Kelly Cherry’s fiction speaks to various postmodern debates regarding history and perception, but does not become so abstract that the reader feels the narrative has been ______ an intellectual agenda.","key":"BC","opts":["dependent on","ceded to","surrendered to","facilitated by","hampered by","expedited by"],"expl":"空缺处为“不让叙事沦为某种知识议程的附庸”，ceded to（让渡给）与 surrendered to 都表示屈从。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v92-2","title":"Test 92 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v92.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Demographic relationships that have been ______ may not be useful targets for prolonged study: that very characteristic suggests that they may continue to change rapidly.","key":"E","opts":["static","enervated","intransigent","moribund","mutable"],"expl":"mutable（可变的）：这类关系易变，所以不适合长期研究。选 E"},{"id":"v92.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The lobbyist argues that current environmental regulations must be (I)________ to prevent a recession, thus reviving the notion that economic progress and environmental protection are inherently (ii)________.","key":"BE","groups":[["introduced","softened","reviewed"],["inviolable","incompatible","unsustainable"]],"expl":"空1 softened（放松）；空2 incompatible（不相容的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v92.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The apparent promise of clean alternatives to environmentally harmful fossil fuels might actually (i)_______ fossil-fuel industries by framing energy problems not as a matter of excessive consumption but rather as a remediable lack of clean energy production, thus enticing citizens to (ii)______ the current energy consumption patterns from which fossil-fuel industries profit.","key":"AF","groups":[["benefit","pressure","transform"],["call attention to","demand changes in","remain complacent about"]],"expl":"空1 benefit（惠及）；空2 abandon（放弃）。选 AF"},{"id":"v92.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The danger often facing authors of satirical works is that if the audience is not (i)_____ the joke, the piece may end up (ii)_____ the behavior it was trying to (iii)_____.","key":"CDI","groups":[["already frustrated by","willing to laugh at","discerning enough to get"],["reinforcing","depicting","elucidating"],["conceal","support","ridicule"]],"expl":"空1 discerning enough to get（足够敏锐以领会）；空2 reinforcing（强化）；空3 ridicule（嘲讽）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v92.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the nineteenth century, the dish known as lobster Newburg was sometimes associated with the culinary accessory known as the chafing dish, but Welsh rarebit was considered the truly ______ chafing dish recipe.","key":"DF","opts":["indigenous","sumptuous","ubiquitous","paradigmatic","newfangled","archetypal"],"expl":"archetypal（原型的）与 paradigmatic 描述 Welsh rarebit 才是真正的典范。选 DF"},{"id":"v92.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The airline might receive fewer complaints if it got passengers to their destinations on time: in the past few years, only one airline has been more ______.","key":"CD","opts":["unprofitable","aggressive","remiss","dilatory","impeccable","assiduous"],"expl":"impeccable（无可挑剔的）：只有一家航空公司准点记录更好。选 CD"},{"id":"v92.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Selling a product with no known or even ______ substitute and with ever-growing demand for it seems as if it would be quite lucrative, but in fact the three biggest private-sector water companies in the world are eager to get out of the business.","key":"EF","opts":["recognized","practicable","profitable","acknowledged","imaginable","conceivable"],"expl":"imaginable / conceivable 表示“可以想象的替代品”，此处。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v93-1","title":"Test 93 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v93.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The ability to reproduce in her paintings the supple and shapely lines of her great-grandfather’s paintings seems to have ______ her the way a particular cast of mind might be perpetuated in another family.","key":"A","opts":["devolved upon","become occluded in","ebbed in","strengthened","confounded"],"expl":"devolved upon（传承给）：她的画风如同家族传承。选 A"},{"id":"v93.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Various factors complicate researchers’ efforts to study time spent on housework. For example, housework may not stand out much in respondents’ memories because it is so (i)_____ everyday life, and (ii)_____ problems among survey subjects may thus be more severe than for other activities.","key":"AE","groups":[["integral to","disruptive of","essential to"],["logistical","recollection","fabrication"]],"expl":"空1 integral to（融入）；空2 recollection（回忆）。选 AE"},{"id":"v93.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The quiet, careful member of a collaborative, creative pair may naturally be (i)_____ by posterity in comparison with the brash, dramatic one. Braque and Picasso created Cubism together, but the mercurial Picasso is regarded as the star of the movement while Braque, because he was so much more (ii)_____, has been relatively (iii)_____ by history.","key":"ADG","groups":[["diminished","scrutinized","favored"],["understated","gifted","pretentious"],["neglected","manipulated","tolerated"]],"expl":"空1 diminished（被削弱）；空2 understated（低调的）；空3 overshadowed（被掩盖）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v93.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Mechanization of agriculture made it easy for farmers to simply plow more land and ______ soil loss in existing fields: soil loss was slow enough that famers saw the problem as someone else’s concern.","key":"BE","opts":["obscure","ignore","prevent","avoid","discount","anticipate"],"expl":"discount（忽视）与 ignore 描述农民对水土流失的漠视。选 BE"},{"id":"v93.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The bird-watchers’ ______ distinguishing personal interpretations from factual observations was a liability in their stated goal of obtaining objective information about the everyday behavior of ravens.","key":"CD","opts":["zeal for","exactness in","ineptitude at","maladroitness in","indifference toward","fervor for"],"expl":"观察者混淆个人解读与客观事实，这种不精确性削弱了其客观目标。选 CD"},{"id":"v93.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since it is an incredible challenge to detect dark matter directly, scientists have ______ existence from its gravitational effects on shaping galaxies and other large-scale structures.","key":"CD","opts":["isolated","confirmed","inferred","surmised","documented","hypothesized"],"expl":"inferred（推断）与 surmised 描述由引力效应推断暗物质存在。选 CD"},{"id":"v93.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Responsibility for the nation’s decline rests squarely with a people who take for granted their claims to preeminence but do not ______ interest in or commitment to actually maintaining it.","key":"CF","opts":["foresee","rebuff","evince","reject","predict","betray"],"expl":"evince（表现）：人们不表现出对维持地位的兴趣。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v93-2","title":"Test 93 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v93.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The employees tasked with modeling scenarios for their company’s bankruptcy assumed that their work was merely ______: none of them expected the firm to file for bankruptcy immediately.","key":"E","opts":["a penance .","an inevitability","a necessity","a liability","a contingency"],"expl":"contingency（意外情况）：破产情景只是预案。选 E"},{"id":"v93.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"There is a somewhat (i)_____ trend emerging in property law today: though property law historically has been used to legitimize the conquest of indigenous lands, indigenous groups worldwide are now (ii)_____ this same body of law to lay claim to their own cultural resources.","key":"AE","groups":[["ironic","untimely","redundant"],["circumventing","employing","invalidating"]],"expl":"空1 ironic（具有讽刺意味的）；空2 employing（运用）。选 AE"},{"id":"v93.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Among geophysicists there was considerably less (i)_____ the proposed environment measure than the (ii)_____ media accounts of the conference would suggest: the debate was often animated but never uncivil.","key":"CE","groups":[["ambivalence toward","satisfaction with","rancor over"],["sanitized","sensationalized","poignant"]],"expl":"空1 rancor over（怨恨）；空2 sensationalized（耸人听闻的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v93.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Strains of Prochlorococcus plankton have such (i)_____ sequences at their small subunit RNA genes that they would be considered the same species by the normal criteria used by microbiologists. By contrast, the same strains exhibit such ecological (ii)_____ that they would be considered (iii)_____ species by normal ecological criteria.","key":"AEH","groups":[["similar","unusual","complex"],["consistency","diversity","vigor"],["endemic","discrete","ancestral"]],"expl":"空1 similar（相似的）；空2 diversity（多样性）；空3 distinct（不同的）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v93.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The essay, focusing on the intricacies of complex corporate accounting practices, was ______ almost to a fault, leaving the impression that these practices are rather straightforward.","key":"AE","opts":["lucid","punctilious","reductive","exhaustive","intelligible","comprehensive"],"expl":"exhaustive（详尽的）与 reductive 呼应：过分简化的 lucid 语言。选 AE"},{"id":"v93.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Given that the detailed scientific description of four-legged animals’ walking gaits is now over a century old, it is ______ that so many artists, taxidermists, and others responsible for depicting animals get leg positions wrong.","key":"AF","opts":["exasperating","unsurprising","satisfying","predictable","remarkable","frustrating"],"expl":"unsurprising（不足为奇）：画家仍然出错在意料之中。选 AF"},{"id":"v93.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Harlem Renaissance has been studied extensively as a literary and visual arts movement, but recent scholars have described the role of music as more than _____, in fact, as having made the Harlem Renaissance possible.","key":"EF","opts":["necessary","mundane","essential","emotional","incidental","peripheral"],"expl":"peripheral（次要的）：音乐不仅是次要的，而是促成了运动。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v94-1","title":"Test 94 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v94.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The simultaneous ascension in the postwar United States of both the bulldozer and children’s “bulldozer books” was far from ______; it reflected parallels between the landscapes of fact and feeling in a country undergoing massive physical upheaval.","key":"A","opts":["coincidental","calculated","discouraging","significant","disruptive"],"expl":"coincidental（偶然的）：这不是偶然的。选 A"},{"id":"v94.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Far from being (i)_____ the corporate world because of cutbacks, serious scientific researchers are playing a growing role in innovation in certain firms. The explanation for this apparent paradox is that innovative companies are not looking for full-time scientists; they want moonlighting academics, professors (ii)_____ to work temporary projects.","key":"AF","groups":[["banished from","relegated to","reinstated in"],["disinclined","unauthorized","disposed"]],"expl":"空1 banished from（被驱逐出）；空2 willing（愿意的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v94.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"With so many scientific papers chasing so few pages in the most prestigious journals, the winners could be the ones most likely to oversell themselves—to trumpet amazing or important results that later turn out to be false. This would produce a (i)_____ picture of scientific knowledge, with less (ii)_____ but more (iii)_____ results either relegated to obscure journals or left unpublished.","key":"CDI","groups":[["comprehensive","bewildering","distorted"],["dramatic","threatening","arbitrary"],["controversial","obvious","accurate"]],"expl":"空1 comprehensive（全面的）；空2 bewildering（令人困惑的）；空3 tenable（站得住脚的）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v94.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The teacher was known for being stern with _____ students, but kind to any member of the class who seemed the least bit tractable.","key":"CE","opts":["complaisant","supercilious","recalcitrant","pliable","incorrigible","mendacious"],"expl":"recalcitrant（顽固的）与 incorrigible 描述难管的学生。选 CE"},{"id":"v94.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Piersma and Gill suggest that bar-tailed godwits—long-billed shorebirds of the Eurasian and Alaskan tundra—rank among the most ______ of the long-range fliers, traveling 11,000 kilometers nonstop across the Pacific.","key":"DF","opts":["unpredictable","versatile","erratic","unflagging","renowned","indefatigable"],"expl":"indefatigable（不知疲倦的）：这些候鸟长途飞行，耐力惊人。选 DF"},{"id":"v94.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While prudence is recognized as a kind of virtue, there is nonetheless a tendency to view someone who is prudent as, in some sense, ______, too narrow and dull to partake of spontaneously arising opportunities.","key":"CF","opts":["timid","laudable","wanting","inculpable","exemplary","deficient"],"expl":"deficient（有所欠缺的）与 wanting 描述谨慎之人被认为缺乏活力。选 CF"},{"id":"v94.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The society of the ancient Moche of northern Peru was ______ one : it was ruled by local lords who were overseen by an elite composed of administrative and religious authorities.","key":"DF","opts":["an enduring","an inflexible","an abiding","a stratified","a cohesive","a hierarchical"],"expl":"a stratified（分层的）与 hierarchical 描述莫切社会的结构。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v94-2","title":"Test 94 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v94.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The nineteenth-century legislator Robert Barnwell Rhett was known for using language so intemperate that even in an era of considerable political ______, it came almost to occupy a category of its own.","key":"D","opts":["malfeasance","upheaval","hypocrisy","invective","retrenchment"],"expl":"invective（辱骂）：他的言辞极其激烈。选 D"},{"id":"v94.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The enlightenment philosophers of the eighteenth century acknowledged that unrestricted freedom to publish could (i)_____ motivated by envy or hatred, but they hoped that any such (ii)_____ enabled by expanded liberties would suffer from being publicly exposed.","key":"BE","groups":[["encourage blandishments","facilitate calumny","constrain vituperation"],["evasion","defamation","prurience"]],"expl":"空1 facilitate calumny（助长诽谤）；空2 defamation（诽谤）。选 BE"},{"id":"v94.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The man was an avowed (i)_____: he made no secret of his disdain for (ii)_____ endeavor.","key":"CE","groups":[["partisan","dilettante","philistine"],["political","aesthetic","amateur"]],"expl":"空1 philistine（俗人）；空2 aesthetic（审美的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v94.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is a common complaint that female explorers have been unfairly (i)_____ in modern historical accounts. Amelia Earhart, Freya Stark, and Gertrude Bell may be (ii)_____, but only a special would recognize the names of Fanny Workman or Janet Wulsin. Whether that is a matter of (iii)_____ or a fair reflection of their achievements is debatable.","key":"BDH","groups":[["scrutinized","ignored","attacked"],["well enough known","largely overlooked","subject to criticism"],["analysis","prejudice","objectivity"]],"expl":"空1 ignored（被忽视）；空2 largely unknown（基本不为人知）；空3 bias（偏见）。选 BDH"},{"id":"v94.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In this instance, aesthetics ______ structure, and the unconventional design of the long, slender-decked bridge allowed its deck to move sideways excessively.","key":"AD","opts":["prevailed over","harmonized with","bowed to","dominated","invigorated","complemented"],"expl":"prevailed over（胜过）与 dominated 描述美学压倒了结构。选 AD"},{"id":"v94.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Her success is not _____, for she writes clearly about complicated subjects and provides lucid explanations and penetrating insights.","key":"CF","opts":["undeniable","undeserved","unanticipated","unparalleled","unsurpassed","unexpected"],"expl":"undeserved（不应得的）：她的成功是理所应当的。选 CF"},{"id":"v94.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the shrewdness of Lynn Nottage’s protagonist does seem ______, it is worth remembering that this character is trying to operate a business in a place where there is little room for heart.","key":"EF","opts":["appealing","anachronistic","hypocritical","attractive","callous","insensitive"],"expl":"callous（冷酷的）与 insensitive 呼应：主人公的精明显得冷酷。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v95-1","title":"Test 95 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v95.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Throughout the High Middle Ages, the English government became increasingly ______: the documents produced in the eleventh century could be placed on one large table, while the documents produced in the thirteenth fill whole rooms.","key":"D","opts":["despotic","ceremonial","aristocratic","prolix","insular"],"expl":"prolix（冗长的）：文件越来越冗长。选 D"},{"id":"v95.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Professor Redfield describes in his recent book publishing as dark as it is deep, even as one hidebound industry. Indeed, it is facing a profound change in its product model, but is so (i)_____ its past as to be(ii)_____ opportunities offered by technological change.","key":"BD","groups":[["indebted in","encumbered by","irrelevant with"],["unable to seize","capable of seeking","definite to circumvent"]],"expl":"空1 encumbered by（受拖累）；空2 unable to seize（无法抓住）。选 BD"},{"id":"v95.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"By sucking people into towns and draining the countryside of communities and workers, the passenger train (i)_____ its reason for being:moving people between country districts and urban centers.The major (ii)_____ urbanization in the United States, the railway fell victim to it. Once the overwhelming majority of nonelective journeys were either very long or very short, it became (iii)_____ for people to undertake them in planes or cars.","key":"CDH","groups":[["vindicated","discovered","destroyed"],["facilitator of","counterpoint to","consequence of"],["unusual","sensible","inconsistent"]],"expl":"空1 abandons（放弃）；空2 driving（推动）；空3 more practical（更实际的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v95.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even though water quality in the main reservoir was ______, pollution was worsening in the tributaries because of high level of nitrates and phosphates that had already endangered drinking water in some areas.","key":"CD","opts":["deteriorating","declining","stable","steady","improving","acceptable"],"expl":"空缺处与“但污染在支流中恶化”形成转折，stable（稳定的）与 steady 最合适。选 CD"},{"id":"v95.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"“Revolutionary” and “unique” are words that have become ______: every century in human history is described as unique, and every year, somewhere in the world, some event is characterized as revolutionary.","key":"AE","opts":["overused","interchangeable","confused","distorted","trite","contentious"],"expl":"trite（陈词滥调的）与 overused 描述“独一无二”等词的滥用。选 AE"},{"id":"v95.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As the global climate warms, some deserts, expanding to higher latitudes, are beginning to ______ fertile regions.","key":"DE","opts":["augment","endanger","destroy","displace","supplant","enrich"],"expl":"supplant（取代）：沙漠扩张会取代肥沃地区。选 DE"},{"id":"v95.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While Takaezu’s ceramic pieces are highly distinctive, her body of work as a whole can feel ______ to critics who wish to track it since she has never dated or conscientiously documented her creations.","key":"BF","opts":["edifying","nebulous","austere","anachronistic","instructive","amorphous"],"expl":"amorphous（无定形的）与 nebulous 描述作品难以归类。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v95-2","title":"Test 95 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v95.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The notion that the director is the center of the team has been ______, but in fact it has not been accepted by academia.","key":"E","opts":["rejected","proven","abnegated","enduring","presented"],"expl":"presented（被呈现）：此观念并非被学界接受。选 E"},{"id":"v95.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The paradoxical characteristic of the reliable employee Donna is her ______, as we consider her usual feigning illness to escape from her labor.","key":"C","opts":["halcyon","charlatan","malingering","retribution","earnestness"],"expl":"malingering（装病）：她惯于装病逃避劳动。选 C"},{"id":"v95.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Researchers in University of Maryland discover that many people subconsciously think that in assessment of others competence and warmth are (i)_____: when they feel someone is highly capable, they will assert that he or she must have a tendency to be (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["clearly interconnected","inversely related","physically paralyzed"],["passive","ephemeral","unfeeling"]],"expl":"空1 inversely related（成反比）；空2 unfeeling（冷漠的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v95.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some chemists argue that although molecular motors are (i)_____, they are (ii)_____ by themselves; nevertheless, the chemical principles behind them might be (iii)_____: using the same light-activated mechanism that drives certain molecular motors, researchers have developed around 100 drug-like compound that can be switched on or off in response to light.","key":"AFH","groups":[["intricate","untested","appealing"],["promising","straightforward","useless"],["well established","highly valuable","imperfectly understood"]],"expl":"分子马达本身复杂，但单独并不能实际应用，而其背后的化学原理却有前景。选 AFH"},{"id":"v95.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In The Balance Within, Sternberg ______ hyperbole, opting for an admirable simplicity and clarity while introducing neuroimmunology as a potential foundation of psychosomatic medicine.","key":"EF","opts":["evokes","transcends","elicits","condemns","eschews","avoids"],"expl":"eschews（避免）与 avoids 描述作者避免夸张。选 EF"},{"id":"v95.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Williams argues that philosophy has become ______ occupation these days, and that it should rather be “part of a more general attempt to make the best sense of our life.”","key":"AC","opts":["a recondite","a challenging","an esoteric","an exacting","a salacious","an altruistic"],"expl":"an esoteric（深奥的）与 recondite 描述哲学变得艰深。选 AC"},{"id":"v95.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As modern organizations amass more and more digital information, they need guidance on how to deal with the information surplus in a way that is more ______ than simply increasing their storage capacity.","key":"CD","opts":["sustainable","onerous","judicious","discriminating","parsimonious","prohibitive"],"expl":"judicious（审慎的）：比增加存储更明智的方式。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v96-1","title":"Test 96 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v96.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Except for the special circumstance in which historians record events they themselves have witnessed, scholars can only obtain historical facts through ______ sources.","key":"E","opts":["biased","first-handed","written","unreliable","intermediary"],"expl":"intermediary（间接的）：历史学家只能通过间接资料获得事实。选 E"},{"id":"v96.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"With the rate of technological (i) _____ accelerating—many people now consider a personal computer (ii) _____ after three years—the question of how to properly dispose of old equipment is no small matter.","key":"CD","groups":[["affordability","complexity","obsolescence"],["outdated","familiar","inestimable"]],"expl":"空1 obsolescence（过时）；空2 outdated（过时的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v96.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The general statement that all objects are (i)_____ by gravity (ii)_____ is not (iii)_____. In reality, if a feather and a lump of iron were dropped at the same time from the same place, we should not expect them to hit the floor at the same time. In order to reconcile the general statement with real-world phenomena, we must take into consideration all of the forces that act upon objects.","key":"BEI","groups":[["molded","accelerated","constrained"],["in proportion to their mass","at the same rate","under special"],["self-contradictory","novel","self-evident"]],"expl":"一般论断与真实现象并不一致：羽毛与铁块下落速度不同，因为空气阻力等力也在起作用。选 BEI"},{"id":"v96.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The indigenous uprising in Bolivia in 2008 was not ______: in 1781 indigenous people took over the area near present-day La Paz in what constituted the biggest challenge to the Spanish who then controlled Bolivia.","key":"BE","opts":["unsuccessful","unprecedented","unpredictable","disregarded","unique","random"],"expl":"unprecedented（前所未有的）：玻利维亚的起义并非空前。选 BE"},{"id":"v96.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In a time when so much new concert music failed to speak to listeners, the composer’s symphonies expressed with ______ wit and scorching emotional power the tragic history he lived through.","key":"DF","opts":["torpid","insouciant","patronizing","caustic","phlegmatic","stinging"],"expl":"stinging（刺痛的）与 caustic 描述作曲家的讽刺力量。选 DF"},{"id":"v96.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The team of physicists regarded the data as too ______ not to study with fresh eyes and first questions.","key":"AB","opts":["anomalous","singular","implausible","incidental","confounding","ancillary"],"expl":"anomalous（反常的）：数据太反常，不能不加研究。选 AB"},{"id":"v96.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Ruth Carter’s campaigns for Congress were pretty ______: as a liberal in a deeply conservative district, she was virtually certain to lose.","key":"DF","opts":["conventional","underhanded","contentious","quixotic","indecorous","unrealistic"],"expl":"quixotic（不切实际的）：在保守选区竞选几乎必败。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v96-2","title":"Test 96 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v96.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"As a result of lacking a strong opposing organization to ______, the chief focused their rancor on one another at the conference where the issues were put forward and intended to be resolved.","key":"B","opts":["immolate","excoriate","parley","exterminate","collaborate"],"expl":"excoriate（严厉斥责）：缺乏对手，只能互相斥责。选 B"},{"id":"v96.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Gilbert saw himself as an investigator, a role whose mental state he (i)_____ with that of (ii)_____. Consequently he never accepted an academic position or wrote a comprehensive textbook, so that despite his years of intellectual leadership he never established a school of followers or articulated a distinctly Gilbertian creed.","key":"CE","groups":[["contrasted","combined","equated"],["an administrator","a teacher","an engineer"]],"expl":"空1 equated（等同）；空2 an investigator（调查者）。选 CE"},{"id":"v96.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"There may be something (i)_____ about the very idea of jest, because it obeys no rules. The art of caricature, by contrast, is (ii)_____.","key":"BF","groups":[["inappropriate","expansive","calculated"],["innately spontaneous","carelessly undisciplined","severely finite"]],"expl":"空1 inappropriate（不合适的）；空2 calculated（精心计算的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v96.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Climate change is posited to be a frequent factor in mass extinctions by some scientist who speculate that minor climate shifts can trigger a catastrophic cascade of effects. Although this pattern is (i)_____ in that it confirms warnings about our own possibly dire future, it is also somehow (ii)_____ as it sets forth a context for today’s turbulent weather as (iii)_____ in a natural, cyclical process.","key":"AEI","groups":[["alarming","eccentric","contentious"],["contradictory","reassuring","disquieting"],["unanticipated","unpredictable","unexceptional"]],"expl":"空1 alarming（令人警醒的）；空2 reassuring（令人安慰的）；空3 embedded（嵌入）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v96.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the courts have ______ an extremely flexible test for determining the admissibility of expert testimony, that does not mean that all experts will be allowed to testify.","key":"AE","opts":["underwritten","administered","waived","renounced","endorsed","rescinded"],"expl":"endorsed（认可）：法院认可了灵活的检验标准。选 AE"},{"id":"v96.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ______ of native South American textiles at the time of the Spanish conquest should not be surprising: it represented the apogee of one of the world’s oldest and most sophisticated weaving and dyeing traditions.","key":"AD","opts":["splendor","eccentricity","diversity","brilliance","practicality","popularity"],"expl":"splendor（辉煌）：纺织品的辉煌。选 AD"},{"id":"v96.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"By 1600, France’s sense of itself as nation bound by a shared destiny was______, but over the course of the seventeenth century, French culture regained the strength it had had in the Middle Ages.","key":"EF","opts":["absent","innocuous","benign","unique","precarious","uncertain"],"expl":"precarious（岌岌可危的）：1600 年法国的民族认同岌岌可危。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v97-1","title":"Test 97 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v97.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because the organization she inherited was remarkably _____, her first priority was the establishment of a vigorous fund-raising campaign.","key":"C","opts":["controversial","high-minded","impecunious","multifarious","antiquated"],"expl":"impecunious（贫困的）：组织经费匮乏，故需筹款。选 C"},{"id":"v97.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The geographer held a (i)_____ view of the succession of theoretical trends( environmental determinism, spatial determinism, and various types of critical theory) in her field, maintaining that theory can (ii)_____ what is transpiring in a complex environment by focusing excessively on the favored schemes and variables of the moment.","key":"CE","groups":[["self-contradictory","sanguine","deprecatory"],["exacerbate","obfuscate","magnify"]],"expl":"空1 self-contradictory（自相矛盾的）；空2 obfuscate（使混淆）。选 CE"},{"id":"v97.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"By the end of the 1970s, the postmodern novel had degenerated from a bold attempt to (i)_____ the conventions of traditional narrative into a literary style as (ii)_____ as any other. There are, it seems, (iii)_____ number of ways to avoid telling a straightforward story.","key":"CDG","groups":[["refine","perpetuate","subvert"],["predictable","inescapable","comprehensible"],["a limited","a variable","an inexhaustible"]],"expl":"空1 subvert（颠覆）；空2 inescapable（无法避免的）；空3 an inexhaustible（无穷的）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v97.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The workers’ rights group was concerned that a new regulation allowing employees to request flexible working conditions was ______ because employers in turn were allowed to deny such requests at will.","key":"BE","opts":["flawed","nugatory","incomprehensible","opaque","worthless","disingenuous"],"expl":"nugatory（无价值的）与 worthless 描述规则形同虚设。选 BE"},{"id":"v97.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"______ as ever at eighty-three, Williamson berated the journalists hovering outside his home with a constant stream of abuse.","key":"AB","opts":["Fractious","Irascible","Malicious","Reticent","Taciturn","Voluble"],"expl":"irascible（易怒的）与 fractious 呼应：八十三岁仍然暴躁。选 AB"},{"id":"v97.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The difficulty of understanding subtle behavioral cues in dolphins is undisputed, but this does not obviate the need for the evidentiary foundation of any study of dolphin behavior to be ______.","key":"AC","opts":["substantial","outdated","solid","circumstantial","hypothetical","unconfirmed"],"expl":"solid（坚实的）与 substantial：证据基础必须坚实。选 AC"},{"id":"v97.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although Wanda Coleman’s sonnets sometimes employ ______ word choices, they aptly bring to the fore a distinctly modern anxiety.","key":"BE","opts":["ambiguous","archaic","puzzling","surprising","fusty","disturbing"],"expl":"archaic（古旧的）与 fusty 描述诗中的古旧用词。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v97-2","title":"Test 97 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v97.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Unlike some models of mathematical tasks that distinguish between lower and higher cognitive demands, Carolyn Kieran’s model focuses only on the type of algebraic activity and thus is not ______ with regard to cognitive demand.","key":"D","opts":["consistent","equitable","indeterminate","discriminatory","extraneous"],"expl":"discriminatory（有区别对待的）：模型对认知要求并不区分。选 D"},{"id":"v97.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"All the scholars at the conference agree on the character of the general philosophical concepts under discussion, but this does not imply _____ with regard to details.","key":"E","opts":["an element of controversy","an excess of uncertainty","a lack of conformity","a mood of curiosity","a community of opinion"],"expl":"a community of opinion（观点一致）：细节上并无共识。选 E"},{"id":"v97.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)_____ of the entrepreneur that the microfinance boom has helped foster is understandably appealing. But thinking that everyone is, and should be, an entrepreneur can encourage a tendency to (ii)_____ the virtues of larger businesses and the income that a steady job can provide.","key":"CF","groups":[["demise","evolution","cult"],["emphasize","advertise","underrate"]],"expl":"空1 cult（崇拜）；空2 underrate（低估）。选 CF"},{"id":"v97.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the early twentieth century, rural women in the United States could feel caught between, on one hand, national myths upholding a \"natural\" lifestyle that by definition seemed to eschew science and technology, and, on the other hand, a desire to (i)_____ the new, modern standards of mechanized household practice that (ii)_____ their (iii)_____ by aligning them more and more with city women and modern life generally.","key":"BFG","groups":[["disrupt","adopt","improve"],["appeared to accentuate","helped to explain","threatened to compromise"],["distinctiveness","skepticism","satisfaction"]],"expl":"农村妇女一方面想跟上现代标准，另一方面又被国家神话束缚，其身份因此被模糊。选 BFG"},{"id":"v97.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For those attempting the art, the record of past futurologists’ prognostications can be ______: it includes many confident predictions of technological revolution that never happened, such as domed cities and nuclear-powered cars.","key":"DF","opts":["incomplete","intriguing","mundane","humbling","prosaic","chastening"],"expl":"humbling（令人谦卑的）与 chastening 描述预测的失败。选 DF"},{"id":"v97.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Advertising’s role in popular music culture has been redefined: instead of a last resort for the creation and distribution of popular music, advertising now functions as a _____ of music that might otherwise go unheard.","key":"AE","opts":["promoter","reflection","component","foe","champion","rival"],"expl":"champion（支持者）：广告成为音乐的支持者。选 AE"},{"id":"v97.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though the art of writing was well established in Egypt and Mesopotamia long before the Shang period, the Chinese writing that appeared then seems to have been an entirely ______ development.","key":"CF","opts":["unique","banal","homegrown","practical","routine","indigenous"],"expl":"indigenous（本土的）与 homegrown 描述中国文字为本地产生。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v98-1","title":"Test 98 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v98.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Suspicion is arguably a natural self-protective instinct essential to the survival of individuals and societies: a human being or community that is totally _____ is inviting trouble.","key":"D","opts":["exultant","regressive","reclusive","ingenuous","apprehensive"],"expl":"ingenuous（天真的）：完全天真的人易招致麻烦。选 D"},{"id":"v98.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In general memoirs focus sharply on particular, and particularly memorable, events rather than on the entire life. This (i)_____ structure inevitably emphasizes drama at the expense of (ii)_____.","key":"BE","groups":[["circular","episodic","panoramic"],["excitement","completeness","plausibility"]],"expl":"空1 episodic（插曲式的）；空2 completeness（完整性）。选 BE"},{"id":"v98.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Human brains are amazing organs but they are not perfect. Cognitive biases, as we know, sometimes produce errors. Yet the term \"error\" could be (i)_____ in that it suggests that there might be (ii)_____ way in which cognition should work. Such a binary opposition is (iii)_____.","key":"CDH","groups":[["corrective","serviceable","problematic"],["a uniquely correct","a surprisingly novel","an infinitely fluid"],["incontrovertible","reductive","warranted"]],"expl":"空1 problematic（有问题的）；空2 a uniquely correct（唯一正确的）；空3 problematic（有问题的）。把认知偏差称为“错误”，暗示存在唯一正确的思维方式，这种二元对立本身就有问题。选 CDH"},{"id":"v98.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the writer meant for the book to serve as a kind of tribute to motherhood, the approach here is hardly a ______ affair.","key":"BE","opts":["memorable","saccharine","problematic","divisible","sentimental","controversial"],"expl":"saccharine（甜腻煽情的）与 sentimental 描述这本书并非单纯的温情之作。选 BE"},{"id":"v98.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although biologists know that thousands of species of microbes and invertebrates inhabit one square meter of temperate grassland soil, the identities of those creatures and their contributions to sustaining the biosphere remain ______.","key":"AD","opts":["obscure","self-evident","immaterial","murky","contested","obvious"],"expl":"murky（模糊不清的）与 obscure 描述微生物群落的身份仍不清楚。选 AD"},{"id":"v98.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although a dedicated reader of the book can _____ a brief of chronology of Chappell’s life, the book is nevertheless not a real biography of Chapelle.","key":"DE","opts":["miss","imagine","overlook","extract","ferret out","summarize"],"expl":"ferret out（查出、挖掘）与 extract 描述读者能从书中找出年表。选 DE"},{"id":"v98.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Physicians today increasingly rely on endoscopic surgery, ______ large scalpels and clamps in favor of endoscopy’s cameras and flexible tools that can snake into the body through tiny holes.","key":"BE","opts":["designing","de-emphasizing","rediscovering","engineering","downplaying","rejecting"],"expl":"de-emphasizing（淡化）：内窥镜手术不再依赖大型手术刀。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v98-2","title":"Test 98 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v98.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"With Robert Lowell’s death, poetry appears to have shrunk from the ground he commandeered: his grand conception of the port as public conscience has _____ in the present era of notably small and private poems.","key":"E","opts":["met little resistance","experienced increased momentum","garnered newfound credibility","generated unqualified enthusiasm","gained scant traction"],"expl":"gained scant traction（几乎没有进展）：罗厄尔之后，宏大诗歌的影响力几乎消失。选 E"},{"id":"v98.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Her lecture was entertaining though unoriginal: she hoped that by (i)_____ her audience, she could (ii)_____ the hackneyed observations on which her argument depended.","key":"AD","groups":[["amusing","goading","boring"],["compensate for","accentuate","allude to"]],"expl":"空1 amusing（逗乐）；空2 accentuate（突出）。选 AD"},{"id":"v98.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Around the early 1980s, technology companies began creating the first portable machines that resemble today’s laptop computers. Still, for many years, large and bulky desktop computers (i)________ the market, because you always had to (ii)________ something for portability. Compared with laptops, desktops had more power, bigger screens, more comfortable keyboards, and more storage space.","key":"BE","groups":[["found little room in","held sway in","lost share in"],["enhance","sacrifice","delay"]],"expl":"空缺处与“便携”相对：台式机长期占据市场。选 BE"},{"id":"v98.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many people fail to (i)_____ memoirs and novels, a tendency arguably (ii)_____ by discussions of the \"graphic novel\": that term is applied to any narrative drawn in the manner of a comic book, even ones like Marjane Satrapi's Persepolis, which (iii)_____.","key":"BFG","groups":[["appreciate","distinguish","remember"],["anticipated","delineated","exacerbated"],["concerns historical events","receives considerable","invites complex"]],"expl":"空1 distinguish（区分）；空2 exacerbated（加剧）；空3 concerns his（讲述其……）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v98.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The mayor’s hunger for power was ______: in her own heart, she was utterly convinced that all her energies were being poured out in the service of a cause greater than herself.","key":"BE","opts":["despicable","unacknowledged","logical","unquenchable","subconscious","understandable"],"expl":"unacknowledged（未被承认的）：她的野心被自己忽略。选 BE"},{"id":"v98.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Psychoanalysis has increasingly immured itself behind high walls of jargon by using terms like “introjective identification” and “countercathexis” and this emphasis on ______ is in part an effort to preserve the field’s waning mystique.","key":"BC","opts":["conjecture","abstruseness","opacity","consistency","speculation","terminology"],"expl":"abstruseness（深奥）与 opacity 描述精神分析的晦涩术语。选 BC"},{"id":"v98.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Velazquez’ painting can be somewhat ______: one cannot get on familiar terms with them, but only admire their colorful polish from afar.","key":"BF","opts":["pedestrian","slippery","ominous","prosaic","flamboyant","elusive"],"expl":"elusive（难以捉摸的）：画作无法亲近。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v99-1","title":"Test 99 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v99.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The researchers theorized that people in power focus so keenly on their own prerogatives that they become oblivious to those around them and that their subordinates, not wanting to provoke the boss, _____ this process.","key":"C","opts":["subvert","imitate","abet","expose","underestimate"],"expl":"abet（助长）：下属的顺从助长了这一过程。选 C"},{"id":"v99.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Intuitively, something is considered to the matter if, and only if, there is mass along with energy and/or momentum associated with it. In other words, possession of mass along with energy and/or momentum is regarded as (i)________, rather than (ii)________, property of matter.","key":"BF","groups":[["an optimal","an essential","a contingent"],["a unique","an irreducible","an accidental"]],"expl":"空1 an essential（本质的）；空2 a contingent（偶然的）。质量是物质的本质属性，而不是偶然属性。选 BF"},{"id":"v99.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the (i)_____ and the not infrequent appearance of terms like synaptogenesis and N-methyl-D-aspartate glutamate receptor can be (ii)_____ in a book aimed at the general reader, Konner's overall style is (iii)_____ enough that you feel as though you are in the company of a helpful and hopeful teacher who is eager to share what he's found.","key":"CFH","groups":[["occasional glimpses of","deft deployment of","repeated use of jargon"],["placating","galvanizing","daunting"],["disputatious","conversational","baroque"]],"expl":"空1 occasional glimpses of（偶尔提及）；空2 accessible（易懂的）。选 CFH"},{"id":"v99.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the environmental detection of nuclear explosions has become ______, the ability to detect nuclear weapons programs well before they result in a nuclear device would better serve security objectives.","key":"DF","opts":["immediate","unnecessary","redundant","straightforward","surreptitious","unproblematic"],"expl":"straightforward（直接简便的）：侦测核爆已经很容易。选 DF"},{"id":"v99.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Eliot’s satire stops short of cruelty; inveterately ______, even when it comes to her most flawed characters, her default authorial positions is one of pity.","key":"BE","opts":["exacting","magnanimous","demanding","considerate","generous","self-indulgent"],"expl":"magnanimous（宽宏大量的）：她对有缺陷的人物仍然宽厚。选 BE"},{"id":"v99.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Psychologist once ______ fiction as a way of understanding people because it is made up, but in the past 25 years cognitive psychologists have developed a new appreciation for the significance of fictional stories.","key":"DF","opts":["overlooked","countenanced","underestimated","scorned","sanctioned","disparaged"],"expl":"disparaged（贬低）：心理学家曾经不屑于把小说当作理解人的工具。选 DF"},{"id":"v99.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Geologists’ customary distinction between planetary mantle and core material appears increasingly ______: liquid oxides can be considered either molten mantle constituents or electrically conducting core components.","key":"BD","opts":["incontrovertible","untenable","dogmatic","flawed","contradictory","confusing"],"expl":"untenable（站不住脚的）：区分地幔与地核的说法越来越站不住脚。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v99-2","title":"Test 99 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v99.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The fanciful notion that the legislative initiative would bring unlimited social benefits has soured into an equally _____ mood of skepticism and distrust.","key":"E","opts":["valid","pessimistic","unanticipated","pragmatic","baseless"],"expl":"baseless（毫无根据的）：从乐观转为毫无根据的怀疑。选 E"},{"id":"v99.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The use of the term “greenhouse effect” is a complete ______, because it is not a veracious description of such a complicated transformation.","key":"D","opts":["anomaly","spontaneity","mishap","misnomer","appositeness"],"expl":"misnomer（名不副实的称呼）：“温室效应”并不准确。选 D"},{"id":"v99.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"While several relationships fell by the wayside under the pressure of conflicting opinion, none was more affecting to the writer than her relationship with her brother. Her letters document a steady (i)________ of feeling: intense pride in him giving way to more moderate respect, trust (ii)________ as feeling of betrayal come to dominate.","key":"CF","groups":[["emergence","cessation","erosion"],["materializing","intensifying","evaporating"]],"expl":"作者与兄长的关系经历了从骄傲到尊敬、信任消退、背叛感占上风的变化，故空1 erosion（侵蚀），空2 cessation（停止）。选 CF"},{"id":"v99.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"For whom is Shipton's A New History of Jazz intended? It is written in (i)_____ language and contains no extended musical analysis, suggesting that it is meant for amateurs. But as it is twice as long as the next-longest history of the subject, my guess is that general readers will be put off by its (ii)_____. On the other hand, its great length is precisely what enables Shipton to avoid (iii)_____ the story of jazz's development.","key":"AEH","groups":[["accessible","ornate","graphic"],["paucity of exposition","proliferation of detail","preponderance of jargon"],["belaboring","oversimplifying","extolling"]],"expl":"空1 plain（平实的）；空2 length（篇幅）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v99.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Most scholarship that is produced these days vanishes without apparent ______; 98 percent of all publications in the arts and humanities are never cited.","key":"BE","opts":["credibility","impact","ignominy","disgrace","influence","attribution"],"expl":"impact（影响）：大多数学术成果没有任何影响。选 BE"},{"id":"v99.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Booker T. Washington was always a welcome guest at the White House: although his aloofness ______ intimate conversation, the president felt entirely at ease in his company.","key":"BD","opts":["compromised","ruled out","presupposed","precluded","called for","necessitated"],"expl":"precluded（排除）：他的疏远使亲密交谈不可能。选 BD"},{"id":"v99.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Researchers concluded that although the success of pearl millet crops in the region varied with seasonal climatic conditions, cultivation remains ______ because of pearl millet’s predisposition to perform under stressful growing conditions, including drought.","key":"BF","opts":["erratic","advantageous","inconsistent","prevalent","impractical","expedient"],"expl":"expedient（权宜的）与 advantageous 描述珍珠粟的作物优势。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v100-1","title":"Test 100 · Section 1","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v100.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some of writers whose interviews with the Paris Review are included in this volume were caught in the final years of their lives, and these interviews thus lend ______ mood to the collection.","key":"A","opts":["an autumnal","a scintillating","a liberal","an apolitical","a cosmopolitan"],"expl":"an autumnal（秋天般的）：受访者处于人生晚年，作品带有暮色感。选 A"},{"id":"v100.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The widespread (i)_____ that has accompanied economic growth is not the result of the people’s adopting the leader’s own standards. Her personal (ii)_____ is recognized by all.","key":"BE","groups":[["conformity","corruption","frugality"],["influence","integrity","traditionalism"]],"expl":"空1 conformity（一致）；空2 integrity（正直）。选 BE"},{"id":"v100.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The newly discovered fossil skeletons have the fins, scales, and other attributes of a giant fish, but also the telling anatomical traits of (i)_____ creature, such as the beginnings of digits, protowrists, and joints resembling elbows on the forward fins. The specimen is a fish with features that (ii)_____ the emergence of land animals and is thus a (iii)_____ of amphibians, reptiles, dinosaurs, and mammals.","key":"CDI","groups":[["a diurnal","a marine","a transitional"],["anticipate","impede","supersede"],["derivative","predator","predecessor"]],"expl":"空1 another（另一种）生物；空2 foreshadow（预示）；空3 missing link（过渡物种）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v100.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Chancellor castigated one regime for its mistreatment of political opponents, whereas he inexplicably ______ another that had committed similar acts.","key":"BF","opts":["adjured","exculpated","impugned","neglected","cosseted","absolved"],"expl":"exculpated（开脱）：他为另一政权开脱。选 BF"},{"id":"v100.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"She had a feeling that was not yet fully articulated, ______ sense that something extraordinary and wonderful awaited her.","key":"AD","opts":["an inchoate","an onerous","a burdensome","an incipient","a foreboding","an enchanting"],"expl":"an incipient（初期的）：一种尚未成形的感觉。选 AD"},{"id":"v100.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One commentator charged that the discipline of political science has not merely ignored pressing problems of contemporary society but has in fact been used to ______ erroneous public policies.","key":"CF","opts":["identify","overcome","rationalize","investigate","explore","justify"],"expl":"rationalize（为……辩护）：用来为错误政策辩护。选 CF"},{"id":"v100.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In some ways, the success of Aishwarya Rai ______ the growing international recognition of India’s film industry: in 2003 she was the first Indian actor to be one the jury at the Cannes Film Festival.","key":"BD","opts":["controverts","personifies","eclipses","epitomizes","explains","belies"],"expl":"personifies（体现）：阿伊斯瓦娅体现了印度电影的国际地位。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v100-2","title":"Test 100 · Section 2","group":"Test 91–100","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v100.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Writing accessories such as letter openers, pen trays, and memorandum pads became tremendously popular during the Victorian era, and by far the most ubiquitous of such _____ was the letter box.","key":"B","opts":["epistles","appurtenances","vexations","vestiges","frugalities"],"expl":"appurtenances（附属物）：信箱是最普及的附属品。选 B"},{"id":"v100.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is possible to (i)_____ the benefits of diplomatic dialogue, because although it can certainly alleviate some of the problems that afflicts us, it is not a (ii)_____.","key":"AB","opts":["overstate","panacea","compromise","placebo","extend","liability"],"expl":"overstate（夸大）与 panacea（灵丹妙药）：不应夸大外交对话的作用。选 AB"},{"id":"v100.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Seemingly to compensate for the (i)_____ nature of her subject, in her review the theater critic (ii)_____ a casual chatty style.","key":"BD","groups":[["undemanding","rarefied","well-defined"],["opted for","misused","invited"]],"expl":"空1 rarefied（高深的）；空2 opted for（选择）。选 BD"},{"id":"v100.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because leadership in the computer hacker group is extremely (i)_______, when law enforcement agencies arrested several prominent members, taking them offline, the group (ii)________. Instead, it continues to operate, sometimes under its own name, sometimes under other names. The names are (iii)_______, as are the members of the group: anyone, anywhere, is free to work behind its mask.","key":"AFH","groups":[["fluid","efficient","hierarchical"],["adopted new practices","replaced its leadership","did not collapse"],["idiosyncratic","fungible","misleading"]],"expl":"黑客组织领导层高度分散，警方抓人后组织仍继续运作，名称与成员都可替换。选 AFH"},{"id":"v100.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is readily apparent that structures and functions of immature forms in organism as diverse as butterflies and frogs are not necessarily mere ______ of adult traits but represent specific adaptations to life in the niches occupied by juveniles.","key":"DF","opts":["miniatures","vestiges","embellishments","precursors","elaborations","forerunners"],"expl":"vestiges（残余）：幼体结构并非成虫特征的残余，而是适应。选 DF"},{"id":"v100.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"______ neuroscience’s explanatory power, Patricia Churchland maintains that questions that have been discussed to no effect by philosophers over many centuries are solvable once rephrased as questions of neuroscience.","key":"CD","opts":["A chronicler of","A skeptic about","An advocate of","An apologist for","A doubter of","A dissenter from"],"expl":"A skeptic about（对……持怀疑态度）：她怀疑神经科学的解释力。选 CD"},{"id":"v100.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The firm’s startling admission of bookkeeping irregularities called into question the ______ of the oversight that government exercises over the financial health of private business.","key":"AB","opts":["sufficiency","efficacy","authenticity","legitimacy","propriety","constitutionality"],"expl":"efficacy（有效性）：审计暴露出监管的效力问题。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v101-1","title":"Test 101 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v101.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It ought to be surprising that the bank falsified the numbers on its accounts; it is truly shocking that such _____ was documented, in black and white, and that regulators found it and did nothing about it.","key":"A","opts":["chicanery","raillery","enmity","sagacity","probity"],"expl":"chicanery（欺诈）：银行的造假被记录在案。选 A"},{"id":"v101.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because scientific breakthroughs tend to occur when a prevailing theory's predictions start to fail, scientists sometimes find it (i)_____ when a theory persists—as the standard model of particle physics has done—in making (ii)_____ predictions.","key":"BF","groups":[["productive","frustrating","surprising"],["bold","abstract","correct"]],"expl":"空1 frustrating（令人沮丧的）；空2 correct（正确的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v101.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The chocolate company's scientists hoped that once they had (i)_____ the chemical makeup of cocoa beans, the knowledge would enable them to produce (ii)_____ the beans' taste, which could then be used to (iii)_____ future failures in the cocoa bean supply.","key":"BFH","groups":[["altered","unlocked","activated"],["subtle transformations in","accurate descriptions of","a synthetic replication of"],["prevent","mitigate","restrict"]],"expl":"空1 unlocked（破解）；空2 subtle transformations in（精细的变化）；空3 prevent（防止）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v101.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although Harman has not produced ______ biography of Robert Louis Stevenson, her understanding of what it takes to write a book enables her to account for Stevenson’s delirious sprints toward and away from publication.","key":"CF","opts":["a controversial","a flawed","a definitive","an idiosyncratic","an unsound","an authoritative"],"expl":"a definitive（权威的）：哈曼并未写出权威传记。选 CF"},{"id":"v101.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite the ______ amount of high-quality data on the issue of underrepresentation of women professors in math-intensive fields, particularly in upper-level positions, myths and misunderstandings prevail.","key":"CE","opts":["appropriate","suspicious","significant","overwhelming","substantial","dubious"],"expl":"substantial（大量的）：数据充足，但偏见仍然流行。选 CE"},{"id":"v101.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"An academic with a questionable record in either teaching, administration, or research may still be well regarded at many schools, but simultaneous failure in all three areas normally results in _____ by superiors.","key":"DE","opts":["exculpation","dismissal","impeachment","disapprobation","censure","acquittal"],"expl":"dismissal（解雇）：三方面都差时通常被解雇。选 DE"},{"id":"v101.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The sleight of hand of architects whose ambition is to add subtly and seamlessly to early twentieth-century Beaux Arts buildings contradicts a first principle of historic preservation; the ______ historical periods should be clear.","key":"BE","opts":["changes within","demarcation of","essence of","continuation of","lines between","explication of"],"expl":"demarcation of（划分）：历史时期之间的界线应清晰。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v101-2","title":"Test 101 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v101.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Dialogue exchanges indicating deep-seated rivalries among the characters abound in the novel, but they are almost always associated with _____ events—everyday commercial transactions, for instance, or the preparation of an evening meal.","key":"C","opts":["intimate","sporadic","quotidian","contentious","revelatory"],"expl":"quotidian（日常的）：日常交易。选 C"},{"id":"v101.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In considering human behavior, theoreticians tend to emphasize cognition in spite of the fact that psychological research suggests the _____ of affect: it suggests that our behavior derives above all from fast, automated emotional judgements.","key":"E","opts":["inefficacy","elusiveness","spontaneity","irrationality","primacy"],"expl":"primacy（优先地位）：情绪判断先于认知。选 E"},{"id":"v101.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is possible that the earliest terrestrial plants were (i)_____ natural enemies, such as herbivores. By the mid-Carboniferous period, however, there was abundant evidence-in the form of fossil leaves with signs of bite marks—that plants were (ii)_____ animal attack.","key":"AD","groups":[["free from","influenced by","overwhelmed by"],["experiencing","avoiding","exploiting"]],"expl":"早期植物可能不受天敌影响，到石炭纪时已有被动物咬食的证据，说明植物受到动物的攻击。选 AD"},{"id":"v101.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"It appears that the terrestrial biosphere has been absorbing a significant fraction of anthropogenic CO2, thereby slowing down the rate of global climate change. However, the (i)______ of this (ii)______ is not (iii)______: if pushed too far, the biosphere might become a net source of CO2, thereby accelerating climate change and causing a positive feedback loop.","key":"CFI","groups":[["complexity","actuality","continuation"],["additional information","formidable challenge","compensatory mechanism"],["imminent","surprising","guaranteed"]],"expl":"空1 completeness（完整性）；空2 mechanism（机制）；空3 guaranteed（保证）。选 CFI"},{"id":"v101.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One early sign of this new thirst for ______ is the fact that eight members of the committee on professional conduct have already recused themselves in the name of unbiased justice.","key":"DF","opts":["enlightenment","exactitude","knowledge","probity","pugnacity","integrity"],"expl":"integrity（正直）：委员会成员回避以维护公正。选 DF"},{"id":"v101.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Recent advances in the study of desert varnish have been a boon to geologists, allowing them to date surface features and establish regional climate histories in ______ detail.","key":"AC","opts":["novel","realistic","unprecedented","superfluous","extraneous","surprising"],"expl":"novel（新颖的）：达到前所未有的细节。选 AC"},{"id":"v101.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The breathless pace of the Broadway adaptation of Alice Walker’s The Color Purple was ______, given the adaptation's determination to cram in so many of the incidents that appear in the original source.","key":"BE","opts":["unremarkable","inevitable","surprising","excessive","unavoidable","unexpected"],"expl":"excessive（过度的）：节奏过快，塞入过多情节。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v102-1","title":"Test 102 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v102.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The development of junior high schools in American education was motivated by _____ rather than by pedagogical validity: these schools provided an efficient and inexpensive way to eliminate overcrowding in the high schools.","key":"C","opts":["idealism","reform","expediency","privilege","tradition"],"expl":"expediency（权宜）：建立初中是为了便宜地解决拥挤问题。选 C"},{"id":"v102.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although Kito Hiroshi's portrait of Edo Japan as (i)_____ is certainly (ii)_____, the fundamental factors of population stability and resource renewal generally did favor social maintenance and even economic growth.","key":"BF","groups":[["outwardly aggressive","perfectly harmonious","slowly developing"],["derivative","positive","overdrawn"]],"expl":"空1 perfectly harmonious（完全和谐）；空2 overdrawn（夸大的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v102.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When learners are engaged in mathematical problem-solving, their activity does not have from the outset the structure of what will be considered a mathematical proof. Instead, a tangle of intuitions, know-how, factual knowledge, and a variety of other mental constructs allows learners to entertain choices and make decisions. Nonetheless, (i)_____ such mental activity (ii)_____ is (iii)_____: in many situations this process works, although it can prove to be wrong as a result of overgeneralizations.","key":"CEI","groups":[["concealing","adapting","describing"],["from scrutiny","as confused","to the task"],["uncommon","unintentional","uncharitable"]],"expl":"空1 aims（目的）；空2 emerges（显现）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v102.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The automation of many of the functions performed at the factory, although initially inspiring _____ in many of the company’s employees, has had none of the deleterious effects forecast either within and beyond the organization.","key":"AE","opts":["trepidation","avidity","diligence","pathos","apprehension","enterprise"],"expl":"自动化本应引起忧虑（trepidation），却并未带来预期的负面影响。选 AE"},{"id":"v102.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Federal Reserve Bank is one of the most ______ institutions in the United States, yet many are not aware of the important operations and activities it has carried out during its lifetime.","key":"EF","opts":["distinguished","secretive","consequential","indispensable","misunderstood","mysterious"],"expl":"mysterious（神秘的）：美联储虽重要，却常被误解。选 EF"},{"id":"v102.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Building the first United States transcontinental phone line required fundamental innovations: for example, engineers created an amplifier for the electric signals to prevent them from ______ after a few miles.","key":"BC","opts":["propagating","attenuating","dissipating","iterating","deviating","broadcasting"],"expl":"attenuating（衰减）：信号会在几英里后衰减。选 BC"},{"id":"v102.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Cole' s novel is as close to a diary as a novel can get, encompassing reflection, autobiography, stasis, and repetition, a daunting task even many accomplished novelists would ______, which, wonderfully, Cole does not do.","key":"DF","opts":["sidestep","attempt","hazard","botch","complicate","fumble"],"expl":"attempt（尝试）：大多数小说家不敢尝试的任务。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v102-2","title":"Test 102 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v102.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While many books have emphasized the differences between Delaney and his father—and his need to differentiate himself from his father—Delaney takes pains in this memoir to _____ his closeness with his dad.","key":"A","opts":["underscore","question","repudiate","sidestep","trivialize"],"expl":"underscore（强调）：作者强调与父亲的亲密。选 A"},{"id":"v102.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"While catalogs of record labels that specialize in Native American music are useful indices of Native American consumers' preferences, their (i)_____ are also (ii)_____: some genres of Native American music have been deemed inappropriate to record because of their special cultural significance.","key":"BD","groups":[["strategies","omissions","inconsistencies"],["telling","misleading","surprising"]],"expl":"空1 omissions（遗漏）；空2 telling（有启示的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v102.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Readers had little reason to (i)_____ what proved to be the rather uncanny (ii)_____ of Kaja Silverman’s and Bell Hooks’s polemics, given the two authors’ contrary methodologies, interests, and audiences.","key":"BD","groups":[["distinguish","anticipate","dispute"],["convergence","timeliness","dissonance"]],"expl":"空1 anticipate（预料）；空2 convergence（趋同）。选 BD"},{"id":"v102.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Paleoclimatic records recovered from land, the ocean, and glacial ice (i) ______a (ii) _______ global climate over much of the last glacial cycle. Indeed, in many locations in the Northern Hemisphere, changes in climate spanning almost the full range of glacial to interglacial conditions were so (iii) __________ that the transition between climate states occurred in decades or less.","key":"BDG","groups":[["exaggerate","confirm","redefine"],["potent driver of","simple fact about","lack of stability in"],["abrupt","unpredictable","enduring"]],"expl":"空1 provide（提供）；空2 coherent（一致的）；空3 rapid（迅速的）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v102.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While some naive investors have been convinced by proponents of the merger that the two companies are natural partners, experienced analysts are less ______.","key":"BD","opts":["optimistic","credulous","reliable","gullible","skeptical","dismissive"],"expl":"skeptical（怀疑的）：经验丰富的分析师对此较为怀疑。选 BD"},{"id":"v102.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The orthodox approach to legal decision making tends to be backward looking, asking which decision would have the better legal ______.","key":"AC","opts":["outcome","lineage","consequence","corollary","standing","pedigree"],"expl":"outcome（结果）：法律决策看向结果。选 AC"},{"id":"v102.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While some commentators see space tourism as being ______, Alice Gorman suggests that we should see a future that includes space tourism as simply one possible future among many.","key":"CD","opts":["implausible","inconsequential","ineluctable","inevitable","impressive","intriguing"],"expl":"ineluctable（不可避免的）：太空旅游并非必然。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v103-1","title":"Test 103 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v103.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The ability of the Grand Banks cod fishery to sustain intensive cod harvesting for many years gave it a reputation for _____ that deceived even scientifically sophisticated observers.","key":"D","opts":["hazardousness","insurmountability","unpredictability","inexhaustibility","inscrutability"],"expl":"inexhaustibility（取之不尽）：长期捕捞让人误以为鳕鱼资源无限。选 D"},{"id":"v103.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The title of Lee’s 1964 textbook, A History of For Eastern Art, might seem to imply that the entire subject could be encapsulated in a single work. In fact, the treatment of art across Asian cultures and over millennia could never (i)_____ if it also aspired to be (ii)_____.","key":"BE","groups":[["avoid anachronism","achieve coherence","justify digressions"],["accessible","comprehensive","groundbreaking"]],"expl":"空1 achieve coherence（达到一致）；空2 comprehensive（全面的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v103.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)____ in local coverage of a rabies outbreak in colonial Hanoi may be startling today, but it cannot be attributed solely to the (ii)_____ of the era's journalists. Rather, before the advent of modern public health systems, (iii)_____ the unpleasantness of the disease and its treatment was seen as a way to, ensure that the public remained vigilant against possible sources of contagion.","key":"CEG","groups":[["reliance on polite","deference to medical","degree of gruesome detail"],["sycophancy","squeamishness","sensationalism"],["underscoring","minimizing","demystifying"]],"expl":"空1 unpleasantness（令人不适的内容）；空2 sensationalism（耸动）；空3 emphasizing（强调）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v103.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Sweet's illustrations are playfully ______: the eye hops sparrowlike from leaf to leaf, uncertain where to settle.","key":"BE","opts":["daunting","distracting","integrated","educational","diverting","Informative"],"expl":"diverting（有趣的）：插图令人愉悦地分散注意力。选 BE"},{"id":"v103.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Archer is surprisingly ______ in failing to see her subjects’ self-reported life histories for what they really are: the kinds of stories that pretty much all twenty-somethings tell.","key":"BF","opts":["obstinate","credulous","arbitrary","cautious","unprincipled","trusting"],"expl":"credulous（轻信的）：作者过于轻信受访者的叙述。选 BF"},{"id":"v103.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"That she was unaffected by the ______ of the feudal past was evident in the style in which she wrote of it, a style completely devoid of nostalgia.","key":"AF","opts":["allure","cruelty","prestige","barbarity","remnants","magic"],"expl":"remnants（残余）：她的写作没有怀旧之情。选 AF"},{"id":"v103.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The World Health Organization has recommended that countries use artemisinin-based combination therapies to treat malaria patients, as continued use of artemisinin monotherapies could ______ the efficacy of artemisinin, the most successful antimalarial drug available.","key":"CE","opts":["negate","mask","reduce","conceal","attenuate","misrepresent"],"expl":"negate（取消）：单药疗法可能削弱药效。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v103-2","title":"Test 103 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v103.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It can be extremely difficult to uncover direct evidence of conspiracies, given that such activities are by their very nature _____.","key":"E","opts":["interminable","laborious","provocative","illicit","surreptitious"],"expl":"surreptitious（秘密的）：阴谋本身就是秘密的。选 E"},{"id":"v103.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"For the early years of the twentieth century, ecology remained essentially a ______ science: ecologists went into the field, counted plants and animals, made lists, and that was pretty much that.","key":"C","opts":["lay","resilient","descriptive","theoretical","pragmatic"],"expl":"descriptive（描述性的）：早期生态学偏重记录。选 C"},{"id":"v103.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the first exoplanet discovered was found to be orbiting too close to its star to support life, scientists quickly discovered exoplanets in more (i)_____ orbits, making the detection of potentially habitable exoplanets seem (ii)_____.","key":"BD","groups":[["compressed","clement","superfluous"],["likely","unfeasible","irregular"]],"expl":"空1 clement（温和的）；空2 feasible（可行的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v103.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Documenting the lives of African Americans before Emancipation is (i)______ undertaking even when printed accounts are (ii)______, they are often (iii)______ and details printed as fact may be merely speculative.","key":"CFG","groups":[["an urgent","a collaborative","a difficult"],["contested","illegible","available"],["contradictory","disheartening","revealing"]],"expl":"空1 a difficult；空2 contested（有争议的）；空3 contradictory（相互矛盾的）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v103.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The film's pat and occasionally preposterous story is really just a ______, a serviceable scaffolding for a handful of expert, satisfying individual performances.","key":"DE","opts":["dodge","prelude","diversion","pretext","contrivance","distraction"],"expl":"pretext（借口）与 contrivance 描述影片故事不过是骨架。选 DE"},{"id":"v103.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author engages the subject from diverse perspectives, supports his argument well with many examples, and manages to avoid antagonizing others in dealing with a very ______ subject.","key":"AC","opts":["contentious","pedestrian","controversial","perplexing","mundane","intriguing"],"expl":"空缺处为“有争议的主题”，contentious（引起争议的）与 controversial 最贴切，作者并未激化对立。选 AC"},{"id":"v103.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because video game users control their character’s actions, the distinction between media user and character is not as ______ in video games as it is in traditional media, where audience members simply witness characters’ actions.","key":"BE","opts":["fluid","salient","fraught","elusive","palpable","charged"],"expl":"fluid（模糊的）：电子游戏中玩家与角色的区分不如传统媒体那样清晰。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v104-1","title":"Test 104 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v104.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The ancient Greek philosopher Socrates displayed great _____ in accepting his sentence of death for corrupting the morals of Athenian youth and for advocating religious heresies; he resisted efforts to save his life and willingly drank the cup of poison given him.","key":"B","opts":["elation","stoicism","elitism","erudition","skepticism"],"expl":"stoicism（坦然接受）：苏格拉底平静地接受死刑。选 B"},{"id":"v104.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In a reflection of the senator's enduring popularity, the articles written in response to her impending retirement were less a (i)_____ evaluation than a (ii)_____ summary of her career.","key":"CE","groups":[["valedictory","plodding","frank"],["scathing","glowing","schematic"]],"expl":"空1 valedictory（告别式的）；空2 glowing（称赞的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v104.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When potentially disruptive change appears on the horizon, managers’ approach should be to assemble the capabilities to (i)______ that change before it affects the mainstream business. The (ii)______ to run two businesses, one with processes attuned to the existing business model and another geared toward the new model. While apparently onerous, this parallel operation is far less dangerous than either (iii)______ innovation irrevocably or remaining committed to tried-and-true methods that are threatened with obsolescence.","key":"CEI","groups":[["obstruct","stimulate","handle"],["competition might have","requirement is","mistaken approach is"],["jumping into","exploring","rejecting"]],"expl":"空1 anticipate / meet（应对）；空2 need（需要）；空3 pays off（有回报）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v104.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Catherine’s ______ made it nearly impossible to discuss beliefs with her that she didn’t already hold.","key":"AB","opts":["insularity","parochialism","ideology","openness","assertiveness","receptiveness"],"expl":"parochialism（狭隘）与 insularity 描述凯瑟琳的思想封闭。选 AB"},{"id":"v104.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because the country’s media are now operating freely and the electoral authorities have been changed, there should be no repeat of the ______ of last year’s election, when media coverage and vote counts were manipulated by the intelligence agency.","key":"AF","opts":["chicanery","blundering","ingenuousness","naivete","vindictiveness","subterfuge"],"expl":"chicanery（欺诈）：去年选举中的舞弊。选 AF"},{"id":"v104.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many readers are bemused to discover that Ella Wheeler Wilcox's book Poems of Passion was thought to be ______ when it was published in 1883, as the book seems fairly innocuous.","key":"AC","opts":["scandalous","radical","unseemly","uninteresting","pedestrian","eccentric"],"expl":"scandalous（丑闻式的）：作品当年被认为有伤风化。选 AC"},{"id":"v104.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the rate at which absolute global sea level is rising may seem ______, it has been far from an incidental factor in human history.","key":"DF","opts":["disconcerting","intractable","improbable","imperceptible","unnerving","trivial"],"expl":"imperceptible（难以察觉的）：海平面上升虽然缓慢，却影响深远。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v104-2","title":"Test 104 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v104.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In the Middle Ages, Europeans placed the holy city of Jerusalem at the center of maps, reflecting the prevailing _____ of the era.","key":"D","opts":["iniquity","parsimony","anthropocentrism","cosmology","proximity"],"expl":"cosmology（宇宙观）：地图反映中世纪的宇宙观。选 D"},{"id":"v104.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Their remote jungle habitat and their extreme shyness have (i)_____ any thorough investigation of orangutans except in the (ii)_____ conditions of captivity.","key":"CF","groups":[["subsumed","simplified","precluded"],["primitive","heightened","unnatural"]],"expl":"空1 precluded（排除）；空2 unnatural（非自然的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v104.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Historians have been (i)_____ African American fraternal organizations, in part due to the (ii)_____ historical evidence: the relevant records are scarce and difficult to obtain.","key":"AE","groups":[["hindered in studying","confident in assessing","eager to categorize"],["discrepancies in","insufficiency of","approach to"]],"expl":"空1 hindered in studying（在研究上受阻）；空2 insufficiency of（不足）。选 AE"},{"id":"v104.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"An innovative musician, accompanist extraordinaire, and protomodern hipster, Lester Young (1909-1959) remains a (i)_____ in the jazz firmament. Some of the reasons are obvious: although he dressed with conspicuous cool, he chose an artistic trajectory that seemed calculated to (ii)_____ the spotlight-his best work was in the bands of other musicians, such as Billie Holiday and Count Basie, rather than at the front of his own. Moreover, he was shy, subtle, and sensitive-traits not usually associated with great (ii)______.","key":"BDI","groups":[["bright star","lesser light","permanent fixture"],["shun","intensify","exploit"],["imagination","restraint","celebrity"]],"expl":"空1 legend（传奇人物）；空2 avoid（避开）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v104.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author’s description of the ______ contamination of ocean water with plastic materials— and the resulting threat to marine life—constitutes a valuable lesson in the urgency of managing trash more responsibly than we currently do.","key":"BD","opts":["inadvertent","ubiquitous","perilous","pervasive","abating","diminishing"],"expl":"ubiquitous（无处不在的）：塑料污染遍布海洋。选 BD"},{"id":"v104.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"However much people what to avoid physical pain and feelings of anxiety, both are ______ self-preservation in a dangerous world.","key":"BE","opts":["compatible with","essential for","complementary to","reliant on","indispensable for","noteworthy for"],"expl":"indispensable for（对……不可或缺）：两者都是自我保护所必需的。选 BE"},{"id":"v104.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Katz’s attitude toward Pancho Villa can hardly be called ______: a thesis runs through Katz’s book to the effect that history has denied Pancho Villa his due.","key":"EF","opts":["unsympathetic","dogmatic","inflexible","judgmental","neutral","impartial"],"expl":"neutral / impartial 描述 Katz 对 Villa 的态度不算中立。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v105-1","title":"Test 105 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v105.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The fact that there are so many varieties of youthful dissent indicates that there is considerably less _____ to this counterculture than has been suggested.","key":"E","opts":["hypocrisy","relevance","spontaneity","degeneracy","coherence"],"expl":"coherence（连贯性）：青年反文化缺乏内在一致性。选 E"},{"id":"v105.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Discovering that cooler stars, which constitute three-quarters of our galaxy, can also be surrounded by habitable zones warm enough to harbor liquid water and, potentially, microbes and bacteria, has (i)_____ the (ii)_____ the search for extraterrestrial life.","key":"BD","groups":[["assuaged","expanded","jeopardized"],["target territory in","popular discomfort with","primary motivation for"]],"expl":"空1 jeopardized（危及）；空2 target territory in（目标范围）。选 BD"},{"id":"v105.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The unattractive hyena is unjustly (i)_____. It was long believed that when bob lions and hyenas were present at a kill, the latter invariably stole from the former, but this notion proved to be (ii)_____: we now know that the lion is just as (iii)_____ the hard-won prey of the hyena.","key":"AFG","groups":[["maligned","imperiled","forgotten"],["divisive","convoluted","untrue"],["apt to pilfer","capable of overtaking","likely to become"]],"expl":"鬣狗长期被冤枉，人们以为狮子总是抢鬣狗的猎物，但狮子同样会抢夺鬣狗辛苦获得的猎物。选 AFG"},{"id":"v105.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since responsibility for content is often ______ in multiauthor papers, it is easy to suppose that such papers may contain more instances of questionable academic practices than do papers by a single author.","key":"BD","opts":["ignored","diluted","disputed","weakened","highlighted","foregrounded"],"expl":"diluted（被稀释）：多作者论文中个人责任被分散。选 BD"},{"id":"v105.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"When Kim Dae Jung was decisively elected South Korea’s president in December 1997, he was considered something of ______, but nevertheless the right man for the time and the job.","key":"CD","opts":["an unknown","an expert","a maverick","a nonconformist","a dilettante","an authority"],"expl":"a maverick（特立独行的人）：金大中被视为异类。选 CD"},{"id":"v105.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author argued that the industrial agricultural system that prevails in the United States is unsustainable and, therefore, anything that ______ it should be questioned.","key":"BD","opts":["streamlines","reinforces","encumbers","buttresses","endangers","hampers"],"expl":"hampers（阻碍）：凡是阻碍不可持续农业的都应受质疑。选 BD"},{"id":"v105.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Whereas the original editor had sacrificed clarity for brevity and her successor had been too ______, the new editor took an intermediate approach, explicit as to the purport of each document and not too ambitious in detail.","key":"BD","opts":["discriminating","prolix","bombastic","verbose","cryptic","inscrutable"],"expl":"verbose（冗长的）与 prolix 描述后任编辑过于啰嗦。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v105-2","title":"Test 105 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v105.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The mountain pine beetle is not _____ like other major pests ravaging much of the American landscape: it is native to the western pine forests.","key":"A","opts":["an interloper","a nuisance","an anomaly","a mystery","a predator"],"expl":"an interloper（外来入侵者）：松甲虫并非外来物种。选 A"},{"id":"v105.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While Zora Neale Hurston never avowed an affiliation with surrealism, an artistic movement celebrating the unconscious mind's creative power, French surrealist Guy Ducomet’s citing her as an inspiration seems quite _____ given Hurston's intensely imaginative work.","key":"A","opts":["tenable","arcane","audacious","prescient","eccentric"],"expl":"tenable（站得住脚的）：此说法在文学上并不牵强，符合想象力丰富的作品。选 A"},{"id":"v105.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"While writers on Parker often present her as an avaricious stick figure, thus making her an object of (i)_____. Nash, by contrast, gives a more (ii)_____ and sympathetic portrait of the woman.","key":"CF","groups":[["adulation","praise","opprobrium"],["intense","polemical","nuanced"]],"expl":"空1 opprobrium（谴责）；空2 nuanced（细致入微的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v105.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Our contemporary preference for natural expression over artifice is (i)_____ the traditional Western view that the skill with which you expressed a position corresponded closely to the credibility of your argument. Rhetorical styles might vary, but style itself was never a matter of (ii)_____. And “style” was not just a well-turned sentence: poor expression, it was believed, (iii)_____ poor thought.","key":"AEI","groups":[["a departure from","a reflection on","an endorsement of"],["substance","indifference","intention"],["ameliorated","elevated","betrayed"]],"expl":"当代崇尚自然表达，与传统西方重视修辞技巧的观点相悖；风格并非纯粹修饰，而与说服力密切相关。选 AEI"},{"id":"v105.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Einstein called Amalie Noether the most significant mathematical genius produced since higher education of women began; so transformative was her theorem of mathematical symmetry that some consider the temporal qualification in Einstein’s statement ______.","key":"CE","opts":["disingenuous","fawning","expendable","flattering","superfluous","manifest"],"expl":"superfluous（多余的）：时间限定语可有可无。选 CE"},{"id":"v105.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A key characteristic in the author’s presentation of his character’s dreary life is ______, paragraphs are short, sentence are laconic, patterns of repetition and circularity are evoked by means of symbolic shorthand.","key":"BD","opts":["redundancy","economy","hyperbole","concision","exaggeration","restraint"],"expl":"concision（简洁）：作者用短句和省略体现简洁风格。选 BD"},{"id":"v105.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Human hearing is remarkably ______: an attentive listener knows if a band’ s drummer is as little as one thousandths of a second late on the beat.","key":"DF","opts":["sophisticated","adaptable","independent","sensitive","versatile","discerning"],"expl":"sensitive（敏感的）：听觉的敏锐度惊人。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v106-1","title":"Test 106 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v106.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Saturn's rings seem _____, but it now appears that several decades ago, the shape of the innermost rings was altered by a mysterious event that all our telescopes and spacecraft failed to detect.","key":"A","opts":["immutable","fragmentary","luminous","unique","concentric"],"expl":"immutable（不变的）：土星环本以为恒定不变。选 A"},{"id":"v106.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Rocks of the Morrison Formation in the western United States yield many dinosaur fossils but few plant fossils. This apparent (i)_______ of plants leads some scientists to speculate that the region was once mostly barren. But others have (ii)_______, noting that the herbivorous dinosaurs there would have needed an abundant food supply.","key":"BF","groups":[["attrition","dearth","attenuation"],["abdicated","acceded","demurred"]],"expl":"空1 attrition（减少）；空2 proposed a different explanation（提出另一种解释）。选 BF"},{"id":"v106.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The general claim that artists are the preeminent specialists in (i)_____ is refuted by the obvious fact that the great mathematical and scientific discoveries of the past and present have been as much the result of (ii)_____ thinking as have great (iii)______ discoveries.","key":"BFI","groups":[["revelation","creativity","symbolization"],["original","anachronistic","systematic"],["historical","empirical","artistic"]],"expl":"数学与科学的重大发现同样依赖抽象推理，这说明艺术家并非唯一的创造性专家。选 BFI"},{"id":"v106.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Much honored for her work in both theater and film, the director was prolific-too much so, according to some critics who thought she sometimes took on projects ______.","key":"AC","opts":["haphazardly","unprofitably","indiscriminately","unflaggingly","inappropriately","prematurely"],"expl":"indiscriminately（不加区分地）：导演接下了太多项目。选 AC"},{"id":"v106.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some species of the genus Daphnia (commonly known as water fleas) are phenotypically ______, altering their diurnal migration behavior and developing exaggerated morphological defenses in response to predators.","key":"DF","opts":["immutable","methodical","determinate","plastic","arbitrary","pliable"],"expl":"plastic（可塑的）：水蚤能根据捕食者改变行为与形态。选 DF"},{"id":"v106.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Yang Hong’s studies of ancient Chinese tombs transcribe the tombs’ epitaphs and inscriptions, noting whether these texts corroborate available information about the deceased’s life or ancestry or ______ it by presenting biographical material not found elsewhere.","key":"CE","opts":["disseminate","contradict","supplement","obviate","augment","promulgate"],"expl":"contradict（反驳）：墓志铭可能证实，也可能反驳已有信息。选 CE"},{"id":"v106.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Wilkinson believes that the subversion of science is widespread, though generally more subtle than the particularly ______ cases he selected to draw attention to his book.","key":"AC","opts":["blatant","innocuous","conspicuous","controversial","insignificant","disconcerting"],"expl":"blatant（明目张胆的）：作者挑选的是最显眼的例子。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v106-2","title":"Test 106 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v106.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In recent years, the country's farmers have been extremely _____, contributing a major portion of the disturbances and protests against government policies.","key":"C","opts":["discerning","tractable","restive","mercurial","circumspect"],"expl":"restive（不安分的）：农民频繁抗议。选 C"},{"id":"v106.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Sinden notes that in the face of warnings about the perils of climate change, the need to agree on strategies for reducing greenhouse-gas emissions is increasingly urgent. The question of who should reduce emissions is not (i)________. Rather, according to Sinden, it is the question of who should bear the costs of these reductions that is (ii)_______.","key":"AE","groups":[["particularly vexed","universally resolved","politically innocuous"],["redundant","contentious","prescient"]],"expl":"空1 the central issue（核心问题）；空2 contentious（有争议的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v106.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many elected officials have (i)_____ into believing that the new reforms represent a solution rather than (ii)_____ of the problem. Unfortunately, such self-deception is not uncommon among politicians.","key":"BF","groups":[["conned others","deluded themselves","persuaded some"],["an elucidation","a resolution","an exacerbation"]],"expl":"空1 deluded themselves（自欺）；空2 an exacerbation（加剧）。选 BF"},{"id":"v106.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"As theories, quantum field theory and theory of general relatively have been astonishingly (i)_____ that no experiment yet has shown a crack in either of them, even though both of them (ii)_____ wildly counterintuitive properties in physical reality. And yet even proponents note that the two theories are (iii)_____, a fact that has disallowed theorists—at least so far—from incorporating both into a self-consistent theory of quantum gravity.","key":"AFH","groups":[["successful","popular","implausible"],["downplay","result in","posit"],["difcfi ult for laypeople to","deeply at odds with each","similar to earlier physical"]],"expl":"空1 confirmed（经受住了检验）；空2 posit（提出）；空3 incompatible（不相容的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v106.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although torrential rains can sometimes be highly destructive, human survival generally proves much more ______ without rain than during periods of its overabundance.","key":"CE","opts":["ponderous","unmanageable","onerous","tedious","arduous","unlikely"],"expl":"onerous（沉重的）：没有雨水时，人类生存更困难。选 CE"},{"id":"v106.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author’ s latest novel may ______ those who generally spurn her writing: its unvarnished prose has little in common with the labyrinthine interior explorations of her earlier work.","key":"BE","opts":["entice","gall","surprise","placate","rankle","appease"],"expl":"gall（惹恼）：新小说会让平时反对她的人不满。选 BE"},{"id":"v106.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many child development experts emphasize that the effects of a controlling parenting style are ______ individual differences in children’s personality: for instance, such effects are less pronounced among children who are temperamentally agreeable.","key":"CF","opts":["confounded with","unaffected by","sensitive to","detrimental to","damaging to","modulated by"],"expl":"modulated by（受……调节）：专制教养的影响会因孩子性格而异。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v107-1","title":"Test 107 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v107.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Dr. Jack Kevorkian became a subject of controversy in the 1990s by assisting terminally ill people to commit suicide in contravention of Michigan statutes’ _____ such actions.","key":"B","opts":["justifying","proscribing","presaging","abjuring","substantiating"],"expl":"proscribing（禁止）：法律禁止此类行为。选 B"},{"id":"v107.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In China, beginning in the 1920s, the field of geography was (i)_____ discourse, alive to indigenous Chinese traditions even as it (ii)_____ key elements of Western scientific geography.","key":"BF","groups":[["an arcane","a hybrid","a subjective"],["ignored","questioned","absorbed"]],"expl":"空1 a hybrid（混合的）；空2 absorbed（吸收）。选 BF"},{"id":"v107.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The current organization of agricultural production is certainly not (i)_____ addressing the problem of world hunger. Much of the corn and soy grown in the world feeds cattle, pigs and chickens being raised for meat. This despite the (ii)_____ that is (iii)_____ such a process: two to five times more grain is required to produce the same number of calories in meat as can be obtained through the direct consumption of grain.","key":"BFI","groups":[["responsible for","optimal for","incapable of"],["pragmatism","fecundity","inefficiency"],["discouraged by","regulated by","inherent in"]],"expl":"空1 efficient（高效的）；空2 inefficiency（低效）；空3 entailed（涉及）。选 BFI"},{"id":"v107.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"He opens in a style that is notably contentious for a scientific paper, ______ previous works that, in his dim view, have too quickly drawn analogies between human thought and animal thought.","key":"EF","opts":["ignoring","cataloging","espousing","endorsing","disparaging","belittling"],"expl":"disparaging（贬低）：作者批评前人的类比。选 EF"},{"id":"v107.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Claire Tomalin’ s biography of Dickens offers a seamless application of \"the life” to\"the art\" -and what ______ balancing act it is, in which, just barely, Dickens' art is not lost amid a smothering welter of facts.","key":"AB","opts":["a perilous","a daring","an inadequate","a successful","an insufficient","an unconventional"],"expl":"a daring（大胆的）：在生活与艺术间的平衡十分大胆。选 AB"},{"id":"v107.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the incongruities of modern industry, according to Reck and Graedel, is that we manufacture modern products with the most sophisticated technologies available yet generally adopt relatively ______ approaches to recycling them.","key":"BC","opts":["economical","basic","crude","conventional","inefficient","inexpensive"],"expl":"crude（粗陋的）与 basic 描述回收方法落后。选 BC"},{"id":"v107.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The actor was quick to warn new members of the cast that the director's cherubic countenance belied ______ temperament.","key":"BF","opts":["a deceitful","a choleric","a morose","an imperious","a vengeful","an irascible"],"expl":"a choleric（易怒的）：慈祥外表掩盖了暴躁性格。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v107-2","title":"Test 107 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v107.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Numerous studies have documented the influence of advertisers on media content, disproving the popular notion of a _____ between business and editorial operations.","key":"B","opts":["cooperation.","separation","competition","collusion","disaffection"],"expl":"separation（分离）：广告影响媒体，打破了商业与编辑间的分隔假设。选 B"},{"id":"v107.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While Fernandez-Armesto has amply documented the commercial, migratory, scientific, or religious motives of explorers throughout history, it is often harder to _____ the motives of modern explorer.","key":"B","opts":["generate","penetrate","extinguish","utilize","criticize"],"expl":"penetrate（洞悉）：现代探险者的动机难以探明。选 B"},{"id":"v107.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"An affinity for (i)_____ is a characteristic of Bynum's work and of her rhetorical strategy as a historian, and it is often both refreshing and illuminating. But this predilection for (ii)_____ can be vexing, too, by appearing to eschew necessary distinctions.","key":"AF","groups":[["paradox","humor","understatement"],["daring hyperbole","indiscriminate eclecticism","unresolvable ambivalences"]],"expl":"空1 paradox（悖论）；空2 indiscriminate eclecticism（无差别的折中）。选 AF"},{"id":"v107.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"A (i)______ assumption of the model is that (ii)______ the living standards of people living adjacent to a protected area will necessarily enhance conservation within the protected area. Studies of conservation attitudes of people in South Africa and Tanzania have found a positive correlation between affluence and conservation attitudes, but it is unlikely that an improvement in the living standards of communities near protected areas will inevitably (iii)______ the long-term viability of many species within the protected areas.","key":"ADG","groups":[["misguided","conservative","compelling"],["raising","discounting","assessing"],["increase","inhibit","prevent"]],"expl":"空1 implicit（隐含的）；空2 improving（改善）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v107.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For all the ______ that would later come to plague the committee, the atmosphere when it was initially convened was one of optimistic camaraderie.","key":"AD","opts":["acrimony","controversy","apathy","rancor","despair","frustration"],"expl":"acrimony（争执）：委员会后来的纷争与一开始的乐观形成对比。选 AD"},{"id":"v107.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Agnita Tennant’s three-volume translation represents only part one of Pak Kyung-ni’s epic novel of Korean history, but, although seeded with intriguing premonitions of future events, the work reads as ______ narrative.","key":"AD","opts":["an independent","a dramatic","a preliminary","a self-contained","an uncontrived","an introductory"],"expl":"a self-contained（自成一体的）：虽为第一部，却可独立阅读。选 AD"},{"id":"v107.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scholars have learned from the demographic reconstructions of the precipitate population decline in the Caribbean after the Spanish conquest that we should be cautious before we treat early accounts of a large preconquest population as though they are ______.","key":"BC","opts":["exaggerated","accurate","authentic","persuasive","hyperbolic","deceptive"],"expl":"exaggerated（夸大的）：早期的人口估计可能被夸大。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v108-1","title":"Test 108 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v108.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"To some extent, the relationship between nitrous oxide and methane in Earth's atmosphere could be described as _____: nitrous oxide releases oxygen when destroyed by ultraviolet radiation, while methane is an oxygen consumer.","key":"C","opts":["necessary","ephemeral","inverse","anomalous","ubiquitous"],"expl":"inverse（相反的）：二者此消彼长。选 C"},{"id":"v108.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"A Sociological jurisprudence has a (i)_____ rather than (ii)_____ focus: it is concerned with what actually goes on in the legal system, not with what ought to go on.","key":"BE","groups":[["humanitarian","descriptive","hypothetical"],["an elitist","a normative","an applied"]],"expl":"空1 descriptive（描述性的）；空2 normative（规范性的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v108.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"For decades scientists believed in the (i)_____ of long-term memories: they were unstable for a few hours but then became etched into the brain for good. Current research, however, suggests that recalling a memory causes it to revert temporarily to an insecure state in which the recollection can be (ii)_____. Thus, memory is much more (iii)_____ than scientists had previously thought it to be.","key":"BEI","groups":[["accuracy","immutability","predictability"],["instilled","modified","observed"],["reliable","constrained","fluid"]],"expl":"空1 stability（稳定）；空2 altered（改变）；空3 fluid（易变的）。选 BEI"},{"id":"v108.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While other authors surely ______ American novelist Toni Morrison's literary style, there really was no precedent for the sorts of books she conceived.","key":"CF","opts":["appreciated","dismissed","influenced","adopted","analyzed","informed"],"expl":"influenced（影响）：其他作家可能受莫里森影响。选 CF"},{"id":"v108.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The dearth of ______ vocabulary reassures readers of the book that they are initiated in an exclusive sect.","key":"AB","opts":["pretentious","affected","commonplace","coarse","riveting","ordinary"],"expl":"pretentious（做作的）：缺乏做作的词汇使读者感到亲切。选 AB"},{"id":"v108.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It can be a daunting task to plunge into the disparate and extensive data sets on the carnivores and ______ meaningful patterns from their extraordinary morphological behavioral, and ecological diversity.","key":"AD","opts":["distill","conjure","distinguish","extract","conceal","hide"],"expl":"distill（提炼）：从数据中提炼规律。选 AD"},{"id":"v108.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Land near Bangladesh's coastal rivers is ______: temporary islands, or chars, form in the main rivers as sediments are deposited and then disappear during floods.","key":"CE","opts":["fecund","scant","ephemeral","exiguous","transitory","treacherous"],"expl":"ephemeral（短暂的）：沙洲出现后很快消失。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v108-2","title":"Test 108 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v108.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"As British biochemist Joseph Needham became immersed in the study of China's history, he began to envision science as _____ endeavor, noting that \"the peoples of the whole world have all made their contributions.\"","key":"A","opts":["an ecumenical","a competitive","a redemptive","a misunderstood","an underappreciated"],"expl":"an ecumenical（普世的）：科学是全球共同事业。选 A"},{"id":"v108.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"During the decade 2000-2010 in the United States, the increase in self-employed Hispanic entrepreneurs (i)______ the increase in Hispanic workers overall. Historically, Hispanics have been (ii)_____ in the self-employment sector, so this change reduced the amount by which the Hispanic self-employment rate trailed the overall self-employment rate.","key":"CD","groups":[["catalyzed","tracked","exceeded"],["underrepresented","undercompensated","underappreciated"]],"expl":"西班牙裔自雇者的增长几乎与整体西班牙裔劳动力增长同步，缩小了与总体自雇率的差距。选 CD"},{"id":"v108.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unlike, say, locusts, which simply raze entire fields, stinkbugs wreak their havoc (i)______. The injury they do to corn, for instance, is (ii)______ the ear is husked, at which point certain kernels-the ones into which a stinkbug stuck its pointy mouth-will reveal themselves to be sunken and brown.","key":"BD","groups":[["periodically","insidiously","instantaneously"],["invisible until","ameliorated when","apparent before"]],"expl":"臭虫的损害隐蔽地发生，只有玉米被剥开后才显现出来。选 BD"},{"id":"v108.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The traditional set of nine planets could have been retained by defining a planet as any object that has the unique combination of characteristics of any one of the nine objects that were considered planets in the late twentieth century. That definition would not be (i)_____; that is, it does not contradict the evidence. Its (ii)_____, however, renders it less (iii)_____ than definitions based on astronomical criteria, such as orbit, size, and gravitation.","key":"CDI","groups":[["paradoxical","subjective","false"],["arbitrariness","inconsistency","generality"],["expedient","stable","defensible"]],"expl":"空1 invalid（无效的）；空2 practicality（实用性）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v108.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite its stellar performances, the film is ______: it seems mysteriously incomplete in essential ways, yet feels repetitive at the same time.","key":"DF","opts":["wanting","dull","offensive","curious","distasteful","peculiar"],"expl":"wanting（有所欠缺的）：影片关键处不完整。选 DF"},{"id":"v108.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It’s when his technique is ______ rather than when he’s trying his hardest to impress that Murakami’s spell as a novelist is most persuasive.","key":"BC","opts":["unconventional","inconspicuous","low-key","polished","clever","unorthodox"],"expl":"low-key（低调的）：他的技巧不刻意时最有说服力。选 BC"},{"id":"v108.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Katherine’s disobedient behavior earned her a ______ from her parents.","key":"BF","opts":["eulogy","rebuke","panegyric","mockery","commendation","reproof"],"expl":"reproof（责备）：与 rebuke 同义，描述父母的训斥。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v109-1","title":"Test 109 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v109.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The research institute publishes new material on its Web site well in advance of its appearance in print; inevitably, there is a lot of dross, but fortunately, much of the material is both _____ and free.","key":"D","opts":["speculative","specious","copious","valuable","perplexing"],"expl":"valuable（有价值的）：网站上有大量糟粕，但仍有宝贵内容。选 D"},{"id":"v109.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"At first glance, each of the stories in the anthology seemed (i)_____, upon closer inspection of their protagonists, implied morals, and fantasy elements, however, subtle similarities among the stories emerged to (ii)_____ this initial observation.","key":"CD","groups":[["compelling","implausible","idiosyncratic"],["impugn","bolster","explain"]],"expl":"空1 idiosyncratic（独特的）；空2 bolster（支持）。选 CD"},{"id":"v109.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"During Nigeria's colonial period, the country’s Igbo societies had (i)_____ sense of gender distinctions, but the idea of a strict division of labor along gender lines (ii)_____. Indeed, the social roles of women and men were quite (iii)_____, based on what people did rather than on existential categories like gender.","key":"ADG","groups":[["an elastic","a well-developed","a diminishing"],["did not exist","was emerging","hardly changed"],["fluid","dissimilar","traditional"]],"expl":"空1 an elastic（有弹性的）；空2 was rigid（僵硬）；空3 fluid（流动的）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v109.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Once deemed too ______ the big bang model of the birth of the universe has turned out to be one of the most robust scientific theories, with experimental verification going back billions of years.","key":"AD","opts":["daring","complex","intractable","audacious","ambiguous","unpopular"],"expl":"audacious（大胆的）：大爆炸理论曾被认为过于大胆。选 AD"},{"id":"v109.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Gaige accomplishes a surprising feat: modeling her novel on one of the most ______ narratives in all of literature, she creates a remarkably understated tale.","key":"AC","opts":["sensational","revered","extravagant","imitated","suspenseful","chilling"],"expl":"revered（受推崇的）：小说以经典叙事为蓝本。选 AC"},{"id":"v109.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"When discussing the United States Army's 1876 campaign against the Sioux, Powers is occasionally ______ context: he describes General Crook's march to the Battle of the Rosebud but neglects to mention how it fit into the army's overall strategy.","key":"CE","opts":["misinformed about","obsessed with","frugal with","preoccupied with","stinting with","unscrupulous about"],"expl":"preoccupied with（过于关注）：忽视战略背景，属于只关注局部。选 CE"},{"id":"v109.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Judge Jones brought some welcome levity to the often tense, though sometimes ______, proceedings.","key":"BF","opts":["humorous","tedious","stressful","inconsequential","fraught","tiresome"],"expl":"fraught（充满紧张的）与 tense 呼应。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v109-2","title":"Test 109 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v109.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Ronald Ferguson, whose work is widely admired by policy makers, has never been profiled by the news media, perhaps because his views are _____ and therefore difficult to capture in a sound bite.","key":"A","opts":["nuanced","controversial","empirical","influential","unorthodox"],"expl":"nuanced（细致的）：观点细致，难以用简短的话概括。选 A"},{"id":"v109.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Mathematical knowledge has long been regarded as being essentially stable and hence rooted in a world of ideas only superficially ______ to historical forces.","key":"C","opts":["indifferent","superior","susceptible","extraneous","oblivious"],"expl":"susceptible（易受影响的）：数学知识只是表面上不受历史力量影响，实际上仍然会受影响。选 C"},{"id":"v109.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Xie proposes that sleep achieves its restorative function by switching the brain into a state that facilitates the clearance of waste products resulting from neural activity during wakefulness, indeed, the very (i)_____ of such waste products in the waking brain may (ii)_____ the switch to sleep state.","key":"BF","groups":[["utilization","accumulation","analysis"],["delay","succeed","trigger"]],"expl":"空1 accumulation（积累）；空2 trigger（触发）：废物的积累会促使脑进入睡眠状态。选 BF"},{"id":"v109.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Books about humor are rarely funny. Their goal, after all, is to (i)_____ the workings of that which we find comic, not to (ii)_____ laughter, and understanding why jokes are funny is not in itself (iii)_____.","key":"BEG","groups":[["celebrate","analyze","improve"],["explain","occasion","recall"],["amusing","helpful","admirable"]],"expl":"空1 analyze（分析）；空2 occasion（引起）；空3 helpful（有帮助的）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v109.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although technically their members were hunter-gatherers, many early Native California communities exhibited traits more typically associated with well-developed agrarian societies and, therefore, are often presented in the ethnographic literature as ______.","key":"CE","opts":["archaic","pragmatic","anomalous","exemplary","exceptional","utilitarian"],"expl":"anomalous（反常的）：这些社群的特征与其狩猎采集身份不符，因此被视为反常。选 CE"},{"id":"v109.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The vast majority of universities in the United States promote themselves as institutions of free speech and thought, construing censorship as ______ their search for knowledge.","key":"DF","opts":["subordinate to","obviated by","secondary to","antipathetic to","conducive to","inconsistent with"],"expl":"conducive to（有助于）：大学视言论自由为有利于求知的条件。选 DF"},{"id":"v109.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Louise Gluck has lone been a poet of ______ ideals; only in her later work does she veer toward a partial accommodation to human weakness and imperfection.","key":"CE","opts":["admirable","nontraditional","uncompromising","unorthodox","absolute","lofty"],"expl":"uncompromising（不妥协的）：格吕克早期作品的理想是不妥协的。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v110-1","title":"Test 110 · Section 1","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v110.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The watchword in astronomy is ______: all claims must be examined critically in the light of current knowledge, and one's mind should never be closed to the possibility that a theory could be wrong.","key":"C","opts":["implausibility","imagination","wariness","determination","incoherency"],"expl":"wariness（谨慎）：天文学应保持审慎。选 C"},{"id":"v110.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Lohr’s (i)______ the trappings of literary celebrity creates a Romantic aura for him: by distancing himself from all public discourse about himself or his work, Lohr becomes an even greater, albeit more (ii)______, celebrity than most authors manage in all their interviews and memoirs.","key":"AF","groups":[["refusal to wear","eagerness to understand","inability to renounce"],["renowned","appealing","mysterious"]],"expl":"空1 refusal to wear（拒绝沾染）；空2 elusive（难以捉摸的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v110.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The latest encyclopedia (i)_____ the (ii)______ made by many other books on how things work —giving (iii)_____ for every device, no matter how complicated—by taking just as long as is needed to explain things.","key":"CEH","groups":[["repeats","exposes","avoids"],["assumption","mistake","compromise"],["a brief historical","an equal number of words","at least one illustration"]],"expl":"空1 avoids（避免）；空2 mistake（错误）；空3 an exhaustive（详尽的）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v110.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the early-twentieth-century United States, the enforcement of the “separate but equal”doctrine in the treatment of African Americans was ______: much attention was paid to separation but scant to equality.","key":"BF","opts":["meticulous","selective","ruthless","ineffective","unwavering","lopsided"],"expl":"lopsided（不平衡的）：隔离被重视，平等却被忽视。选 BF"},{"id":"v110.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Unlike French cuisine, which works as a conversation among regional variations but recognizes the ______ of Parisian cuisine, Italian cuisine affirms a system based on the sum of equally regarded local cuisines.","key":"AD","opts":["preeminence","versatility","sophistication","hegemony","heaviness","heterogeneity"],"expl":"hegemony（霸权）与 preeminence 描述巴黎菜的主导地位。选 AD"},{"id":"v110.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Early natural history collections in eighteenth-century Europe were ______: a bear's tooth might sit incongruously alongside a piece of silverwork or, in the menagerie, a South American capybara might be housed next to an African baboon.","key":"EF","opts":["painstakingly arranged","impressively comprehensive","meticulously organized","highly exotic","fundamentally miscellaneous","thoroughly eclectic"],"expl":"highly exotic（高度异域的）与 incongruous 配合：收藏品并排列放，显得不协调。选 EF"},{"id":"v110.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The early stages of being trained to ride a motorcycle are all about developing muscle memory, repeating combinations of hand-foot movements until they are ______ and precise.","key":"CE","opts":["aberrant","innate","reflexive","inborn","automatic","calculated"],"expl":"reflexive（条件反射般的）与 automatic 描述动作熟练。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v110-2","title":"Test 110 · Section 2","group":"Test 101–110","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v110.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In general, the relationship between neural activity and behavioral output is _____: multiple behaviors can be associated with activation of the same neurons and multiple neurons can trigger the same behavior.","key":"D","opts":["deterministic","hardwired","random","complicated","cumulative"],"expl":"complicated（复杂的）：神经活动与行为之间的关系并不简单。选 D"},{"id":"v110.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"While the professor was once known for expressing herself (i)_______, that is no longer true. Her writing style is much more (ii)_______ than it was when she started her career over 30 years ago.","key":"CD","groups":[["caustically","idiosyncratically","plainly"],["florid","acerbic","succinct"]],"expl":"空1 idiosyncratically（独具一格地）；空2 succinct（简洁的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v110.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is incorrect to think of eighth-century Japan as (i)_____. In western and central Japan, for example, there was considerable (ii)______, with many inhabitants deriving their ancestry from the Wa and Yamato peoples and at least a third being descendants of Korean immigrants unrelated to those peoples.","key":"CE","groups":[["culturally conservative","politically unstable","ethnically homogeneous"],["tension","variation","obscurity"]],"expl":"空1 culturally conservative（文化保守的）；空2 genetic diversity（遗传多样性）。选 CE"},{"id":"v110.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"If a figure such as the editor and writer Pauline Hopkins presents (i)_____ challenges to a would-be biographer because of her confounding periods of science, largely unknown personal life, and (ii) _____ papers, the problems posed by John Edward Bruce are of the opposite kind: he published (iii)_____ throughout his life, had an extensive correspondence, and left a huge trove of materials at his death.","key":"CEG","groups":[["unpredictable","negligible","colossal"],["abundant","meager","lucid"],["indefatigably","sporadically","secretively"]],"expl":"空1 an interesting（有趣的）挑战；空2 unfinished（未完成的）；空3 extensive publications（大量出版物）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v110.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Khirigsuurs, distinctive stone-mounded monuments, are so ______ in central and western Mongolia that it has been argued that they were the defining features of the human landscapes of prehistoric Inner Asia.","key":"AC","opts":["ubiquitous","multifarious","prevalent","varied","admired","overwhelming"],"expl":"ubiquitous（无处不在）：此类石墓在蒙古中部与西部随处可见。选 AC"},{"id":"v110.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Artists such as Jimi Jones reveal how _____ art categories really are: Jones successfully uses materials relatively foreign to the hegemonic concept of fine art while working in a style commonly associated with high culture.","key":"BF","opts":["fragmented","contrived","pervious","prescriptive","conventional","artificial"],"expl":"artificial（人为的）：艺术类别其实是人为划分的。选 BF"},{"id":"v110.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The manufacturing company' s swift maneuver enabled it to evade the full impact of the increasing cost of raw materials, which brought the downfall of firms that responded less ______.","key":"BC","opts":["ruthlessly","deftly","adroitly","carefully","extravagantly","cautiously"],"expl":"deftly（巧妙地）：公司灵活应对成本上升。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v111-1","title":"Test 111 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v111.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"It is ironic that the scientist’s work was criticized recently for its _____ research methodology, since other researchers have argued for years that this same methodology was based absolutely on impeccable logic.","key":"E","opts":["fastidious","esoteric","abstruse","impervious","specious"],"expl":"specious（看似有理实则站不住的）：方法看似合理，其实经不起推敲。选 E"},{"id":"v111.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"For private fossil collectors, a fossil’s value is (i)______ the object itself. For scientists, however, the value of a fossil is usually (ii)______. Most paleontological research focuses not only on the fossil itself, but also on the fossil’s location, the kind of rock it was found in, its position in the historical sequence, and how the fossil is positioned relative to other fossils.","key":"BE","groups":[["inherent in","distinct from","unknowable from"],["enigmatic","contextual","controversial"]],"expl":"空1 the object itself（物件本身）；空2 contextual（语境性的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v111.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Arguments based on mere possibilities (i)_____ the difficulty of discussing future technology, not least since they (ii)_____ public debates on technological options. A mere possibility argument such as “Agricultural biotechnology can have serious effects on ecosystems that we still know nothing about” can be taken by opponents of the technology to be (iii)_____ whereas proponents tend to dismiss it completely.","key":"ADG","groups":[["epitomize","mitigate","outweigh"],["polarize","forestall","undergird"],["decisive","empirical","dogmatic"]],"expl":"空1 illustrate（说明）；空2 short-circuit（绕开）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v111.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Ruth Carter's campaigns for Congress were pretty ______: as a liberal in a deeply conservative district, she was virtually certain to lose.","key":"DF","opts":["conventional","underhanded","contentious","quixotic","indecorous","unrealistic"],"expl":"quixotic（不切实际的）：在保守选区中竞选自由派，几乎注定失败。选 DF"},{"id":"v111.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To most ethicists, self-interested action connotes the opposite of moral conduct, and its ______ is for them a virtual prerequisite for serious ethical discourse.","key":"CE","opts":["dispersion","promulgation","abjuration","circumscription","repudiation","dissemination"],"expl":"repudiation（否定）与 abjuration 类似：自利行为在伦理学中被摒弃，故不能为其辩护。选 CE"},{"id":"v111.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The recognition of ______ the movements of the Sun, Moon, planets, and stars gave many ancient societies the ability to project the past into the future, lending a predictability to the variable cosmos.","key":"BE","opts":["volatility in","periodicity in","reciprocity of","perturbation in","recurrence of","uniformity of"],"expl":"periodicity in（周期性）：古人认识到天体运动的周期。选 BE"},{"id":"v111.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The professional curator in Native American tribal museums ideally serves as ______, using her museological training to design exhibits that effectively convey to museumgoers the messages that the tribal community chooses to disseminate.","key":"AD","opts":["a mediator","an advocate","a transcriber","a translator","a facilitator","an ambassador"],"expl":"a mediator（调解人）：策展人应担任中介，把社区的信息传递给观众。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v111-2","title":"Test 111 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v111.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"For Confucius, names had _____ contents, no matter how time marched on and the affairs of the world changed, the proper names of things absolutely could not vary.","key":"C","opts":["largely transparent","uniquely adaptive","eternally stable","dangerously slippery","increasingly conventional"],"expl":"eternally stable（永恒稳定）：孔子认为名称应该不变。选 C"},{"id":"v111.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Astronomy dominated ancient science partly because it was ______ in a way that the physics and biology of the time were not: even in prehistory, people probably used the apparent motion of the Sun, for example, as a crude clock, calendar, and compass.","key":"C","opts":["precise","exciting","practical","lucrative","provocative"],"expl":"practical（实用的）：天文学是实用的科学。选 C"},{"id":"v111.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"An architect of Koolhaas’ (i)_____ might plausibly prefer designing on paper to building in concrete. Remaining within the realm of his own imagination, he need not worry about pesky clients who can dilute a project into mediocrity. But in fact, what Koolhaas enjoys most is the opportunity to engage with a client. When asked if he would consider designing a house for himself, he replied that the idea bored him, that it would feel too (ii)_____. For him, the whole point of architecture is the encounter with the other.","key":"BF","groups":[["unbridled ambition","unfettered originality","unalloyed pragmatism"],["sybaritic","altruistic","solipsistic"]],"expl":"空1 ambition（抱负）；空2 engaging with a client（与客户合作）。选 BF"},{"id":"v111.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Belief in the harmful effects of the drug has all the hallmarks of a viewpoint that is not (i)_____ even though the notion that the drug has negative consequences has been (ii)_____ multiple epidemiological studies over the past decade. Yet the true believers have (iii)_____, critiquing each new study that challenges their views and continuing to lean on supporting research that was retracted long ago.","key":"AFG","groups":[["amenable to refutation","driven by self-interest","capable of propagation"],["refined by","cited by","upended by"],["persisted","splintered","capitulated"]],"expl":"空1 open to refutation（可被反驳）；空2 refuted（反驳）；空3 defiance（抗拒）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v111.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"She criticizes the view that American democracy is ______, its strings pulled not by voters but by a power elite or ruling class.","key":"AC","opts":["a sham","an irrelevance","a charade","a success","an achievement","an enigma"],"expl":"a sham（骗局）与 charade 描述美国民主并非真正由选民决定。选 AC"},{"id":"v111.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Until fairly recently, hitchhiking was not an uncommon practice in the United States, but today's motorists are likely to see the occasional hitchhiker as ______, thinking “l didn’t know people still did that!”","key":"CE","opts":["a parvenu","an adventurer","an anachronism","a daredevil","a throwback","an upstart"],"expl":"an anachronism（过时之物）：搭车如今已成为过时的现象。选 CE"},{"id":"v111.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Legal scholars envision environmental politics as the pursuit of opposing and ______ interests and therefore likely to lead to confrontation rather than compromise.","key":"BC","opts":["selfish","fixed","immutable","competing","irrational","innocuous"],"expl":"competing（相互竞争的）：环境政治是对立而竞争的利益。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v112-1","title":"Test 112 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v112.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Since the fundamental frequency of an object's vibration is determined by its size and shape, a sequence of sounds having _____ pitch is perceived to have been produced by a single object.","key":"D","opts":["discernible","predictable","unusual","identical","melodious"],"expl":"identical（相同的）：同一物体产生的声音音高相同。选 D"},{"id":"v112.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The notion that scientists consider the work they do to be (i)_____ contradicts popular stereotypes that depict the work of scientists (and the scientists themselves) as being formal and rigid, following lockstep procedures in which the (ii)_____ elements of researchers’ personalities fail to enter their labors.","key":"BD","groups":[["socially useful","emotionally satisfying","intellectually demanding"],["affective","cognitive","conjectural"]],"expl":"空1 socially useful（社会有用的）；空2 personal（个人的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v112.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A certain (i)_____ governs the way most of us think about routines. A routine is sometimes conceived as constraining—a self-made prison of inflexible habits that prevent people from changing their lives. But routine is also seen as (ii)_____: activities that become routine (iii)_____, allowing us to expend energy on other things.","key":"CDH","groups":[["pessimism","misunderstanding","polarity"],["liberating","alterable","unintentional"],["are often tedious","demand less attention","encourage personal"]],"expl":"空1 paradox（悖论）；空2 liberating（解放性的）；空3 become automatic（变得自动化）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v112.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the features of spoken discourse is that a speaker need not be maximally ______: if an interlocutor is confused, he or she can interrupt and ask for clarification.","key":"EF","opts":["honest","forthcoming","courteous","meticulous","explicit","unambiguous"],"expl":"explicit（明确的）：说话人不必把话说得最清楚。选 EF"},{"id":"v112.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Enlightened thinkers in late-eighteenth-century Europe broadly endorsed the concept of progress, yet theories of progress were usually _____ a strong streak of pessimism, a sense of the challenges inherent in the human condition.","key":"EF","opts":["rooted in","requisite for","essential for","contradicted by","tempered by","moderated by"],"expl":"tempered by（被缓和）：进步论带有悲观情绪。选 EF"},{"id":"v112.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Voltaire's spirit was one of tolerant cosmopolitanism, even though he didn’t have the ______ to see that one challenge for such a spirit would be whether it was able to endure those who had no wish to be cosmopolitan.","key":"DF","opts":["hubris","generosity","ambition","awareness","arrogance","insight"],"expl":"insight（洞察力）：伏尔泰缺乏看到这一挑战的洞察。选 DF"},{"id":"v112.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Islands harbor a disproportionate amount of Earth’s biodiversity and are characterized by the presence of a great number of ______ plant and animal species; these species are often in danger of extinction by invasive predators.","key":"BE","opts":["transplanted","indigenous","adaptable","protean","endemic","anomalous"],"expl":"endemic（特有的）：岛屿上有大量特有物种。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v112-2","title":"Test 112 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v112.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The field suffers from being puffed up with its own importance, and that attitude of _____ seems to infect every professional utterance.","key":"C","opts":["self-justification","self-abnegation","self-congratulation","self-persuasion","self-castigation"],"expl":"self-congratulation（自我陶醉）：这个领域充满自我夸耀。选 C"},{"id":"v112.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Stigler brings a fundamental (i)______ to his protagonists, somehow treating them with respect even while he reveals these sometimes prickly characters behaving in (ii)______ ways.","key":"BF","groups":[["sentimentality","sympathy","baseness"],["spontaneous","perceptive","petulant"]],"expl":"空1 sympathy（同情）；空2 petulant（任性的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v112.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The (i)______ seen in most of eastern Eurasia is (ii)______ on the Mongolian plateau, despite only 200 millimeters of annual precipitation, because evaporation decreases at higher altitudes and latitudes.","key":"BD","groups":[["variability in temperatures","tendency toward aridity","complexity of ecosystems"],["reversed","discernible","exacerbated"]],"expl":"空1 tendency toward aridity（干旱倾向）；空2 discernible（可察觉的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v112.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"William Newman and Lawrence Principe point out that prior to the seventeenth century the terms “alchemy” and “chemistry” were largely (i))_____ in European usage. It was from the third decade of the eighteenth century that the two terms began to (ii)_____. Newman and Principe suggest that a third term, “chymistry,” should be used to denote the transitional early modern phase when “alchemy and “chemistry” were becoming (iii)_____.","key":"AFH","groups":[["interchangeable","absent","misapplied"],["coalesce","proliferate","diverge"],["increasingly more","steadily less synonymous","fundamentally less"]],"expl":"空1 interchangeable（可互换的）；空2 be distinguished（被区分）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v112.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In mid-twentieth-century Japanese monster movies, a giant creature typically attacks Japan and is ultimately vanquished either by some fortuitous scientific discovery or by another equally ______ plot device.","key":"BD","opts":["extravagant","expedient","tenable","convenient","plausible","dubious"],"expl":"convenient（方便的）与 expedient 描述情节装置的权宜性。选 BD"},{"id":"v112.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Strong chemical bonds and large energetic reactions are dramatic and easy to observe and understand, but a lot of the world around us and inside us operates on more ______ atomic and molecular interactions.","key":"BC","opts":["pervasive","delicate","subtle","dynamic","conspicuous","vigorous"],"expl":"subtle（微妙的）：生命的许多过程运作得更细微。选 BC"},{"id":"v112.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"By 2004 the idiosyncratic building had become ______ part of the city's urban landscape— hence the outrage when its owners announced that they planned to destroy its facade as part of a renovation.","key":"AB","opts":["an integral","a distinctive","an imperfect","a forgotten","a disregarded","a unique"],"expl":"an integral（不可或缺的）：建筑已成为城市景观的组成部分。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v113-1","title":"Test 113 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v113.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The philosophy of Zhuangzi, because it implied a spiritual elite who could transcend the bonds of the world and wander in a realm beyond life and death, appealed to a society dominated by ______.","key":"B","opts":["conventional morality","aristocratic tastes","dogmatic sensibilities","a pragmatic outlook","an egalitarian worldview"],"expl":"aristocratic tastes（贵族品味）：庄子的超脱哲学适合贵族阶层。选 B"},{"id":"v113.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"When Marx wrote, “the philosophers have only interpreted the world in various ways; the point, however, is to change it,” he was not only (i)_____ philosophers. He was (ii)_____ interpretation itself, as if thinking were an idle affairs compared with action, where real people make their mark on the world.","key":"BF","groups":[["consoling","slighting","praising"],["analyzing","extolling","disparaging"]],"expl":"空1 consoling（安慰）；空2 the point is to change（重在改变）；空3 idle（无用的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v113.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Why investors found Internet companies so (i)_____ in the early to mid-1990s is a mystery: the market for online advertising at the time was(ii)_____, and while Internet start-ups were everywhere, most were offering (iii)_____ rather than real services, and none were making any money.","key":"CDG","groups":[["daunting","alien","appealing"],["negligible","rebounding","untapped"],["optimistic promises","sizable returns","captive markets"]],"expl":"空1 appealing（吸引人的）；空2 nascent（初始的）；空3 vaporware（空头承诺）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v113.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Throughout her life, Suzanne Césaire remained ______, articulating a greater awareness of the complexity of Caribbean identity than most of her peers had, with a focus on multicultural influences that anticipated later theorists’ concerns.","key":"DE","opts":["an iconoclast","an outlier","an idealist","a visionary","a trailblazer","a romantic"],"expl":"a visionary（有远见者）：苏珊·塞萨尔超越同代人。选 DE"},{"id":"v113.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Certainly, the system of peer review of academic articles submitted for publication has intrinsic biases, some of them ______ factors like the homogeneity of the research community.","key":"AC","opts":["attributable to","explained by","exacerbated by","unconnected to","mitigated by","commensurate with"],"expl":"attributable to（归因于）：偏见可归因于研究群体同质化。选 AC"},{"id":"v113.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Beavers can modify the landscape in dramatic ways that are often______ humans, which is why media reports tend to emphasize what nuisances beavers are.","key":"DF","opts":["surprising to","derided by","misunderstood by","annoying to","unexpected by","unwelcome to"],"expl":"unexpected by（出乎……意料）：海狸的改变让人类意外。选 DF"},{"id":"v113.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One can expect that future generations will steadily become less ______ as new technologies enable the substitution of online activities for social, work-and shopping-related travel.","key":"BC","opts":["charitable","itinerant","peripatetic","reticent","munificent","inquisitive"],"expl":"peripatetic（四处奔走的）：未来人们的出行会减少。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v113-2","title":"Test 113 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v113.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Twentieth-century tussles in cosmology illustrate the ______ of science, for they highlight both the human drive to explore nature and the limits that our minds inevitably impose on our understanding.","key":"D","opts":["objective methodologies","theoretical evolution","cooperative nature","psychological aspects","serendipitous discoveries"],"expl":"psychological aspects（心理层面）：宇宙学展示了科学的人性面向。选 D"},{"id":"v113.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Biologists traditionally thought that restricted gene flow was _____ the development of adaptations in a population, but empirical evidence shows that adaptation can be maintained despite very high levels of gene flow.","key":"A","opts":["an impediment to","a consequence of","a harbinger of","a requisite of","an aberration in"],"expl":"an impediment to（阻碍）：传统认为基因流动阻碍适应。选 A"},{"id":"v113.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the university president can deploy considerable (i)_____, and her emotional reticence never seems rude, one nevertheless cannot help being aware of the (ii)_____ behind the affable public persona.","key":"BD","groups":[["cunning","charm","erudition"],["reserve","acumen","sagacity"]],"expl":"空1 charm（魅力）；空2 reserve（保留）。选 BD"},{"id":"v113.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"For years, wine writers have (i)_____ the public’s (ii)_____ the manifest charms of sherry. Why doesn't everyone love sherry, they asked, celebrating it as the most (iii)_____ wine in the world.","key":"AEH","groups":[["lamented","ignored","exacerbated"],["devotion to","indifference to","curiosity about"],["fashionable","underappreciated","notorious"]],"expl":"空1 lamented（哀叹）；空2 indifference to（漠不关心）；空3 underappreciated（被低估的）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v113.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Pop music continually recycles itself, building new hits around familiar themes, and successful new acts often do not even bother to disguise their ______.","key":"AC","opts":["appropriations","innovations","influences","pilferage","originality","complicity"],"expl":"influences（影响）：新乐队也不掩饰其影响来源。选 AC"},{"id":"v113.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To accommodate the ______ nature of clouds, pioneering meteorologist Luke Howard added compound nomenclature to his cloud classification system as a way of marking the regular transitions that occur among the three main cloud types.","key":"DE","opts":["unusual","essential","solitary","unstable","dynamic","scattered"],"expl":"dynamic（动态的）：云的动态本质需要复合命名。选 DE"},{"id":"v113.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Audiences in Edo, Japan, knew that no work appearing on the Kabuki stage was ever ______: if a Kabuki play outlived its first production, it would inevitably be reworked in subsequent performances.","key":"DE","opts":["revised","singular","original","fixed","final","recorded"],"expl":"fixed（固定的）：歌舞伎剧目从不固定。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v114-1","title":"Test 114 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v114.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some of the writers whose interviews with the Paris Review are included in this volume were caught in the final years of their lives, and these interviews thus lend _____ mood to the collection.","key":"A","opts":["an autumnal","a scintillating","a liberal","an apolitical","a cosmopolitan"],"expl":"an autumnal（秋日般的）：受访者处于晚年，使文集带有暮色。选 A"},{"id":"v114.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Throughout his career he has never displayed a disinterested respect for the truth—for what was actually said and done rather than for what the wishes had been. Given such a (i)_____ historical fact, it will certainly be seen as (ii)_____ that he should now embark on publishing a magazine ostensibly dedicated to history.","key":"AE","groups":[["cavalier disregard for","skeptical appreciation of","critical approach to"],["unimportant","ironic","appropriate"]],"expl":"空1 cavalier（轻率的）；空2 surprising（令人惊讶）。选 AE"},{"id":"v114.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the (i)_____ nature of contemporary science, the (ii)_____ of many individuals (iii)_____: the work of women and minority scientists has too often been exploited or deemed rudimentary and unworthy of inclusion into science history books.","key":"AEI","groups":[["collaborative","controversial","sophisticated"],["motivations","contributions","idiosyncrasies"],["manifest themselves","point to a solution","remain overlooked"]],"expl":"空1 collaborative（合作的）；空2 contributions（贡献）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v114.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the academic world, the peer-review process and editorial deliberations are largely ______, with only brief traces of these discussions appearing in acknowledgement sections or the occasional footnote that mentions a reviewer’s critique.","key":"EF","opts":["protracted","contentious","adversarial","inconclusive","invisible","concealed"],"expl":"invisible（不可见的）：审稿过程通常是隐形的。选 EF"},{"id":"v114.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Cooper was one of the twentieth century’s most ______ intellectuals: throughout a very long life he took up a great many causes, most of them unpopular.","key":"CD","opts":["notorious","eloquent","controversial","polarizing","articulate","detested"],"expl":"controversial（有争议的）：库珀一生支持的多是不受欢迎的事业。选 CD"},{"id":"v114.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While some studies have made claims for dogs’ superiority to cats in terms of intelligence (and other studies have made the opposite claim), it is more widely recognized that, because of the huge differences in these animals’ instinctual priorities, such comparisons are ______.","key":"DF","opts":["presumptive","essential","inconclusive","baseless","indispensable","invalid"],"expl":"inconclusive（不确定的）：狗与猫比较并无定论。选 DF"},{"id":"v114.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Throughout human history, intelligence and consciousness have been ______ concepts: those possessing much of the former are assumed, in some ill-defined way, to be more conscious than those less astute.","key":"BC","opts":["disputed","allied","conflated","loaded","contested","misjudged"],"expl":"conflated（混为一谈）：智力与意识常被混同。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v114-2","title":"Test 114 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v114.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"All biographies of ancient figures are necessarily _______, in that, in order to understand historical legends as human beings, there has to be some sort of translation into the categories of our own experience.","key":"A","opts":["anachronistic","pointless","comprehensive","intrusive","laudatory"],"expl":"anachronistic（以今律古的）：古人传记难免以现代经验去理解。选 A"},{"id":"v114.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In spite of its rather (i)_____ subject matter, Brinkley’s is (ii)_____ work, one that is moderated by grace and restraint and tempered by a caution that in no way suggests timidity.","key":"AE","groups":[["coarse","sophisticated","endearing"],["an indifferent","a subtle","an upsetting"]],"expl":"空1 coarse（粗俗的）；空2 a subtle（微妙的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v114.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"We should (i)_____ a history built on need and desire. The present always uses the past for its own purposes, but the best historical writing attempts to (ii)_____ that inescapable impulse in order to understand history in its own terms.","key":"BE","groups":[["be surprised by","be wary of","not misconstrue"],["embellish","contain","recognize"]],"expl":"空1 be wary of（警惕）；空2 contain（抑制）。选 BE"},{"id":"v114.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Anonymous sources have a tendency to (i)_____ the information content of news stories in which they are quoted. Most of these sources are (ii)_____ because they spin and leak selectively for political, personal, or institutional gain; all the balancing quotations from other sources can never remove their (iii)_____.","key":"CDH","groups":[["contradict","corroborate","degrade"],["unreliable","intransigent","obsequious"],["transparency","taint","obscurity"]],"expl":"空1 contradict / 空2 unreliable（不可靠的）；空3 credibility（可信度）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v114.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It was the Norman conqueror who introduced the forest law into England, but, as with so many institutions that developed after the Norman Conquest of England in 1066, there were some ______ this Norman law.","key":"BD","opts":["archaicisms in","antecedents of","innovations in","precedents for","derivations from","novelties about"],"expl":"antecedents of（先例）：诺曼法律在英格兰已有先例。选 BD"},{"id":"v114.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Those who ______ probabilistic risk assessment in structural engineering indicate that describing the safety of buildings is a matter of calculating probabilities, but that observation, though sound, does little to establish the superiority of probabilistic methodology.","key":"AB","opts":["champion","propound","analyze","disparage","understand","marginalize"],"expl":"disparage（贬低）：批评者认为该方法被高估。选 AB"},{"id":"v114.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In happier times, ours is a raucous, rude, cacophonous city, ______ cursing, good-natured complaining, and laughing aloud.","key":"DF","opts":["an abyss of","an oasis from","a remainder of","a hodgepodge of","a refuge from","a pastiche of"],"expl":"a pastiche of（大杂烩）：城市充满嘈杂与玩笑。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v115-1","title":"Test 115 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v115.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Baron's book implores scientists to present their work in ways that are accessible to the general public in order to save the world at large from scientific illiteracy, ______ that is echoed in other recent publications.","key":"C","opts":["a query","an analysis","an exhortation","an allurement","an implication"],"expl":"an exhortation（呼吁）：书中呼吁科学家公开传播研究。选 C"},{"id":"v115.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"By dramatizing the lives of her subjects with candor, sympathy, and a healthy strain of skepticism, director Esther Bell offers an (i)_____ the whimsy and solipsism (ii)_____ to much of what passes for independent filmmaking.","key":"AF","groups":[["antidote to","antecedent of","affirmation of"],["antithetical","immaterial","endemic"]],"expl":"空1 antidote to（对……的解药）；空2 endemic（普遍存在的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v115.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In general, observational studies tend to (i)_____ the effect of diet on overall health because a healthy diet is often (ii)_____ a healthy lifestyle. People who watch what they eat probably exercise more, avoid smoking, and follow other behaviors (iii)_____ good health. Any of those behaviors might also help explain why these people have lower disease rates.","key":"AEI","groups":[["overstate","clarify","discount"],["irrelevant to","a marker for","a substitute for"],["caused by","unrelated to","linked to"]],"expl":"空1 exaggerate（夸大）；空2 correlated with（与……相关）；空3 linked to（与……相关）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v115.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It has long been thought that smell might have _____ relation with memory, and recent research does indeed confirm that recollections tied to smell can be stronger than memories of other types.","key":"AC","opts":["an intimate","an overstated","a privileged","a complex","a favored","an exaggerated"],"expl":"a privileged（特殊的）：嗅觉与记忆有特殊的关系。选 AC"},{"id":"v115.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Coffee plants manufacture their own pesticide: caffeine, a chemical that is ______ to smaller organisms but stimulating to larger ones.","key":"BE","opts":["anathema","poisonous","displeasing","unsavory","toxic","soporific"],"expl":"咖啡因对小生物有毒（toxic），对大型生物则有刺激作用。选 BE"},{"id":"v115.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some critics, noting the power of photographs to manipulate perceptions, ______ the photographer’s work for intentionally misrepresenting its subjects.","key":"AE","opts":["lambasted","exculpated","lauded","scrutinized","censured","shunned"],"expl":"lambasted（严厉抨击）：批评者指责摄影师刻意歪曲被摄对象。选 AE"},{"id":"v115.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"This book indulges in a number of convenient ______, including its dubious timeline and its veneer of collective authorship.","key":"AF","opts":["fictions","contradictions","analyses","reminiscences","refutations","inventions"],"expl":"fictions（虚构、假设）：书中的时间线与集体作者身份都是方便的虚构。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v115-2","title":"Test 115 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v115.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The organization’s parlous fiscal condition led its members to expect that their plans for expansion would be _____.","key":"C","opts":["justified","abetted","thwarted","countenanced","implicated"],"expl":"thwarted（受挫）：财务困难使扩张计划落空。选 C"},{"id":"v115.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"This artistic and literary movement reflected a widespread nihilistic protest against every aspect of Western culture and thus _____ the particular aesthetic values of that culture.","key":"E","opts":["exemplified","revivified","recapitulated","superseded","repudiated"],"expl":"repudiated（否定）：该运动否定西方文化的审美价值。选 E"},{"id":"v115.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"She may have been (i)_____ when she was finance minister, fighting deficits, but now as prime minister she is marked by her (ii)_____.","key":"BE","groups":[["collaborative","austere","resourceful"],["discretion","largesse","platitudes"]],"expl":"空1 austere（节俭的）；空2 largesse（慷慨馈赠）。选 BE"},{"id":"v115.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some recent research shows that people tend to (i)_____ advice from (ii)_____ source, even to the point that we are willing to forgive an adviser's poor track record. This can drive those offering advice to (iii)_____ and bodes ill for advisers who try to be honest about gaps in their knowledge.","key":"BEI","groups":[["expect","trust","disregard"],["an unfamiliar","a confident","a candid"],["check their facts","disclaim their expertise","exaggerate their certainty"]],"expl":"空1 prefer / rely on（偏好）；空2 credible（可信的）；空3 more（更多地）。选 BEI"},{"id":"v115.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The fact that no single Cantonese dictionary is seen as ______ is one of the main reasons why most Hong Kong authors do not depend on formal reference tools when writing in Cantonese.","key":"BD","opts":["dependable","authoritative","meticulous","definitive","topical","comprehensive"],"expl":"definitive（权威的）：没有一部粤语词典被视为权威。选 BD"},{"id":"v115.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because connections made of the material are ______ to fail at high temperatures, it is particularly suited for sacrificial thermal cutoff switches; it is, of course, unsuited to applications where heat durability is needed.","key":"CF","opts":["unlikely","disinclined","apt","sure","bound","liable"],"expl":"apt（易于）：这种材料在高温下容易失效，适合用作牺牲性断路开关。选 CF"},{"id":"v115.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"On close reading, the poem comes across as ______, devoid of any real interest or substance.","key":"AC","opts":["vapid","curious","insipid","allusive","singular","problematic"],"expl":"vapid（空洞乏味的）：诗歌缺乏实质内容。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v116-1","title":"Test 116 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v116.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"EI Greco was one of the most fervent of painters, to the extreme of mania while Velazquez, by contrast, was one of the most _____.","key":"A","opts":["phlegmatic","obstreperous","edifying","grandiloquent","Fanciful"],"expl":"phlegmatic（冷静淡泊的）与 mania 相对：委拉斯开兹相当冷静。选 A"},{"id":"v116.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is (i)_____ that the toucan's bill is (ii)_____ ; in fact it isn't particularly heavy and seems not to unbalance the bird especially.","key":"BF","groups":[["an advantage","a misconception","a surprise"],["occasionally hazardous","unusually strong","uncomfortably bulky"]],"expl":"空1 a misconception（误解）；空2 unusually strong（异常沉重）。选 BF"},{"id":"v116.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"It is true that the cost of human-based space infrastructures, such as the International Space Station (ISS), is much higher than the cost of unmanned missions. However, the (i)_____ such projects (ii)_____ their (iii)_____. The ISS is a major accomplishment for all countries involved: it is the largest on-orbit structure ever built as well as the largest multinational cooperative project in history.","key":"BDG","groups":[["expenditures for","benefits of","doubts about"],["reach beyond","detract from","militate against"],["scientific output","unconventional design","extended lifespan"]],"expl":"空1 cost（代价）；空2 justifies（证明……合理）；空3 value（价值）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v116.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In gases, connections between atoms or molecules are even more ______ than they are in liquids, as the particles move randomly and chaotically, bouncing off each other.","key":"CF","opts":["energetic","unpredictable","tenuous","robust","intermittent","loose"],"expl":"tenuous（薄弱的）：气体中原子间的联系更弱。选 CF"},{"id":"v116.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Given the important role that apologies can play in human relations and the almost daily news reports of the latest celebrity or political apology, the ______ of empirical research on the subject is surprising.","key":"BE","opts":["weakness","scarcity","complexity","impartiality","want","sophistication"],"expl":"scarcity（稀缺）：关于道歉的实证研究却很少。选 BE"},{"id":"v116.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The term \"digital divide\" is often ______: instead of a binary distinction between\"haves\" and \"have nots,\" access to information technology varies along multiple dimensions, including the type of service and connection speed.","key":"AB","opts":["ambiguous","unhelpful","scornful","tendentious","pejorative","useless"],"expl":"ambiguous（模糊的）：“数字鸿沟”一词过于含混。选 AB"},{"id":"v116.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The dating of the prehistoric monument Stonehenge necessarily entails a great deal of speculation, with the result that several rather ______ chronologies have been proposed.","key":"CD","opts":["impenetrable","meticulous","disparate","inconsonant","confounding","apposite"],"expl":"disparate（彼此不同的）：推测性很强，因此提出了多种各异的年代序列。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v116-2","title":"Test 116 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v116.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The United States Constitution was intended to be adaptable to the demands of the various crises of human affairs, and judicial reinterpretation is the necessary means by which this _____ is preserved.","key":"A","opts":["flexibility","reiteration","misapprehension","paradox","contingency"],"expl":"flexibility（灵活性）：司法再解释保持了宪法的灵活性。选 A"},{"id":"v116.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The idea that arguments based on probability are deployed only by (i)_____ persons is (ii)_____ even among scientists. Perhaps such an evaluation has partly to do with the origins of the subject in the mathematics of gambling games, not generally regarded as pastimes for people of good character.","key":"BD","groups":[["exacting","disreputable","prominent"],["widespread","controversial","deplored"]],"expl":"空1 elite / 空2 widely accepted（被广泛接受）。选 BD"},{"id":"v116.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because the currents that flow back and forth between the Galapagos Islands and the Ecuadoran mainland create connections, the evolutionary (i)_____ of the sea creatures in the two areas, compared with that of the land dwellers, has been (ii)_____.","key":"CF","groups":[["association","sophistication","separateness"],["disguised","derailed","diminished"]],"expl":"空1 association（关联）；空2 sophisticated（复杂的）？按照原键，描述二者的研究状况。选 CF"},{"id":"v116.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Books that diagnose problems in democratic governance usually conclude with suggestions for procedural change. By contrast, the authors of this new study have, in their previous studies, always stuck closely to the data in their work, (i)_____ to propose measures that might (ii)_____ the circumstances they document. In this new study, however, in a break from their usual (iii)_____, they conclude by outlining some possible reforms.","key":"BEG","groups":[["creating incentives","forgoing opportunities","anticipating reasons"],["verify","ameliorate","exacerbate"],["reticence","assiduity","tendentiousness"]],"expl":"空1 willing（愿意）；空2 realistic（现实的）。选 BEG"},{"id":"v116.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even the most skeptical readers could hardly deny that the novelist' s best books are remarkably ______: they thrum with energy, imagination, and something resembling white-hot inspiration.","key":"CE","opts":["inventive","engaging","spirited","compassionate","vigorous","warmhearted"],"expl":"spirited（充满生气的）与 vigorous 描述小说的活力。选 CE"},{"id":"v116.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ______ list of interviewees included everyone from an oceanographer to a microbiologist, to a filmmaker.","key":"BE","opts":["profligate","sweeping","circumscribed","elite","comprehensive","meager"],"expl":"comprehensive（全面的）：受访者名单涵盖很广。选 BE"},{"id":"v116.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because Latin American colonial societies were fundamentally organized along hierarchical bases, the spatial arrangement of the cities and towns was also ______ ranking.","key":"BD","opts":["subordinate to","imbued with","equated with","permeated by","compromised by","constrained by"],"expl":"imbued with（被……渗透）：城市布局反映等级秩序。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v117-1","title":"Test 117 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v117.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"To write convincing fiction about the tedium of ordinary life may be one of the hardest challenges facing a novelist, who must find a way to engage the reader despite a focus on _____ events.","key":"C","opts":["distressing","dubious","quotidian","unwonted","nebulous"],"expl":"quotidian（日常的）：日常琐事的平淡。选 C"},{"id":"v117.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Much scholarship on the early Tana Tradition of coastal East Africa has been characterized by faith in the (i)_____ of that tradition, but detailed analysis of ceramics suggests that there were (ii)_____ the decorative motifs on early Tana Tradition jars, making it difficult to view the various Tana communities as a monolithic whole.","key":"BD","groups":[["originality","homogeneity","longevity"],["regional differences in","practical reasons for","periodic revivals of"]],"expl":"空1 coherence（一致性）；空2 surprisingly（出人意料地）。选 BD"},{"id":"v117.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The obsidian found across the Pungaere-Upokorau area in New Zealand has previously been thought to come from two distinct sites (Pungaere and Waiare), but considering that the visual characteristics and chemical composition of the obsidian in the area are so (i)_____, there is no reason to continue regarding Waiare as (ii)_____ source, especially in view of the fact that finds of obsidian near Waiare settlement and in the Waiare Stream are (iii)_____.","key":"CDG","groups":[["diverse","anomalous","consistent"],["a separate","the primary","a declining"],["rare","varied","abundant"]],"expl":"空1 similar（相似的）；空2 cannot be drawn（无法得出）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v117.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Song, speech, and music are typically one in the blues: the instrument complements the voice, and though they may play instrumental solos, the most ______ blues artists sing through both voice and instrument.","key":"BE","opts":["innovative","exemplary","original","reminiscent","representative","nostalgic"],"expl":"exemplary（典范的）：最具代表性的布鲁斯艺人。选 BE"},{"id":"v117.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The 1901 steel negotiations featured Morgan in his most famously ______ mode: knocking heads together, barking out prices for properties, and forcing titans to truckle to his will.","key":"CD","opts":["quixotic","eccentric","histrionic","theatrical","chivalrous","importunate"],"expl":"histrionic（做作的）：摩根常以戏剧化方式行事。选 CD"},{"id":"v117.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Holy People in Navajo sacred narratives do not act as moral ______: when they teach, it is as often by what they do wrong as by what they do right.","key":"DF","opts":["agents","arbiters","defenders","paragons","ethicists","exemplars"],"expl":"exemplars（典范）：圣者并非道德的典范。选 DF"},{"id":"v117.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Since it is an incredible challenge to detect dark matter directly, scientists have ______ its existence from its gravitational effects on shaping galaxies and other large-scale structures.","key":"CD","opts":["isolated","confirmed","inferred","surmised","documented","hypothesized"],"expl":"inferred（推断）：通过引力效应推断暗物质存在。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v117-2","title":"Test 117 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v117.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Drug companies rarely pursue new pharmacotherapies for rare disease because of the high failure rates and the cost of research, which make the companies’ chances of recovering their investments _____.","key":"B","opts":["tenable","dubious","invaluable","sanguine","expensive"],"expl":"dubious（可疑的）：收回投资的机会很渺茫。选 B"},{"id":"v117.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The watchword in astronomy is _____: all claims must be examined critically in the light of current knowledge, and one’s mind should never be closed to the possibility that a theory could be wrong.","key":"C","opts":["implausibility","imagination","wariness","determination","incoherency"],"expl":"wariness（谨慎）：天文学的座右铭是谨慎。选 C"},{"id":"v117.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Meegan Garber argues that the typical suburban lawn, which was originally designed to (i)_____ homes even as it enforced the distance between them, may be considered (ii)_____ domestic space: the whole neighborhood is invested in the appearance of each neighbor's yard.","key":"BE","groups":[["beautify","connect","circumscribe"],["utilitarian","common","contested"]],"expl":"空1 bind（连接）；空2 a shared（共享的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v117.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Victories in intellectual battles in the human sciences are rarely (i)_____. While factionalism may persist, (ii)_____ also tend to occur, as reigning paradigms selectively (iii)_____ those revisionist contributions that offer greater analytical comprehension or enrich our range of empirical reference.","key":"AFG","groups":[["total","acknowledged","benign"],["betrayals","distortions","accommodations"],["incorporate","expunge","misrepresent"]],"expl":"空1 decisive（决定性的）；空2 ideological（意识形态的）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v117.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The North Atlantic Oscillation is seesaw of atmospheric pressure between a persistent high over Portugal’s Azores islands and an equally ______ low over Iceland.","key":"AC","opts":["enduring","delimited","abiding","variable","anemic","bounded"],"expl":"enduring（持久的）与 abiding 描述北大西洋涛动中的两极。选 AC"},{"id":"v117.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even though some governments are now expressing alarm over their nations’ ______ birth rates, the planetary threat of human overpopulation has not ceased to concern many scientists and environmentalists.","key":"DF","opts":["fluctuating","incommensurate","burgeoning","flagging","thriving","languishing"],"expl":"flagging（下降的）：一些政府担忧出生率下降。选 DF"},{"id":"v117.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"At every turn in her novels, Patricia Highsmith eschews simple distinctions between good and evil, right and wrong, choosing instead to examine how ______ such distinctions can be.","key":"AF","opts":["plastic","palpable","parochial","arbitrary","concrete","malleable"],"expl":"malleable（可塑的）：区分对错的标准可以被改变。选 AF"}]},{"id":"v118-1","title":"Test 118 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v118.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Accustomed to the author's ponderous prose, readers will likely be startled by the _____ that characterizes his new work.","key":"B","opts":["prolixity","jocularity","abstruseness","predictability","pessimism"],"expl":"jocularity（诙谐）：作者的新作风格轻快。选 B"},{"id":"v118.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The psychologist's new findings present the discipline with a (i)_____: although her results pose a problem for the standard theory, the alternative theories she proposes are (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["predicament","paradigm","prototype"],["unconvincing","persuasive","versatile"]],"expl":"空1 predicament（困境）；空2 unconvincing（不足令人信服的）。选 AD"},{"id":"v118.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Maupassant's own writings were often notable for their (i)_____, so there is something ironic in the publication of such a (ii)_____ new work devoted to his life: a densely packed compendium of detail about Maupassant's own forty-two-year existence, Johnston's 1,336-page biography is anything but (iii)_____.","key":"BFI","groups":[["inventiveness","concision","ambition"],["rancorous","groundbreaking","sprawling"],["celebratory","original","economical"]],"expl":"空1 concision（简洁）；空2 exhaustive（详尽的）。选 BFI"},{"id":"v118.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Executives of successful companies frequently fail to exploit innovative new products because often they see only the difficulties and not the benefits of shifting financial and human resources from their profitable ongoing concern to something ______.","key":"BE","opts":["impractical","risky","earthshaking","vague","speculative","intangible"],"expl":"risky（有风险的）：转向新产品被视为有风险。选 BE"},{"id":"v118.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Stannard may be hoping to resurrect Spark's literary reputation with this book, given its _____ praise for her creative talents.","key":"EF","opts":["unctuous","genuine","grudging","reluctant","unstinting","generous"],"expl":"unstinting（慷慨不吝的）：赞美不遗余力。选 EF"},{"id":"v118.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The tools of science are so specialized that we accept them as a kind of ______ machinery for producing knowledge: we know that they work, but cannot explain why.","key":"AD","opts":["occult","efficacious","potent","arcane","impersonal","reliable"],"expl":"occult（神秘的）：科学工具像神秘机器。选 AD"},{"id":"v118.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The pupil had a reputation for obduracy, but the teacher found her to be, on the contrary, quite ______.","key":"DF","opts":["zealous","truculent","bellicose","tractable","efficient","complaisant"],"expl":"tractable（温顺的）与“不固执”呼应。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v118-2","title":"Test 118 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v118.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Massive geological changes do not always happen gradually; for example, asteroid and comet impacts and volcanic eruptions cause ______ changes in Earth's environment.","key":"B","opts":["transitory","precipitate","predictable","inconspicuous","incalculable"],"expl":"precipitate（突然的）：撞击与火山喷发造成突发变化。选 B"},{"id":"v118.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The songwriter's (i)_____ nature can lead her audiences to forget that her songs are about painful experiences just as often as they are about (ii)_____ ones.","key":"BE","groups":[["forthright","jocose","turgid"],["engaging","exultant","ponderous"]],"expl":"空1 forthright（直率的）；空2 engaging（吸引人的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v118.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although weeds often (i)_____ and are (ii)_____ human activities, their cussedness and refusal to play by human rules makes them subversive and the very essence of wildness.","key":"AF","groups":[["follow","thwart","ignore"],["unaffected by","impervious to","dependent on"]],"expl":"空1 thwart（挫败）；空2 impervious to（不受影响）。选 AF"},{"id":"v118.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Many perplexed observers find present-day museum design a choice between outlandishly sculptural structures that (i)_____ the proper display of art and neutral containers so (ii)_____ to art that all architectural presences is lost. But the New Museum persuasively demonstrates that honoring art and honoring architecture need not be (iii)_______ propositions.","key":"AFH","groups":[["ignore","enhance","honor"],["submissive","demeaning","impervious"],["carefully considered","mutually exclusive","entirely practical"]],"expl":"空1 impede（妨碍）；空2 neutral（中立的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v118.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The patrician old guard fancied itself ______ elite acting in ways that served the public interest; but in practice it proved to be intent on retaining its special advantages.","key":"CF","opts":["a maligned","a learned","a benevolent","an idealistic","an impartial","a disinterested"],"expl":"a benevolent（仁慈的）：所谓贵族实际只为自身利益。选 CF"},{"id":"v118.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The removal of methane from transport emissions is a major ______ for automakers and catalyst suppliers: after decades, there has been little progress in developing catalysts that can initiate methane oxidation at the required temperatures.","key":"BF","opts":["accomplishment","challenge","embarrassment","triumph","expense","obstacle"],"expl":"challenge（挑战）：甲烷催化剂仍是难题。选 BF"},{"id":"v118.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The television network seems to regard its longest-running comedy show as ______, keeping it in the schedule even as the humor it churns out is notoriously hit-or-miss.","key":"CE","opts":["flourishing","outdated","inviolable","archaic","sacrosanct","immovable"],"expl":"sacrosanct（神圣不可侵犯的）：节目被视为不可动摇。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v119-1","title":"Test 119 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v119.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"If we admire Winslow Homer as he wished to be admired, for his avoidance of claptrap and sentimentality, we may fear that Wood has done him a disservice by introducing _____ note into his discussion of the painter.","key":"D","opts":["an acerbic","a supercilious","an austere","a maudlin","an ironic"],"expl":"a maudlin（伤感的）：作者引入感伤语调会损害其形象。选 D"},{"id":"v119.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"For many who are not philosophers. the word \"metaphysics\" still retains connotations of (i)_____, so that many hard scientists still use the term as a byword for (ii)_____ thinking.","key":"BE","groups":[["impenetrability","amorphousness","sterility"],["innovative","imprecise","simplistic"]],"expl":"空1 sterility（空洞）；空2 imprecise（不精确的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v119.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"According to linguists and cognitive scientists, the human mind specializes in producing analogies. Part of the reason cognitive scientists believe analogy is a (i)_____ cognitive process is that drawing analogies requires some sort of similarity mapping of one concept onto another, and similarity mapping is a component of the inductive thinking we depend on. Another argument for the (ii)_____ of analogical reasoning in human reasoning is that metaphors, which are linguistically embedded analogies, are (iii)_____ language.","key":"CEG","groups":[["creative","distinctive","fundamental"],["versatility","centrality","difficulty"],["pervasive in","expressed in","embellishments of"]],"expl":"空1 fundamental（根本的）；空2 central（核心的）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v119.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In Roth' s fiction, politics is an element that doesn't naturally occur in ______ form but is always getting confused and mixed up with shame and anger, baseball and sex.","key":"AE","opts":["an unalloyed","an unbiased","an uncontroversial","an objective","a neat","a tendentious"],"expl":"an unalloyed（纯粹的）：政治很少以纯粹形式出现。选 AE"},{"id":"v119.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For many centuries, bearing life’s risks was supposed to be part of the human condition, and so any strategy for evading those risks was considered ______ of the natural order of things.","key":"BC","opts":["a rejection","a subversion","a violation","an overcoming","an improvement","an amelioration"],"expl":"a violation（违背）：规避风险被视为违背自然秩序。选 BC"},{"id":"v119.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the virtues of the essay collection is that it presents ______ views side by side, showing a wide range of thought and highlighting the contentious nature of many of the arguments within the discipline.","key":"AC","opts":["dissonant","congenial","incongruent","inconstant","authoritative","whimsical"],"expl":"dissonant（不协调的）：文集呈现的是不同观点。选 AC"},{"id":"v119.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For many readers, dissatisfaction with the book’s contents will be ______ by the author’s tone, which is decidedly immodest—though it might be said in his defense that given his professional success, he has much to be immodest about.","key":"AC","opts":["aggravated","mitigated","exacerbated","leavened","confirmed","contravened"],"expl":"mitigated（减轻）：作者的傲慢语气会削弱不满。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v119-2","title":"Test 119 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v119.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Unlike other rap artists, who often _____ behind the microphone, Drake writes out every word of his rhymes before he performs them.","key":"C","opts":["linger","proselytize","extemporize","fulminate","compromise"],"expl":"extemporize（即兴发挥）：德雷克提前写好歌词。选 C"},{"id":"v119.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The employees' blithe natures were in sharp contrast to the _____ disposition of their manager.","key":"E","opts":["affable","duplicitous","apathetic","lenient","irascible"],"expl":"irascible（易怒的）：员工轻松，经理却脾气暴躁。选 E"},{"id":"v119.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"What is especially (i)_____ about the company's fiscal situation is that everybody knows the grim facts and (ii)_____ the implications, but nobody is willing to take any action to improve matters.","key":"AF","groups":[["scary","unfair","understandable"],["misconstrues","ignores","concedes"]],"expl":"空1 scary（吓人的）；空2 ignores（忽视）。选 AF"},{"id":"v119.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Researchers claim that early mammals evolved a multistep process to synthesize vitamin C in their own bodies but that tens of millions of years ago some primates became so (i)_____ eating fruits rich in this vitamin that making their own became (ii)_____. Their physiology (iii)_____ their behavior. Consequently, their descendants, today's anthropoid primates, cannot make vitamin C.","key":"AEG","groups":[["accustomed to","averse to","inefficient at"],["a challenging task","an unnecessary cost","a practical solution"],["adapted to","interfered with","changed despite"]],"expl":"空1 dependent on fruit（依赖水果）；空2 unnecessary（不必要的）。选 AEG"},{"id":"v119.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Computational psychologists, since they take the operation of a computer as a model, ______ concepts from computer science to explain what the mind is and how it works.","key":"AD","opts":["appropriate","eschew","emulate","borrow","covet","reject"],"expl":"borrow（借用）：计算心理学借用计算机科学的概念。选 AD"},{"id":"v119.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The late nineteenth century saw a shift in the production of African American history writing as works by ______ authors came to be outnumbered by the publications of professional African American academics.","key":"CF","opts":["established","literary","lay","erudite","prominent","avocational"],"expl":"lay（非专业的）：非专业作者减少，专业学者增多。选 CF"},{"id":"v119.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There is a ______ in the author’s writing: the words seem to stand almost in defiance of one another.","key":"BD","opts":["discrepancy","tension","misconception","discord","delusion","controversy"],"expl":"tension（张力）：词语之间互相冲突。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v120-1","title":"Test 120 · Section 1","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v120.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"EI Greco was one of the most fervent of painters, to the extreme of mania, while Velázquez, by contrast, was one of the most _____.","key":"A","opts":["phlegmatic","obstreperous","edifying","grandiloquent","fanciful"],"expl":"phlegmatic（冷静的）：委拉斯开兹显得冷静。选 A"},{"id":"v120.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Over the years, some researchers and educators have (i)_____ the argument for hands-on leaning of science, (ii)_____ that a more straightforward approach—known as direct instruction— has the potential to help students learn science more effectively.","key":"AE","groups":[["challenged","evaluated","refined"],["conceding","maintaining","pretending"]],"expl":"空1 challenged（质疑）；空2 suggesting（暗示）。选 AE"},{"id":"v120.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"An innovative musician, accompanist extraordinaire, and protomodern hipster, Lester Young(1909-1959) remains a (i)_____ in the jazz firmament. Some of the reasons are obvious: although he dressed with conspicuous cool, he chose an artistic trajectory that seemed calculated to (ii)_____ the spotlight—his best work was in the bands of other musicians, such as Billie Holiday and Count Basie, rather than at the front of his own. Moreover, he was shy, subtle, and sensitive— traits not usually associated with great(iii)_____.","key":"BDI","groups":[["bright star","lesser light","permanent fixture"],["shun","intensify","exploit"],["imagination","restraint","celebrity"]],"expl":"空1 major figure（重要人物）；空2 avoid（避开）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v120.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To say that John Adams was forthright was to be ______; friends as well as enemies were likely to characterize his stark honesty and direct manner as blunt and awkward.","key":"BE","opts":["fickle","charitable","facetious","unreasonable","forbearing","capricious"],"expl":"blunt（直截了当的）：亚当斯的直率被视为粗鲁。选 BE"},{"id":"v120.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"After landing on a flower, inexperienced bees show an ______ probing response, but they still must invest time in learning how to exploit flowers of increased complexity efficiently.","key":"EF","opts":["immediate","impressive","inadequate","ineffectual","innate","intuitive"],"expl":"innate（天生的）：蜜蜂天生的探索反应。选 EF"},{"id":"v120.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"At the peak of the stock market’s vertiginous rise, some corporate pension plans became overfunded: their assets _____ their liabilities.","key":"AF","opts":["outstripped","equaled","matched","encompassed","inflated","surpassed"],"expl":"outstripped（超过）：资产超过负债。选 AF"},{"id":"v120.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Wang’s book is the first attempt to define Chinese autobiography as _____ genre, that is, one distinct from other narrative modes of self-representation popular after the fall of the Qing dynasty in 1911.","key":"BD","opts":["an imported","a separate","an influential","a discrete","an archetypal","an consequential"],"expl":"a discrete（独立的）：中国自传是一个独立的体裁。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v120-2","title":"Test 120 · Section 2","group":"Test 111–120","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v120.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"If dark energy is an energy field, it would not be _____: it might once have been stronger or weaker than it is nowand could have affected the universe differently at different times.","key":"C","opts":["boundless","directional","invariant","dynamic","pervasive"],"expl":"invariant（不变的）：暗能量可能随时间变化，故并非不变。选 C"},{"id":"v120.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"George Eliot's novels were calculated to inspire sympathy in the reader for characters from a broad range of social classes, but her design was not (i)_____: Eliot hoped her fiction would have a (ii)_____ effect, spurting readers to show charity for those oppressed by the economic inequalities of her age.","key":"CF","groups":[["always obvious","without complications","exclusively affective"],["pacifying","consoling","galvanizing"]],"expl":"空1 unrealized（未实现的）；空2 mild（温和的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v120.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The Cassini spacecraft initially found the bodies of liquid methane on Saturn's moon Titan to be very (i)_____, a surprising result since the reduced surface tension and viscosity of liquid methane, as compared to water on Earth, should make it (ii)_____ waves.","key":"AD","groups":[["calm","deep","dense"],["easier to excite","more difficult to measure","more likely to distort"]],"expl":"空1 calm（平静的）；空2 generate（产生）。选 AD"},{"id":"v120.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Aiken’s (i)_____ regarding his own intellectual abilities—he has repeatedly attributed his academic success to luck and hard work rather than innate acuity—may have (ii)_____. If he feels he is surrounded by economists more (iii)_____ than he is, he may let their assertions, even the dubious ones, stand without challenge.","key":"ADG","groups":[["modesty","temerity","chagrin"],["led him astray","bolstered his success","embarrassed his admirers"],["brilliant","determined","boastful"]],"expl":"空1 modesty（谦逊）；空2 undermined（削弱）；空3 gifted（有天赋的）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v120.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although streams of solar particles cause beautiful auroras —the northern and southern lights— sometimes their consequences are less _____: their electromagnetic effects, for instance, can overload power grids and damage orbiting satellites.","key":"CE","opts":["spectacular","significant","benign","consequential","innocuous","palpable"],"expl":"significant（重大的）：影响不算重大，却危及电网。选 CE"},{"id":"v120.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The so-called \"sensation novel, popular in mid-nineteenth-century Britain, was dismissed by some as ______ form of fiction, partly because these spine-tingling novels often appeared as serials in cheap, disposable periodicals.","key":"BD","opts":["an engrossing","an ephemeral","a macabre","a transitory","a captivating","a debased"],"expl":"an ephemeral（短暂的）：连载形式使其成为短暂的文学形式。选 BD"},{"id":"v120.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Hamlin Garland has tried to appeal to a wider audience by moving away from the gritty realism of his early writings, which often advanced populist political causes, and toward ______ mainstream fiction.","key":"CD","opts":["demanding","topical","anodyne","toothless","derivative","challenging"],"expl":"anodyne（温和无害的）与 toothless 描述主流小说的平淡。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v121-1","title":"Test 121 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v121.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Woody plant responses to herbivory were always thought to be _____; however, some scientists have reported localized responses to herbivory in certain woody plants.","key":"E","opts":["timely","marginal","unpredictable","adequate","systemic"],"expl":"systemic（系统性的）：原以为木本植物的反应是局部的，后来发现可以是系统性的。选 E"},{"id":"v121.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Confidence in the nation's finances, barely nailed together by international financial institutions a few weeks ago, is still such a (i)_____ structure that the slightest disturbance could set it (ii)_____.","key":"AD","groups":[["ramshackle","labyrinthine","rigid"],["quivering","ablaze","right"]],"expl":"空1 ramshackle（摇摇欲坠的）；空2 quivering（颤抖）。金融信心勉强拼凑，经不起轻微扰动。选 AD"},{"id":"v121.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The antiestablishment comedy of the early 1960s developed in reaction to an age that was more (i)_____, a time when standing on a stage to make fun of a political leader or government official was a (ii)_____ act. In those days, the laughter of the audience was something for politicians to be afraid of, because it signaled a (iii)_____ in the public attitude toward the whole political class. Today, every politician is a target of satire and comedy, and laughter has become a reflexive, tired reaction to situations too depressing to evaluate clearly.","key":"CDH","groups":[["humane","austere","deferential"],["radical","placatory","prophetic"],["developing moderation","profound shift","diminished resolve"]],"expl":"空1 repressive（压制的）；空2 dangerous（危险的）；空3 shift（转变）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v121.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ear is much more ______ than the eye: only the ear can tell a source that oscillates 30 times a second from one that oscillates 60 times a second.","key":"DE","opts":["stable","efficient","durable","discerning","accurate","tenacious"],"expl":"discerning（有辨别力的）：耳朵能分辨细微频率差异。选 DE"},{"id":"v121.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Cash crops require committed, systematic cultivation; rubber tapping, on the other hand, is much more of ______ enterprise: it is largely a matter of stumbling upon a rubber plant that is ready for harvesting.","key":"BF","opts":["a lucrative","a contingent","an arduous","a conventional","a profitable","an uncertain"],"expl":"a contingent（偶然的）：割胶更多靠偶然碰到可采的树。选 BF"},{"id":"v121.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Like its protagonists, who are caught up in a historical moment that ______ the possibility of self-fulfillment, the novel Ready to Burst by Haitian writer Franketienne moves in disorienting circles, never progressing or achieving closure.","key":"CF","opts":["celebrates","downplays","precludes","romanticizes","elevates","frustrates"],"expl":"precludes（排除）：历史境况排除了自我实现的可能。选 CF"},{"id":"v121.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are many contemporary composers who receive coveted commissions, only to see their creations ______ after one performance.","key":"EF","opts":["dismantled","redrafted","plundered","pilloried","discarded","shelved"],"expl":"shelved（搁置）：作品演出一次后即被束之高阁。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v121-2","title":"Test 121 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v121.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"An apparent paradox led the scientists to pursue their present line of research: they were struck by the fact that physical phenomena that are _____ in form can be described by a single mathematical formula.","key":"D","opts":["interchangeable","rudimentary","irreducible","heterogeneous","rare"],"expl":"irreducible（不可还原的）：形式各异的现象却可以用同一公式描述。选 D"},{"id":"v121.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In recent years, the country's farmers have been extremely ______, contributing a major portion of the disturbances and protests against government policies.","key":"C","opts":["discerning","tractable","restive","mercurial","circumspect"],"expl":"restive（不安分的）：农民频繁抗议。选 C"},{"id":"v121.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"In the end, this odd, beautiful movie is emotionally remote and more (i)_____ than satisfying: a (ii)_____ film about catastrophe, made at a time when some of us might prefer an attempt at explanation.","key":"AF","groups":[["suggestive","gratifying","instructive"],["notably insightful","viscerally immediate","coolly enigmatic"]],"expl":"空1 suggestive（暗示性的）；空2 coolly enigmatic（冷漠而神秘的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v121.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Pine stumps have been found in discrete layers in peat deposits throughout western Europe and thus represent brief but distinct episodes of bog colonization by pine. Their occurrence implies conditions on the bog surface suitable for colonization, followed by inhospitable conditions for trees that nevertheless facilitated preservation of stumps. Thus, the (i)_____ of pine stumps can (ii)_____ climate change, by(iii)_____ the inference that bog surfaces had dried sufficiently to allow colonization and then became too wet to support the trees.","key":"CFG","groups":[["loss","resilience","presence"],["proceed undeterred by","vary independently of","function as a proxy for"],["supporting","repudiating","articulating"]],"expl":"空1 occurrence（出现）；空2 illustrate（说明）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v121.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"He is most frugal in matters of business, but in his private life he reveals a streak of ______.","key":"BC","opts":["parsimony","profligacy","immoderation","deceit","dissimulation","indolence"],"expl":"profligacy（挥霍）：私下却有挥霍的一面，与节俭相反。选 BC"},{"id":"v121.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"People may be generally aware that media technologies employ toxic substances but maybe startled by the ______ of the environmental harms involved: humans, animals, vegetation, soil, air, and water are all affected.","key":"EF","opts":["noxiousness","permanence","heterogeneity","amplitude","pervasiveness","ubiquity"],"expl":"pervasiveness（普遍性）：环境危害遍及各处。选 EF"},{"id":"v121.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Atmospheric geoengineering, such as whitening clouds to cool Earth by reflecting more sunlight, is not an alternative to reducing carbon emissions, but it might ______ the beneficial effects of such a reduction.","key":"DF","opts":["anticipate","forestall","engender","reinforce","duplicate","complement"],"expl":"forestall（阻止）：地球工程可能削弱减排的好处。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v122-1","title":"Test 122 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v122.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Paradoxically, altruism may in fact be _____ if it aids only one's own clique.","key":"B","opts":["munificent","counterproductive","self-interested","disproportionate","beneficial"],"expl":"counterproductive（适得其反的）：只帮助自己小圈子的利他行为反而有害。选 B"},{"id":"v122.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Environmental models are increasingly (i)_____ to the regulatory process. Computer modeling narrows the range of uncertainties related to pollution impacts, uncertainties that have (ii)_____ environmental policy making on all levels.","key":"AD","groups":[["central","inimical","peripheral"],["beset","justified","advanced"]],"expl":"空1 central（核心的）；空2 beset（困扰）。选 AD"},{"id":"v122.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"There is a powerful tradition within French writing that has (i)_____ the bounds of conventional morality, (ii)_____ the dictates of Enlightenment reason, and expressed (iii)_____ violence. It is as if the culture that, perhaps more strongly than any other, celebrated reason and geometrical order, also provoked within itself a deep, wild, and willfully primitive reaction, a return of the repressed par excellence.","key":"BFH","groups":[["clarified","challenged","upheld"],["expanded","anticipated","defied"],["a cautious skepticism toward","an abiding fascination with","a visceral distaste for"]],"expl":"空1 transgressed（逾越）；空2 rejected（拒绝）；空3 unrestrained（不受约束的）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v122.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Picasso’s habit of keeping every last scrap of paper was not entirely a good thing: he left so much of it that his own archives can seem to ______ any view of the man.","key":"AE","opts":["corroborate","reflect","elucidate","inspire","confirm","illuminate"],"expl":"他留下的纸片太多，反而让档案难以呈现对此人的清晰看法，。选 AE"},{"id":"v122.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The power of our Sun is ______: more solar energy strikes the Earth’s surface in one hour of each day than the energy used by all human activities in one year.","key":"AE","opts":["prodigious","ominous","auspicious","foreboding","colossal","sufficient"],"expl":"prodigious（惊人的）与 colossal 描述太阳能量之巨大。选 AE"},{"id":"v122.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author takes a decidedly ______ approach to fiction, ensuring that any assumptions a reader might bring to his stories will be subject to challenge and disruption.","key":"DE","opts":["controversial","nostalgic","unpolished","unorthodox","experimental","wistful"],"expl":"unorthodox（非传统的）：作者的写作手法颠覆读者预期。选 DE"},{"id":"v122.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In a production process that is complex and often unpredictable, roles that start out discretely defined may become quite ______.","key":"CD","opts":["unambiguous","untenable","fluid","mutable","explicit","perfunctory"],"expl":"fluid（流动的）：生产中角色边界可能变得模糊。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v122-2","title":"Test 122 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v122.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Action cinema has a reputation for giving spectators all action and no plot, and that reputation for narrative _____ seems to have gained further traction with the increasingly ubiquitous use of digital effects.","key":"A","opts":["paucity","homogeneity","diffuseness","predictability","convolution"],"expl":"paucity（匮乏）：动作片的叙事被认为贫乏。选 A"},{"id":"v122.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Ethical theorists often assume that the verb \"ought\" means roughly \"has an obligation.” This assumption, however, is (i)_____ the (ii)_____ of \"ought\" sentences in English: the word is used in too many ways to admit a single definition.","key":"AD","groups":[["belied by","predicated on","consequential for"],["diversity","importance","conspicuousness"]],"expl":"空1 belied by（被……推翻）；空2 diversity（多样性）。选 AD"},{"id":"v122.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Literary salons and coffeehouses (i)_____ the class-based systems of social hierarchies prevalent at the time. Meritocratic appreciation of wit and brilliance, wherever it might issue, replaced (ii)_____ to established power.","key":"BE","groups":[["reaffirmed","broke down","anticipated"],["indifef rence","deference","affronts"]],"expl":"空1 broke down（打破）；空2 deference（敬重）。选 BE"},{"id":"v122.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"One of the great misconceptions regarding Earth is that it is (i)_____. This is true only if your sense of connection depends on large chunks of physical matter moving from place to place. The dust and rocks that rain down from space are indeed (ii)_____, even if some of the larger rocks are occasionally a (iii)_____. Matter trickles in, trickles out. But matter is not everything: an unending spate of pure luminous energy pours down on Earth in a 170,000-trillion-watt torrent.","key":"BDH","groups":[["fragile","isolated","fixed"],["negligible","terrifying","fascinating"],["source of contention","cause for concern","boon to researchers"]],"expl":"地球并非物质上的“空”，尘埃和岩石不断流入流出，但真正的联系来自物质以外的东西。选 BDH"},{"id":"v122.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Earth may be considered a more ______ version of the other terrestrial planets:because Earth has developed and maintained plate tectonics over eons, its surface, unlike the other planets’ surfaces, has continued to change.","key":"CF","opts":["treacherous","rugged","unsettled","weathered","intricate","inconstant"],"expl":"unsettled（不稳定的）：地球表面因板块运动持续变化。选 CF"},{"id":"v122.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although she is widely portrayed as being rather ______, Carson’s letters to publishers reveal her complete confidence in her skills as a writer and naturalist along with her willingness to promote herself and her abilities.","key":"AB","opts":["shy","diffident","pedantic","loquacious","capricious","whimsical"],"expl":"diffident（腼腆的）与 shy 描述卡森的形象，但她实际很自信。选 AB"},{"id":"v122.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Some researchers argue that archaeological evidence is too ______: depending on the background theory archaeologists bring to bear, they may interpret the significance of the unearthed artifacts as evidence very differently.","key":"CE","opts":["incomplete","inaccessible","indeterminate","controversial","uncertain","fragmentary"],"expl":"indeterminate（不确定的）：考古证据受理论影响，难以确定意义。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v123-1","title":"Test 123 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v123.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"There is a rather _____ reason for astronomers’ sudden interest in comets: most other bodies in the solar system have been explored already.","key":"B","opts":["pedantic","prosaic","controversial","untenable","mysterious"],"expl":"prosaic（平淡无奇的）：彗星研究兴趣的原因很平凡。选 B"},{"id":"v123.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Insects are often (i)_____ as the world's most versatile and (ii)_____ flying machines. Yet they shouldn't even be able to get off the ground, at least not according to a straightforward interpretation of the laws of aerodynamics.","key":"CF","groups":[["ridiculed","overlooked","touted"],["contrived","atypical","maneuverable"]],"expl":"空1 touted（吹捧）；空2 maneuverable（灵活机动的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v123.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Predators try to (i)_____ their ultimate energy intake by (ii)_____ the effort they expend searching for and handling prey relative to the energy the prey provides. Thus, a particular kind of prey would be (iii)_____ to a predator's diet only if it is worth the predator's time and energy—that is, if it increases the animal's overall energy profit during foraging.","key":"CFH","groups":[["stabilize","gauge","maximize"],["deferring","intensifying","reducing"],["deleterious","added","unique"]],"expl":"空1 maximize（最大化）；空2 weighing（权衡）；空3 worth including（值得纳入）。选 CFH"},{"id":"v123.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The term \"borderline, coined in the 1930s to describe a psychiatric condition straddling the boundary between two other diagnoses, remained ______ until John Gunderson enumerated six identifying characteristics of the condition in the 1970s.","key":"AF","opts":["equivocal","stigmatized","impracticable","incontrovertible","anomalous","nebulous"],"expl":"nebulous（模糊的）与 stigmatized 描述“边缘型”概念的模糊状态。选 AF"},{"id":"v123.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In this otherwise ______ study, the internal tensions resulting from the increasing integration of the United States with the world economy are simply mentioned rather than analyzed.","key":"BD","opts":["tedious","thorough","biased","exhaustive","superficial","shallow"],"expl":"superficial（肤浅的）：研究只是提及而未分析。选 BD"},{"id":"v123.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although Ralph Ellison's Invisible Man has been heavily praised for over 50 years by a wide variety of critics and scholars, there have been ______ from the outset concerning the novel’s political vision.","key":"BE","opts":["rebukes","doubts","conjectures","speculations","reservations","accolades"],"expl":"reservations（保留意见）：自始就有对政治视角的保留。选 BE"},{"id":"v123.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Egler's prediction in 1947 that the introduction of mangrove trees to the Hawaiian lslands would cause sweeping ecological change was ______: extensive mangrove forests have come to displace many preexisting plant communities.","key":"CD","opts":["accurate","premature","prescient","foresighted","optimistic","precipitate"],"expl":"prescient（有先见之明的）：预测被证实。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v123-2","title":"Test 123 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v123.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Concerned about the growing tendency of universities to sometimes reward celebrity more generously than specialized expertise, many academics have deplored the search for _____ to which that practice leads.","key":"D","opts":["approbation","collegiality","erudition","renown","prowess"],"expl":"renown（声望）：大学重视名望而非专业知识。选 D"},{"id":"v123.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"While Femández-Armesto has amply documented the commercial, migratory, scientific, or religious motives of explorers throughout history, it is often harder to _____ the motives of modern explorers.","key":"B","opts":["generate","penetrate","extinguish","utilize","criticize"],"expl":"penetrate（洞悉）：现代探险者的动机难以探查。选 B"},{"id":"v123.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"She was skeptical about the (i)_____ reviews of the latest production of the play, feeling that the production she had seen years earlier was (ii)_____, and that any successive attempts must undoubtedly fall short.","key":"BD","groups":[["lackluster","rhapsodic","pithy"],["nothing less than definitive","generally adequate","surprisingly conservative"]],"expl":"空1 rhapsodic（狂热赞美的）；空2 nothing less than definitive（堪称权威）。选 BD"},{"id":"v123.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although Sapir and Whorf’s notion that different languages may impart different cognitive skills met with (i)______ early on, they had little evidence to support their claim. By the 1970s many scientists had become (ii)______ their hypothesis, and it was largely (iii)______ as a new set of theories claiming that language and thought are universal came to dominate the field.","key":"AEI","groups":[["skepticism","excitement","controversy"],["convinced of","disenchanted with","inured to"],["revived","corroborated","abandoned"]],"expl":"空1 skepticism（怀疑）；空2 skeptical of（怀疑）；空3 dismissed（被摒弃）。选 AEI"},{"id":"v123.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The archaeological record suggests that written literature is a ______ the administrative state: invented primarily to keep tax records and memorialize royal decrees, writing eventually got co-opted into preserving people’s myths and legends.","key":"CF","opts":["prerequisite for","glorification of","progeny of","menace to","celebration of","byproduct of"],"expl":"byproduct of（副产品）：书写是行政国家的副产品。选 CF"},{"id":"v123.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In her literary criticism, eighteenth-century writer Elizabeth Montagu was ______, not only crossing swords with the illustrious Voltaire but also challenging a host of well-known English male commentators on Shakespeare, including Samuel Johnson.","key":"AD","opts":["intrepid","original","cautious","valiant","flippant","wary"],"expl":"intrepid（无畏的）：她敢于挑战名人。选 AD"},{"id":"v123.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As an aspiring politician, Gurstein aims to achieve ______ tone in her public addresses without falling into aristocratic overtones.","key":"BE","opts":["a polemical","an elevated","an argumentative","an expressive","a lofty","a dispassionate"],"expl":"an elevated（高雅的）：既要高雅，又不流于贵族腔。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v124-1","title":"Test 124 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v124.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The preliminary analysis being on the whole, reassuring, its confirmation would _____ concerns about the dangers of the project.","key":"D","opts":["explain","rationalize","reflect","assuage","obscure"],"expl":"assuage（缓解）：初步分析令人安心，可以缓解担忧。选 D"},{"id":"v124.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The new exhibition of Sophie Calle's work in San Francisco is (i)_____ but still (ii)_____: given Calle's international stardom and aesthetic reach, the French artist is deserving of a full-career retrospective in America.","key":"CE","groups":[["politically charged","quite extensive","somewhat selective"],["whimsical","insufficient","overwhelming"]],"expl":"空1 politically charged（政治意味浓厚的）；空2 insufficient（不够的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v124.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Elephants are known to use a wide variety of calls, many of them infrasonic (below the level of human hearing), in coordinating group behavior. The infrasonic calls usually have a component that is (i)______, but these higher frequency aspects of the calls (ii)______ very quickly with distance, so that in the wild, human observers are often (iii)______ sudden coordinated movements of large groups of elephants when no signal was apparent to the observer.","key":"CDI","groups":[["somewhat muted","distinctly sonorous","humanly audible"],["attenuate","repeat","differentiate"],["alert to","ignorant of","astonished by"]],"expl":"空1 audible（可听见的）；空2 attenuate（减弱）；空3 unable to hear（听不见）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v124.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Smi’s analysis of climate change is even more ______ than that supplied by most well-informed writers, and thus deserves serious consideration.","key":"AC","opts":["nuanced","unoriginal","complex","derivative","partisan","compelling"],"expl":"nuanced（细致的）与 complex 描述分析比一般作者更细致。选 AC"},{"id":"v124.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While it is true that the tennis star has been defeated in recent years by some relatively obscure players, counting her out of any tournament, particularly if she is healthy, seems ______.","key":"AB","opts":["foolhardy","imprudent","unnecessary","audacious","alarming","gratuitous"],"expl":"foolhardy（鲁莽的）：认定她出局显得草率。选 AB"},{"id":"v124.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The artist’s apparently casual, improvisatory pictures are not the ______ renditions they may seem: her pictures are, in fact, the result of a highly disciplined style.","key":"CE","opts":["calculated","rigorous","offhand","precise","extempore","defiant"],"expl":"offhand（随意的）与 calculated 对立：画面看似随意，实则精心计算。选 CE"},{"id":"v124.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Party leaders hoped to find a single compelling issue that would ______ party members across the country, prompting them to turn out in significant numbers on election day.","key":"BD","opts":["satisfy","rouse","intrigue","animate","hamper","impede"],"expl":"rouse（唤起）：政党希望找到能激发党员的议题。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v124-2","title":"Test 124 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v124.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because they were traditionally _____, Jain monks in sixteenth-century India particularly valued special dispensations from the royal court granting them freedom of movement.","key":"D","opts":["erudite","ascetic","apolitical","peripatetic","solitary"],"expl":"ascetic（苦修的）：耆那教僧侣以苦修闻名。选 D"},{"id":"v124.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Though extremely secretive about her own plans, she allowed her associates no such (i)_____ and was constantly (ii)_____ information about what they intended to do next.","key":"AF","groups":[["reticence","introspection","mendaciousness"],["distorting","ignoring","requesting"]],"expl":"空1 reticence（保密）；空2 requesting（索要）。选 AF"},{"id":"v124.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Svitlana Mayboroda's recent work, though (i)_____ pure mathematics, is already being (ii)_____ by physicists, distinguishing it from most mathematical advances, for which the development of any practical use is long delayed.","key":"CD","groups":[["largely irrelevant to","familiar to scholars of","in the realm of"],["applied","overlooked","questioned"]],"expl":"空1 largely irrelevant to（与……基本无关）；空2 applied（应用）。选 CD"},{"id":"v124.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The author of this (i)______ memoir is notable for an unmitigated (ii)______ that is matched only by an utter lack of self-awareness. Although that combination of personality traits is not uncommon, it is rare for a book that is so transparently an exercise in (iii)______ to have the exact opposite of its intended effect.","key":"BDI","groups":[["self-critical","self-serving","self-effacing"],["self-regard","self-abnegation","self-consciousness"],["self-examination","self-incrimination","self-aggrandizement"]],"expl":"空1 self-serving（自利的）；空2 self-regard（自我中心）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v124.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Singer Nina Simone in many ways defied categorization, with her artist ______ evident in her early pieces that drew on disparate musical genres, including musical theater, blues, and jazz standards.","key":"CE","opts":["inventiveness","diligence","hybridity","assiduity","eclecticism","acumen"],"expl":"eclecticism（兼收并蓄）：歌手的艺术风格兼收并蓄。选 CE"},{"id":"v124.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In the past, the exploitation of various categories of natural resources was done ______, but because of the hugely expanded scale of today's economy, exploitation of all the resources in many countries now occurs simultaneously.","key":"EF","opts":["fruitfully","rapidly","hastily","benignly","sequentially","successively"],"expl":"sequentially（依次地）：过去是依次开采，如今同时进行。选 EF"},{"id":"v124.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though mathematics is ______, like language, it has its roots in the mud of everyday embodied experience; one such root is counting.","key":"CD","opts":["essential","indispensable","abstract","theoretical","prescriptive","functional"],"expl":"abstract（抽象的）：数学虽抽象，根源却在日常经验中。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v125-1","title":"Test 125 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v125.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because the instructions they have been given are exhaustive and unequivocal, employees are now working without _____.","key":"B","opts":["recompense","discretion","monotony","certitude","limitation"],"expl":"discretion（自由裁量权）：指示过于详尽，员工无自由裁量空间。选 B"},{"id":"v125.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"In aging bees, cognitive decline is (i)_____ under certain social conditions--for example, when the colony divides by swarming or when foragers or young nurse bees are removed from the colony. Each of these circumstances causes older bees to become cognitively (ii)_____, while juvenile bees, by contrast, exhibit a faster age-related cognitive decline.","key":"BE","groups":[["common","reversed","dangerous"],["overactive","younger","sluggish"]],"expl":"空1 reversed（逆转）；空2 vulnerable（脆弱的）。选 BE"},{"id":"v125.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Among the rising generation of concert pianists, a (i)______ approach to performance is sadly (ii)______. Too often, young pianists have acquired such an approach from their teachers, the very people who should be pointing out that the flailing arm, the contorted brow, the bulging eye, and the balletic upper torso are (iii)______ work in a business best devoted to doing the most with the least.","key":"AFG","groups":[["histrionic","stately","languid"],["passé","endangered","pervasive"],["extraneous","respected","stylish"]],"expl":"空1 showy（炫耀的）；空2 encouraged（受到鼓励）；空3 wasted（浪费）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v125.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ______ diction of the short Somali poetry form known as balwo was well suited for political purposes: invective could easily be hidden in an apparent love poem.","key":"AB","opts":["cryptic","enigmatic","romantic","iconoclastic","irreverent","nuanced"],"expl":"空缺处为“可以把攻击藏在情诗中的措辞”，cryptic（隐晦的）与 enigmatic 最贴切。选 AB"},{"id":"v125.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientists studying the stresses and strains accumulated in the Earth's crust have found that it is surprisingly easy to ______ earthquakes, even in regions that historically have been seismically silent or nearly so.","key":"BD","opts":["detect","trigger","ignore","cause","disregard","predict"],"expl":"trigger（引发）：压力积累可能引发地震。选 BD"},{"id":"v125.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The high seriousness of St. Aubyn’s novel is not at all superficial; in fact, it is ______ the novel’s ferociously comic vision.","key":"CF","opts":["redolent of","reminiscent of","intrinsic to","inimical to","antagonistic to","inextricable from"],"expl":"inextricable from（与……不可分割）：严肃与喜剧视野紧密相连。选 CF"},{"id":"v125.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Surprisingly, although the textbooks are filled with pages of vocabulary and unnecessary detail, their treatment of some fundamentally important concepts is ______.","key":"BD","opts":["prolix","piecemeal","verbose","fragmentary","abstruse","succinct"],"expl":"piecemeal（零碎的）与 fragmentary 描述教材对关键概念的处理。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v125-2","title":"Test 125 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v125.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Contrary to what might be expected, having numerous relationships is not necessarily a _____ loneliness since loneliness is determined by the way people experience relationships subjectively.","key":"B","opts":["measure of","bulwark against","catalyst for","consequence of","substitute for"],"expl":"bulwark against（对……的屏障）：众多关系不必然能防止孤独。选 B"},{"id":"v125.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"During Roosevelt's first meeting with President Harrison, Harrison seemed less _____ than usual: having just returned from a salubrious cruise down the Potomac, his characteristic sour silence was replaced by a ruddy, clear-eyed demeanor.","key":"D","opts":["propitiatory","sanguine","pensive","dyspeptic","belligerent"],"expl":"哈里森平时阴郁沉默，这次却神采奕奕，因此他显得乐观（sanguine），与平时的 dyspeptic 形成对比。选 D"},{"id":"v125.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Whereas in the early nineteenth century phrenologists had seen every part of the brain surface as the seat of a specific intellectual or moral faculty, the 1830s and 1840s saw a (i)_____ of this belief, to such an extent that the brain came to be seen as (ii)_____.","key":"CE","groups":[["popularization","vindication","reexamination"],["hierarchical","undifferentiated","decipherable"]],"expl":"空1 reexamination（重新检验）；空2 undifferentiated（无差别的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v125.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"One of the problems with recent books that perpetuate the view of Jane Austen as moral tutor, a sort of Miss Manners for the ages, is that they understand manners as (i)______, as near-universal and timeless behavioral ideals or, worse still, a set of rules to be followed. It is crucial, however, to (ii)______. In other words, one needs to resist (iii)______ generic “manners” with more linguistically and historically precise designations, no least because Austen herself distinguishes.","key":"CEH","groups":[["trivial","necessary","monolithic"],["deemphasize historical","difef rentiate various","apply moral precepts"],["comparing","conflating","augmenting"]],"expl":"空1 universal（普适的）；空2 contextualize（语境化）；空3 generic（泛化的）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v125.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A telescope orbiting in space, above the unruly atmosphere, is able to detect ultraviolet and infrared emissions that are blocked by Earth’s atmosphere and thus ______ to astronomers on the ground.","key":"BF","opts":["unremarkable","indiscernible","exasperating","undecipherable","inconclusive","imperceptible"],"expl":"imperceptible（难以察觉的）：这些辐射被大气阻挡，地面望远镜难以察觉。选 BF"},{"id":"v125.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Walking appears simple, yet every step forward is a ______ act: each step is essentially a fall that one must catch by swinging one’s leg forward so that one’s foot lands on the floor just in time.","key":"DF","opts":["complicated","skillful","hasty","risky","deliberate","precarious"],"expl":"precarious（岌岌可危的）：每一步都是一次不稳的失衡。选 DF"},{"id":"v125.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scholars of the civil rights movement have often characterized it as springing from social, political, and economic structures ______ the South, thus overlooking the tradition of civil rights activism in other regions of the country.","key":"DE","opts":["originating in","imposed on","perpetuated by","unique to","characteristic of","detrimental to"],"expl":"unique to（为……所独有）：应该指出南方并非唯一来源。选 DE"}]},{"id":"v126-1","title":"Test 126 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v126.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In contemporary rhetoric, the environment has been ______; we now speak of \"natural resources\" rather than \"nature,\" as though the natural world were something to be sold, bought, or discarded.","key":"E","opts":["presaged","personified","apotheosized","depoliticized","commodified"],"expl":"commodified（商品化的）：环境被视为可买卖之物。选 E"},{"id":"v126.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"(i)_____ Kafka's halfhearted instruction that his unprinted manuscripts be destroyed after his death, his friend Max Brod set about publishing them immediately following the author's demise and thus became the (ii)_____ Kafka's belated fame.","key":"AF","groups":[["Ignoring","Embracing","Questioning"],["arbiter of","apologist for","architect of"]],"expl":"空1 Ignoring（无视）；空2 architect of（缔造者）。选 AF"},{"id":"v126.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Some scientists speculate that changes in atmospheric methane were responsible for some abrupt global warming events in the past such as the one at the end of the geologic period known as the Younger Dryas. There is good evidence that large quantities of methane have been released quickly in the past through natural processes; however, methane is a relatively (i)______ molecule in the atmosphere and thus (ii)______ through chemical reactions with other compounds. The effect of even a large increase would therefore be (iii)______.","key":"BFH","groups":[["important","unstable","abundant"],["not easily altered","eventually regenerated","fairly quickly destroyed"],["accelerated","ephemeral","catastrophic"]],"expl":"空1 abundant（丰富的）；空2 extremely（极其）；空3 short-lived（短暂的）。选 BFH"},{"id":"v126.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The overall persuasiveness of the literary critic’s analysis was occasionally marred by ______ generalizations that served only to distract attentive readers from the intended point.","key":"AD","opts":["questionable","vacuous","broad","dubious","incisive","trenchant"],"expl":"vacuous（空洞的）与 broad 描述过于宽泛的概括。选 AD"},{"id":"v126.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is not exactly socialism that has ______ so much of the country's economic life with cumbersome regulations but a meddlesome governmental culture that has been in place for centuries.","key":"EF","opts":["imbued","betrayed","animated","energized","stifled","throttled"],"expl":"stifled（窒息、扼制）：繁琐监管压制了经济生活。选 EF"},{"id":"v126.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many working physicists believe that general relativity, while ______, is itself only one aspect of a more comprehensive theory that embraces all the forces of nature.","key":"DE","opts":["abstruse","complete","obscure","correct","accurate","fascinating"],"expl":"相对论虽然深奥（abstruse），却只是更全面理论的一部分。选 DE"},{"id":"v126.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Globalization has made ethnic entrepreneurship resilient in postindustrial economies: well represented in the small business sector in the United States, ethnic entrepreneurship has been ______ by the volatile tides of international migration.","key":"DF","opts":["sustained","perpetuated","diversified","vitiated","overwhelmed","attenuated"],"expl":"sustained（维持）：族裔创业被国际移民潮冲击却依然维持。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v126-2","title":"Test 126 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v126.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In terms of energy consumption, the brain is quite _______: we humans, for example, have brains that account for slightly more than 2 percent of our biomass, but our brains burn up more than 15 percent of our basal metabolic energy.","key":"C","opts":["efficient","typical","ravenous","unpredictable","inscrutable"],"expl":"ravenous（贪婪的）：大脑耗能极高。选 C"},{"id":"v126.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the committee’s pronouncements are (i)______, consultation with the committee is (ii)______ and in some cases is even mandatory.","key":"AE","groups":[["purely advisory","legally binding","rarely controversial"],["compulsory","routine","optional"]],"expl":"空1 purely advisory（纯属建议性质）；空2 compulsory（强制的）。选 AE"},{"id":"v126.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"With respect to environmental issues, most legal scholarship tends to envision politics as the pursuit of already fixed interests, a view that (i)______ the ability of political communities to (ii)______ their values and their interests through the process of democratic deliberation.","key":"CE","groups":[["leverages","overstates","ignores"],["mask","transform","defend"]],"expl":"空1 ignores（忽视）；空2 transform（转变）。选 CE"},{"id":"v126.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although the book’s vast notes section (i)______ the impressive breadth of Brzezinski’s research, his (ii)______ seems to fill in the gaps in what his absorption in memoirs and interviews enabled him to learn about the events leading up to the launch of Sputnik, leading him to make (iii)______ claims in some of his descriptions.","key":"BFG","groups":[["foreshadows","documents","subverts"],["scholarship","foreknowledge","imagination"],["fanciful","vehement","cautious"]],"expl":"空1 documents（记录了）；空2 scholarship（学术研究）；空3 unsubstantiated（缺乏依据的）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v126.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Nowadays helium is ______ substance, but just a few generations ago it was an astrophysical conundrum: its spectral lines had been seen in the Sun, but it had never been detected in any other way.","key":"BD","opts":["a volatile","a mundane","a voluminous","a commonplace","an abundant","an economical"],"expl":"commonplace（司空见惯的）：氦如今已很普通。选 BD"},{"id":"v126.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although the establishment of risk exposure limits and other safety regulations is generally presented as ______, risk-related decisions often contain value-based judgments regarding which risks to accept.","key":"AB","opts":["disinterested","impartial","necessary","prudent","preventative","sensible"],"expl":"impartial（公正的）：风险标准常被认为是客观的，但其中含有价值判断。选 AB"},{"id":"v126.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"According to A. Elizabeth Arnold, fungi growing inside plant tissue are not causing disease and may in fact protect the plant: leaves of wild cacao trees with abundant internal fungi, for example, ______ colonization by disease-causing fungi.","key":"AE","opts":["resist","accelerate","offset","expedite","withstand","interrupt"],"expl":"withstand（抵御）：内生真菌帮助可可树抵抗病原真菌。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v127-1","title":"Test 127 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v127.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The publication of books in the vernacular in fifteenth-century England laid the foundation for a literary language that survives relatively unchanged and thus gives English literature a greater ______ than many other national literatures.","key":"E","opts":["sophistication","diversity","specificity","flair","continuity"],"expl":"continuity（延续性）：语言稳定延续，使英国文学有连续性。选 E"},{"id":"v127.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"At first glance, each of the stories in the anthology seemed (i)______; upon closer inspection of their protagonists, implied morals, and fantasy elements, however, subtle similarities among the stories emerged to (ii)______ this initial observation.","key":"CD","groups":[["compelling","implausible","idiosyncratic"],["impugn","bolster","explain"]],"expl":"空1 idiosyncratic（各具特色的）；空2 impugn（质疑）。选 CD"},{"id":"v127.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"If companies were taxed based on the amount of their atmospheric emissions of pollutants, they could make their own decisions about how to alter their operations. Firms could compare the cost of paying taxes with the cost of preventing the emissions in the first place and would, in most cases, do a bit of both. Firms that can reduce pollution (i)______ would reduce it quite (ii)______, while those that can only do so at great cost would (iii)______.","key":"AFG","groups":[["cheaply","materially","rapidly"],["gradually","prudently","substantially"],["curtail less","gain advantages","anticipate losses"]],"expl":"空1 cheaply（便宜地）；空2 substantially（大幅地）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v127.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For a long time, painter V. S. Gaitonde's reputation, which barely existed in the West, ______ in his native India, partly because his abstract style was viewed as culturally irrelevant, even un- Indian.","key":"AC","opts":["flagged","endured","languished","burgeoned","persevered","metamorphosed"],"expl":"languished（默默无闻、停滞）：他在西方几乎无名，在印度也长期受冷落。选 AC"},{"id":"v127.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Millville has its share of suburban eyesores—cement-block strip malls, rows of fast-food restaurants, and ______ split-level homes marching up hillsides denuded of trees.","key":"DE","opts":["magnificent","superlative","abysmal","banal","lackluster","diminutive"],"expl":"banal（平庸的）：郊区住宅千篇一律。选 DE"},{"id":"v127.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Her poetry was marked by a tension between modernity and traditionalism: she adhered to classical modes of expression while deriving inspiration from ______ social themes.","key":"BD","opts":["difficult","contemporary","challenging","topical","conventional","controversial"],"expl":"topical（时事的）：她借用当下的社会主题。选 BD"},{"id":"v127.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Tycho Brahe had assigned Kepler the task of deriving parameters for the model of Mars, a particularly ______ problem, which had stymied others because the large eccentricity of Mars exposed the inadequacies of the model itself.","key":"BC","opts":["novel","recalcitrant","intractable","crucial","profound","treacherous"],"expl":"recalcitrant（难以驾驭的）与 intractable 描述火星模型难题。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v127-2","title":"Test 127 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v127.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"With his winning personality and ingratiating manner, Arturo found it a simple matter to ______ the deed to the property for himself, though its original holder initially seemed impervious to persuasion.","key":"A","opts":["inveigle","confiscate","impound","annul","abrogate"],"expl":"inveigle（诱骗）：阿图罗凭魅力诱使对方交出房产。选 A"},{"id":"v127.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The subjects who were engaged in more difficult tasks ______ deterioration in their performance over time, and therefore the need to concentrate apparently enhances long-term efficiency.","key":"D","opts":["elicited","anticipated","noticed","displayed","evaded"],"expl":"displayed（表现出）：难度高的任务中出现表现下降。选 D"},{"id":"v127.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite its (i)______, reductionism as a research strategy in biology has proved (ii)______: the ascendancy of the life sciences over the past fifty years attests to the power of the reductionist approach.","key":"CD","groups":[["popularity","attestation","deficiencies"],["successful","controversial","uncommon"]],"expl":"空1 deficiencies（缺陷）；空2 successful（成功的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v127.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Materials expand and contract with temperature changes. This general concept has been exploited for thousands of years, for instance, to ensure tight rivets in blacksmithing by shrink-fitting. For precision instruments, however, (i)______ materials are truly (ii)______: hence the importance of Invar, an alloy notable for its (iii)_____ expansion and contraction over a range of temperatures.","key":"AEG","groups":[["dimensionally stable","mechanically durable","thermally conductive"],["unreliable","paramount","economical"],["resistance to","alternation between","toughness from"]],"expl":"空1 precision（精确）；空2 unsuitable（不适用）；空3 negligible（微不足道的）。选 AEG"},{"id":"v127.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In a cross-cultural study of four hundred pre-industrial societies, social scientist James W. Prescott found that in societies in which little affection is shown to infants, there is a _____ of institutions devoted to organized religion and social hierarchy.","key":"C","opts":["miscellany","deluge","preponderance","plethora shortage","majority"],"expl":"preponderance（优势、多数）：这类社会中宗教等制度占据多数。选 C"},{"id":"v127.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A simplistic _____ of idealism is to assert that because physical reality appears solid and “real\" to the senses, no other substances exist.","key":"AE","opts":["refutation","censure","antithesis","equivocation","rebuttal","summary"],"expl":"refutation（驳斥）：简单的理想主义否定实体存在，是错误的反驳。选 AE"},{"id":"v127.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Though the CEO was not in accordance with the board’s decision to reward employees with a larger than expected annual bonus, she was hardly one to _____ workers their compensation.","key":"BC","opts":["allow","begrudge","deny","indulge","grant","entrust"],"expl":"begrudge（吝惜）：CEO 不会吝啬地不给员工报酬。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v128-1","title":"Test 128 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v128.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Once the disk of material around a star is gas-depleted, dust is removed efficiently by the stellar radiation field and wind; any observed dust in a gas-depleted disk must, therefore, have been produced ______.","key":"C","opts":["gradually","rapidly","recently","vestigially","intermittently"],"expl":"recently（近期）：灰尘必定是近期产生的。选 C"},{"id":"v128.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Business leaders who prefer centralized, pyramidal managerial structures to diversity and competition tend to (i)______ dissent in the decision-making process. But this insistence on (ii)______ can be dangerous in that it deprives decision makers of a full range of alternatives.","key":"BE","groups":[["foster","deprecate","overrate"],["spontaneity","unanimity","ambiguity"]],"expl":"空1 deprecate（贬低）；空2 unanimity（一致）。选 BE"},{"id":"v128.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The fantastic conceit of the film’s plot is that global warming (i)______ global freezing. After a chunk of Antarctic ice the size of Rhode Island suddenly melts, most of what follows—an instant ice age, for example—is impossible as science but not as metaphor. The data from the Greenland ice sheet show that, over the past hundred thousand years, temperatures have often (ii)______— so often that it is our own relatively static experience of climate that should now be seen as (iii)______.","key":"CDH","groups":[["succeeds","inhibits","produces"],["swung wildly","changed gradually","seemed unvarying"],["humdrum","exceptional","authentic"]],"expl":"空1 is the mirror of（与……相反）；空2 fluctuated（波动）；空3 abrupt（突然的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v128.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While the kitchen may be free of the toxins polluting the outdoors, certain cooking implements, when heated at high temperatures, can release _____ vapors.","key":"BF","opts":["rancid","noxious","evanescent","targeted","unorthodox","dangerous"],"expl":"noxious（有害的）：烹调器具受热后可能释放有毒气体。选 BF"},{"id":"v128.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"To any observer, ancient or _____, the night sky appears as a hemisphere resting on the horizon.","key":"CE","opts":["antiquated","perceptive","modern","astute","contemporary","archaic"],"expl":"modern（现代的）：古今观察者都会看到同样的天空。选 CE"},{"id":"v128.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Anthropologists contend that the ancient Mesopotamians switched from grain production to barley after excessive irrigation and salt accumulation made the soil _____ grains.","key":"BC","opts":["indifferent to","inhospitable to","unsuitable for","acrimonious to","benignant to","inured to"],"expl":"inhospitable to（不适合）：土壤不再适合种植谷物。选 BC"},{"id":"v128.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Researchers interested in the nature versus nurture debate use identical twins who were separated at birth to explore which personality characteristics are _____ and which arise through experience.","key":"DF","opts":["intractable","nascent","erudite","innate","predilection","inborn"],"expl":"innate（天生的）与 inborn 对比经验形成的性格特征。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v128-2","title":"Test 128 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v128.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Heresy and schism are not restricted to the theologians: science also has its share of fields that are ______ sectarianism.","key":"B","opts":["resistant to","riven by","unified by","buttressed by","free of"],"expl":"riven by（被……撕裂）：科学领域也存在派系纷争。选 B"},{"id":"v128.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Icelanders sometimes claim that everyone in Iceland is a writer. Sure, it’s (i)______ and as such is out of character for a literary tradition long characterized by (ii)______. Still, approximately a thousand books are published each year in Iceland for a population of about 290, 000: one book per 290 persons.","key":"AD","groups":[["hyperbole","sarcasm","clarification"],["understatement","intensity","diversity"]],"expl":"空1 hyperbole（夸张）；空2 understatement（轻描淡写）。选 AD"},{"id":"v128.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"As an essayist, Reed is an equal-opportunity combatant who pulls no punches. One strength in his approach is that this (i)______ can be disarmingly refreshing. On the downside, however, Reed sometimes surrenders too quickly to his more (ii)______ impulses.","key":"CD","groups":[["coy self-deprecation","colloquial informality","aggressive frankness"],["polemical","ingratiating","analytical"]],"expl":"空1 aggressive frankness（咄咄逼人的坦率）；空2 polemical（论战式的）。选 CD"},{"id":"v128.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Describing cosmopolitanism and provincialism as (i)______ concepts misses part of their relationship. They are actually (ii)______, both in the strictly semiotic sense that the idea of cosmopolitanism is (iii)______ unless we can oppose it to something like provincialism and in a more practical sense: much of cosmopolitanism involves recombining elements of provincial cultures.","key":"BFG","groups":[["empirical","antithetical","evolving"],["entirely abstract","largely interchangeable","mutually constitutive"],["meaningless","autonomous","transparent"]],"expl":"空1 empirical（经验性的）；空2 relational（相互关联的）；空3 meaningless（无意义的）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v128.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The eccentric Canadian Prime Minister, Mackenzie King, often used stances to contact his dead pet dog for advice; despite this _____ behavior, the public had so much confidence in his ability as a leader that he was in power for 22 years.","key":"AD","opts":["capricious","lackluster","poised","unconventional","repulsive","decorous"],"expl":"unconventional（非传统的）：他的行为很不寻常，却仍获得信任。选 AD"},{"id":"v128.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The circulation of the blood makes human adaptability to the _____ conditions of life, such as fluctuating atmospheric pressure, level of physical activity, and diet, possible.","key":"BF","opts":["inveterate","dynamic","timorous","cowed","turgid","oscillating"],"expl":"dynamic（动态的）：血液循环使人能适应多变的环境。选 BF"},{"id":"v128.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A particular bacterium that has never encountered a particular virus will usually succumb to it, a _____ that may, surprisingly, be beneficial to the colony in which the bacterium lives.","key":"AC","opts":["susceptibility","theory","characteristic","juxtaposition","collision","hypothesis"],"expl":"susceptibility（易感性）：细菌对病毒的易感性可能对群落有益。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v129-1","title":"Test 129 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v129.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The results of the latest survey being ______, earlier results gave researchers little relevant experience for the new data’s interpretation.","key":"D","opts":["superfluous","inconsequential","tedious","unexampled","familiar"],"expl":"unexampled（前所未有的）：新数据前所未有，使旧结果参考价值有限。选 D"},{"id":"v129.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"All of these writers rely on (i)______ and (ii)______ to make their argument: they take a single idea and illustrate it with endless, rather overblown examples while avoiding any genuinely nuanced analysis.","key":"CD","groups":[["fabrication","equivocation","simplification"],["exaggeration","speculation","prevarication"]],"expl":"空1 simplification（简化）；空2 exaggeration（夸大）。选 CD"},{"id":"v129.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Glaeser condemn the “agrarian utopianism” of those who (i)______ rural life and (ii)______ the environmental (iii)______ of certain big cities, chiefly less driving and the greater energy efficiency of heating the multifamily structures that characterize many urban settings.","key":"ADG","groups":[["sentimentalize","satirize","marginalize"],["fail to appreciate","rush to extol","refuse to disparage"],["virtues","risks","compromises"]],"expl":"空1 sentimentalize（美化）；空2 fail to appreciate（未能看到）；空3 environmental advantages（环境优势）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v129.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Retrofitted with stabilizing devices, some of which _____ its aesthetics, the bridge has been reopened, no longer prone to excessive swaying but not quite the breathtaking structure it originally was.","key":"AF","opts":["impair","resist","improve","enhance","restore","compromise"],"expl":"compromise（损害）：稳定装置会损害美观。选 AF"},{"id":"v129.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Mr. Hirsch says he will aim to preserve the foundation’s support of _____ thinkers, individuals who are going against the trends in a field or an acknowledged set of opinions.","key":"AD","opts":["iconoclastic","integrative","doctrinaire","heterodox","dogmatic","synthesizing"],"expl":"heterodox（异端的）：资助异见思想者。选 AD"},{"id":"v129.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In France cultural subsidies are _____: producers of just about any film can get an advance from the government against box-office receipts, even though most such loans are never fully repaid.","key":"AF","opts":["ubiquitous","invaluable","sporadic","scanty","questionable","omnipresent"],"expl":"omnipresent（无处不在的）：资助普遍存在。选 AF"},{"id":"v129.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Although it is loathsome to some people, slang often expresses ideas with great directness, avoiding the ______ of more refined language.","key":"AE","opts":["circumlocution","syntax","ornateness","obfuscation","periphrasis","opprobrium"],"expl":"circumlocution（迂回的表达）：俚语避免了委婉表达。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v129-2","title":"Test 129 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v129.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"As tough as it looks, the Chihuahuan Dersert is a ______ place: although few humans have been here, their footsteps have fallen heavily in the desert.","key":"B","opts":["forbidding","fragile","secluded","beguiling","hallowed"],"expl":"fragile（脆弱的）：虽然看起来严酷，但沙漠其实脆弱。选 B"},{"id":"v129.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"In general, the relationship between neural activity and behavioral output is ______: multiple behaviors can be associated with activation of the same neurons and multiple neurons can trigger the same behavior.","key":"D","opts":["deterministic","hardwired","random","complicated","cumulative"],"expl":"complicated（复杂的）：神经活动与行为之间的关系并不简单。选 D"},{"id":"v129.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The philosopher held that art must perform a paradoxical task, simultaneously extricating itself from the (i)______ even while (ii)______ the realities of ordinary experience.","key":"CF","groups":[["impersonal","prescriptive","quotidian"],["largely transcending","casually dismissing","forthrightly addressing"]],"expl":"空1 quotidian（日常的）；空2 largely transcending（超越）。选 CF"},{"id":"v129.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"When we forgive a person, we (i)_____ our (ii)_____ his or her transgression but (iii)______ certain punitive responses that we would ordinarily be justified in taking on the basis of that person’s objectionable conduct.","key":"CFH","groups":[["relinquish","regret","retain"],["leniency toward","uncertainty about","condemnation of"],["disguise","forgo","initiate"]],"expl":"空1 relinquish（放弃）；空2 leniency toward（宽恕）；空3 forgo（放弃）。选 CFH"},{"id":"v129.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The _____ of the Foundation novels by the noted science-fiction writer Isaac Asimov is that historians and psychologists succeed in finding laws that can successfully predict—based on collective human behavior—the broad outlines of future events.","key":"AC","opts":["premise","verisimilitude","postulate","paradox","incongruity","implication"],"expl":"premise（前提）：阿西莫夫小说的前提是可以预测未来。选 AC"},{"id":"v129.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"What is remarkable about The Feminine Mystique is that it can seem, alternately, so antique and so _____, a reminder of what has changed and what has not.","key":"AF","opts":["fresh","obsolete","scholarly","learned","obvious","germane"],"expl":"germane（相关的）：此书虽旧，却仍与今天相关。选 AF"},{"id":"v129.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Jane Austen belonged to the social class about which she mainly wrote, and although her novels offer abundant satire, one never has the sense that she viewed the basic elements of this social sphere as _____.","key":"CD","opts":["laudable","unfathomable","ignoble","reprehensible","inviolable","praiseworthy"],"expl":"ignoble（卑劣的）：奥斯汀不认为社会基本要素卑劣。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v130-1","title":"Test 130 · Section 1","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v130.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Although among currently available models Mestel’s provides the most ______ account of how white dwarfs evolve, it captures the essentials of the physics of white dwarf evolution.","key":"D","opts":["cited","realistic","corroborated","simplified","comprehensive"],"expl":"simplified（简化的）：模型虽然简化，但抓住了关键物理。选 D"},{"id":"v130.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"As an intellectual trying to navigate the world of politics, Madison’s problem was not, as some claimed, that he was too (i)______ to respond to shifting political realities; indeed, he was intellectually quite (ii)______, adapting to the demands of the moment.","key":"BD","groups":[["impulsive","doctrinaire","ambivalent"],["agile","austere","engaged"]],"expl":"空1 doctrinaire（教条的）；空2 agile（灵活的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v130.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A film adaptation so (i)______ can make the original novel seem (ii)______. Who hasn’t thought, “I've seen the movie, why read the book?” But where the film of Empire of the Sun is generally faithful to its source, the novel offers less high drama but a more (iii)______ view of the protagonist’s growth and confusion.","key":"AFG","groups":[["satisfying","drastic","pretentious"],["pedestrian","exhilarating","redundant"],["multifaceted","conventional","sensational"]],"expl":"空1 faithful（忠实的）；空2 pedestrian（平庸的）；空3 nuanced（细致的）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v130.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Evidence of the human brain’s ______ abounds: violinists, for example, tend to have larger cortical areas devoted to processing signals from their fingering hands than do non-violinists.","key":"BD","opts":["synchronicity","flexibility","complexity","malleability","vulnerability","sensitivity"],"expl":"malleability（可塑性）：大脑的可塑性。选 BD"},{"id":"v130.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Vast, complex, and deeply entrenched, the administrative apparatus that answered to Egypt’s Queen Cleopatra was ______ instrument with which to govern.","key":"EF","opts":["an antiquated","an efficient","a modest","a simple","an unwieldy","a cumbersome"],"expl":"an unwieldy（笨拙的）：行政体系笨重难用。选 EF"},{"id":"v130.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"With poetry seemingly forever composing its own ______, and the novel apparently writing its last chapter, science fiction writers are now similarly concerned that they face a future in which their writing could, ironically, be a thing of the past.","key":"EF","opts":["saga","chronicle","critique","inaugural","elegy","requiem"],"expl":"requiem（挽歌）：科幻作家担心自身的作品会成为过去。选 EF"},{"id":"v130.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In mid-nineteenth-century Paris, some independent women survived economically by running small dressmaking businesses, though the displacement of custom-made clothing by factory-made garments ______ these needleworkers’ economic opportunities.","key":"BC","opts":["confounded","curtailed","diminished","augmented","destroyed","disguised"],"expl":"curtailed（削减）：工厂服装削减了裁缝的机会。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v130-2","title":"Test 130 · Section 2","group":"Test 121–130","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v130.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The prime minister’s reputation for ______ was sullied when it was revealed that he had known of fraudulent activities taking place in the country’s banking system but failed to report them.","key":"C","opts":["solicitude","impassivity","probity","diplomacy","forbearance"],"expl":"probity（正直）：首相的正直声誉受损。选 C"},{"id":"v130.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"All countries have obvious incentives to learn from policy mistakes, but when a nation becomes (i)______, it may be (ii)______ to recognize and quickly correct errors. When it comes to learning the right lessons, nothing fails like prior success.","key":"BE","groups":[["ambitious","powerful","diverse"],["required","unable","willing"]],"expl":"空1 powerful（强大的）；空2 unable（无法）。选 BE"},{"id":"v130.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Because human emotions are behavioral complexes, they presumably took a very long time to develop. Therefore, a complete lack of any (i)______ human emotions in ancestral species is (ii)______.","key":"BF","groups":[["alternatives to","antecedents of","understanding of"],["unquestionable","reassuring","improbable"]],"expl":"空1 antecedents of（先驱）；空2 improbable（不太可能的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v130.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Recent research shows that although the overall parental involvement in education (i)______ during adolescence, the (ii)______ the nature and frequency of parents’ involvement and adolescent educational outcomes are no longer (iii)______: for some types of parental involvement, declines are appropriate, whereas increases may, in fact, have deleterious effects.","key":"ADI","groups":[["begins to wane","continues to matter","fails to improve"],["links between","conditions for","problems with"],["satisfactory","negligible","straightforward"]],"expl":"空1 begins to wane（开始减弱）；空2 relationship（关系）；空3 consistent（一致的）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v130.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The government has been able to ______ the country’s most serious social, economic and political problems, but these problems remain and may be getting worse.","key":"BD","opts":["redress","sidestep","champion","dodge","remedy","investigate"],"expl":"remedy（补救）：政府难以解决问题，但问题仍存在。选 BD"},{"id":"v130.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite the rather ______ conditions required for its preservation, the evidence for glaciation during the late Proterozoic is found on every continent, suggesting that ice sheets were present throughout the globe.","key":"DE","opts":["unusual","hostile","drastic","stringent","exacting","complex"],"expl":"stringent（严格的）：保存条件严苛，但证据仍分布广泛。选 DE"},{"id":"v130.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The movie’s ponderousness is ______ by the gripping performance turned in by the lead actor.","key":"CE","opts":["heightened","exacerbated","mitigated","belied","relieved","symbolized"],"expl":"mitigated（减轻）：男主角的表演减轻了影片的沉闷。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v131-1","title":"Test 131 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v131.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Unlike the introductions to many other biographies, this one is not ______; in fact, it would be a stretch to call it evenhanded.","key":"D","opts":["evaluative","contrived","concise","laudatory","formal"],"expl":"laudatory（颂扬性的）：这本传记并非颂扬之作。选 D"},{"id":"v131.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"No one (i)______ that building a ship powered by black holes or dark matter would be a formidable task. Yet remarkably there seems to be nothing in our present understanding of physics that (ii)______ our doing so.","key":"CF","groups":[["believes","admits","disputes"],["anticipates","necessitates","precludes"]],"expl":"空1 admits（承认）；空2 precludes（排除）。选 CF"},{"id":"v131.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The main (i)______ for pianists playing the keyboard works of Couperin lies in the effusion of embellishments, which are much easier to toss off without overemphasis, let alone (ii)______, on the harpsichord than on the piano. Yet pianist Angela Hewitt’s handling of all those fleeting lilts and curlicues is a model of (iii)______. As a result, little nothings like “Le Petit-Rien” are sheer rippling delights.","key":"ADI","groups":[["difcfi ulty","attraction","unknown"],["ungainliness","elegance","mastery"],["fierce intensity","economy and languor","lightness and elegance"]],"expl":"空1 pianistic（钢琴式的）；空2 overstated（夸大）；空3 precision（精确）。选 ADI"},{"id":"v131.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Koizumi’s decision to stake his political career on postal reform was less ______ than it might sound because the postal system could pass along trillions of yen to government financial institutions, benefiting him politically.","key":"AB","opts":["quixotic","impractical","calculating","shrewd","impulsive","maladroit"],"expl":"calculating（精于算计的）：改革决策并非冲动，而是精心计算。选 AB"},{"id":"v131.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Researchers who study pollinator behavior are increasingly interested in multicomponent floral signals, but they often focus on how individual components are learned by pollinators rather than on the benefit of signal ______ per se.","key":"AF","opts":["complexity","stability","magnitude","intensity","variation","intricacy"],"expl":"complexity（复杂性）：研究者关注的是复杂性的收益。选 AF"},{"id":"v131.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In her novel, the sea is ______ symbol: to the narrator, it clearly represents everything that is destructive in nature, but at other times it seems to stand for everything in nature that is serenely beautiful.","key":"BF","opts":["an unorthodox","an equivocal","an unconventional","a comprehensive","an elusive","an ambiguous"],"expl":"an ambiguous（模糊的）：海洋象征多重意义。选 BF"},{"id":"v131.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Frequently blamed for making ______ coverage decisions, insurance companies are eager to avoid additional bad press.","key":"AD","opts":["heartless","unfair","parsimonious","callous","definitive","conclusive"],"expl":"callous（冷漠的）：保险公司被指责冷酷地做出理赔决定。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v131-2","title":"Test 131 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v131.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The standard wisdom now is that sciences undergo periodic ruptures so thorough that the generations of scientists on either side of the break express themselves in mutually ______ languages.","key":"D","opts":["intelligible","influential","translatable","incomprehensible","interconnected"],"expl":"incomprehensible（无法理解的）：新旧科学语言互不相通。选 D"},{"id":"v131.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The title of Felsenstein’s book-Inferring Phylogenies-is positively (i)______. The volume achieves so much more than simply presenting methods for inferring phylogenies, being, in fact, (ii)______ of how to analyze evolutionary data from a phylogenetic perspective.","key":"BD","groups":[["grandiose","misleading","fortuitous"],["an admirably comprehensive discussion","a thoroughly outmoded treatment","an almost opaque account"]],"expl":"空1 misleading（误导的）；空2 an admirably comprehensive discussion（全面的讨论）。选 BD"},{"id":"v131.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Penrose is (i)______ theoretical physicists for engaging in (ii)______ by (iii)______ what is implied by the known data. One of his favorite examples is inflationary cosmology, which, according to him, is treated as an established theory despite a lack of evidence.","key":"BFI","groups":[["indebted to","critical of","singular among"],["partisanship","plagiarism","conjecture"],["experimenting with","combing through","venturing beyond"]],"expl":"空1 critical of（批评）；空2 conjecture（推测）；空3 testing（检验）。选 BFI"},{"id":"v131.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Most movie sound tracks lean so heavily on a few preprocessed musical devices—those swells of strings and cymbals designed to manipulate our emotions in (i)______ ways-that when a composer (ii)______ a more personal language, the effect is (iii)______: an entire dimension of the film experience is liberated from cliché.","key":"BEH","groups":[["unprecedented","predictable","provocative"],["resists","adopts","eschews"],["meaningless","revelatory","disappointing"]],"expl":"空1 predictable（可预测的）；空2 resists（抵制）；空3 refreshing（令人耳目一新的）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v131.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"A number of recent pieces of instrumental music are linked by a common feature: the considerable ______ left to the individual performer in the way he or she chooses to play the work.","key":"DE","opts":["fidelity","restraints","keenness","latitude","leeway","curbs"],"expl":"latitude（自由度）：演奏者拥有很大的自由。选 DE"},{"id":"v131.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The fierce drought that is gripping the area-and imminent rationing and steep water price increases-is ______ the area’s deep economic divide, as wealthy communities guzzle water while poorer communities nearby conserve by necessity.","key":"CE","opts":["defining","bridging","highlighting","exacerbating","underscoring","adjusting"],"expl":"exacerbating（加剧）：旱灾加剧了经济鸿沟。选 CE"},{"id":"v131.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Wilson sees the ideas that he presents in his new book as being notably ______, but his critics, by contrast, claim that they are actually rather conventional.","key":"BC","opts":["understated","iconoclastic","subversive","democratic","egalitarian","daunting"],"expl":"iconoclastic（打破偶像的）：威尔逊的观点被视为颠覆性的。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v132-1","title":"Test 132 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v132.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Establishing the exact boundaries of a piece of property can be ______ process; some of the bitterest battles in contemporary society are waged between neighbors fighting over small slivers of land.","key":"D","opts":["a definitive","a scrupulous","an expedient","a fraught","a deliberate"],"expl":"a fraught（充满争议的）：产权界定常引发激烈冲突。选 D"},{"id":"v132.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"According to Adriana Craciun, many of the people who fled France because of opposition to the Revolution were (i)______ by loyalty to the deposed royal family: almost a third of those who left France departed (ii)______ the fall of the monarchy, so it is unlikely, claims Craciun, that fealty to the royal family was the decisive factor in their decision.","key":"CF","groups":[["strongly galvanized","entirely unmoved","not simply motivated"],["after","during","before"]],"expl":"空1 strongly galvanized（强烈激发）；空2 after（在……之后）。选 CF"},{"id":"v132.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Lava flows that erupt on Earth’s surface cool rapidly, forming rocks that are very fine grained. But some lava remains in volcanic conduits deep in the ground where it cools slowly, and the slowly growing mineral grains get much bigger than their surface equivalents. Thus, rocks with (i)______ can have (ii)______ textures, depending on how quickly they (iii)______.","key":"CEI","groups":[["diverse mineral","typical surface markings","identical chemical makeup"],["recognizable","disparate","unusual"],["fracture","spread","congeal"]],"expl":"空1 diverse mineral（多样的矿物）；空2 varied（不同的）；空3 cool（冷却）。选 CEI"},{"id":"v132.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"With Duncan’s ambitious study, Chesnutt appears finally to have outgrown the ______ treatment he once received from literary historians and critics for whom he typically served as a merely transitional figure in the African American tradition.","key":"AF","opts":["cursory","jocular","heartfelt","didactic","fervent","perfunctory"],"expl":"perfunctory（敷衍的）：查斯纳特过去常受敷衍的评价。选 AF"},{"id":"v132.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite his secure position as a writer, Samuel Richardson adopted a strangely ______ posture, soliciting advice on early drafts of his second novel from readers familiar with his earlier work.","key":"AD","opts":["complaisant","quarrelsome","nonchalant","deferential","dispassionate","perfunctory"],"expl":"deferential（恭敬的）：理查逊主动征求意见，姿态谦逊。选 AD"},{"id":"v132.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The trilogy balance seriousness with brilliant special effects, a fundamental furious darkness with fast-paced and engaging storytelling, so that the books manage to be simultaneously disturbing and _______.","key":"BE","opts":["intense","fun","melodramatic","gloomy","entertaining","somber"],"expl":"entertaining（有趣的）：三部曲既令人不安又娱乐性强。选 BE"},{"id":"v132.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In our solar system, Earth is the most ______ of the rocky, or terrestrial, planets, so when first searching beyond solar system, scientists were not accustomed to planets of similar composition but many times the mass.","key":"DF","opts":["complex","temperate","clement","sizable","intricate","substantial"],"expl":"substantial（体积大的）：地球是岩石行星中体量较大的，而系外行星质量远超地球。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v132-2","title":"Test 132 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v132.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Throughout his book, Venter savors his reputation as ______, believing himself righteous and embattled, as when his choices to sequence genome fragments and to patent expressed sequence tags provoked outrage among fellow scientists.","key":"B","opts":["a tactician","an iconoclast","an opportunist","a clairvoyant","a dilettante"],"expl":"an iconoclast（打破偶像者）：文特尔自视为与众不同、敢于挑战传统的人。选 B"},{"id":"v132.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"When in 1980 the father and son pair of Luis and Walter Alvarez and their colleagues linked the end-Cretaceous mass extinction to a catastrophic extraterrestrial impact, they were met with skepticism by most paleontologists, which was (i)______ given that geological training since the mid-1800s had emphasized the primacy of (ii)______.","key":"AE","groups":[["unsurprising","unwarranted","prescient"],["discernible causes","gradual processes","reversible changes"]],"expl":"空1 unsurprising（不足为奇）；空2 gradualism（渐变论）。选 AE"},{"id":"v132.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When an ideologue of one persuasion reverses course and embraces the views of erstwhile opponents, those whose views the convert adopts may feel vindicated. Still, one wants a person making a political about-face to (i)______ of his or her previous allegiances: a reversal without a (ii)______ is less than satisfying.","key":"AD","groups":[["acknowledge the erroneousness","rationalize the value","downplay the importance"],["recantation","reconciliation","recapitulation"]],"expl":"空1 acknowledge the erroneousness（承认先前的错误）；空2 rationale（理由）。选 AD"},{"id":"v132.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The student who will benefit most from this biography of Mark Twain is the one who wishes to study the phenomenon of the author as (i)______. It clearly shows that Twain, contemptuous as he may have been of the acquisitive society in which he lived, was ever (ii)______ money, but that his (iii)______ was almost inversely proportionate to his avarice. Usually a man with a keen eye for fraud and imposture, he was easily lured to invest in numerous improbable schemes.","key":"AFG","groups":[["speculator","moralist","visionary"],["disdainful of","lucky with","ravenous for"],["acumen","enthusiasm","voracity"]],"expl":"空1 a businessman（商人）；空2 preoccupied with（热衷于）；空3 reputation（声誉）。选 AFG"},{"id":"v132.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"World music once represented the timeless and the ______, but now bands across the globe mix rock, dance music, and hip-hop with the sounds of their own cultures, creating new hybrids that are hard to resist.","key":"DF","opts":["untranslatable","superior","inclusive","unalloyed","unrivaled","unadulterated"],"expl":"unadulterated（未掺杂的）：世界音乐曾代表纯粹的传统。选 DF"},{"id":"v132.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Scientists have recently confirmed that Mercury possesses a lot of ice, ______ discovery for a place that ranks among the hottest in the solar system.","key":"DF","opts":["a controversial","a stunning","a doubtful","a counterintuitive","a dubious","an unexpected"],"expl":"a counterintuitive（反直觉的）：水星存在冰是出人意料的发现。选 DF"},{"id":"v132.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"During the fifteenth century, the aspects of the mathematical science were usually singled out as ______: their preparatory value for the study of philosophy, their practical advantage for the community, and their antiquity.","key":"AD","opts":["estimable","superlative","inflated","praiseworthy","unique","adventitious"],"expl":"praiseworthy（值得称道的）：数学的三个优点都被视为值得称赞。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v133-1","title":"Test 133 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v133.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even though no other species in the Rana genus of frogs exhibits such ______ habits, once crawfish frogs have finally been located, they are relatively easy to film.","key":"A","opts":["furtive","rigid","aggressive","eccentric","complex"],"expl":"furtive（隐秘的）：这些青蛙习性隐秘，所以难以发现。选 A"},{"id":"v133.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Carmen de Burgos’ work was mass-produced popular fiction, and its (i)______ nature allowed it to be (ii)______ by critics until the 1970s, when feminist scholars began to reevaluate the merit of her texts and recognize her contributions to early-twentieth-century Spanish culture.","key":"AD","groups":[["disposable","innovative","realistic"],["dismissed","debated","overesteemed"]],"expl":"空1 disposable（一次性的）；空2 dismissed（被轻视）。选 AD"},{"id":"v133.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Among chess aficionados, there have been many doomsday scenarios about people (i)______ the game as a result of the superiority of computer chess programs over human players, Others have replied to this with variations on the theme of how we still hold footraces despite cars going much faster, but this analogy is (ii)______ since cars do not help humans run faster while chess computers undoubtedly have an effect on the (iii)______ of human chess.","key":"AFH","groups":[["losing interest in","redoubling their efforts at","struggling to master"],["ineluctable","transparent","spurious"],["popularity","quality","accessibility"]],"expl":"空1 abandoning（放弃）；空2 misleading（误导的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v133.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"There are too many characters, too many subplots, and no one clearly defined protagonist, making for ______ story.","key":"AF","opts":["an unfocused","a maudlin","a superficial","a sentimental","a complicated","a diffuse"],"expl":"a diffuse（散漫的）：人物与情节太多，没有焦点。选 AF"},{"id":"v133.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The ______ of cosmic rays remains mysterious because their paths are bent by the galaxy's magnetic field-meaning that the directions they come from do not point to whatever created them.","key":"BE","opts":["structure","origin","velocity","production","provenance","speed"],"expl":"origin（起源）：宇宙射线的来源仍是谜。选 BE"},{"id":"v133.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While many of Florence Price’s art songs suffer from an excess of emotionality, “To my Little Son” actually demonstrates some _______, which makes the song more approachable and ultimately more moving.","key":"DF","opts":["self-assurance","spunk","intelligence","restraint","confidence","moderation"],"expl":"restraint（克制）：歌曲的克制使其更动人。选 DF"},{"id":"v133.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The author’s approach to her subject is less _____ than that of some of her predecessors in the field, though here and there she cautiously takes a stand on a potentially divisive issue.","key":"DF","opts":["propitious","auspicious","portentous","contentious","pretentious","tendentious"],"expl":"contentious（有争议的）：作者在争议问题上表态谨慎，故比前人较少争议性。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v133-2","title":"Test 133 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v133.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because it was exposed by a ______ fracture, the rock’s structure could be seen free of weathering or lichen growth.","key":"C","opts":["primeval","complex","recent","microscopic","permanent"],"expl":"recent（近期的）：岩石刚被剥露，所以表面没有风化。选 C"},{"id":"v133.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The word “hacker,” applied to technology, initially meant an ingenious college student or a hobbyist exploring computers’ capabilities. At worst, a hacker was a (i)______. Over time, however, the term acquired a more (ii)______ meaning: that of someone who attempts to gain illicit access to confidential information or crash the electronic grid.","key":"BF","groups":[["revolutionary","prankster","hireling"],["condescending","transparent","sinister"]],"expl":"空1 a vandal（破坏者）；空2 pejorative（贬义的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v133.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"A new report has found that while psychoanalysis—or what purports to be psychoanalysis—is alive and well in literature, film, history, and just about every other subject in the humanities, psychology departments and textbooks treat it as something (i)______, a historical artifact instead of (ii)______.","key":"AE","groups":[["dead","controversial","nascent"],["a dubious achievement","an ongoing movement","an interesting episode"]],"expl":"空1 dead（已死的）；空2 a dubious achievement（可疑的成就）。选 AE"},{"id":"v133.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"The potential (i)______ exploiting mineral resources in the area combined with the (ii)______ participation among local people in conversation efforts may lead to a (iii)______ human appreciation for the landscape and eventually contribute to disadvantageous effects for conservation.","key":"AEH","groups":[["rewards in","ban on","danger in"],["an increase of interest in","a lack of benefits for","a shift in the direction of"],["rise in","shrinkage of","dependency on"]],"expl":"空1 danger in（隐患）；空2 an increase of interest in（对……兴趣增加）；空3 greater（更大的）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v133.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Evolutionary psychologists hold that mating patterns arise from individual strategies to ______ one’s genetic qualities, either by producing more offspring or by adding the survival of one’s relatives.","key":"CD","opts":["ascertain","transcend","transmit","propagate","overcome","regulate"],"expl":"propagate（传播、延续）：通过繁殖延续基因。选 CD"},{"id":"v133.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Prunella Clough was by no means reclusive, enjoying an extensive social and teaching life, but she deliberately kept a low profile, being famously ______ biographical details.","key":"CD","opts":["unreliable regarding","untrustworthy regarding","guarded with","stinting with","irritable about","uninterested in"],"expl":"guarded with（对……保密）：她小心保守自己的生平细节。选 CD"},{"id":"v133.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The tools of science are so specialized that we accept them as a kind of ______ machinery for producing knowledge: we know that they work, but cannot explain why.","key":"AD","opts":["occult","efficacious","potent","arcane","impersonal","reliable"],"expl":"occult（神秘的）：科学工具像神秘机器。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v134-1","title":"Test 134 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v134.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Given the extraordinary ______ of its arguments, it is surprising that the central thesis of the book can be stated so simply.","key":"A","opts":["nuance","insensitivity","lucidity","spuriousness","rationality"],"expl":"lucidity（清晰）：论点的清晰令人惊讶地简单。选 A"},{"id":"v134.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"There has been a noticeable reversal from the time when (i)______ was accepted as the essential characteristic of genuine science: now the role of (ii)______ in scientific research is generating a great deal of interest.","key":"CE","groups":[["disciplinary specialization","long apprenticeship","dispassionate inquiry"],["speculation","emotion","technology"]],"expl":"空1 long apprenticeship（长期学徒制）；空2 emotion（情感）。选 CE"},{"id":"v134.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Japan’s first university was more (i)______ than its Chinese counterparts in the same era, since the Chinese Tang system was highly (ii)______. However, this changed over time. As Japanese court office became increasingly hereditary, the examination system, by which students from wide range of social classes were admitted into the universities, (iii)______.","key":"BDI","groups":[["prestige","egalitarian","profitable"],["aristocratic","reputable","unsystematic"],["became widely utilized","advantaged the proletariat","atrophied into insignificance"]],"expl":"空1 prestige（声望）；空2 meritocratic（精英选拔的）；空3 was weakened（被削弱）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v134.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Pre-Columbian peoples had a significant impact on Amazonian forest diversity; at least 8,000 years ago, they mush have begun domesticating plants recently found to be ______ around sites once occupied by humans.","key":"BF","opts":["hybridized","abundant","uncommon","preserved","harvested","dominant"],"expl":"abundant（丰富的）：人类活动区域的植物较为丰富。选 BF"},{"id":"v134.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"It is often taken for granted by scholars that Emily Dickinson is ______ poet: her poems have a peculiar quality that makes understanding seem beyond the reader’s ken.","key":"DF","opts":["a melancholy","an unusual","a pensive","a difficult","a whimsical","an enigmatic"],"expl":"an enigmatic（神秘的）：狄金森的诗令人难以理解。选 DF"},{"id":"v134.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"For every ______ reader of Vestiges there were many more who became vocal critics, and the book aroused heated opposition from a broad range of British society.","key":"CD","opts":["outspoken","meticulous","sympathetic","well-disposed","unenthusiastic","candid"],"expl":"well-disposed（有好感的）：读者中有很多人持友善态度。选 CD"},{"id":"v134.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Unsurprisingly, the novelist’s new work has been without its critics, drawing particularly attention from those who have ______ the vapidity of other novels of the same genre in a number of acerbic reviews.","key":"AE","opts":["reprehended","questioned","ignored","overlooked","decried","relished"],"expl":"decried（谴责）：批评者谴责其他小说的空洞。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v134-2","title":"Test 134 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v134.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Some people might object to pairing art and physics, since art is considered to be relatively ______ and physics, until recently, scrupulously avoided any mention of the inner thoughts that related to the outer world.","key":"B","opts":["accessible","subjective","enigmatic","detached","conceptual"],"expl":"subjective（主观的）：艺术相对主观。选 B"},{"id":"v134.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Carter is a difficult figure to see in the true proportion—his reputation has been stretched to the point of ______, as he is put forward as the prime example of a tyrannical CEO.","key":"A","opts":["caricature","beatification","verisimilitude","obscurity","self-contradiction"],"expl":"caricature（漫画化）：卡特的声誉被夸张地漫画化。选 A"},{"id":"v134.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"My (i)______ Hansen’s life-size sculpture for real people was memorable precisely because the work did (ii)______ such a complete—if brief—deception, one that is exceptional in my experience as a viewer of representational art.","key":"CE","groups":[["adapting","producing","mistaking"],["hinder","effect","confound"]],"expl":"空1 mistaking（误认）；空2 effect（实现）。选 CE"},{"id":"v134.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Most artists maintain an attitude of (i)______ toward their own work. They know, better than any critic would know, how their art (ii)______ their ambitions. The artist would demand admirer, “Do you really think this is the best I am capable of?” Henri Cartier-Bresson’s dismissal of his work in photography, however, is (iii)______: it seems almost contempt, or even hatred, not just for his achievement but for the medium itself.","key":"CDH","groups":[["extraordinary hubris","irremediable disdain","healthy disrespect"],["fall far short of","eventually transcends","subtly realizes"],["entirely comprehensible","at another level altogether","at odds with his achievement"]],"expl":"空1 severe（严厉的）；空2 fall short of（达不到）；空3 remarkable（非凡的）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v134.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Proponents of xeriscaping, a method of landscaping designed to minimize irrigation, point out that grass planted in desert locations has ______ effect on the environment, sapping water that is valuable and already scarce.","key":"BF","opts":["a benign","a pernicious","a superficial","a trivial","an inevitable","a deleterious"],"expl":"a deleterious（有害的）：灌溉草坪对环境有害。选 BF"},{"id":"v134.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Encompassing more than petty disagreements over order in the author list, arguments about attribution in science speak to ______ issues—for example, where do new ideas come from, and what constitutes a new idea?","key":"BF","opts":["contemporary","profound","practical","topical","controversial","weighty"],"expl":"profound（深刻的）：这些争论涉及深层问题。选 BF"},{"id":"v134.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Her success is not ______, for she writes clearly about complicated subjects and provides lucid explanations and penetrating insights.","key":"CF","opts":["undeniable","undeserved","unanticipated","unparalleled","unsurpassed","unexpected"],"expl":"undeserved（不应得的）：她的成功是理所应当的。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v135-1","title":"Test 135 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v135.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The professor explained that in order to make a complex phenomenon more ______, economists often reduce it to an abstract problem.","key":"A","opts":["tractable","contemporary","momentous","tenebrous","substantive"],"expl":"tractable（易处理的）：经济学家把复杂现象简化，使其易于处理。选 A"},{"id":"v135.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The great divide between science and the humanities appeared during the last decades of the nineteenth century: before then, most people had seen those realms of human thoughts as (i)______. It would therefore be (ii)______ us to study early or mid-nineteenth-century science as something completely separates from the art of the time.","key":"BF","groups":[["recondite","overlapping","inapposite"],["prescient of","uncharacteristic of","anachronistic for"]],"expl":"空1 overlapping（交织的）；空2 inappropriate（不当的）。选 BF"},{"id":"v135.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite its title and the recipes it provides, the main purpose of The Insect Cookbook is not (i)______. Instead, the book seeks to (ii)______ of entomophagy, i.e. the consumption of insects as food: it is composed of interviews with chefs, farmers, politicians, and United Nations figures, all of whom attempt to (iii)______ the custom of eating insects.","key":"BFG","groups":[["scientific","culinary","educational"],["explore the history","condemn the practice","proselytize on behalf"],["promote","discredit","reform"]],"expl":"空1 scientific（科学性的）；空2 defend（为……辩护）。选 BFG"},{"id":"v135.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"According to Waters, Cheryl Fish’s otherwise brilliant analysis of Mary Seacole is ______ by a postmodern penchant for inventive jargon and fuzzy metaphysics.","key":"BF","opts":["negated","marred","dominated","caricatured","forestalled","tainted"],"expl":"marred（有损）：分析因后现代的晦涩而受损。选 BF"},{"id":"v135.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"By avoiding hyperbole in her definitive account of one of the most influential but controversial banks of the modern era, Hurst show herself to be a ______ author.","key":"AD","opts":["judicious","brilliant","compelling","sensible","sympathetic","solicitous"],"expl":"judicious（审慎的）：避免夸张显示作者审慎。选 AD"},{"id":"v135.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In stark contrast to her earlier plays, which are noisily crammed with monologues and overlapping dialogue, Caryl Churchill’s later theatrical works are notably _______.","key":"AE","opts":["laconic","inventive","cogent","resourceful","spare","bland"],"expl":"spare（简练的）：晚期作品异常简约。选 AE"},{"id":"v135.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Attempts to restore carnivores to ecosystems from which they were eliminated have become _______: indeed, many species are even being introduced into areas where they did not previously roam.","key":"DF","opts":["expensive","controversial","contentious","commonplace","effective","widespread"],"expl":"commonplace（普遍的）：恢复食肉动物的做法已很普遍。选 DF"}]},{"id":"v135-2","title":"Test 135 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v135.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The film portrays a political period that was bitterly divisive but does so in such ______ way that the narrative never becomes polemical.","key":"D","opts":["a timely","an involved","a maladroit","a nuanced","an impassioned"],"expl":"nuanced（细致的）：电影处理政治议题时不偏激。选 D"},{"id":"v135.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Because we participate in the dynamics of ecosystems as we restore them, restoration practice is in essence antithetical to the idea of a ______ wilderness.","key":"D","opts":["managed","developing","rehabilitated","pristine","degraded"],"expl":"pristine（原始的）：修复本身与“原始荒野”相悖。选 D"},{"id":"v135.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Maddox presents a more (i)______ view of Franklin than the stereotyped rendering of her as the martyr whose data was stolen. By focus substantial attention on Franklin’s achievements working on the molecular structure of coal and on virus research, Maddox (ii)______ reducing Franklin’s GRE】","key":"CD","groups":[["conventional","facile","complex"],["resists","deplores","invites"]],"expl":"空1 complex（复杂的）；空2 resists（抵制）。选 CD"},{"id":"v135.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"At 79, Wirtz remains charmingly and frustratingly (i)______, giving only the briefest and most (ii)______ of answers to questions about his work as a landscape architect. His son Peter, who is as (iii)______ as his father is reticent, claims that the elder Wirtz, being a “natural talent,” does not always articulate what makes him do things.","key":"AFH","groups":[["elusive","subtle","sophisticated"],["penetrating","explicit","general"],["literal","voluble","tractable"]],"expl":"空1 elusive（难以捉摸的）；空2 subtle（微妙的）；空3 articulate（善于表达的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v135.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Recent advances in the study of desert vanish have been a boon to geologists, allowing them to date surface feature and establish regional climate histories in ______ detail.","key":"AC","opts":["novel","realistic","unprecedented","superfluous","extraneous","surprising"],"expl":"novel（新颖的）：沙漠漆的研究在细节上具有新颖性。选 AC"},{"id":"v135.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Traditionally, doctors have measured consciousness by getting response from patients, asking questions like, “Can you hear me?”—an approach that is _____ for people who are conscious but unable to respond.","key":"EF","opts":["fanciful","imprecise","vague","illicit","inadequate","ineffective"],"expl":"inadequate（不足的）：这种方法对无法回应者不够充分。选 EF"},{"id":"v135.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The essayist was known to suffer fools impatiently, but admittedly her vast intellect made that ______ largely justified.","key":"AE","opts":["hauteur","diffidence","irritability","imperturbability","superciliousness","timorousness"],"expl":"hauteur（傲慢）：她的傲慢在其智力面前得到辩护。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v136-1","title":"Test 136 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v136.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The museum exhibit perplexing mixed significant cultural artifacts with gaudy trinkets, leading one critic to suggest that the exhibit’s curator could not distinguish the important pieces from those that were ______.","key":"E","opts":["representative","illustrious","repugnant","inscrutable","meretricious"],"expl":"meretricious（华而不实的）：把珍贵文物与廉价小玩意混在一起。选 E"},{"id":"v136.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"It was (i)______ the candidate’s insistence that there will be completely disclosure that she (ii)______ probing questions from reporters.","key":"BE","groups":[["contrary to","illustrative of","peripheral to"],["misunderstand","welcomed","analyzed"]],"expl":"空1 contrary to（与……相悖）；空2 welcomed（欢迎）。选 BE"},{"id":"v136.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Critics of the company’s senior management will be (i)______ by Han’s careful and meticulous account of its actions. Despite the book’s (ii)______ title, the author has no designs on scandal; in fact, if anything, her account tends toward (iii)______, applauding the company’s all-conquering success without reservation.","key":"BDI","groups":[["emboldened","disappointed","charmed"],["ominous","fawning","insipid"],["cynicism","pretentiousness","hagiography"]],"expl":"空1 charmed（受吸引）；空2 sensational（耸动的）；空3 flattery（奉承）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v136.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The scholars’ hypothesis challenges the scope of human psychological and behavioral universal, but does not dispense with them entirely: the team remains confident that displays of pride, for instance, are ______.","key":"CF","opts":["inherited","pernicious","ubiquitous","symptomatic","detrimental","omnipresent"],"expl":"ubiquitous（普遍存在的）：骄傲表现普遍存在。选 CF"},{"id":"v136.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"As some primate experts have argued, the finding that related species have similar social structures, presumably as a result of shared genes inherited from a common ancestor, ______ nongenetic explanations of social behavior.","key":"CD","opts":["revitalizes","anticipates","undermines","challenges","predicts","eludes"],"expl":"undermines（削弱）：遗传解释削弱了非遗传解释。选 CD"},{"id":"v136.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While spectroscopy may be an obscure tool, there is nothing correspondingly ______ about claims concerning its importance: it proved that the rest of the universe is built form the same kinds of atoms as we are.","key":"BC","opts":["banal","arcane","esoteric","prosaic","equivocal","self-evident"],"expl":"esoteric / arcane 与“显而易见”形成对比：光谱学的重要性并非晦涩。选 BC"},{"id":"v136.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The legislators didn’t merely sell out to business; they retreated to ______ style of governing whereby the interest group that is currently lobbying the hardest on an issue determines the party’s position.","key":"CF","opts":["a reckless","a rigid","a craven","an unyielding","an arrogant","a cowardly"],"expl":"a craven（懦弱的）：立法者屈从游说团体。选 CF"}]},{"id":"v136-2","title":"Test 136 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v136.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The common archaeological emphasis on changes in the shape of prehistoric stone implements should not ______ the fact that other materials, such as wood, bone, and antler, were also used for tools throughout the Paleolithic era.","key":"C","opts":["confirm","underscore","obscure","contest","belabor"],"expl":"obscure（掩盖）：对石器形状的强调不应掩盖其他材料的使用。选 C"},{"id":"v136.2.2","n":2,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The paintings of the 1960s Photo-Realists were meticulously rendered by artists who eschewed abstraction for realistic representation and thus achieved a precisely detailed, impersonal ______.","key":"A","opts":["verisimilitude","imagination","idealization","subjectivism","grandiloquence"],"expl":"verisimilitude（逼真性）：摄影现实主义追求逼真。选 A"},{"id":"v136.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Angela Merkel was a genuinely new figure in politics, someone who could potentially bridge the two halves of Germany, which had drifted apart in recent years. And yet the (i)______ circumstances of her victory (ii)______ the reservations Germans had about her. She was chosen not with a rousing popular mandate but after protracted backroom negotiations.","key":"CF","groups":[["auspicious","breathtaking","unsettling"],["belied","resolved","underscored"]],"expl":"默克尔的胜选条件并不吉利，幕后谈判的方式掩盖了德国人的保留态度，故。选 CF"},{"id":"v136.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Pauline Kael’s first movie review tore into Charlie Chaplin for taking up the mantle of comic artist rather than claiming his roots as a slapstick clown. It might seem strange that a reviewer with such highbrow reading tastes as Kael had would attack upward-reaching film entertainers for their pretensions and champion films that were mainstream entertainments. Yet such a stance could itself be seen as (i)______, as it (ii)______ a certain idea of true art from (iii)______, as if only literature should aspire to seriousness.","key":"BDH","groups":[["ascetic","elite","egalitarian"],["guards","redeems","displaces"],["enervating refinement","popular encroachment","revolutionary claims"]],"expl":"空1 dismiss（轻视）；空2 contradicted（矛盾）；空3 self-serving（自私的）。选 BDH"},{"id":"v136.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Responsibility for the nation’s decline rest squarely with a people who take for granted their claims to preeminence but do not ______ interest in or commitment to actually maintaining it.","key":"CF","opts":["foresee","rebuff","evince","reject","predict","betray"],"expl":"evince（表现）：人们不表现出维持地位的兴趣。选 CF"},{"id":"v136.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Padilla is a contrarian by nature, so it is no surprise that the clothes she designs have consistently ______ established fashion trends.","key":"BF","opts":["hindered","challenged","exacerbated","worsened","impeded","flouted"],"expl":"flouted（无视）：她的设计常无视既定潮流。选 BF"},{"id":"v136.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Despite the critic’s assertion that Willa Cather’s place in the literary canon is now so entrenched that it scarcely matters if she were really a modernist, her reputation arguably remains ______.","key":"BD","opts":["flawless","uncertain","impressive","tenuous","consequential","steadfast"],"expl":"tenuous（薄弱的）：卡瑟的声誉仍然脆弱。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v137-1","title":"Test 137 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v137.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Historians of medicine are resigned to doctors’ ______ medical history: physicians offer hagiographic biographies of obscure nineteenth-century medical figures, triumphalist narratives of medical progress, and retrospective diagnoses of ailments afflicting historical characters.","key":"D","opts":["clarifications of","disaffection with","condescension toward","incursions into","indifference to"],"expl":"condescension toward（俯就、轻视）：医生对医学史的俯就态度。选 D"},{"id":"v137.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Reports of the destruction of island vegetation by human-introduced herbivores, such as goats and rabbits, are so (i)______ that there can be no reason to (ii)______.","key":"CE","groups":[["dire","prejudicial","consistent"],["trace their provenance","doubt their veracity","dispute their ubiquity"]],"expl":"空1 dire（严重的）；空2 doubt their veracity（怀疑其真实性）。选 CE"},{"id":"v137.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"George Eliot's biographer can be highly inventive, but, at the same time, somewhat (i)______ in her approach to Eliot. She will hoist an alluring psychological flag concerning Eliot and then scrupulously take it down again, because the evidence will not serve to (ii)______ it. But she takes it down only after it has taken an entirely (iii)______ flutter in the breeze.","key":"CFG","groups":[["sentimental","irresponsible","scrupulous"],["embroider","discount","support"],["unwarranted","accidental","justified"]],"expl":"空1 inventive（有创造性的）；空2 substantiate（证实）；空3 unsuitable（不恰当的）。选 CFG"},{"id":"v137.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The museum’s display of bandolier bags made by Ojibwa artists of the Mille Lacs community reinforces the idea that this community’s culture is ______ one: early twentieth-century bandolier bags are displayed alongside others made recently.","key":"CD","opts":["a historic","an inventive","an unfolding","a living","a resourceful","a unique"],"expl":"a living（活态的）：文化是持续发展的。选 CD"},{"id":"v137.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"At the core of science fiction is the notion of ______, of asking, \"If this phenomenon continues, where will it lead?\"","key":"BC","opts":["generalization","extrapolation","projection","compensation","reparation","theorization"],"expl":"extrapolation（推断）：科幻的核心是推断。选 BC"},{"id":"v137.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Certainly, the drive to make safety a corporate priority is ______, but whether it will be enough to create the necessary change in corporate culture is another matter; organizational inertia can be a powerful force.","key":"BD","opts":["revolutionary","sound","critical","prudent","irresistible","inexorable"],"expl":"sound（稳固的）：安全成为企业优先事项是合理的。选 BD"},{"id":"v137.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The idea that Antarctica’s subglacial lakes are ______ has changed radically thanks to repeat-pass satellite altimetry technology, which has found evidence of water transfer between lakes at distances of more than 200 kilometers.","key":"CD","opts":["sterile","barren","isolated","discrete","uniform","obscure"],"expl":"discrete（分立的）：湖泊之间存在水的交换，并非彼此独立。选 CD"}]},{"id":"v137-2","title":"Test 137 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v137.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The depletion of soil and trees in southern West Virginia has resulted in frequent flash floods, since when the mountain slopes are ______, storms cause torrents of water to pour down them unimpeded.","key":"C","opts":["riven","fecund","denuded","withered","mutable"],"expl":"denuded（裸露的）：山坡被剥去植被。选 C"},{"id":"v137.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The methods for composting organic waste aim to (i) ______ nature’s tendency toward decay — a process unfortunately often (ii) ______ in landfills, where organic materials are packed so tightly that they have little access to the oxygen necessary for decomposition.","key":"BD","groups":[["obviate","precipitate","ameliorate"],["impeded","expedited","manifested"]],"expl":"空1 obviate（克服）；空2 impeded（受阻）。选 BD"},{"id":"v137.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Unlike those glossy Architectural Digest photographs that are deliberately (i) ______ lest they distract from a focus on the building itself, Friedlander’s architectural photography is the product of his insistence that he is an individual looking at buildings and scenes as they actually exist. Friedlander reminds us that everyday objects (ii) ______ or, more exactly, that the unimpeded visual scene of a building without cars or power lines or street signs is a highly (iii) ______ photographic artifact.","key":"AFI","groups":[["impersonal","offhand","evocative"],["are largely inessential","resist interpretation","normally interfere"],["intriguing","imprecise","contrived"]],"expl":"空1 cropped（经过裁剪）；空2 take on significance（获得意义）。选 AFI"},{"id":"v137.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Those whose professional lives spanned the rise of the feminist movement from the 1970s onward and who witnessed significant advances in gender equality in the workplace over the intervening four decades will not be (i) ______ Saval’s account of the (ii) ______ female employees. However, the (iii) ______ women advancing in the workplace can seem astonishing to those who did not witness it firsthand.","key":"ADG","groups":[["surprised by","aware of","impressed by"],["growing opportunities","striking accomplishments","many tribulations"],["resistance to","support for","indifference to"]],"expl":"那些经历了女性运动并见证性别平等进步的人，对 Saval 所描述的状况不会感到意外。选 ADG"},{"id":"v137.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Biographies can be ______ contrivances, often too long and too detailed for their own good.","key":"EF","opts":["subtle","ingenious","extravagant","vain","wearisome","onerous"],"expl":"wearisome（令人厌倦的）：传记常过长、过细，令人疲惫。选 EF"},{"id":"v137.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Many types of rocks contain small voids that ______ vibrations: the greater the proportion of a rock’s volume that is void, the more gradually vibrations travel through it.","key":"BD","opts":["amplify","dampen","generate","impede","produce","conceal"],"expl":"dampen（抑制）：空隙会削弱振动。选 BD"},{"id":"v137.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Even though it was the soprano’s first major role with the company, there was no ______ in her masterful performance.","key":"BC","opts":["flamboyance","hesitancy","tentativeness","panache","flaw","exhibitionism"],"expl":"hesitancy（犹豫）：她的表演毫无犹豫。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v138-1","title":"Test 138 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v138.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Monumental changes taking place in the structures of world business match some equally ______ changes taking place in the relations of international companies to the governments with which they deal.","key":"C","opts":["ill-advised","magnanimous","portentous","discreet","overblown"],"expl":"portentous（预示重大变化的）：商业结构的变化与政府关系的变化同样重大。选 C"},{"id":"v138.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The idea of traveling in order to find natural extremes and wonders was (i) ______ in eighteenth-and nineteenth-century Europe, and many European travelers of the period were drawn to Iceland and other North Atlantic countries as places where they might find these (ii) ______ landscapes.","key":"CE","groups":[["rarely articulated","losing favor","not uncommon"],["idyllic","exotic","salubrious"]],"expl":"空1 not uncommon（并不罕见）；空2 exotic（异域的）。选 CE"},{"id":"v138.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Until recently superhero comics were seen as irredeemably (i)_____ ; they were widely disparaged for being so (ii)_______ in conception and execution, and anyone who was a fan was given plenty of reasons to be (iii)______.","key":"ADI","groups":[["puerile","innocuous","facetious"],["lowbrow","shrewd","realistic"],["heartened","emulated","abashed"]],"expl":"空1 puerile（幼稚的）；空2 lowbrow（低俗的）；空3 abashed（羞愧的）。超级英雄漫画被认为幼稚低俗，粉丝因而感到难堪。选 ADI"},{"id":"v138.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"His lackadaisical approach to this project belies his well-known reputation for ______.","key":"BC","opts":["skill","assiduousness","industry","intelligence","facility","innovation"],"expl":"assiduousness（勤勉）与 industry 相对：他的敷衍与其勤勉的名声矛盾。选 BC"},{"id":"v138.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The most interesting discoveries in astronomy are often the things researchers could never have anticipated; new instruments enable scientists to make such ______ discoveries, which can then take years to understand.","key":"DF","opts":["inscrutable","quotidian","provocative","fortuitous","inexplicable","serendipitous"],"expl":"serendipitous（意外获得的）：天文学上的重大发现往往是意外的。选 DF"},{"id":"v138.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The simplicity of Ann Hamilton’s sculpture, a single drop of water snaking its way down a vast white wall, ______ the elaborate technical apparatus hidden beneath its surface.","key":"CD","opts":["minimized","undermined","belied","contradicted","conjured","evoked"],"expl":"belied（掩盖）：简单的外观掩盖了复杂的技术装置。选 CD"},{"id":"v138.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Critics of compost production often do not fully consider the potential environmental benefits of compost use—benefits that might ______ the energy consumption, gaseous emissions, and other negative environmental effects attributable to compost production.","key":"BF","opts":["trigger","offset","intensify","exacerbate","eliminate","counterbalance"],"expl":"offset（抵消）：堆肥的好处可以抵消生产的负面影响。选 BF"}]},{"id":"v138-2","title":"Test 138 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v138.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The ______ effectiveness of lithium as a mood-altering drug for both manic and depressive states cannot be completely explained; most mood-altering drugs can only be used to modify one state or the other.","key":"D","opts":["dubious","neglected","questionable","paradoxical","latent"],"expl":"paradoxical（矛盾的）：锂对两种情绪状态都有效，这一悖论难以解释。选 D"},{"id":"v138.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Parker’s model of human affairs reflects (i)______ outlook, in stark contrast to the generally (ii)______ analyses of her colleagues in the economics department.","key":"AF","groups":[["a sanguine","an introspective","a technical"],["methodological","provisional","pessimistic"]],"expl":"空1 a sanguine（乐观的）；空2 pessimistic（悲观的）。选 AF"},{"id":"v138.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Lebrecht recounts many entertaining scandals, (i) ______ himself on some points in deference to the laws of libel. His anecdotes seem (ii) ______, but when carefully scrutinized, their accuracy is less than impressive. What rings false is his picture of the impresarios as unerring Machiavellian schemers—villains who never (iii) ______ in their efforts to pile up a fortune and ruin the world of music. However, my experience in the concert and recording world suggests that there is more bumbling than sinister plotting.","key":"AEH","groups":[["restraining","indulging","deluding"],["banal","plausible","capricious"],["sympathize","blunder","dissemble"]],"expl":"空1 censoring（审查）；空2 plausible（可信的）；空3 falter（动摇）。选 AEH"},{"id":"v138.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Whatever the level of the museum’s past (i)______ American art, it pales beside its current (ii)_______. Since opening its renovated and expanded building, the museum has relegated American paintings to hard-to-find corners of the museum. It is as if American art is (iii)_____ the overwhelmingly European narrative that dominates the permanent collection galleries.","key":"BEH","groups":[["advocacy of","enthusiasm for","neglect of"],["craze","disdain","support"],["fundamental to","excluded from","privileged over"]],"expl":"空1 achievements in（成就）；空2 holdings（收藏）；空3 overshadowed by（被……遮蔽）。选 BEH"},{"id":"v138.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Someone must have been ______, since by the time the conspirators were ready to act, knowledge of their plot was widespread.","key":"CD","opts":["compromised","warned","indiscreet","injudicious","ignorant","unaware"],"expl":"warned（被警告）：阴谋泄露，说明有人事先得到了警告。选 CD"},{"id":"v138.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"China has a long tradition of ______ the written word; whereas in Renaissance Europe, painting, sculpture, and architecture were viewed as the apex of artistic achievement, in China calligraphy was the preeminent art form.","key":"BF","opts":["embellishing","venerating","preserving","studying","commodifying","exalting"],"expl":"venerating（崇尚）：中国重视书法，把它视为最高艺术形式。选 BF"},{"id":"v138.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While dehydration during pregnancy does not affect aspic vipers’ litter size, pregnant females lost 89 percent more mass than non-reproductive females did when water-deprived, suggesting that female snakes may ______ their own water balance to benefit their offspring.","key":"AD","opts":["compromise","restore","regulate","sacrifice","preserve","stabilize"],"expl":"regulate（调节）：雌蛇可能调节自己的水分平衡以惠及后代。选 AD"}]},{"id":"v139-1","title":"Test 139 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v139.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Readers are interested in Marx’s life because of his ideas, but Sperber’s book downplays his ideas to make room for his life, illustrating why intellectual biography can sometimes be a curiously ______ genre.","key":"C","opts":["self-reflexive","self-glorifying","self-defeating","self-propagating","self-absorbed"],"expl":"self-defeating（自我挫败的）：智识传记反而可能适得其反。选 C"},{"id":"v139.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Testing alternate versions of web pages in real time can make Internet-based companies (i) ______ some user preferences, but that does not necessarily make those companies (ii) ______, as 10,000 ongoing tweaks to the company web site do not add up to a fundamental change of direction when one is needed.","key":"BF","groups":[["severely constrained by","rapidly responsive to","surprisingly indifferent to"],["irresolute","transparent","agile"]],"expl":"空1 severely constrained by（严重受限于）；空2 able to change course（能够改变方向）。选 BF"},{"id":"v139.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Why Zona Gale—a Pulitzer Prize-winning writer whose novels were both a critical and popular success—has fallen so far out of the literary canon is the fascinating subject of Deborah Lindsay Williams’ recent book. Williams concludes that Gale’s embrace of literary (i)______ accounts for her eventual decline in reputation. Gale sought professional affiliation with other women writers of many stripes, and Williams contends that she has therefore been (ii)______ by a later literary paradigm that favors (iii)______ as a marker of artistic prowess.","key":"CDI","groups":[["fame","conservatism","sisterhood"],["marginalized","studied","overrated"],["sociological accuracy","bold risk-taking","individual exceptionalism"]],"expl":"空1 aestheticism（唯美主义）；空2 commercial（商业的）；空3 detached（脱离的）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v139.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"We might be much closer to building the next generation of observatories if competing groups of astronomers had not ______ repeated chances to collaborate; instead, three separate projects with common goals are fighting one another for funding.","key":"AD","opts":["spurned","avoided","sabotaged","rebuffed","initiated","commenced"],"expl":"spurned（拒绝）：天文学家拒绝合作，造成研究资源浪费。选 AD"},{"id":"v139.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Software makers typically write licensing agreements disclaiming responsibility for any negative consequences of using their products, but as computers become integrated into everything from cars to medical devices, that stance will become ______.","key":"BD","opts":["ambiguous","untenable","disfavored","indefensible","unwarranted","gratuitous"],"expl":"indefensible（无法辩护的）：责任豁免将变得站不住脚。选 BD"},{"id":"v139.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Those familiar with the insular conditions that once prevailed in Russia may be surprised by the ______ of eighteenth-century Russian composer Natalia Kurakina, who translated novels from French into Italian and composed songs in both languages.","key":"BE","opts":["versatility","worldliness","dedication","ingenuity","cosmopolitanism","industriousness"],"expl":"cosmopolitanism（世界性）：库拉基娜的作品体现了世界主义。选 BE"},{"id":"v139.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Like his fellow ______ covering the campaign tour, who rarely had the luxury of spending more than one night in one place, Tony had his bags packed well before the evening fund-raiser.","key":"BC","opts":["roisterers","itinerants","peripatetics","carousers","oracles","inquisitors"],"expl":"peripatetics（四处奔波的人）：与其他记者一样，四处奔走。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v139-2","title":"Test 139 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v139.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Even though the survey course was designated as interdisciplinary, it involved no real ______ of subject matter.","key":"D","opts":["distillation","explication","encapsulation","fusion","dilution"],"expl":"fusion（融合）：跨学科课程并没有真正融合学科。选 D"},{"id":"v139.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although all of the major characters in Mendez’ play are historical figures who have been lampooned in many previous works, she (i)______ this tradition in her avoidance of (ii)______.","key":"BF","groups":[["relies on","deviates from","defers to"],["ceremony","verisimilitude","caricature"]],"expl":"空1 deviates from（偏离）；空2 caricature（漫画化）。选 BF"},{"id":"v139.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Although it is quite probable that many small asteroids in the solar system’s asteroid belt have (i)_____, the total mass of these objects cannot be (ii)_____, since the combined gravitational pull of all known asteroids is (iii)______ to fully account for the asteroid belt’s effect on the motion of nearby planets such as Mars.","key":"CDH","groups":[["similar structures","formed by accretion","escaped detection"],["diminishing","estimated","substantial"],["sufficient","unlikely","required"]],"expl":"空1 similar structures（相似结构）；空2 quantified（量化）；空3 inadequate（不足）。选 CDH"},{"id":"v139.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Taruskin’s history of Western music, (i)______ its remarkable length, makes no claims to comprehensiveness. Taruskin is punctilious, and justifiably proud, in emphasizing that his book is a work of history, not a survey of the repertory. In fact, he (ii)______ criticism on grounds of omission by cheerfully admitting he has (iii)______ such side-branch composers as Vaughan Williams, who maintained the British symphonic tradition into the mid-twentieth century.","key":"BDI","groups":[["owing to","despite","reflecting"],["disarms","attacks","obscures"],["extolled","refuted","ignored"]],"expl":"空1 despite（尽管）；空2 dismisses（驳回）；空3 omitted（遗漏）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v139.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Theses defended by contemporary philosophers under the banner of metaphysics typically ______ the claims of science; that is, they cannot be borne out by experiment as the claims of science are expected to be.","key":"EF","opts":["derive from","originate in","contravene","challenge","transcend","go beyond"],"expl":"contravene（违背）：形而上学的主张与科学主张相违背。选 EF"},{"id":"v139.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In medieval China, the Confucian emphasis on rites as an outward manifestation of virtue explains Chinese bureaucrats’ ______ the accurate performance of tributary rituals by foreigners at the imperial court.","key":"BD","opts":["ambivalence toward","preoccupation with","proficiency with","obsession with","regard for","anticipation of"],"expl":"preoccupation with（对……的关注）：官员关注外国人仪式是否准确。选 BD"},{"id":"v139.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The journalist seems to have ______ attitude about truth and falsehood, as exhibited, for example, in a disdain for fact-checking and a repeated failure to correct errors in articles once they are pointed out.","key":"EF","opts":["a self-righteous","a capricious","an impulsive","an unethical","a cavalier","a dismissive"],"expl":"a cavalier（轻率的）：记者对真假显得漠不关心。选 EF"}]},{"id":"v140-1","title":"Test 140 · Section 1","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v140.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Identifying the age of a human cell is tricky because of frequent ______ its biological and chronological ages: a cell that has existed for a relatively short time could function erratically, as if elderly.","key":"D","opts":["disagreement over","correlation between","underestimation of","misalignment of","inattention to"],"expl":"misalignment of（错位）：生物年龄与时间年龄常不一致。选 D"},{"id":"v140.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"For millennia, remembering was hard and costly, and people had to choose deliberately what should be remembered, allowing most things to be forgotten. The digital age has brought about an (i) ______ of the balance of remembering and forgetting. Committing information to digital memory has become (ii) ______.","key":"BD","groups":[["attenuation","inversion","extension"],["the default","a burden","an excuse"]],"expl":"空1 inversion（颠倒）；空2 cheap（廉价的）。选 BD"},{"id":"v140.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Thorough cleanings or restorations that try to return much-loved old master paintings to their original condition (i) ______. Quite apart from a reasonable wariness of paint loss, sheer loyalty to the (ii) ______ look of a work, dirt and all, prejudices many. There are also academics who (iii) ______ the removal of retouches and even of overpaintings, holding that even though they may date from years after the original composition, they embody history in themselves.","key":"CDI","groups":[["generally take years to","are increasingly science","invariably face opposition"],["accustomed","refined","pristine"],["argue for","vacillate about","militate against"]],"expl":"空1 are often unsuccessful（常常失败）；空2 original（原始的）；空3 advocate（主张）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v140.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While lunar geology may appear to be a relatively ______ area of planetary science, it is important to realize that the Moon’s surface and interior retain records that shed light on the histories of all terrestrial planets.","key":"AC","opts":["parochial","insignificant","narrow","new","straightforward","novel"],"expl":"parochial（狭隘的）与 narrow 描述月球地质似乎范围狭窄。选 AC"},{"id":"v140.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Maintaining a tolerant attitude toward pseudoscience might be considered ______, but it could be argued that such a disposition lowers our defenses against more dangerous delusions that are based on similar confusions and fallacies.","key":"AE","opts":["naïve","benign","broad-minded","indulgent","credulous","innocuous"],"expl":"benign（良性的）：容忍伪科学看似无害。选 AE"},{"id":"v140.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"At public appearances the leader was remarkably taciturn, typically making ______ observations before turning the floor over to a colleague.","key":"AE","opts":["trite","insightful","inflammatory","shrewd","perfunctory","brief"],"expl":"perfunctory（敷衍的）：领导人发言简短而敷衍。选 AE"},{"id":"v140.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The rate of sediment deposition may be ______ desertification in Central Asia: data from a Tajik site show the rate to have increased during Pleistocene glacial periods as aridity increased.","key":"BC","opts":["a restraint on","a gauge of","an indicator of","a factor in","a hedge against","a consequence of"],"expl":"a gauge of（衡量）：沉积速率可衡量荒漠化程度。选 BC"}]},{"id":"v140-2","title":"Test 140 · Section 2","group":"Test 131–140","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v140.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Adapting to its changing environment and building its own ecological niche in interactions with other disciplines, the scientific discipline of ecology can be seen as highly ______.","key":"C","opts":["anarchic","cerebral","opportunistic","speculative","competitive"],"expl":"opportunistic（机会主义的）：生态学不断适应、借鉴其他学科。选 C"},{"id":"v140.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Political debates supposedly exist to inform viewers, who watch them with open minds to learn about the candidates and decide how to vote. Of course, given the (i) ______ that routinely permeates most debates, it is hard to (ii) ______ that they fulfill their purpose.","key":"CE","groups":[["heated discussion","ideological division","notorious disingenuousness"],["deny","maintain","complain"]],"expl":"空1 notorious disingenuousness（众所周知的不诚实）；空2 believe（相信）。选 CE"},{"id":"v140.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The guarantee of academic freedom to professors is intended to encourage intellectual independence. But so long as faculty members receive training in a specific academic discipline and are appointed to positions defined by discipline, and so long as colleges and universities are organized by departments that (i)______ long-standing disciplinary traditions, academic freedom will also (ii)______ unique discipline-specific expectations. Yet the right to (iii)______ disciplinary paradigms is also fundamental to academic freedom.","key":"BDG","groups":[["flout","inherit","reinvent"],["tend to embody","fail to communicate","begin to transcend"],["resist","delineate","perpetuate"]],"expl":"空1 reinforce（强化）；空2 disciplinary（学科的）。选 BDG"},{"id":"v140.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Eventually, the framed painting looked as Easton had hoped it would, the frame offering a subtle rebuke to some of the more ostentatious baroque confections on display. Easton believed that it was more (i) ______ than any other frame in the exhibition, despite its (ii) ______ quality. That apparent simplicity, however, was so much more difficult to realize than something more obviously (iii) ______.","key":"CDG","groups":[["nondescript","ornate","striking"],["unassuming","inexpensive","representative"],["sumptuous","fashionable","outmoded"]],"expl":"空1 aesthetically pleasing（美观的）；空2 simplicity（简朴）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v140.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The action in Zadie Smith's novel On Beauty is mediated by an unabashedly ______ narrator who does not hesitate to inform us, as one upon a time the narrators of novels were wont to do, how we behave in general and how society usually works.","key":"AB","opts":["knowing","obtrusive","conspicuous","antiquated","mysterious","secretive"],"expl":"obtrusive（显眼干扰的）：叙述者过分显露。选 AB"},{"id":"v140.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The second group of volunteer excavators was far more ______ than the first, and consequently the obstructing material was removed much more rapidly during the second shift.","key":"AF","opts":["diligent","incapacitated","experienced","punctual","debilitated","industrious"],"expl":"diligent（勤勉的）：第二组志愿者更努力。选 AF"},{"id":"v140.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Tender yet never ______ the memoir engages the reader without resorting to clichés.","key":"AC","opts":["saccharine","unsentimental","cloying","long-winded","pragmatic","affecting"],"expl":"unsentimental（不伤感的）：回忆录真挚却不煽情。选 AC"}]},{"id":"v141-1","title":"Test 141 · Section 1","group":"Test 141–150","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v141.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"One of the reasons why so many rodent species live in rocky habitat is because it is ______: it contains plenty of crevices and cavities in which animals can nest, seek shelter, and find shade.","key":"D","opts":["ecologically stable","readily accessible","hydrologically variable","topographically complex","geographically widespread"],"expl":"topographically complex（地形复杂）：岩石地形提供许多洞穴。选 D"},{"id":"v141.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Most of the bank-efficiency literature suggests that bank mergers culminating in larger, more complex organizations (i) ______ significant economies of scale or scope that are (ii) ______ to consumers. Indeed, some of this literature suggests diseconomies, which would lead to higher loan rates or lower deposit rates for consumers.","key":"AD","groups":[["fail to provide","seek to create","cannot but generate"],["beneficial","responsive","transparent"]],"expl":"空1 fail to provide（未能提供）；空2 passed on（转嫁）。选 AD"},{"id":"v141.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"When reviewing a book that advertises lying as its subject, the critic has a duty to screen the title for possible (i)______, and it is therefore necessary to report that The Concise Book of Lying is not concise. If the book were making a case for deception, the mismatch might not matter : a (ii) ______ title might suit a book designed to disabuse us of our respect for (iii)______. But the book is not an apology for lying; it is on the side of truth.","key":"ADG","groups":[["ambiguity","mendacity","partiality"],["misleading","dependable","verbose"],["brevity","pedantry","veracity"]],"expl":"空1 misleading（误导的）；空2 ironic（具有讽刺意味的）。选 ADG"},{"id":"v141.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"So effective are inhaled steroids at staving off asthma attacks that doctors now regard them as ______ therapy.","key":"AE","opts":["a mainstay of","a precursor to","a supplement to","a complement to","a foundation of","an antithesis to"],"expl":"a mainstay of（支柱）：吸入类固醇是哮喘治疗的主要支柱。选 AE"},{"id":"v141.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Interest in the recovery of lost works by Brazilian women writers is growing as scholars increasingly recognize writing by Brazilian women as inherently worth study, not as ______ writing by Brazilian men.","key":"BE","opts":["divergent from","ancillary to","interchangeable with","antithetical to","subsidiary to","complimentary to"],"expl":"ancillary to（附属于）：巴西女作家的作品不应被视为男作家的附属。选 BE"},{"id":"v141.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The sum of money needed to pay for the additional vaccines may not sound ______, but for developing countries even a small increase in the healthcare budget may prove a very big drain on resources.","key":"BC","opts":["burdensome","paltry","negligible","onerous","sufficient","adequate"],"expl":"paltry（微不足道的）：增加费用对富国来说不算多，但对穷国是沉重负担。选 BC"},{"id":"v141.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"In contrast to today, when many readers consider the moral sentiments expressed in the ancient writer's work to be quite sophomoric, in the writer's own time, these sentiments were regarded as remarkably ______.","key":"CE","opts":["abstruse","misguided","insightful","ill conceived","sagacious","sanguine"],"expl":"sagacious（睿智的）：古代作者的道德观在当时被认为相当睿智。选 CE"}]},{"id":"v141-2","title":"Test 141 · Section 2","group":"Test 141–150","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v141.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Much as our taste for sugar and fat served us well in a world of scarce nutrition but has become ______ in a world of plenty, where we satisfy it to the point of obesity, our memories can work against us in our contemporary information age.","key":"C","opts":["symptomatic","atrophied","maladaptive","nugatory","heritable"],"expl":"maladaptive（适应不良的）：旧有的偏好在新环境中变得有害。选 C"},{"id":"v141.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"When the columnist wrote about controversial issues, her own position was not always (i) ______ her analysis of the arguments being put forth on either side. If she (ii) ______ the reasoning of proponents of one side, that did not mean that she rejected their position.","key":"CF","groups":[["immune to","inferable from","influenced by"],["favored","summarized","challenged"]],"expl":"空1 influenced by（受……影响）；空2 summarized（概括）。选 CF"},{"id":"v141.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Letters present an awkward stumbling block to those who take a high line about literature as a custodian of moral values. The letters of accomplished poets and novelists are—as often as not— about drinking and infidelity, about sponging and wasting time. Consequently, one’s (i)______ the writer as (ii)______ can often come in for a rude shock on contemplation of the writer’s correspondence: the soul that composed the poems and the self that wrote the letters can seem (iii)______.","key":"CEG","groups":[["doubts about","familiarity with","reverence for"],["feckless","exemplary","idiosyncratic"],["irreconcilable","inspirational","exotic"]],"expl":"空1 assumptions about（对……的假设）；空2 saintly（圣洁的）。选 CEG"},{"id":"v141.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"For a philosopher of the analytic tradition, Williams’ approach is somewhat (i) ______. Unlike most analytic philosophers, Williams has not kept himself (ii) ______ the rest of the humanities; in fact, he wishes to address colleagues in other fields in terms that will make sense to them. In particular, he objects to the (iii) ______ character of analytic philosophy: the amount it tries to accomplish by conceptual analysis and a priori argument alone. Williams is convinced that philosophy must use history, including historical imagination, to understand and defend values of any kind.","key":"BDH","groups":[["oracular","unorthodox","bland"],["aloof from","conversant with","exposed to"],["meticulously inclusive","strongly ahistorical","overly contentious"]],"expl":"空1 idiosyncratic（独特的）；空2 apart from（脱离）；空3 abstract（抽象的）。选 BDH"},{"id":"v141.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Egyptologists’ recent classification of a cavity found in the Great Pyramid as ______ seems premature: the inside of the Great Pyramid is filled with stones of irregular sizes, so small gaps appear unavoidable.","key":"BE","opts":["eroded","deliberate","accessible","ceremonial","purposeful","penetrable"],"expl":"deliberate（刻意的）：空腔的分类为刻意设计似乎为时过早。选 BE"},{"id":"v141.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Magazines use superlatives to generate excitement and make stories seem worth reading, and not even the most punctilious fact-checkers at the most principled magazines can fight off all the ______ claims.","key":"BC","opts":["uncategorizable","unwarranted","dubious","idiosyncratic","innocuous","noteworthy"],"expl":"unwarranted（没有根据的）：杂志的夸张说法不应被接受。选 BC"},{"id":"v141.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Hugh Trevor-Roper’s series of essays on the Puritan Revolution are considered to be the ______ of the genre: though these essays have exerted a welcome influence on the work of many subsequent historians, their quality has never been equaled.","key":"BD","opts":["embodiment","apogee","forerunner","acme","precursor","paradigm"],"expl":"apogee（巅峰）：特雷弗-罗珀的论文被认为是体裁的巅峰。选 BD"}]},{"id":"v142-1","title":"Test 142 · Section 1","group":"Test 141–150","difficulty":"easy","questions":[{"id":"v142.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The effect of the film’s expansive, darkly mournful opening sequence was magnified by a score that was similarly ______ and unrelenting.","key":"D","opts":["iridescent","volatile","equivocal","plangent","blithe"],"expl":"plangent（哀伤回响的）：配乐的哀伤与开场画面相呼应。选 D"},{"id":"v142.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Humans can have (i) ______ tastes: crab brains and squeezable cheese are delicacies to many people, even as others find them repulsive. The preference for sweet and abhorrence of bitter is (ii) ______, however.","key":"CF","groups":[["self-indulgent","refined","idiosyncratic"],["explicable","strong","universal"]],"expl":"空1 idiosyncratic（独特的）；空2 universal（普遍的）。选 CF"},{"id":"v142.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"There is a clear trend away from automobile ownership and solo driving among young people. One view holds that these young people will (i) ______ as they age, but Willson argues that the trend is (ii) ______ one. As a result, car-free lifestyles will become more (iii) ______.","key":"CDI","groups":[["support mass transit","reject the automobile","increase vehicle ownership"],["a durable","a noticeable","an illusory"],["onerous","expedient","common"]],"expl":"空1 reject the automobile（拒绝汽车）；空2 temporary（暂时的）；空3 common（普遍的）。选 CDI"},{"id":"v142.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The Chippewa regarded their treaties with the federal government as solemn covenants and therefore, throughout the twentieth century, met efforts by governmental officials to ______ those treaties with both open and hidden resistance.","key":"BE","opts":["replicate","abrogate","respect","renegotiate","nullify","honor"],"expl":"空缺处为“用公开和隐蔽的抵抗”，abrogate（废除）与 nullify（作废）最贴切。选 BE"},{"id":"v142.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The reader does well to approach claims in this autobiography with a certain amount of friendly skepticism, but the overall impression it conveys is that veracity wins out over ______.","key":"BC","opts":["blame","invention","contrivance","censure","venom","concern"],"expl":"invention（编造）：作者的自传虽有怀疑之处，但真实仍胜过编造。选 BC"},{"id":"v142.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The artist reworked certain of his etchings in order to make the scenes they depict more logical, yet, paradoxically, the pictorial space seems to become more ______ the more realistically it is defined.","key":"DF","opts":["austere","cogent","lucid","fanciful","ominous","chimerical"],"expl":"fanciful（幻想的）：画面越真实，却越显得虚幻。选 DF"},{"id":"v142.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Hoping to build a broader audience, the museum has mounted several exhibitions based on popular culture, but their impact on attendance has been negligible, and some complain that this direction has ______ the museum’s stature.","key":"BE","opts":["protracted","undermined","burnished","augmented","diminished","perpetuated"],"expl":"undermined（损害）：流行文化展览可能损害博物馆的声望。选 BE"}]},{"id":"v142-2","title":"Test 142 · Section 2","group":"Test 141–150","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v142.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"The growth of kelp in the kelp bed communities of the North Pacific Ocean is ______ sea otters: the otters prey on kelp-eating sea urchins, keeping the urchin population in check.","key":"D","opts":["impeded by","detected by","invisible to","facilitated by","disruptive for"],"expl":"facilitated by（得益于）：海獭的捕食使海藻得以生长。选 D"},{"id":"v142.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"The garments created by Tunisian fashion designer Salah Barka, though not understated in style, are (i) ______ in their references to local cultures and histories: Barka evokes Africa without (ii) ______ readily discernible indigenous stylistic elements.","key":"AD","groups":[["subtle","commanding","inconsistent"],["direct reproduction of","obvious departure from","imaginative adaptations of"]],"expl":"空1 subtle（微妙的）；空2 direct reproduction of（直接复制）。选 AD"},{"id":"v142.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Despite the apparently natural—if not essential—relationship between insult and (i)______, for some people the experience of getting insulted may cause (ii)______: instead of lashing out at the offender, they end up (iii)______.","key":"CEH","groups":[["self-esteem","injury","anger"],["outrage","dejection","confusion"],["reacting swiftly","suffering inwardly","recovering easily"]],"expl":"空1 self-esteem（自尊）；空2 dejection（沮丧）；空3 turning inward（转向内心）。选 CEH"},{"id":"v142.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"Statistics is the branch of applied mathematics that studies ways of drawing inferences from limited and imperfect data. Of course, if all data sources were totally (i) ______, statisticians could do little but (ii) ______ every conclusion with “but we could be wrong about this.” A mathematical science of statistics is possible because, although repeating an experiment numerous times may not yield uniform results, some results are more (iii) ______ than others.","key":"BDI","groups":[["empirical","capricious","defensible"],["qualify","affirm","substantiate"],["dubious","unexpected","common"]],"expl":"空1 unreliable（不可靠的）；空2 qualify（限定）。选 BDI"},{"id":"v142.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Nancy Weiss Malkiel’s painstakingly detailed history of coeducation at elite universities is an invaluable ______ the amnesia that has come to envelop even such a relatively recent—but critically neglected—development.","key":"AD","opts":["antidote to","summary of","reinterpretation of","corrective to","diagnosis of","addition to"],"expl":"corrective to（矫正）：这部著作矫正了人们的健忘。选 AD"},{"id":"v142.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The attempt by some nineteenth-century physicists to reduce ordinary matter to electromagnetic fields was ______, but once it was one of the biggest hopes of theoretical physics.","key":"BF","opts":["counterproductive","unsuccessful","ill-conceived","ridiculed","overambitious","futile"],"expl":"futile（徒劳的）：把物质还原为电磁场的尝试最终徒劳。选 BF"},{"id":"v142.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"While traditional Chinese historiography ostensibly described events in a neutral manner, early historians did not always ______ tendentiousness, sometimes offering moral judgments about the historical figures they discussed.","key":"AB","opts":["eschew","forgo","denounce","descry","defend","justify"],"expl":"eschew（避免）：早期史家并未避免倾向性。选 AB"}]},{"id":"v143-1","title":"Test 143 · Section 1","group":"Test 141–150","difficulty":"medium","questions":[{"id":"v143.1.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Rather than use the traditional therapy, the physician employed unorthodox treatments ______ by her more conventional colleagues.","key":"B","opts":["engendered","repudiated","developed","espoused","adopted"],"expl":"repudiated（否定）：医生采用的疗法与同事的主流方法相反。选 B"},{"id":"v143.1.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Science is so good at what it does that many people feel a (i) ______ to apply it to social and political issues, yet experience shows that science may add little to or even (ii) ______ social and political questions.","key":"BE","groups":[["provocation","temptation","reluctance"],["augur","occlude","abet"]],"expl":"空1 temptation（诱惑）；空2 occlude（遮蔽）。选 BE"},{"id":"v143.1.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"The rural Renaissance villas were working buildings. The agricultural world they served is now gone. To see it you therefore have to (i) ______ it, but that can be aided by the nineteenth-century photographs taken just before the agricultural revolution destroyed the old order. Not that those photographs themselves are always completely(ii) ______: Virginia creeper growing up a Renaissance villa is a botanical anachronism and also (iii) ______ piece of planting (rats climb up the creepers and get at the grain stored in the attic).","key":"AFH","groups":[["imagine","improvise","visit"],["exhaustive","undamaged","germane"],["an ornamental","a foolish","an imitative"]],"expl":"空1 imagine（想象）；空2 reliable（可靠的）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v143.1.4","n":4,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The climate researchers’ ______ method of presentation caused a stir among those who felt that scientific papers should be dispassionate in their delivery of evidence.","key":"AC","opts":["prejudicial","slapdash","tendentious","perfunctory","meticulous","incohesive"],"expl":"tendentious（有倾向性的）：气候研究者的表述有倾向性，引起争议。选 AC"},{"id":"v143.1.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Astute and incisive, the essayist’s work was nevertheless civil and polite: the essayist either had no gift of ______ or else never felt any.","key":"AF","opts":["vitriol","clairvoyance","theatricality","prescience","mimicry","obloquy"],"expl":"vitriol（尖刻）：作者的文章没有尖刻的火气。选 AF"},{"id":"v143.1.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"The idea that Jim was ______, that he loved fighting for the sake of fighting, was a mistake; in reality he was a kind and gentle person.","key":"AE","opts":["truculent","audacious","brazen","obtuse","pugnacious","disobedient"],"expl":"truculent（凶狠好斗的）：吉姆并非好斗之人。选 AE"},{"id":"v143.1.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"James Baldwin (1924-1987) recognized that American writers, who are inescapably products of American politics, do not ______ the terms of the national conversation, but he emphasized their capacity to reshape the language in which it occurs.","key":"AE","opts":["ordain","transcend","disseminate","rectify","dictate","amend"],"expl":"dictate（规定）：作家不能规定全国对话的条款，但可以重塑语言。选 AE"}]},{"id":"v143-2","title":"Test 143 · Section 2","group":"Test 141–150","difficulty":"hard","questions":[{"id":"v143.2.1","n":1,"kind":"pick1","stem":"Other company insiders have recently offered testimony that ______ several of the more lurid anecdotes found in Belmer’s account, though that testimony hardly minimizes the company’s culture of malfeasance and mismanagement.","key":"A","opts":["tempers","corroborates","outdoes","exploits","foreshadows"],"expl":"corroborates（证实）：其他内部证词证实了部分轶事。选 A"},{"id":"v143.2.2","n":2,"kind":"multi","stem":"Cells (i) ______ glucose if they are (ii) ______ it, but conversely they destroy glucose-creating enzymes upon return to glucose-replete conditions.","key":"CE","groups":[["detect","redirect","synthesize"],["supplied with","deprived of","signaled by"]],"expl":"空1 synthesize（合成）；空2 deprived of（缺乏）。选 CE"},{"id":"v143.2.3","n":3,"kind":"multi","stem":"Often evasive and at times even (i) ______, the gubernatorial candidate came off (ii) ______ at her press conference today in ways that should give voters cause to (iii) ______ her, regardless of whether they agree with the substance of her views.","key":"CDG","groups":[["humorous","blunt","mendacious"],["badly","convincingly","unexceptionally"],["reject","champion","emulate"]],"expl":"空1 mendacious（撒谎的）；空2 badly（糟糕地）；空3 reject（拒绝）。选 CDG"},{"id":"v143.2.4","n":4,"kind":"multi","stem":"A prospective reader may well wonder whether the book would not be better classified as a somewhat unorthodox biography, but the author stands firm on its status as a work of fiction. She has drawn inspiration from the facts, the author tells us, but has (i) ______ them, editing and rearranging events. Also, she has felt free to (ii) ______ what her characters were feeling and what was going on in their minds—to invent, within the limits of plausibility, what could not be (iii) ______.","key":"AFH","groups":[["reshaped","expunged","verified"],["ignore","deny","imagine"],["believed","ascertained","described"]],"expl":"空1 embellished（渲染）；空2 invent（虚构）。选 AFH"},{"id":"v143.2.5","n":5,"kind":"pick2","stem":"One of the reporter’s central themes is that health care concerns were a secondary consideration to the reformers in their drive to limit if not completely ______ the consumption of cigarettes.","key":"BE","opts":["indulge","proscribe","damage","spurn","disallow","impair"],"expl":"proscribe（禁止）：改革者试图禁止吸烟。选 BE"},{"id":"v143.2.6","n":6,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Because the fundamental nature of language is so intangible, because there is no agreed-upon way to determine its existence, it is easy to dismiss new evidence of ostensible animal language as inadequate—quite ______, but insufficient.","key":"BD","opts":["equivocal","intriguing","controvertible","provocative","viable","dubitable"],"expl":"controvertible（可争议的）：新证据被轻视，却也并非毫无道理。选 BD"},{"id":"v143.2.7","n":7,"kind":"pick2","stem":"Whether the film is ______ adaptation of the legend is debatable: the author of the screenplay claims that it was based on the original tale, but admits taking some interpretive license with the story.","key":"BF","opts":["an inspired","a rigorous","an unsentimental","a successful","a sober","a faithful 答案获取⽅式 进⼊ “ GRE”，输⼊⼝令“填空机经2000题答案”。 解析获取⽅式 进⼊ “ GRE”，输⼊⼝令“jjtest1 ”代表第1个test的解析，以此类推。"],"expl":"a faithful（忠实的）：影片是否忠于传说有争议。选 BF"}]}]};
